hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11484","(11479) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi informed us, Musaddad informed us, Abu al-Ahwas informed us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from people of the family of Safwan ibn Umayya, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed weapons from Safwan ibn Umayya. Safwan said, \As a loan or by force?\"" He said"","" \""Rather"","" as a loan.\"" So he lent him between thirty and forty coats of mail. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought at Hunayn"","" and when Allah defeated the polytheists"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"","" \""Gather Safwan's coats of mail.\"" They found some of his coats missing"","" so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Safwan"","" \""If you wish"","" we shall compensate you for them.\"" He said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" there is in my heart today a faith that was not in it on that day.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11485","(11480) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba informed us, Jarir from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from people of the family of 'Abd Allah ibn Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \O Safwan"","" do you have weapons?\"" Then he mentioned its meaning. [Da'if]"""""
"11486","(11481) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Anas ibn Iyyad al-Laythi informed me, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father: That Safwan ibn Umayya lent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weapons, consisting of eighty coats of mail. He said to him, \As a guaranteed loan or by force?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"","" \""Rather"","" as a guaranteed loan.\"" And some of these reports"","" even if they are mursal"","" are strengthened by their corroborating witnesses along with what has preceded of the connected narrations. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""""
"11487","(11482) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-'Abbas al-Ma'qili informed us, al-Saghani informed us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' said: Sa'id ibn Aruba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \The hand is responsible for what it takes until it returns it.\"" Then al-Hasan forgot his hadith and said"","" \""Your trustee is not liable.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11488","(11483) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us, Muhammad ibn Sharik informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, who said: Ibn 'Abbas used to hold one liable for the loaned property, and he wrote to me instructing me to hold one liable for it. [Sahih]"
"11489","(11484) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Najda informed us, Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us, Sufyan from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ibn 'Abbas regarding the loaned property: He said, \He is liable.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11490","(11485) Imam Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us, Abu al-Hasan ibn Firas informed us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Subayh informed us, Sufyan — (h) — and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Armuwi informed us, Shafi' ibn Muhammad informed us, Abu Ja'far al-Tahawi said: I heard al-Muzani saying, \We read back to al-Shafi'i"","" from Sufyan"","" from 'Amr ibn Dinar"","" from 'Abd al-Rahman\"" — Abu Ja'far said: He is Ibn al-Sa'ib — \""that a man borrowed a camel from another man"","" and it perished. He was brought before Marwan ibn al-Hakam"","" so Marwan sent to Abu Hurayra and asked him. He said"","" 'He is liable.'\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11491","(11486) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb, Qatādah, Ḥabīb, and Yūnus, from Ibn Sīrīn, that Shuʿayh said: \There is no liability upon the trustee (mustawdaʿ) except in the case of treachery (ghulūl)"","" and there is no liability upon the borrower (mustaʿīr) except in the case of treachery.\"" This is the preserved narration from al-Qāḍī Shuʿayh as his own statement. [Ḥasan]"""""
"11492","(11487) ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated it from ʿUbaydah ibn Ḥassān, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ. Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Qāsim ibn Jaʿfar al-Kawkabī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated it. ʿAlī said: \ʿAmr and ʿUbaydah are both weak (ḍaʿīf). It is only narrated from al-Qāḍī Shuʿayh as a non-elevated (mawqūf) statement.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11493","(11488) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from Jābir, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Whoever builds upon the land of a people without their permission"","" his building shall be demolished; and if he builds with their permission"","" he shall be entitled to its value.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11494","(11489) He said: And Sharīk narrated to us from Jābir, from ʿĀmir, who said: \Its value shall be assessed on the day he is evicted from it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11495","(11490) Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: Qays and Isrāʾīl narrated from Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, from Shuʿayh, regarding one who builds upon the land of a people with their permission: \He shall be entitled to the value of his building.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11496","(11491) He said: And Qays narrated to us from Jābir, from al-Qāsim, from Shuʿayh, a statement similar to that of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. And a marfūʿ (elevated) narration has been reported concerning this, but it is not established. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"11497","(11492) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Maymūn ibn Maslamah narrated to us: Kathīr ibn Abī Ṣābir narrated to us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Muslim al-Khaffāf narrated from ʿUmar ibn Qays, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever builds upon the plots of a people with their permission"","" he shall be entitled to its value; and whoever builds without their permission"","" his building shall be demolished.\"" ʿUmar ibn Qays al-Makkī is weak (ḍaʿīf) and cannot be used as evidence"","" and those below him in the chain are also weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11498","(11493) Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Baghdad: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ṣawwāf narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Marwazī narrated to us, both saying: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad narrated from Wāqid ibn Muḥammad, who said: I heard my father saying: ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn ʿUmar, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \Do you know which month you consider most sacred?\"" They said: \""This month of ours.\"" He said: \""Do you know which land you consider most sacred?\"" They said: \""This land of ours.\"" He said: \""Do you know which day is most sacred?\"" They said: \""This day of ours.\"" He said: \""Indeed"","" Allah has made sacred upon you your blood"","" your wealth"","" and your honours"","" except by right"","" just as the sanctity of this day of yours"","" in this land of yours. Have I not conveyed?\"" He said this three times"","" and to all of that they responded: \""Yes"","" indeed.\"" [Bukhārī 6785"","" Muslim 66]"""""
"11499","(11494) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, mentioning it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: \Do you know which land? Do you know which day?\"" And he said: \""Is this not our month? Is this not our land? Is this not our day?\"" And he added in it: \""From this month of yours.\"" And he added at the end: He said: \""Woe to you"","" or destruction be upon you! Do not return after me as disbelievers"","" striking one another's necks.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh"","" from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11500","(11495) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Naẓīf al-Miṣrī informed us in Makkah: Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr ibn al-Sarī al-Rāfiqī narrated to us by dictation: Abū ʿUmar Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Hilāl al-Qutabī narrated to us: Hawdhah ibn Khalīfah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from Abī Bakrah, who said: When that day came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted his she-camel and then stopped and said: \Do you know what day this is?\"" We remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)?\"" We said: \""Indeed.\"" Then he said: \""Do you know what month this is?\"" We remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not Dhū al-Ḥijjah?\"" They said: \""Indeed"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Do you know what land this is?\"" We remained silent until we thought he would name it by other than its name. He said: \""Is this not the Sacred City (al-Baladah)?\"" We said: \""Indeed.\"" He said: \""Indeed"","" your wealth"","" your honours"","" and your blood are sacred among you"","" like the sanctity of this day of yours"","" in this month of yours"","" in this land of yours. Let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent\"" — he said this twice — \""for often the one to whom it is conveyed retains it better than the one who heard it.\"" Then he inclined toward his she-camel toward some sheep and began distributing them"","" giving one sheep between two men and one sheep among three men. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn and others. [Bukhārī 1742"","" Muslim 1679]"""""
"11501","(11496) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us by dictation; he informed us: Abū al-Muthannā, Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan, and Hishām ibn ʿAlī — they said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abū Saʿīd, the freedman of ʿĀmir ibn Kurayz, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Do not envy one another"","" do not hate one another"","" do not engage in Najash (artificially inflating prices)"","" do not turn your backs on one another"","" and let not some of you sell over the sale of others. Be servants of Allah"","" brothers to one another. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim: he does not wrong him"","" nor forsake him"","" nor despise him. Taqwā is here.\"" — and he pointed to his chest three times — \""It is sufficient evil for a man that he despise his Muslim brother. Every Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his blood"","" his wealth"","" and his honour.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Muslim 2564]"""""
"11502","(11497) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq — informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission. Would any one of you like for his drinking vessel to be brought and its contents to be spilled out"","" so that his food is lost? Indeed"","" the udders of their livestock store for them their sustenance. So let no one milk the livestock of another without his permission.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik.\n\n[Al-Bukhārī 2435"","" Muslim 1726]"""""
"11503","(11498) And Abū Muḥammad — Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī al-Muḥāribī — narrated to us in al-Kūfah: Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī al-Hamadhānī narrated to us upon returning from Makkah: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: ʿAdīy ibn Thābit narrated to us; he said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī — and he was his grandfather, his mother's father — say:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade plunder (al-Nuhbah) and mutilation (al-Muthlah).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās. [Al-Bukhārī 2474]"""""
"11504","(11499) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās — meaning Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Dawrī — informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say:\n\n\Let none of you take the belonging of his brother in jest. And if any one of you takes the staff of his brother"","" let him return it to him.\"""""""
"11505","(11500) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Oppression (ẓulm) shall be darknesses (ẓulumāt) on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz.\n\n[Al-Bukhārī 2447"","" Muslim 2579]"""""
"11506","(11501) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī informed us in Marw: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Miqsam, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Beware of oppression"","" for oppression shall be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of miserliness (shuhḥ)"","" for miserliness destroyed those before you. It led them to shed their blood and to deem their forbidden things lawful.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Muslim 2578]"""""
"11507","(11502) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq al-Makkī narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣayfī, from Abū Maʿbad, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) to Yemen — the hadith — and at the end of it he said:\n\n\Beware of the supplication of the oppressed"","" for there is no veil between it and Allah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Wakīʿ and others. [Al-Bukhārī 2448"","" Muslim 19]"""""
"11508","(11503) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah, in the Sacred Mosque, in the year 340 AH: al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us: Abū Mushir ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Mushir narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, from Rabiʿah ibn Yazīd, from Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī, from Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who reported from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that He said:\n\n\I have forbidden oppression upon Myself and have made it forbidden among you"","" so do not oppress one another. O My servants"","" you are those who err by night and by day"","" and I am the One who forgives sins"","" and I do not care. So seek My forgiveness and I shall forgive you. O My servants"","" all of you are hungry except whom I feed"","" so ask Me for food and I shall feed you. O My servants"","" all of you are naked except whom I clothe"","" so ask Me for clothing and I shall clothe you. O My servants"","" if the first of you and the last of you"","" and the jinn among you and the humans among you"","" were all to possess the heart of the most God-fearing man among you"","" that would not increase My dominion in the least. O My servants"","" if the first of you and the last of you"","" and the jinn among you and the humans among you"","" were all to possess the heart of the most wicked man among you"","" that would not decrease My dominion in the least. O My servants"","" if the first of you and the last of you"","" and the jinn among you and the humans among you"","" were all to gather in a single plain and ask Me"","" and I were to give each person what he asked for"","" that would not decrease My dominion in the least — except as the needle"","" when dipped into the sea once"","" diminishes it. O My servants"","" it is only your deeds that I have recorded for you. So whoever finds good"","" let him praise Allah"","" and whoever finds other than that"","" let him blame none but himself.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī"","" from Abū Mushir. [Muslim 2577]"""""
"11509","(11504) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; he said: I was informed —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Do you know who the bankrupt one is?\"" They said: \""The bankrupt one among us is he who has neither dirham nor possessions.\"" He said: \""The bankrupt one of my Ummah is the one who will come on the Day of Resurrection with prayers"","" fasting"","" and zakah"","" but he will come having reviled this one"","" slandered this one"","" consumed the wealth of this one"","" shed the blood of this one"","" and struck this one. So this one shall be given from his good deeds"","" and that one shall be given from his good deeds. If his good deeds are exhausted before what is owed against him is fulfilled"","" then some of their sins shall be taken and cast upon him"","" and then he shall be cast into the Fire.\""\n\nThe wording of both their narrations is the same"","" except that in the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān it reads: \""So this one shall be compensated from his good deeds.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others. [Muslim 2582]"""""
"11510","(11505) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\The rights shall be restored to their rightful owners on the Day of Resurrection"","" to the point that the hornless sheep shall receive retribution from the horned sheep.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others. [Muslim 2582]"""""
"11511","(11506) 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubaid al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib from 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam from al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, who said: When this verse was revealed — \Indeed"","" you will die"","" and indeed"","" they will die\"" (39:30) — al-Zubayr said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" will that which occurs between us"","" along with the specific sins"","" be repeated back to us?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" it will certainly be repeated back to you"","" until every rightful person is restored his right.\"" Al-Zubayr said: \""By Allah"","" the matter is indeed severe.\"" [Its chain is munkar.]"""""
"11512","(11507) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, Burayd narrated from his grandfather Abu Burda from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"","" Allah grants respite to the oppressor until"","" when He seizes him"","" He does not let him escape.\"" Then he recited: \""And such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the cities while they are doing wrong. Indeed"","" His seizure is painful and severe.\"" (11:102) Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Sadaqah ibn al-Fadl from Abu Mu'awiya"","" and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr. [Bukhari 4686"","" Muslim 2584]"""""
"11513","(11508) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha' from Mu'awiya ibn Suwayd, i.e., ibn Muqarrin, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven things. He said: \He commanded us to visit the sick"","" to follow funeral processions"","" to spread the greeting of peace"","" to accept invitations"","" to respond to one who sneezes"","" to help the oppressed"","" and to fulfill oaths. And he forbade us from drinking from silver vessels — for whoever drinks from them in this world will not drink from them in the Hereafter — and from wearing gold rings"","" and from riding on silk-covered saddles"","" and from wearing silk"","" brocade"","" heavy silk"","" and istabraq.\"" Both al-Bukhari and Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Shaybani and others. [Bukhari 2446"","" Muslim 2066]"""""
"11514","(11509) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Malas al-Numayri narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us, Humayd narrated, and Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Help your brother"","" whether he is an oppressor or oppressed.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I would help him if he is oppressed"","" but how do I help him if he is an oppressor?\"" He said: \""You prevent him from committing oppression — that is your help to him.\"" [Bukhari 2443"","" Muslim 2066]"""""
"11515","(11510) Abu 'Abdullah informed us, 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated to us, Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated from Humayd from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Help your brother"","" whether he is an oppressor or oppressed.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this — we can help him when he is oppressed — but how do we help him when he is an oppressor?\"" He said: \""You restrain him (by seizing him) above his hands.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Musaddad. [Sahih]"""""
"11516","(11511) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated from Burayd from Abu Burda from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The believer to another believer is like a building"","" one part of which strengthens the other.\"" And he interlaced his fingers. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from Abu Kurayb from Abu Usama. [Bukhari 2446"","" Muslim 2585]"""""
"11517","(11512) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran narrated to us in Baghdad, Abu al-Husayn 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Ali ibn Mukram narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihab that Salim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar informed him that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim — he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Whoever is in need of his brother"","" Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" attends to his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a hardship"","" Allah will relieve him thereby of a hardship from the hardships of the Day of Resurrection. And who covers (the faults of) a Muslim"","" Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" will cover him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutayba from al-Layth. [Bukhari 2442"","" Muslim 2580]"""""
"11518","(11513) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever among you sees an evil"","" let him change it with his hand; if he is unable to do so"","" then with his tongue; and if he is unable to do so"","" then with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Thawri and others. [Bukhari 956"","" Muslim 49]"""""
"11519","(11514) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajanī informed us, saying: Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us, Hamid ibn Abi Hamid narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated from 'Ata' from Muharib from Ibn Burayda from his father, who said: When Ja'far ibn Abi Talib arrived from the land of Abyssinia, the Prophet (ﷺ) met him and said: \Tell me of the most remarkable thing you witnessed in the land of Abyssinia.\"" He said: \""A woman passed by with a basket of food on her head. A man on horseback passed by her and struck her"","" causing it to fall"","" and he threw it away. I watched her as she gathered it back into her basket"","" saying: 'Woe to you"","" on the day when the King shall set up His Throne and take the rights of the oppressed from the oppressor!'\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) laughed until his back teeth became visible"","" and he said: \""How can a nation be sanctified that does not take the right of its weak from its strong without being hindered?\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11520","(11515) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us, Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Abi Sa'd narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from Muharib ibn Dithar from Ibn Burayda from his father, and he mentioned the hadith with its meaning. [Da'if]"
"11521","(11516) Abū Manṣūr — al-Dhufur ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him — informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mātī informed us in Kūfah; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim al-Ghifārī informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr al-Fuqaymī from Muḥammad ibn Muslim from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you see my Ummah unable to say to the oppressor"","" 'You are an oppressor"",""' then know that they have been abandoned.\"" This Muḥammad ibn Muslim is Abū al-Zubayr"","" and he did not hear from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ.\n\n[Weak. Aḥmad 2/163]\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb said: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: Abū al-Zubayr did not hear from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11522","(11517) Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn says: The hearing (samāʿ) of Abū al-Zubayr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ is not established."
"11523","(11518) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us with its authenticity: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī informed us; Shabābah informed us; Abū Shihāb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr from the Prophet (ﷺ) a hadith similar to it. [Weak]"
"11524","(11519) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl informed us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The hand is responsible for what it has taken until it returns it.\"" [Weak. Aḥmad 5/8"","" 2:20346]"""""
"11525","(11520) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik ibn Anas and others informed me from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees his share in a slave (held in partnership)"","" and he has sufficient means to purchase the remainder of the slave's value"","" a fair valuation shall be placed upon the slave"","" and his partners shall be given their shares"","" and the slave shall be fully emancipated upon him. Otherwise"","" only that portion of the slave shall be freed which he has freed.\"" Both (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) agreed upon its inclusion in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Bukhārī 2522"","" Muslim 1501]"""""
"11526","(11521) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr informed us; Ḥumayd narrated — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, and the wording is his: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Musaddad informed us; Yaḥyā narrated from Ḥumayd from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at the home of one of his wives when one of the Mothers of the Believers sent a vessel containing food with a servant. She (the wife in whose home the Prophet was) struck the servant's hand and the vessel broke. He (the Prophet ﷺ) gathered the pieces together, placed the food back into it, and said: \Eat.\"" He detained the servant and the vessel until they had finished eating. Then he sent the intact vessel to the messenger (the wife who had sent it) and kept the broken one. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Bukhārī 2481]"""""
"11527","(11522) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us; Ḥumayd narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) was at the home of one of his wives when one of the Mothers of the Believers sent a large bowl containing food. The wife in whose home the Prophet was struck the servant's hand, and the bowl fell and broke into two pieces. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered the two pieces together and began placing the food that had been in the bowl back into it, saying: \Your mother is jealous.\"" He detained the servant until a bowl was brought from the home of the wife in whose house he was. He then sent the intact bowl to the one whose bowl had been broken and kept the broken one in the home of the one who had broken it. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ with this wording from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUlayyah from Ḥumayd.\n\nSome scholars of knowledge said: Both bowls belonged to the Prophet (ﷺ) and were in the homes of his two wives. There was no liability (taḍmīn) involved; rather"","" he punished the one who broke it by leaving the broken bowl in her home and transferring the intact bowl to the home of her companion. And Allah knows best. [Bukhārī 5225]"""""
"11528","(11523) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us; Sufyān said: Fulayt narrated to me from Jassrah ibn Dijājah from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I have never seen a food preparer like Ṣafiyyah"","" may Allah be pleased with her. She sent a vessel containing food to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and I struck it with my hand and broke it. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" what is the expiation for this?' He said: 'A vessel in place of a vessel and food in place of food.'\"" Fulayt al-ʿĀmirī and Jassrah ibn Dijājah — there is some discussion regarding them. Then the interpretation of the report is as has passed. And with Allah lies success.\n\nIt has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī that he said regarding a man whose wheat is consumed: \""Upon its owner is food equivalent to his food and a measure equivalent to his measure.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11529","(11524) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us — (ḥ) and Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Shaʿrānī informed us; my grandfather informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed me; my father narrated from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dīlī from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and mentioned the hadith, and in it is: \It is not lawful for a person to take anything from the wealth of his brother except what he gives willingly. Do not oppress"","" and do not return to disbelief after me"","" striking one another's necks.\"" [Ḥasan for other than it]"""""
"11530","(11525) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us; Abū ʿĀmir informed us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan informed me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd informed me; he said: I heard ʿUmārah ibn Ḥārithah al-Ḍamrī narrating from ʿAmr ibn Yathribī al-Ḍamrī, who said: \I attended the sermon of the Prophet (ﷺ) at Minā"","" and among what he said in his sermon was: 'It is not lawful for anyone to take from the wealth of his brother except what his soul is pleased with.' When he (the narrator) heard that"","" he said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" what do you think if I come upon the sheep of my paternal uncle and take a sheep and slaughter it — is there any liability upon me for that?' He said: 'If you find a ewe carrying a knife and a fire-stone in the desert of al-Jamīsh"","" do not touch it.'\"" It was said: It is a desolate land between Makkah and al-Jār where no one dwells. [Weak]"""""
"11531","(11526) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq ibn Yazīd al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me, saying: Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah informed me, saying: Ṣadaqah ibn Yasār informed me from Ibn ʿUmar, and he mentioned the hadith regarding the sermon of the Prophet ﷺ in the middle of the days of Tashrīq during his Hajj, and he said therein: \O people"","" whoever has a trust in his possession"","" let him return it to the one who entrusted it to him. O people"","" it is not lawful for a person to take anything from the wealth of his brother except that which is given with his willing consent.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11532","(11527) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad Dalaḥ ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, saying: al-Firyābī narrated to me, saying: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Muqaddamī narrated to me, saying: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, saying: my brother narrated to me from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī narrated to me, saying: Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, saying: my brother narrated to me from Sulaymān from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, had a young boy who used to bring him earnings, and Abū Bakr used to eat from his earnings. One day he brought something, and Abū Bakr ate from it. The boy said to him: \Do you know what this is?\"" Abū Bakr said: \""What is it?\"" He said: \""I used to practice soothsaying for a man in the Jāhiliyyah"","" and I was not skilled in soothsaying except that I deceived him. Then he met me and gave me this in return for that. This is what you have eaten from.\"" So Abū Bakr inserted his hand and vomited everything that was in his stomach.\n\nThe wording of both their narrations is the same; the difference is only in the chain of narration. al-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ in this manner. [Bukhārī 3842]"""""
"11533","(11528) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl and Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd both said: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Jarīr narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmī from his father from a man from Muzaynah, who said: A woman from among the Muslims of Quraysh prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and invited him and his Companions. He said: My father went with me along with him. He said: We sat in the gatherings of the sons among their fathers. He said: They did not eat until they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a morsel, he threw it down and said: \I find the taste of the meat of a sheep that was slaughtered without the permission of its owner.\"" She said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" he is my brother"","" and I am among the most honored of people to him. If there were anything better than this"","" he would not have entrusted it to me"","" and it is upon me to please him with something better than this.\"" But he refused to eat from it and ordered that the food be given to the captives.\n\nThe Sheikh said: This was because he feared corruption upon him"","" and its owner was absent"","" so he saw it as a matter of public interest to feed it to the captives"","" and Allah knows best. Then he would compensate its owner. [Weak]"""""
"11534","(11529) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists of the people of Madīnah: that they used to assess for every beast that was afflicted the difference between the value of the beast sound of eye and the value of the one afflicted in the eye, and whatever affliction befell the beast, the compensation was assessed according to that.\n\nʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ said: As for the wounds of a slave, they used to assess the wounds of the slave, all of his wounds, according to his value on the day he was afflicted, just as the wounds of a free man are assessed according to his blood-money. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"
"11535","(11530) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said regarding the eye of a beast: \Its compensation is one-quarter of its price.\"" This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nIt has been narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī from ʿUmar that he wrote to Sharīḥ regarding that"","" and it is also munqaṭiʿ. And it was narrated by Jābir al-Juʿfī"","" who is weak"","" from al-Shaʿbī from Sharīḥ that ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" wrote to him regarding that. And it was narrated by Mujālid from al-Shaʿbī"","" who said: ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" wrote to Sharīḥ"","" and it is munqaṭiʿ."""""
"11536","(11531) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, saying: We read it to Abū al-Yamān that Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed him from al-Zuhrī, who said: Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwf narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr ibn Sahl informed him that Saʿīd ibn Zayd said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \Whoever wrongfully takes anything from the land"","" it will be placed around his neck from the seven earths.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it from Abū al-Yamān. [Bukhārī 2452"","" Muslim 1610]"""""
"11537","(11532) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Ṭayfūr narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ from ʿAbbās ibn Sahl ibn Saʿd from Saʿīd ibn Zayd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever seizes a handspan of land unjustly"","" Allah will collar him on the Day of Resurrection with the seven earths.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11538","(11533) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us, saying: Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father that Arwā bint Aws made a claim against Saʿīd ibn Zayd, asserting that he had taken some of his land. She brought the dispute before Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam. Saʿīd said: \How could I take from her land after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever takes a handspan of land unjustly will be collared with it down to the seven earths.'\"" Marwān said to him: \""I will not ask you for any proof after this.\"" He said: \""O Allah"","" if she is lying"","" blind her eyes and kill her in her land.\"" He said: \""She did not die until her sight was lost. One day she was walking in her land when she fell into a pit and died.\"" Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ"","" and al-Bukhārī recorded it from the narration of Abū Usāmah from Hishām. [Bukhārī 3198]"""""
"11539","(11534) The Sheikh, the Imam Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān, informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed me, saying: Sahl ibn Bakkār narrated to us, saying: Abān ibn Yazīd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that he visited ʿĀʾishah while he was engaged in a dispute over a piece of land. She said: \O Abū Salamah"","" avoid the land"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever wrongfully takes even a handspan of land will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from the seven earths.'\"" [Bukhārī 2453"","" Muslim 1612]"""""
"11540","(11535) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us, saying: Ḥarb narrated from Yaḥyā, who said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to me that Abū Salamah narrated to him, and there was a dispute between him and some people over a piece of land, and that he visited ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and mentioned that to her. She said: \O Abū Salamah"","" avoid the land"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever wrongfully takes even a handspan of land will be collared with it from the seven earths on the Day of Resurrection.'\"" Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the narration of Ḥarb ibn Shaddād and Abān ibn Yazīd from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr"","" and al-Bukhārī recorded it from two other routes from Yaḥyā and used them as supporting evidence. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11541","(11536) Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Wahb narrated from Suhayl from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes a hand's span of land unjustly"","" it will be encircled around him from the seven earths.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Jarīr from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ. [Muslim 1611]"""""
"11542","(11537) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed me, al-Ṣūfī narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Khusrawjirdī informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us, Zuhayr — meaning Abū Khaythamah — narrated to them both, Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī narrated to us, Manṣūr ibn Ḥayyān al-Asadī narrated to us, Abū al-Ṭufayl ʿĀmir ibn Wāthilah narrated: I was with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib when a man came to him and said: \What did the Prophet (ﷺ) confide to you?\"" He became angry and said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) did not confide anything to me that he concealed from the people"","" except that he narrated four words to me.\"" The man said: \""What are they"","" O Commander of the Faithful?\"" He said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Allah curses the one who curses his parents; Allah curses the one who slaughters for other than Allah; Allah curses the one who gives refuge to an innovator; Allah curses the one who alters the landmarks of the earth.'\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū al-Ḥasan al-Khusrawjirdī. Muslim narrated it from Surayj and Abū Khaythamah. [Muslim 1978]"""""
"11543","(11538) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from Saʿīd ibn Zayd from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: \Whoever revives dead land"","" it belongs to him"","" and no unjust root has any right.\"" [Weak chain of narration. Abū Dāwūd 3073]"""""
"11544","(11539) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥīm narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUrwah from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives dead land"","" it belongs to him"","" and no unjust root has any right.\"" He said: \""Two men from the Banī Bayāḍah came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) disputing — one of them had planted date palms in the land of the other. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the land belonged to its owner and ordered the owner of the date palms to remove his palms from it.\"" He said: ʿUrwah said: \""The one who narrated to me said: 'I saw them being struck at their trunks with axes"","" and they were deeply rooted date palms"","" until they were removed.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"11545","(11540) And Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Ḥasan narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Abū Shihāb narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, mentioning it with the same meaning, except that he said: \The one who narrated this ḥadīth to me said: 'I saw two men from the Banī Bayāḍah disputing"",""' and he mentioned it.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11546","(11541) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Wahb narrated from his father from Ibn Isḥāq with its chain and its meaning, except that he said at his statement \in place of the one who narrated to me this"",""\"" he said: \""A man from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and my strongest assumption is that he was Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" and I saw the man striking at the roots of the date palms.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11547","(11542) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, and Abū Ṣādiq al-ʿAṭṭār informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me, Suhayl — he is Ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ — informed me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not permissible for any person to take his brother's staff without his goodwill.\"" That is because of the severity with which Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has prohibited a Muslim's wealth from being taken by another Muslim. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is Ibn Saʿd ibn Mālik"","" and Saʿd ibn Mālik is Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated it from Sulaymān"","" and he said ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd. And ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd from ʿUmarah ibn Ḥārithah al-Ḍamrī from ʿAmr ibn Yathribī with the wording mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 5/420"","" 2:24003]"""""
"11548","(11543) And in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: \The ḥadīth"","" according to me"","" is the ḥadīth of Suhayl.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11549","(11544) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Nuʿmān al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥurfī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib from his father from his grandfather that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Let none of you take the belonging of his companion"","" whether in jest or in earnest. And if any of you takes his brother's staff"","" let him return it to him.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of al-Ḥurfī. And in the narration of Ibn Bishrān from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" he said: \""Let none of you take the belonging of his brother"","" whether in jest or in earnest. And if any of you takes his brother's staff"","" let him return it to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11550","(11545) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us, Ḥasan ibn Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from Abū Ḥurrah al-Raqāshī from his paternal uncle that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The wealth of a Muslim is not permissible except with his goodwill.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11551","(11546) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — from Mūsā ibn al-Sāʾib — from Qatādah — from al-Ḥasan — from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever finds his property with a man"","" he has the greater right to it"","" and the buyer shall pursue the one who sold it to him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11552","(11547) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl — from al-Ḥasan: That a man sold a slave-girl belonging to his father while his father was absent. When his father arrived, he refused to ratify the sale, as the slave-girl had borne a child by the purchaser. They brought their dispute before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He ruled that the man should take back his slave-girl and ordered the purchaser to reclaim his payment in full (al-khalāṣ), so he did. The father of the seller said: \Tell him to leave my son (alone).\"" ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to him: \""Then you"","" too"","" leave his son (alone).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11553","(11548) And Abū Ḥāzim informed us — Abū al-Faḍl informed us — Aḥmad narrated to us — Saʿīd narrated to us — Khālid ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us — Muṭarrif narrated to us — from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī: Regarding a man who found his slave-girl in the possession of another man, she having borne a child by him, the owner established proof that she was his slave-girl, and the one in whose possession she was established proof that he had purchased her. ʿAlī said: \The owner of the slave-girl shall take back his slave-girl"","" and the seller shall be held liable for full compensation (al-khalāṣ).\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: And Saʿīd narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Sālim informed us — he said: I heard al-Shaʿbī saying: \""Al-khalāṣ is of no consequence. Whoever sells what he does not own"","" it belongs to its owner"","" and the buyer shall pursue the seller for what he paid. The seller is not liable for more than returning what he received"","" and nothing else shall be exacted from him.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated to us from another route from al-Shaʿbī — from Shurayḥ — that he said: \""Whoever stipulates al-khalāṣ is a fool. Stand by what you have sold"","" or return what you have received. Al-khalāṣ is of no consequence.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nThe Shaykh said: The statement of ʿAlī — \""and the seller shall be held liable for full compensation (al-khalāṣ)\"" — he means"","" and Allah knows best"","" the price and the value of the child"","" which would be consistent with the view of those after him and with what was narrated in the ḥadīth from Samurah from the Prophet ﷺ."""""
"11554","(11549) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb — informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me — al-Ḥasan, that is, ibn Sufyān, said: Abū Bakr, Abū Khaythamah, and ʿAbd al-Aʿlā informed us — they said: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us — from al-Zuhrī — from Saʿīd — from Abū Hurayrah, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The son of Maryam shall soon descend among you as a just ruler. He shall kill the pig"","" break the cross"","" abolish the jizyah"","" and wealth shall abound so that no one shall accept it.\"" The wording is that of ʿAbd al-Aʿlā.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī from Sufyān"","" and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād.\n\n[Bukhārī 2222"","" Muslim 155]"""""
"11555","(11550) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to us — from Mujāhid — from Abī Maʿmar — from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the Conquest, and around the House there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: \Truth has come"","" and falsehood cannot begin nor return. Truth has come"","" and falsehood has perished — indeed"","" falsehood is ever perishing.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī and others"","" and Muslim narrated it from a group from Sufyān.\n\n[Bukhārī 2478"","" Muslim 1781]"""""
"11556","(11551) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Ṣafwān narrated to us — Ibn Abī al-Dunyā narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — from Abī Ḥuṣayn: That a man broke a ṭunbūr (a musical instrument) belonging to another man and brought the matter before Shurayḥ, but he did not hold him liable. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"11557","(11552) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us — Mālik ibn Anas narrated to us — from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah — from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: I was giving Abū ʿUbaydah, Abū Ṭalḥah, and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb a drink made from pressed dates (faḍīkh) and dates, when a man came to them and said: \Indeed"","" wine (khamr) has been forbidden.\"" Abū Ṭalḥah said: \""O Anas"","" get up and break these jars.\"" Anas said: \""So I got up"","" took a stone vessel (mihrās) of ours"","" and struck them with its base until they shattered.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Bukhārī 7253"","" Muslim 1980]"""""
"11558","(11553) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us — Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd al-Madanī narrated to us — from Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ al-Anṣārī, who said: When they lit fires on the day they conquered Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \What have you lit these fires for?\"" They said: \""For the meat of domestic donkeys.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Pour out what is in their pots and break them.\"" A man from the people stood and said: \""Shall we pour out what is in them and wash them?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Or do that.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī ʿĀṣim from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd.\n\nAnd it is as though ﷺ considered them (the pots) to be of no benefit"","" since the forbidden (substance) had been cooked in them"","" so he ordered them to be broken. When he was informed that there was permissible benefit in them"","" he refrained from ordering their breaking. And Allah knows best. As for what is narrated from ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" regarding his authorization of them to sell wine"","" it is mentioned in the Book of the Jizyah with a disconnected chain of narration"","" concerning ʿUmar's denunciation of those who mixed the prices of wine and pork with the war spoils (fayʾ)"","" and the interpretation of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah regarding ʿUmar's statement — may Allah be pleased with him — about authorizing them and their sale. There is nothing in this that constitutes permission from ʿUmar for them to sell it. [Bukhārī 2477"","" Muslim 1802]"""""
"11559","(11554) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us — Maʿmar narrated to us — from al-Zuhrī — from Abī Salamah — from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) applies to everything that has not been divided. But once boundaries have been set and roads have been laid out, there is no right of pre-emption.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. And Hishām ibn Yūsuf similarly narrated it from Maʿmar.\n\n[Bukhārī 2213, Muslim 1608]"
"11560","(11555) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūṣuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us — Maʿmar narrated to us — from al-Zuhrī — from Abī Salamah — from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only established the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) in everything that has not been divided. Once boundaries have been set and roads have been laid out, there is no right of pre-emption. [Ṣaḥīḥ, up to his words \has not been divided\""]"""""
"11561","(11556) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain of narration, identical to it, except that he said: \In every property that has not been divided.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān from ʿAbd al-Razzāq with this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ — up to his words"","" \""has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11562","(11557) Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and he said regarding properties: \That which has not been divided. But when the boundaries have been demarcated and the people have come to know their rights"","" then there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah).\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us of it"","" Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us"","" al-Ḥasan — that is"","" Ibn Sufyān — narrated to us"","" Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us"","" ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11563","(11558) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī al-Akhḍar narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) as long as the property had not been divided and its boundaries had not been demarcated.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11564","(11559) Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Ṣāliḥ, and he said: \In that which has not been divided and whose boundaries have not been recognized.\""\n\nAbū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us of it"","" al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī narrated to us"","" Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us"","" Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us"","" Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11565","(11560) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā narrated to us, Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mukhtār narrated to us, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī al-Akhḍar, who said: al-Zuhrī narrated to me, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When the boundaries have been demarcated"","" there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah).\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq followed them in narrating it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. This wording.]"""""
"11566","(11561) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ — and Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us; and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us. They both said: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Bajalī narrated to us, Salm ibn Ibrāhīm al-Warrāq narrated to us, ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When the boundaries have been demarcated"","" there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains — up to \""has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11567","(11562) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) in houses and lands as long as they had not been divided. But when they were divided and the boundaries were demarcated therein, there was no right of pre-emption (shufʿah) in them.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — up to his words, \has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11568","(11563) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us; and Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah and Saʿīd, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The right of pre-emption (shufʿah) is in that which has not been divided. When the boundaries have been demarcated"","" there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah).\""\n\nThus did Mālik ibn Anas narrate it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ in a mursal form"","" and it has also been narrated from him through other routes in a connected (mawṣūl) form"","" with the mention of Abū Hurayrah in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ — up to his words"","" \""has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11569","(11564) Among them is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mājishūn narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ismāʿīlī — narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd, the brother of Rushdīn ibn Saʿd, narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Mājishūn narrated to us, from Mālik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) in that which has not been divided. When the boundaries have been demarcated, there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah). [Ṣaḥīḥ — up to his words, \has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11570","(11565) And among them is what Abū Manṣūr — al-Ẓufr ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him — informed us by dictation, Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Adamī — in Baghdad, narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr al-Bazzāz — in Baghdad, narrated to us. They both said: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Qatīlah narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The right of pre-emption (shufʿah) is in that which has not been divided. When the boundaries have been demarcated"","" there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — up to his words"","" \""has not been divided.\""]"""""
"11571","(11566) And among them is what Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq, the mu'adhdhin, informed us: Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Marwazī informed us: Abū Qilābah ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī informed us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad al-Shaybānī informed us: Mālik ibn Anas informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) in that which has not been divided. But when the boundaries have been demarcated and the roads have been laid out, there is no right of pre-emption. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11572","(11567) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed me: ʿAlī ibn Naṣr ibn ʿAlī — they said to my father, ʿĀṣim, regarding his ḥadīth from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd and Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, concerning pre-emption — he said: \Bring me the one who heard it from Mālik at the time I heard it.\"" He said: \""Abū Jaʿfar al-Manṣūr came to us in Makkah"","" and the people gathered around him and asked him to instruct Mālik to narrate to them. So he commanded him"","" and he narrated in Makkah"","" and we heard it from Mālik at that time.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11573","(11568) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed me: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Junayd informed me: Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād al-Ṭihrānī informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim, from Mālik — and he mentioned this ḥadīth. Al-Ṭihrānī said: Abū ʿĀṣim said to me: \The ḥadīth of Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah is musnad (connected)"","" and the ḥadīth of Saʿīd is mursal (disconnected).\"" Thus al-Ṭihrānī reported from Abū ʿĀṣim."""""
"11574","(11569) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad al-Shaybānī informed us: Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib or from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right of pre-emption in that which has not been divided. But when the boundaries have been established, there is no right of pre-emption. Thus he came with it, expressing doubt in its chain of narration. And similarly it was reported from Ibn Jurayj and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār, from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. This specific wording]"
"11575","(11570) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dārim informed us: Aḥmad ibn Mūsā ibn Isḥāq informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Usāmah ʿAbd Allāh ibn Usāmah informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us: Ibn Idrīs, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah or from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, or from both of them together, from Abū Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the land has been divided and its boundaries demarcated"","" there is no right of pre-emption in it.\"" Their wording is identical. [Ṣaḥīḥ up to his words \""has not been divided\""]"""""
"11576","(11571) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam ibn Sulaymān, mawlā of Khālid, informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib or from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right of pre-emption in that which has not been divided, and any property that has been divided — there is no right of pre-emption in it. The Shaykh said: What is known by way of deduction from these narrations is that Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī had no doubt regarding his narration from Abū Salamah, from Jābir, from the Prophet ﷺ — as Maʿmar and Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī al-Akhḍar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated from him — nor regarding his narration from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from the Prophet ﷺ as mursal, as Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī narrated from him. It is as though he was doubtful regarding his narration from both of them from Abū Hurayrah, so at one time he would narrate it as mursal from them, and at another time he would connect it from them, and at yet another time he would mention it with doubt regarding that. And Allah knows best. And the narration of ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir, corroborates the narration of those who reported it from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah from Jābir, as does the narration of Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir."
"11577","(11572) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Azdī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Idrīs — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs — (ḥ) and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣfahānī informed us: Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Ibn Idrīs, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right of pre-emption in every undivided share — be it a dwelling or a garden — it is not permissible for him to sell until he consults his partner. And in the narration of some of them: \Until he notifies his partner. If he wishes"","" he may take it"","" and if he wishes"","" he may leave it. But if he sells without notifying him"","" then he has the greatest right to it.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"","" and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr"","" and Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm."""""
"11578","(11573) And Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated it from Ibn Jurayj with this chain, and said in the ḥadīth: \If he sells it"","" then he has the greatest right to the price.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Yaʿlā informed us: Abū Khaythamah informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah — and he mentioned it."""""
"11579","(11574) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us among the last of them — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us: Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Pre-emption applies to that which has not been divided. But when the boundaries have been established"","" there is no right of pre-emption.\"""""""
"11580","(11575) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khumayruwayh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyā, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī, from ʿAwn ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When the boundaries have been demarcated and the people have come to know their respective limits"","" there is no right of pre-emption among them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11581","(11576) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmārah, from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When the boundaries are established in the land"","" there is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah) therein"","" nor in a well"","" nor in a palm-tree orchard.\""\n\n[Sound. Al-Muwaṭṭaʾ 2/717]"""""
"11582","(11577) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; he said: Abū ʿUbayd said regarding the ḥadīth of ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him: \When the shares are distributed"","" there is no restriction (mukābalah).\"" Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-mukābalah refers to confinement (al-ḥabs). It means: when the boundaries are established"","" no one is to be withheld from his right. The origin of this term is from al-kabl"","" which means bond (al-qayd).\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""The jurisprudential import of this ḥadīth is that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" did not consider the right of pre-emption (shufʿah) to be for the neighbour; rather"","" he considered it to be for the partner (al-khalīṭ al-mushārik). This is clear in another ḥadīth of his.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""It was narrated to us by ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs"","" from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmārah"","" from Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm — or from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Ḥazm — the doubt being from Abū ʿUbayd — from Abān ibn ʿUthmān"","" from ʿUthmān"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" who said: 'There is no pre-emption in a well"","" nor in a male palm-tree"","" and the boundaries (al-urf) nullify every right of pre-emption.'\""\n\nIbn Idrīs said: \""Al-urf means landmarks (al-maʿālim).\"" Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""They are the landmarks and the boundaries.\"" He added: \""This is the speech of the people of the Ḥijāz. One says: 'arraftu al-dāra wa al-arḍa taʾrīfan' — meaning"","" 'I divided and demarcated it.'\""\n\nIbn Idrīs said: \""And his statement 'There is no pre-emption in a well"","" nor in a male (faḥl)' — I think al-faḥl here refers to the male date-palm.\""\n\nAnd something similar has been narrated on this matter from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"","" Sulaymān ibn Yasār"","" and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. [Weak]"""""
"11583","(11578) Abū ʬāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṭāʾifī narrated from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The neighbour has the greatest right of proximity (bi-saqabih).\""\n\nAbū Qilābah said: Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""The Arabs say: al-saqab means al-lazīq — that which is adjacent.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah contradicted him with his chain of narration. [Aḥmad 19691]"""""
"11584","(11579) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid narrated to us; al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah, from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd, from Abū Rāfiʿ, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The neighbour has the greatest right of proximity (bi-saqabih).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym. [Bukhārī 2258]"""""
"11585","(11580) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah said: \I heard ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd say: 'Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah placed his hand — this one — upon my shoulder — this one — and I went with him until we came to Saʿd"","" and we sat before him. Then Abū Rāfiʿ came and said to al-Miswar: \""Will you not instruct this one to purchase from me my two houses that are part of his house?\"" So Saʿd"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""By Allah"","" I will not increase for you beyond four hundred dinārs"","" either in instalments or in a lump sum.\"" Abū Rāfiʿ then said: \""Glory be to Allah! I had withheld them for five hundred in cash"","" but had I not heard the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" say: 'The neighbour has the greatest right of proximity (bi-saqabih)"",""' I would not have sold them to you.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"","" and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj"","" from Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah"","" with the same meaning.\n\nIn the context of this narration there is an indication that the ḥadīth was reported concerning something other than pre-emption (shufʿah)"","" and that what was intended by it is that the neighbour has a greater right to be offered the property before others. And if pre-emption was intended by it"","" then Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ narrated"","" saying: Al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""Abū Rāfiʿ"","" in what is narrated from him"","" acted voluntarily in what he did. And the statement of the Prophet"","" peace and blessings be upon him: 'The neighbour has the greatest right of proximity (bi-saqabih)' — it can only carry two meanings"","" with no third: either he intended that pre-emption is for every neighbour"","" or he intended some neighbours to the exclusion of others. And it has been established from the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" that there is no pre-emption in that which has been divided. This indicates that pre-emption belongs to the neighbour who has not shared in the division"","" to the exclusion of the neighbour who has shared in the division.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And upon this basis is carried what follows…\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11586","(11581) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ruled concerning the neighbour (bi-al-jiwār). And from Samurah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The neighbour of a house has a greater right to the house than anyone else.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11587","(11582) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \The neighbour has the greatest right to the pre-emption of his brother. He is to be waited for even if he is absent"","" provided their path is one and the same.\"" [Munkar]"""""
"11588","(11583) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ narrated, saying: Al-Shāfiʿī said regarding this ḥadīth: \We heard some of the scholars of ḥadīth say: 'We fear that this ḥadīth may not be preserved (maḥfūẓ).' It was said to him: 'From where do you say this?' He said: 'It is only narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh"","" and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān has narrated from Jābir with an explanation that the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" said: \""Pre-emption is in that which has not been divided. When the boundaries are established"","" there is no pre-emption.\"" And Abū Salamah is among the ḥuffāẓ (preservers of ḥadīth). And Abū al-Zubayr"","" who is also among the ḥuffāẓ"","" narrated from Jābir something that agrees with the statement of Abū Salamah and contradicts what ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11589","(11584) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; al-Sājī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Ṣafwān al-Thaqafī narrated to us; Umayyah ibn Khālid said: \I said to Shuʿbah: 'Do you narrate from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-ʿArzamī and abandon the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān al-ʿArzamī"","" when his ḥadīth is sound (ḥasan)?' He said: 'It is on account of its soundness that I have abandoned it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11590","(11585) And Abū Saʿd informed us; Abū Aḥmad informed us; al-Sājī narrated to us; Jaʿfar al-Firyābī narrated to us; Abū Qudāmah said: \I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān say: 'If ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān were to narrate another ḥadīth like his ḥadīth on pre-emption"","" I would abandon his ḥadīth.'\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by Musaddad from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān"","" from Shuʿbah"","" that he said that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11591","(11586) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, saying: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal say: I heard my father say — and he narrated the hadith of al-Shufʿah, the hadith of ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir from the Prophet ﷺ — he said: \This is a munkar hadith.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11592","(11587) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Suwayd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baṣrī narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Baylamānī from his father from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no right of pre-emption (shufʿah) for one who is absent"","" nor for a minor"","" nor for a partner against his partner if the latter has preceded him in the purchase.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11593","(11588) And Abū Saʿd narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Mihrān narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Shabbah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us with its chain of narration, similarly, and he added: \And the right of pre-emption is like the untying of a cord.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11594","(11589) And Abū Saʿd narrated to us, saying: Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, mentioning it with its chain of narration from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There is no right of pre-emption for a minor"","" nor for one who is absent. And if a partner has preceded his partner in exercising the right of pre-emption"","" then there is no pre-emption. And the right of pre-emption is like the untying of a cord.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11595","(11590) And Abū Saʿd narrated to us, and Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Mihrān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ḥarashī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from his father from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The right of pre-emption is neither inherited nor does it make one an heir.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baṣrī is matrūk (abandoned)"","" and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Baylamānī is ḍaʿīf (weak); both were declared weak by Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and other Imams of the people of hadith.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in opposition to the first hadith a weak hadith from Jārir"","" raised to the Prophet: \""The minor retains his right of pre-emption until he reaches maturity.\"" Both of them are munkar. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11596","(11591) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Mukram narrated to us; al-Sarī ibn Sahl narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rushayd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bazīʿ narrated to us from Ṣadaqah ibn Abī ʿImrān from ʿAbd al-Malik from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The minor retains his right of pre-emption until he reaches maturity. Then"","" when he reaches maturity"","" if he wishes"","" he may take it"","" and if he wishes"","" he may leave it.\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn Bazīʿ is the sole narrator of this"","" and he is weak. And those below him up to the shaykh of our shaykh are not used as evidence. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11597","(11592) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; Ḥafṣ al-Rabbālī narrated to us; Nāʾil ibn Najīḥ narrated to us from Sufyān from Ḥumayd from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no right of pre-emption for the Christian.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""The hadiths of Nāʾil are very obscure"","" especially when he narrates from al-Thawrī.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11598","(11593) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Sarrāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us; Nāʾil ibn Najīḥ narrated to us, mentioning it, except that he said: \He raised it once to the Prophet ﷺ"","" and another time he did not raise it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And the hadith"","" according to Sufyān"","" is from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl from al-Ḥasan"","" who said: 'There is no right of pre-emption for the Jew or the Christian.'\"" Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī narrated to us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Sufyān"","" mentioning it. This is the correct version — it is the statement of al-Ḥasan.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Iyās ibn Muʿāwiyah that he ruled in favour of granting the right of pre-emption to a dhimmī (non-Muslim under protection). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11599","(11594) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān narrated to us; Muʿādh narrated to us from al-Ashʿath from al-Ḥasan: \He used to hold the view that the absent person retains his right of pre-emption when he arrives"","" and that the minor retains his right of pre-emption when he grows up.\"" He said: \""And there is no right of pre-emption in the case of animals.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11600","(11595) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The right of pre-emption applies to every shared property — whether a dwelling or a garden. It is not permissible for a partner to sell until he informs his partner. If he sells"","" then his partner has the greater right to it until he gives him permission.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ibn Wahb from Ibn Jurayj"","" except that he said: \""The right of pre-emption applies to every shared property — whether in land"","" a dwelling"","" or a garden.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11601","(11596) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated from Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Asadī, Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated to me from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled in favour of pre-emption (shufʿah) among partners in houses and lands.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11602","(11597) It is narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah, from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no pre-emption (shufʿah) except in a house or immovable property.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us of it"","" Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us"","" Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Dāwūd narrated to us"","" Abū Usāmah ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us"","" al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Ḥajwah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk al-Manbajī narrated to us"","" and Abū Ḥanīfah mentioned it.\n\nAbū Aḥmad al-ʿAssāl also narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Dāwūd"","" from Abī Usāmah"","" from al-Ḍaḥḥāk"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn Wāqid"","" from Abū Ḥanīfah — and this is the correct version. The chain of narration is weak.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Sharīḥ that he said: \""There is no pre-emption except in land or immovable property.\"" And from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Sulaymān ibn Yasār"","" who both said: \""Pre-emption applies in houses and lands.\"" And from al-Ḥasan"","" who said: \""There is no pre-emption in animals.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11603","(11598) As for that which Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us of — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us, Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharik narrated to us, Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, Abū Ḥamzah al-Sukkārī narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The partner is entitled to pre-emption"","" and pre-emption applies in everything.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""""
"11604","(11599) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh both informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth al-Marwazī narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated from Abī Ḥamzah, who mentioned something similar as a marfūʿ (elevated) narration, and said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said.\"" ʿAlī said: \""Shuʿbah"","" Isrāʾīl"","" ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays"","" and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh contradicted him"","" narrating it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ"","" from Ibn Abī Mulaykah"","" as a mursal (disconnected) narration — and this is the correct version. Abū Ḥamzah erred in his chain of narration.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""""
"11605","(11600) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Khuldī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Isrāʾīl, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The partner is entitled to pre-emption in everything.\"" This is the correct version — it is mursal (disconnected). [Weak]"""""
"11606","(11601) It has been narrated from Abū Ḥamzah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh, from ʬāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, as a marfūʿ (elevated) narration. Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm informed us, Abū al-Muwajjih informed us, ʿAbdān informed us, and Abū Ḥamzah mentioned it.\n\n(b) And this Muḥammad is al-ʿArzamī, who is abandoned (matrūk) in hadith. It has also been narrated through another weak chain from Ibn ʿAbbās as a mawṣūl (connected) narration. [Weak]"
"11607","(11602) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz narrated to us, ʿAffān ibn Makhlad al-Balkhī narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Hārūn narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Naṣr Manṣūr ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Mufassir al-Maqburī both informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Balkhī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā and ʿAlī ibn Ghimās al-Balkhī both narrated to us — ʿUmar ibn Hārūn narrated from Shuʿbah, from Abī Bishr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Pre-emption applies in slaves and in everything.\"" And in the narration of ʿAffān: \""There is pre-emption in a slave and in everything.\"" ʿUmar ibn Hārūn al-Balkhī alone narrated it from Shuʿbah"","" and he is weak — he cannot be used as a proof. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11608","(11603) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated from Shuʿbah, from Abī Shaybah, from ʿĪsā ibn al-Ḥārith, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Pre-emption is according to the shares of the partners.\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""""
"11609","(11604) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibn Abī Uways informed us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists whose opinions are followed among the people of Madinah, who used to say: Regarding a man who has partners in a house, and the partners concede pre-emption to him except for one man who wishes to take only his proportionate share of the pre-emption — they said: \That is not permissible for him; he must either take all of it or leave all of it.\"" And they used to say regarding a group of men who inherit wealth from their father"","" and one of them dies leaving a child"","" and one of the children sells his share of that wealth — the child and his paternal uncles are partners in pre-emption according to their respective shares"","" provided the wealth has not been divided and the prescribed punishments (ḥudūd) have not been carried out therein. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād mentioned from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmarah al-Ḥazmī that Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm passed a ruling to that effect. [Weak]"""""
"11610","(11605) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm both informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: ʿAbdullāh and ʿUbaydullāh, the two sons of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, set out with an army to Iraq. When when they returned, they passed by Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who welcomed them and made things easy for them. He was the governor of Basrah at the time. He said: \If I could do something beneficial for you"","" I would certainly do it.\"" Then he said: \""Indeed"","" there is some wealth from the treasury of Allah here that I wish to send to the Commander of the Faithful. I shall lend it to you"","" so that you may purchase merchandise from Iraq and sell it in Madinah. Then you shall return the principal to the Commander of the Faithful and the profit will be yours.\"" They both said: \""We would like that.\"" So he did that"","" and he wrote to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) to take the money from them. When they arrived in Madinah"","" they sold the merchandise and made a profit. When they brought this to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" he said: \""Did Abū Mūsā lend to the entire army as he lent to you two?\"" They said: \""No.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""You are the sons of the Commander of the Faithful"","" so he lent you the money. Return the principal and the profit.\"" As for ʿAbdullāh"","" he accepted. But ʿUbaydullāh said: \""This is not right for you"","" O Commander of the Faithful. If the money had been lost or diminished"","" we would have been liable for it.\"" He said: \""Return it.\"" ʿAbdullāh remained silent"","" but ʿUbaydullāh repeated his argument. Then one of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb's companions said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"","" why not make it a qirāḍ (mudārabah/partnership in profit)?\"" He said: \""I have made it a qirāḍ.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) took the principal and half the profit"","" and ʿAbdullāh and ʿUbaydullāh took half the profit of the capital.\n\nThe meaning of their two narrations is the same"","" except that al-Shāfiʿī said in his narration: \""When they returned"","" they passed by a governor of ʿUmar.\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ). Mālik 1396]"""""
"11611","(11606) Abu al-Mihrajan informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us — Ibn Bukayr informed us — Malik, from al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from his father, from his grandfather: that he worked with the property of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan on the condition that the profit would be shared between them. [Da'if]"
"11612","(11607) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Malik ibn Anas informed me — al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub informed me, from his father, that he said: I came to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and said to him: \Merchandise has arrived; would you give me wealth so that I may purchase with it?\"" He said: \""Do you see yourself doing that?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" but I am a mukatib (a slave under a contract of emancipation)"","" so purchase it on the condition that the profit is between you and me.\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he gave me wealth on that basis. [Da'if]"""""
"11613","(11608) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us — Ya'qub ibn Sufyan informed us — Abu Nu'aym informed us — Hisham, from Ayyub, from Nafi': that Ibn 'Umar used to have the property of orphans in his care; he would pay its zakat, give it out as mudarabah (profit-sharing investment), and borrow against it. [Sahih]"
"11614","(11609) And Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas al-A'ṣam informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah: that he was asked about a man who gives another man wealth as qirad (mudarabah) and stipulates for him something like — \the day you gave it to me"","" I shall take it.\"" He said: \""There is no harm in that.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11615","(11610) And Abu Bakr and Abu Zakariyya informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas informed us — Muhammad informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Ibn Lahi'ah and Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Asadi informed me — 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me — from Hakim ibn Hizam: that he used to give wealth as qirad to a man and stipulate upon him that he should not pass through a valley with it, nor purchase livestock with it, nor carry it by sea. If he did any of that, then he would be liable for that wealth. He said: \If he transgressed his command"","" I would hold liable the one who did that.\"" And a related musnad narration has been reported on this matter which is da'if. [Sahih]"""""
"11616","(11611) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Tamtam Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah al-Sadusi informed us — Yunus ibn Arqam al-Kindi, Abu Arqam, informed us — Abu al-Jarud informed us — from Habib ibn Yasar, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, when he gave wealth as mudarabah, would stipulate upon his partner that he should not travel by sea with it, nor descend into a valley with it, nor purchase a living animal with it. If he did so, he would be liable. His condition was then raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he permitted it. [Da'if]"
"11617","(11612) And Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi informed us — Abu Ya'la informed us — Mushja' ibn Mu'ṣṣab, Abu al-Hakam, informed us — Yunus ibn Arqam al-Kindi informed us — and he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. Abu al-Jarud — Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir, who was a Kufan, da'if, whom Yahya ibn Ma'in accused of lying and whom the rest weakened — was singular in transmitting it. [Da'if]"
"11618","(11613) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Aṣbahani informed us — Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us — (h) and Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us — they both said: Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us — Sufyan informed us — Shabib ibn Gharqadah informed us — he heard his people narrating from 'Urwah al-Bariqi: that the Prophet ﷺ gave him a dinar to buy a sacrificial sheep for him. He bought two sheep for him, then sold one of them for a dinar and brought to the Prophet ﷺ a sheep and a dinar. The Prophet ﷺ then invoked blessing in his trade, such that even if he had purchased dust, he would have profited from it. [Bukhari 3643]"
"11619","(11614) And Abu Muhammad informed us — Abu Sa'id informed us — (h) and Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan informed us — Isma'il al-Saffar informed us — they both said: Sa'dan informed us — Sufyan informed us — Shabib ibn Gharqadah informed us — from 'Urwah al-Bariqi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — or he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.\"" These are two hadiths: Shabib ibn Gharqadah heard one of them from 'Urwah al-Bariqi and did not hear the other; rather"","" he heard the tribe informing him about 'Urwah. [Muslim 1873]"""""
"11620","(11615) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed me — Hammad ibn Shakir informed me — Muhammad ibn Isma'il, meaning al-Bukhari, informed me — 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah informed me — Sufyan informed us — Shabib ibn Gharqadah informed us — he said: I heard the tribe relating from 'Urwah that the Prophet ﷺ gave him a dinar to buy a sheep with it. He bought two sheep with it, then sold one of them for a dinar. He came to him with a dinar and a sheep, so he invoked blessing for him in his trade, and had he purchased dust, he would have profited from it. Sufyan said: Al-Hasan ibn 'Umarah came to us with this hadith from him, saying: \Shabib heard it from 'Urwah.\"" So I went to him"","" and Shabib said: \""I did not hear it from 'Urwah; rather"","" I heard the tribe informing him about it. But I heard him say: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.'\"" He said: \""And I saw in his house seventy horses.\"" Sufyan said: \""As if he were buying a sheep as a sacrificial offering.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11621","(11616) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, he said: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī said in the ḥadīth of ʿUrwah ibn Abī al-Jaʿd: \The Prophet ﷺ gave him a dīnār so that he might purchase a sacrificial animal for him.\"" He said: Sufyān said: \""Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah — we heard him narrating it"","" and he would say therein: 'I heard Shabīb say: I heard ʿUrwah.' But when I asked Shabīb"","" he said: 'I did not hear it from ʿUrwah; rather"","" al-Ḥayy narrated it to me from ʿUrwah.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥumaydī 866]"""""
"11622","(11617) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Raqqī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr al-ʿAtakī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrīt narrated to us, from Abī Labīd, from ʿUrwah ibn Abī al-Jaʿd al-Bāriqī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a dīnār and said: 'Purchase a sheep for us with it.' So I set out and purchased two sheep for one dīnār. Then I met a man on the road who bargained with me for a sheep"","" so I sold it to him for one dīnār. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" this is your dīnār and this is your sheep.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'And how did you manage that?' So I informed him. He then said: 'O Allah"","" bless him in the transaction of his hand.' He said: 'I would stand in the marketplace of Kūfah and would not return to my family until I had earned forty thousand.'\""\n\nA group narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Zayd"","" and he is the brother of Ḥammād ibn Zayd"","" and he is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī 1258]"""""
"11623","(11618) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-ʿAbdī informed us, Sufyān informed us, Abū Ḥuṣayn narrated to me, from a shaykh from the people of Madīnah, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him with a dīnār to purchase a sacrificial animal for him. He purchased it for one dīnār and sold it for two dīnārs. He then returned and purchased a sacrificial animal for one dīnār and brought one dīnār to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ gave it in charity and supplicated that he be blessed in his trade.\n\nAnd the ḥadīth of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, with his two sons has already passed in the first chapter. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3386]"
"11624","(11619) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed us, from Riyāḥ ibn ʿUbaydah, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he was asked about a man who was entrusted with goods (māl) and then acted contrary to the terms. Ibn ʿUmar said: \He is liable (ḍāmin) for it"","" and if there is profit"","" the profit belongs to the owner of the capital.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3386]"""""
"11625","(11620) And it is in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās, from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Shāfiʿī, who said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī informed us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from Riyāḥ ibn ʿUbaydah, who said: \A man sent ten dīnārs with a man from the people of Baṣrah to a man in Madīnah. The one who was sent with him purchased a camel with it"","" then sold it for eleven dīnārs. He asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar"","" who said: 'The eleven belong to the owner of the capital"","" and if something were to happen to the camel"","" you would be liable for it.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Ibn ʿUmar held the one who purchases goods on behalf of another to be liable"","" and he held the profit to belong to the owner of the goods"","" and he did not assign the profit to the one who was liable.\"" Al-Rabīʿ said: \""The final position of al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" was that if he exceeded the terms and purchased something with the specific capital and profited from it"","" then the purchase is void. But if he purchased with non-specific capital and then the capital was exhausted"","" then the purchase is valid for him"","" and the profit is his"","" and the loss is upon him"","" and he is liable for the capital.\"" Al-Muzanī also transmitted this. Then he said: \""And he argued that the ḥadīth of al-Bāriqī is not established in his view.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""That is due to the irsāl (broken chain) in its isnād"","" which is that Shabīb ibn Gharrādah did not hear it from ʿUrwah al-Bāriqī; rather"","" he heard it from al-Ḥayy who informed him from him. And the ḥadīth of Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām is also from a shaykh from the people of Madīnah from him. And al-Muzanī interpreted the ḥadīth of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" with his two sons"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" by saying that he asked them to make all of the profit an obligatory act of birr (righteousness) upon them for the Muslims"","" and they did not agree. But when he asked for half"","" they agreed willingly.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Umm 4/35]"""""
"11626","(11621) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made an agreement with the people of Khaybar for half of what would come out of it in the way of fruit or crops. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2329]"
"11627","(11622) Abū Isḥāq al-Isfarāʾīnī al-Imām informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Yazdād informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb al-Rāzī informed us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \For half of what would come out of it in the way of fruit or crops.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"","" and Muslim narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11628","(11623) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his book, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Abū al-Azhar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shuraḥbīl informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled the Jews from the land of the Ḥijāz. And when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he intended to expel the Jews from it. The land, when he conquered it, belonged to Allah, to His Messenger, and to the Muslims. He intended to expel the Jews from it, so the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to allow them to remain on the condition that they would tend the land and they would have half of the fruit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \We shall allow you to remain on that for as long as we wish.\"" So they remained on that basis until ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" expelled them during his caliphate to Taymāʾ and Arīḥāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11629","(11624) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed me, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled the Jews and the Christians from the land of the Ḥijāz. Then he mentioned the ḥadīth similar to the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Shuraḥbīl. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr, and al-Bukhārī narrated it, saying: \And ʿAbd al-Razzāq said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11630","(11625) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me, Usāmah informed me, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When Khaybar was conquered"","" the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to allow them to remain in it on the condition that they would work on half of what would come out of it in the way of fruit and crops. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We shall allow you to remain in it on that for as long as we wish.' So they remained in it on that basis during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" Abū Bakr"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and a portion of the caliphate of ʿUmar. The fruit would be divided according to the shares from half of Khaybar"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take the khums (one-fifth).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11631","(11626) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar—according to what Abū Salamah reckoned—from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Prophet ﷺ fought the people of Khaybar until he drove them into their fortress, and he gained control over the land, the crops, and the palm trees. They said: \O Muhammad"","" leave us in this land to tend it and maintain it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions had no servants to maintain it"","" so he gave them Khaybar on the condition that they would receive half of every crop"","" palm produce"","" and anything else"","" at the discretion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to come to them every year and estimate the yield for them"","" then charge them half. In one year they complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the severity of his estimation"","" and they intended to bribe him. He said: \""O enemies of Allah! You would feed me unlawful gain? I have come to you from the dearest of people to me"","" and you are more hateful to me than an equal number of monkeys and pigs. Neither my hatred of you nor my love for him shall prevent me from dealing justly with you.\"" They said: \""By this the heavens and the earth stand.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ 3321]"""""
"11632","(11627) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd narrated to us, my paternal uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, Nāfiʿ narrated to me, from Ibn ʿUmar, from his father ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a sharecropping agreement with the Jews of Khaybar over those properties for half, their shares being stipulated, and he stipulated upon them that whenever he wished, he would expel them. [Ḥasan. Al-Dāraquṭnī 2988]"
"11633","(11628) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, al-Muʿāfá narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Burqān narrated to us, from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from Miqsam Abī al-Qāsim, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet ﷺ said when he conquered Khaybar and stipulated upon them that the land and all the yellow and white—meaning gold and silver—would be his, the people of Khaybar said to him: \We know the land best"","" so give it to us that we may work it"","" and the produce shall be half for us and half for you.\"" He gave it to them on that basis. When the time came for the palm trees to be harvested"","" he sent Ibn Rawāḥah to them"","" who estimated the yield—which the people of Madinah call al-kharṣ. He said: \""This is such-and-such.\"" They said: \""You have overestimated"","" O Ibn Rawāḥah!\"" He said: \""I will take the palm produce and give you half of what I have stated.\"" They said: \""This is the truth"","" and by it the heavens and the earth stand. We are pleased to accept what you have said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 2255]"""""
"11634","(11629) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthanná narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Sufyān informed us, Ṣāliḥ—who is Ibn Abī al-Akhḍar—informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he called the Jews and said: \We will give you half of the fruit on the condition that you work it. I will let you remain as long as Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" lets you remain.\"" He used to send ʿAbd Allāh to estimate it"","" then give them the choice to take it or leave it. The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding some of that and complained to him. He called ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah and mentioned to him what they had said. ʿAbd Allāh said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" they have the choice: if they wish"","" they may take it"","" and if they leave it"","" we will take it.\"" The Jews were pleased and said: \""By this the heavens and the earth stand.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he passed away: \""Two religions shall not coexist in the Arabian Peninsula.\"" When this reached ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" he sent word to the Jews of Khaybar: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ employed you over these properties and stipulated that he would let you remain—meaning as long as Allah let you remain. Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has now permitted your expulsion. During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" he had made a covenant.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) expelled every Jew and Christian from the land of the Ḥijāz"","" then divided it among the people of al-Ḥudaybiyah. [Munkar al-Isnād]"""""
"11635","(11630) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, al-Ḥasan—who is Ibn Sufyān—and Abū Yaʿlá both said: ʿAbd Allāh—who is Ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ—narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ: that he gave Khaybar to the Jews on the condition that they would work it and cultivate it, and that they would have half of what came out of it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Juwayriyah. [Bukhārī 2338]"
"11636","(11632) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation, Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Aṣamm narrated to me, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me, Abū al-Qāsim al-Manīʿī narrated to us, Abū Mūsá al-Farwī narrated to us, Abū Ḍamrah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ employed the people of Khaybar for half of what came out of crops or fruit. He used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs: eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley. When ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) divided Khaybar, he gave the wives of the Prophet ﷺ the choice between being granted portions of the land and water, or having the wasqs guaranteed to them every year. They differed: some chose the land and water, and some chose the wasqs. ʿĀishah and Ḥafṣah (may Allah be pleased with them both) were among those who chose the land and water. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Ḍamrah. In the narration of ʿAlī ibn Mushir: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khaybar for half of what came out of fruit or crops"",""\"" then he mentioned the rest with the same meaning. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir from Abū Ḍamrah"","" and Muslim narrated it from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" Muslim]"""""
"11637","(11632) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl narrated to us in Baghdād, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, Yaḥyá ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanj, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Prophet ﷺ gave the Jews of Khaybar the palm trees of Khaybar and its land on the condition that they would work it from their own wealth, and that half of its fruit would belong to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11638","(11633) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed me, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: When the Muhājirūn came from Makkah to Madinah, they arrived with nothing in their hands, while the Anṣār were the people of land and property. The Anṣār shared with them on the condition that they would give them half of the fruits of their properties every year and would provide the labour and maintenance. They mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf. [Bukhārī 3630, Muslim 1771]"
"11639","(11634) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Shabīb narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, from Anas, who said: When the Muhājirūn went out from Makkah to Madinah and there was nothing in their hands, the Anṣār shared with them on the condition that they would give them half of the fruits of their properties every year, and would provide the maintenance and labour. He mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Shabīb, and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11640","(11635) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Abī Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn al-Awdī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) in this story. He said: Her father said to her: \How do you know of his strength and trustworthiness?\"" She said: \""As for his strength"","" he lifted the stone by himself"","" and only ten men could lift it. As for his trustworthiness"","" his words were: 'Walk behind me and describe the path to me"","" so that the wind does not expose your body to me.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11641","(11636) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mihran al-Isbahani narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us: Isra'il informed us — he mentioned it and added: He said, \That increased in him a desire for her"","" so he said: 'I wish to marry you to one of these two daughters of mine"","" on the condition that you hire yourself to me for eight years. If you complete ten"","" that is your own doing"","" and I do not wish to make things difficult for you. You will find me"","" if Allah wills"","" among the righteous'\"" — meaning"","" in the goodness of companionship and fidelity to what I have said. Musa said"","" \""That is between me and you. Whichever of the two terms I fulfill"","" there shall be no injustice against me.\"" He said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Allah is witness over what we say"","" and He is a sufficient trustee.\"" So he married him to her"","" and he stayed with him"","" working for him in the tending of his sheep. [Da'if]"""""
"11642","(11637) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: My father and Yahya ibn Ma'in both said: Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: A man from the Jews of al-Hirah met me and asked, \Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?\"" I said"","" \""I do not know. I will go tomorrow to 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas.\"" So I went and asked him"","" and he said"","" \""He fulfilled the greater and the more wholesome of the two.\"" I met the Jewish man and informed him"","" and he said"","" \""Your companion is a scholar.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim"","" from Sulayman"","" from Marwan"","" and added: \""Indeed"","" when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something"","" he acted upon it\"" — and he met the Jewish man"","" as mentioned in the narration's entirety. [Sahih]"""""
"11643","(11638) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan al-Sayrafi in Marw narrated to us: 'Abd al-Samad ibn al-Fadl al-Balkhi narrated to us: Hafs ibn 'Umara al-'Adani narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill?\"" He said"","" \""The more remote and the more wholesome of the two.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11644","(11639) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Abi Ya'qub — may Allah have mercy on him — and he was one of our senior scholars, and he was a righteous man — narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I asked Jibril"","" peace be upon him"","" 'Which of the two terms did Musa"","" peace be upon him"","" fulfill?' He said"","" 'He completed and perfected them both.'\"" [Da'if. Al-Humaydi 545]"""""
"11645","(11640) Abu al-Hasan Sayyid Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hafiz — in the year twenty-five and three hundred — narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me: My father narrated to us: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us: Nafi' informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There were three people walking together when rain overtook them"","" so they took refuge in a cave in a mountain. While they were inside it"","" a boulder fell from the mountain and blocked its entrance. They said to one another"","" 'Consider the best deeds you have ever performed for Allah"","" the Most High"","" and call upon Him with them"","" so that He may relieve you through them.' One of them said"","" 'O Allah"","" I had two elderly parents"","" and I had a wife and small children. I used to tend sheep for them. When I returned in the evening"","" I would begin by giving drink to my parents. One day"","" I went out seeking fodder and did not return until my parents had fallen asleep. I prepared the vessel and then milked into it"","" and I stood with my vessel of milk at the head of my parents"","" while the little ones cried at my feet. I disliked beginning with them before my parents"","" and I disliked waking them from their sleep. I remained standing thus until the dawn broke. O Allah"","" if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance"","" then grant us a relief through which we may see the sky.' So they were given a relief"","" and they saw the sky through it. The second one said"","" 'O Allah"","" I had a cousin whom I loved"","" and she was the most beloved of people to me. I asked her for herself"","" but she said"","" \""Not until you bring me a hundred dinars.\"" I strove until I gathered a hundred dinars and brought them to her. When I was between her legs"","" she said"","" \""Fear Allah; do not break the seal except by its rightful means.\"" So I stood up from her. O Allah"","" if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance"","" then grant us a relief from this.' So they were given a relief from it. The third one said"","" 'O Allah"","" I hired a laborer for a farq of barley. When he completed his work"","" I offered him his wages"","" but he refused to take it and turned away from him. I continued working with him until I had gathered from him cows and their herdsmen. He came to me and said"","" \""Fear Allah and give me my right; do not wrong me.\"" I said to him"","" \""Go to those cows and their herdsmen and take them.\"" He said"","" \""Fear Allah and do not mock me.\"" I said"","" \""I am not mocking you. Go to those cows and their herdsmen and take them.\"" So he went and drove them away. O Allah"","" if You know that I did that seeking Your countenance"","" then grant us relief from what remains of it.\"" So Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic"","" relieved them of it"","" and they went out walking.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb and others"","" from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim"","" and al-Bukhari narrated it from another chain from Nafi'. [Bukhari 2272"","" Muslim 2743]"""""
"11646","(11641) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: Al-Mani'i narrated to me: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Hassan ibn Khalid al-Samti — in the year twenty-eight — narrated to us: Al-Sa'idi 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his grandfather Sa'id ibn 'Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \Allah has never sent a prophet except that he was a shepherd of sheep.\"" They said"","" \""And you"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said"","" \""And I used to tend them for the people of Makkah for a few qararits.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makki"","" from 'Amr ibn Yahya. [Bukhari 2262]"""""
"11647","(11642) Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri in Makkah narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Sahli al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated to us — and Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz dictated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us: Hammad and al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: Khadijah, may Allah be pleased with her, hired the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for two journeys to Jurash, each journey for a qaluws. This is the wording of the hadith of Abu 'Abd Allah. In the narration of Abu Muhammad, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \I hired myself to Khadijah for two journeys for a qaluws.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11648","(11643) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us — al-Zuhri said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, hired a man from Banu al-Dil, then from Banu 'Abad, who was a skilled guide — and al-khirrit is one who is expert in guidance — and he had pledged his hand in allegiance to the family of al-'As ibn Wa'il, and he was upon the religion of the disbelievers of Quraysh. So they felt safe with him and handed over their two mounts, and they appointed for him the Cave of Thawr after three nights. He came to them with their two mounts on the morning of the third night, and they departed. 'Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide set out, and he took them along the route of al-Adhakhir, which is along the coastal road. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ibrahim ibn Musa, from Hisham ibn Yusuf, from Ma'mar. [Bukhari 2263]"
"11649","(11644) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \The parable of you and the parable of the People of the Book before you is the parable of a man who hired laborers and said"","" 'Who will work for me from morning until midday for a qirati?' The Christians did so. Then he said"","" 'Who will work for me from midday until the afternoon prayer for a qirati?' The Jews did so. Then he said"","" 'Who will work for me from the afternoon prayer until sunset for two qiratis?' You did so. The Jews and the Christians became angry and said"","" 'We have more work and less pay?' He said"","" 'Have I diminished anything of your rights?' They said"","" 'No.' He said"","" 'That is My bounty"","" which I give to whom I will.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb"","" and with its meaning 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated it from Ibn 'Umar. And Salim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated it from his father similarly. [Bukhari 2268]"""""
"11650","(11645) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani informed us: 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman informed me: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed me, from al-Zuhri — Salim informed me that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing upon the pulpit saying, \Your remaining time in comparison to the times of the nations before you is like the time between the afternoon prayer and the setting of the sun. The People of the Torah were given the Torah"","" and they worked with it until midday"","" then they were unable to continue"","" so they were given a qirati each. The People of the Gospel were given the Gospel"","" and they worked with it until the afternoon prayer"","" then they were unable to continue"","" so they were given a qirati each. Then you were given the Quran"","" and you worked with it until sunset"","" so you were given two qiratis each. The People of the Torah and the Gospel said"","" 'Our Lord"","" these people have less work and more reward.' He said"","" 'Have I wronged you in any way regarding your rewards?' They said"","" 'No.' He said"","" 'That is My bounty"","" which I give to whom I will.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Yaman"","" and Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ in a manner similar to the narration of Salim from his father"","" and he clarified it further. [Bukhari 7467]"""""
"11651","(11646) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Yaʿlī informed us; Abū Kurayb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū Bakr informed us; al-Qāsim informed us; Yūsuf, Ibrāhīm al-Jawharī, and al-Masrūqī narrated to us — all of them said: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\The parable of the Muslims"","" the Jews"","" and the Christians is like that of a man who hired a people to perform a work for a known wage from morning until evening. They worked until midday"","" then they said: 'We have no need of the wage you stipulated for us"","" and what we have done is of no value.' He said to them: 'Do not do that; complete the remainder of your day and then take your full wage.' But they refused and abandoned the work. So he hired another group after them and said: 'Complete the remainder of this day"","" and you shall have the wage I stipulated for those.' They worked until the time of the ʿAṣr prayer"","" then they said: 'What we have done is of no value"","" and the wage you fixed for us is yours — we have no need of it.' He said to them: 'Complete the remainder of your work"","" for only a little of the day remains"","" and take your wage.' But they refused. So he hired yet another group"","" and they worked for him the remainder of their day until the sun set"","" and they received the full wages of both [previous] groups — the entire wage. That is the parable of the Jews and the Christians"","" who abandoned what Allah commanded them"","" and the parable of the Muslims"","" who accepted the guidance of Allah and what His Messenger ﷺ brought.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ. [Bukhārī 2271]"""""
"11652","(11647) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿĪsā ibn Ḥāmid al-Rukhajī informed us in Baghdād; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīl al-Washshāʾ informed us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī informed us; my father informed me; al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from Abū Masʿūd, who said:\n\n\When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give charity"","" one of us would go to the market and carry loads"","" thereby earning a mudd [of grain]. Yet some of them now possess a hundred thousand\"" — and he did not mean anyone but himself.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā. Al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" used as evidence the Ḥadīth of Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj regarding the leasing of land for gold and silver"","" and the fact that more than one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ practiced hire (ijārah).\n\nHe also mentioned what Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us: [Bukhārī 2273]"""""
"11653","(11648) Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik informed us — that it reached him — that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf leased a piece of land, and it remained in his possession until he passed away. His son said: \I used to think it was his"","" on account of how long it remained in his possession"","" until he mentioned it at the time of his death and instructed us to settle what remained outstanding of its rent in gold or silver.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11654","(11649) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; al-Asfaṭī — meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us; al-Muʿtamir narrated to us, from his father, from Ḥanash, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\n\The Prophet of Allah ﷺ experienced hardship"","" and news of this reached ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him. He went out seeking work so that he might obtain something to send to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. He came to a garden belonging to a man of the Jews and drew water for him — seventeen buckets"","" each bucket in exchange for a date. The Jew gave him a choice and selected seventeen ʿajwah dates from his dates. He brought them to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ"","" who said: 'Where is this from"","" O Abū al-Ḥasan?' He said: 'It reached me of your hardship"","" O Prophet of Allah"","" so I went out seeking work that I might obtain food for you.' He said: 'The love of Allah and His Messenger drove you to this?' ʿAlī said: 'Yes"","" O Prophet of Allah.' The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no servant who loves Allah and His Messenger except that poverty comes to him more swiftly than the flow of a torrent upon its surface. Let the one who loves Allah and His Messenger prepare tijfāf'\"" — meaning patience (ṣabr).\n\nIt is also narrated from Yazīd ibn Ziyād"","" from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"","" who said: \""Someone who heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to me"",""\"" and he mentioned part of the meaning of this story. [Weak]"""""
"11655","(11650) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Mujāhid, who said:\n\n\ʿAlī came out to us wearing a striped cloak wrapped around him"","" and said: 'When the verse {So turn away from them"","" for you are not to be blamed} [al-Dhāriyāt 54:54] was revealed"","" not one of us remained without being certain of destruction"","" when the Prophet ﷺ was commanded to turn away from us when it was revealed.' ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" mentioned that he passed by a woman of the Ansār"","" and before her door there was clay. He said: 'Do you wish that I moisten this clay for you?' She said: 'Yes.' So he stipulated with her that for every bucket [of water] she would give him a date. He moistened it for her and she gave him sixteen dates"","" and he brought them to the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Fāṭimah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" regarding ʿAlī's"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" drawing water for a Jew — each bucket for a date. And it is narrated from Abū Hurayrah regarding an unnamed man drawing water. [Weak]"""""
"11656","(11651) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Hilāl informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, from Abū Ḥanīfah, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ:\n\n\A man shall not outbid his brother [in a transaction]"","" nor shall he propose marriage over his brother's proposal. Do not practice najash [artificial bidding]"","" and do not sell by casting stones [a pre-Islamic method of sale]. And whoever hires a worker"","" let him inform him of his wage.\""\n\nThus did Abū Ḥanīfah narrate it"","" and thus it is in my book from Abū Hurayrah. It is also said"","" through another weak chain"","" from Ibn Masʿūd. [Weak]"""""
"11657","(11652) Ḥammād ibn Salamah also narrated it from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited hiring a worker — meaning until his wage is made clear to him.\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it. It is mursal [disconnected] between Ibrāhīm and Abū Saʿīd. Similarly, Maʿmar narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān, as a mursal report. [Weak]"
"11658","(11653) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Ibn ʿUthmān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn al-Mubārak — informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Yaʿqūb said: ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated to me; Ibn Lahīʿah informed us — both of them — from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Rabiʿah ibn Laqīṭ, who informed him from Mālik ibn Hudhm — meaning from ʿAwf ibn Mālik — who said:\n\n\We went out on a military expedition"","" and our commander was ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"","" and among us were ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ. A severe famine befell us"","" so I went out seeking a livelihood. I came upon a people who wanted to slaughter a camel of theirs. I said: 'If you wish"","" I will slaughter it and do the work for you"","" and give me a portion of it.' I did so"","" and they gave me a portion of it. I prepared it and then went to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He asked me: 'Where is this from?' I informed him"","" and he said: 'I hear that you have taken your wage in advance.' He refused to eat it. Then I went to Abū ʿUbaydah and informed him"","" and he said the same to me and refused to eat it. When I saw that"","" I left it. He said: 'Then we were granted a conquest"","" and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" who said: \""You are the owner of the camel.\""' And he said nothing further to me. In the Ḥadīth of Saʿīd"","" he did not add anything beyond that.\n\nThe Sheikh said: In this [narration] is [the indication] that the wage was unknown and was attached to a specific item in the liability. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11659","(11654) It is narrated from Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Rifāʿah al-Qāḍī, from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, marfūʿ [raised to the Prophet]:\n\n\Give the worker his wage before his sweat dries"","" and inform him of his wage while he is in his work.\""\n\nAbū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿImrān al-ʿAṭṭār al-Isfarāʾinī informed us therein; Abū ʿUmar Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿImrān ibn Abī al-Ward al-Maqdisī informed us in Isfarāyīn; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Zayd al-Qāḍī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Rifāʿah narrated it. And this is weak beyond doubt. [Weak]"""""
"11660","(11655) As for the Ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-ʿAdl informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us; Salīm ibn Ḥayyān informed us, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who used to say:\n\n\I was raised as an orphan"","" I emigrated in poverty"","" and I was a hired worker for Ibn ʿAffān and the daughter of Ghazwān"","" in exchange for food for my stomach and the sole of my foot. I would gather firewood for them when they encamped"","" and I would drive their mounts when they traveled. All praise is due to Allah"","" Who made the religion firm"","" and made Abū Hurayrah an imām.\""\n\nIn this [narration] there is no indication that the Prophet ﷺ knew of it and approved of them continuing in it. And it is possible that this was a mutual agreement (muwāḍaʿah) between them based on mutual consent"","" and not a formal contract (taʿāqud). [Weak. Ibn Mājah 247]"""""
"11661","(11656) And Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) used to see no harm in a man handing a garment to another man and saying: \Sell it for such and such"","" and whatever exceeds that is for you.\"" This is also reported on the authority of Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī"","" who reported to us Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī"","" who reported to us ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"","" from Abī ʿUbayd"","" who reported to us Hushaym"","" who reported to us ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from ʬāʾiʿ"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" to that effect.\n\nAnd this"","" too"","" would be by way of mutual agreement (murāḍāh) and not by way of binding contract (muʿāqadah). And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11662","(11657) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Quraysh reported to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān reported to us, al-Haytham ibn Janād reported to us, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym reported to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, said: \There are three whose adversary I shall be on the Day of Resurrection — and whosoever I oppose"","" I shall overcome: a man who gave a pledge in My name and then proved treacherous; a man who sold a free person and consumed his price; and a man who hired a worker"","" took full work from him"","" but did not give him his wages.\"" [Bukhārī 2227]"""""
"11663","(11658) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to us, Abū Qutaybah Salm ibn al-Faḍl al-Adamī reported to us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī reported to us, Yūsuf ibn Muḥammad ibn Sābiq reported to us, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym reported to us, and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yūsuf ibn Muḥammad. [Authentic]"
"11664","(11659) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh reported to us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz reported to us, al-Zaʿfarānī — meaning al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ — reported to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mahdī reported to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar reported to us, Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ reported to me, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.\""\n\nAnd Abū Ṭāhir reported to us"","" Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl reported to us"","" Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā reported to us"","" Suwayd al-Anbārī reported to us"","" Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār al-Mu'adhdhin reported to us"","" from al-Maqburī"","" from Abū Hurayrah"","" who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11665","(11660) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān reported to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār reported to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar and Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl both said: Musaddad reported to us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid reported to us, al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Musayyab reported to us, Abū Umāmah al-Taymī reported to us, saying: I used to let out mounts for hire in this direction (i.e., for Ḥajj), and there were people who would say to me: \You have no Ḥajj.\"" So I met Ibn ʿUmar and said: \""O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" I am a man who lets out mounts for hire in this direction"","" and people say to me: 'You have no Ḥajj.'\"" He said: \""Do you not enter iḥrām"","" say the talbiyyah"","" perform ṭawāf of the House"","" depart from ʿArafāt"","" and stone the jamarāt?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then you have a Ḥajj. A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him the same question you have asked me"","" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained silent and did not answer him until this verse was revealed: {There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord} [al-Baqarah:198]. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for him"","" recited this verse to him"","" and said: 'You have a Ḥajj.'\"" [Authentic. 2/155/6434"","" Abū Dāwūd 1733]"""""
"11666","(11661) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh reported to us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz reported to us, Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ reported to us, Sufyān reported to us, from Muslimat ibn Nawfal, from a man of Thaqīf, from his father, who said: I heard ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) calling out: \Delay the loads"","" for the hands are suspended and the feet are shackled.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11667","(11662) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān reported to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar reported to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān reported to us, Abū Nuʿaym reported to us, Muslimat ibn Nawfal reported to us, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, Abū al-Mughīrah al-Thaqafī reported to me, my father reported to us, saying: He was with his father at Minā when he heard a caller proclaiming: \O people"","" delay the loads"","" for the feet are shackled and the hands are suspended.\"" I said to my father: \""Who is this?\"" He said: \""ʿUmar.\""\n\nYaʿqūb said: Muslimat is a Kūfan"","" trustworthy (thiqah). And a musnad ḥadīth has been narrated in this regard with a chain that is not strong. [Weak]"""""
"11668","(11663) Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh reported to us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān reported to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī reported to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣalt reported to us, Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ reported to us, from Bakr ibn Wāʾil, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you load"","" do so last"","" for the hands are suspended and the feet are shackled.\"" Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ connected it from Bakr ibn Wāʾil.\n\nAnd Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Wāʾil or Bakr ibn Wāʾil — thus with doubt — from al-Zuhrī"","" tracing it back to the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" who said: \""Delay the loads"","" for the hands are suspended and the feet are shackled.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11669","(11664) In what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān reported to us, from al-Shāfiʿī, who said: Shurayḥ held the view of holding the fuller (qaṣṣār) liable for compensation. He held a fuller liable whose house was burnt. The fuller said: \You hold me liable when my house has been burnt?\"" Shurayḥ said: \""Tell me"","" if his house had been burnt"","" would you have waived your payment to him?\"" Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated this from him.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And it has been narrated on an authority that the scholars of ḥadīth do not consider reliable that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālik held the washer (ghassāl) and the dyer (ṣabbāgh) liable"","" and he said: \""People will not be set right except by that.\"" [Authentic. Al-Umm 4/41]"""""
"11670","(11665) Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā reported to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī said that.\n\nAnd it is narrated from ʿUmar that he held some craftsmen liable, on an authority weaker than this, and we do not know either of them to be established (thābit). And it has been narrated from ʿAlī on another authority that he used not to hold any of the hired workers liable, on an authority that is not established like it. And it is established from ʬāʾiʿ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ that he said: \There is no liability upon a craftsman or upon a hired worker.\"" [Weak. Al-Umm 4/41]"""""
"11671","(11666) Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Shabbān al-ʿAṭṭār in Baghdād — narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Abū al-Jumāhir narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from ʿAlī — that he used to hold craftsmen and goldsmiths liable (for entrusted items), and he said: \Nothing is proper for the people except that.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11672","(11667) And Abū al-Qāsim ibn Shabbān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Shawārib narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qatādah from Khilās — that ʿAlī used to hold the hired worker liable.\n\nThe ḥadīth of Jaʿfar from his father from ʿAlī is mursal, and the scholars of ḥadīth weaken the narrations of Khilās from ʿAlī.\n\nAnd Jābir al-Juʿfī — who is weak — narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿAlī used to hold the hired worker liable. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"11673","(11668) Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from al-Aʿshath, meaning Ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, who said: I witnessed Shurayḥ holding a fuller or a dyer liable. [Weak]"
"11674","(11669) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abū al-Ḍaḥr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū al-Haytham — that some oil of his arrived from Baṣrah, and he hired a porter to carry it. The flask was worth three hundred or four hundred (dirhams). The flask fell and broke. I wanted him to reach a settlement with me, but he refused. So I took him before Shurayḥ. Shurayḥ said to him: \You were given the wage on the condition that you would be liable.\"" So Shurayḥ held him liable. Then the people continued (interceding) until I reached a settlement with him. [Weak]"""""
"11675","(11670) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us: Ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from al-Aʿmash, who said: I asked Ibrāhīm about the fuller, and he said: \He is liable.\"" Then it reached me from Ḥammād that he narrated from Ibrāhīm that he said: \""He is not liable.\"" He (al-Aʿmash) said: \""So I met him and said: 'By Allah"","" I do not know whether I ever saw you with Ibrāhīm or not.' He said: 'Do not do that"","" O Abū Muḥammad"","" for this is difficult for me.'\"" And Allah knows best. [Sound]"""""
"11676","(11671) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr narrated to me: Nāfiʿ narrated from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh from his father that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: \Any man who hires something and its owner passes Dhū al-Ḥulayfah — his hire is due upon him"","" and there is no liability upon him.\"" He means — and Allah knows best — that the hirer took possession of what he hired and passed Dhū al-Ḥulayfah; then the entire hire is due upon him"","" provided no condition of a fixed term was stipulated in the wage. And there is no liability upon him so long as he did not transgress. [Sound]"""""
"11677","(11672) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Taʿzīr (discretionary punishment) is a disciplinary measure"","" not one of the prescribed ḥudūd of Allah. It is permissible to leave it. Do you not see that certain matters occurred during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that were not ḥudūd"","" yet he did not inflict punishment in them — such as misappropriation in the cause of Allah and other such matters — and no prescribed ḥadd was ever brought (forward)"","" so he pardoned.\"" He also said: \""And it has been narrated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" sent (a message) to a woman regarding something that had reached him about her"","" and she miscarried. So he consulted (the people)"","" and someone said to him: 'You are a discipliner (muʾaddib).' ʿAlī said to him: 'If he exercised his judgment (ijtihād)"","" then he erred; and if he did not exercise his judgment"","" then the blood-money is upon you.' He said: 'I adjure you not to sit until you distribute it among your people.'\"" And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""There is no one upon whom a ḥadd is executed but I find something in my soul concerning him"","" except the truth of his execution — except one who dies under the ḥadd of wine-drinking"","" for that is a matter we saw after the Prophet ﷺ. Whoever dies under it"","" I would pay his blood-money — either he said"","" 'from the public treasury"",""' or he said"","" 'from the ʿāqilah of the Imam.'\"" [Sound]"""""
"11678","(11673) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ granted me permission to narrate from him, that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed them, saying: al-Māsarjisī, Abū al-ʿAbbās, narrated to us: Shaybān narrated to us: Salām narrated — I heard al-Ḥasan say: \ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" was informed that a promiscuous woman was being visited by men. So he sent a messenger to her. The messenger came to her and said: 'Respond to the Commander of the Faithful.' She was seized with such terror that the shock reached her womb"","" and her child moved. She went into labor and delivered a male fetus. This was brought to ʿUmar"","" so he sent for the Emigrants and narrated her affair to them"","" and said: 'What do you think?' They said: 'We see nothing upon you"","" O Commander of the Faithful; you are only a teacher and a discipliner.' ʿAlī was among the people"","" and ʿAlī was silent. He said: 'What do you say"","" O Abū al-Ḥasan?' He said: 'I say: if they were close to you in affection"","" then they have sinned; and if this was the result of their ijtihād"","" then they have erred. And I see the blood-money to be upon you"","" O Commander of the Faithful.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth. Go and distribute it among your people.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"11679","(11674) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us therein: Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām al-Qaṣṣār and Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated from Sufyān from Abū Ḥuṣayn from ʿUmayr ibn Saʿīd from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \There is no one upon whom a ḥadd is executed but I find something in my soul concerning him"","" except the wine-drinker. If he were to die"","" I would pay his blood-money"","" because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prescribe it.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī.\n\nWhat he meant by \""he did not prescribe it\"" is that he did not prescribe anything beyond forty (lashes) up to eighty — that is"","" what they added to his ḥadd by way of taʿzīr (discretionary punishment). As for the forty (lashes) with palm branches"","" sandals"","" and the edges of garments — that is a firmly established ḥadd from the Prophet ﷺ. [Bukhārī 6778"","" Muslim 1707]"""""
"11680","(11675) Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh — narrated to us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʬAṭāʾ regarding a teacher who strikes a boy for disciplinary purposes and the boy is injured — he said: \He is liable (for compensation).\"" [Good]"""""
"11681","(11676) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Yaḥyā Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Samarqandī informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yazīd, meaning Abū Maʿshar al-Barrāʾ, narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Akhnas narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a body of water in which there was a person who had been stung (or bitten). A man from the people of that water came to them and said: \Is there among you a practitioner of ruqyah? Indeed"","" there is a man in the water who has been stung (or bitten).\"" So one of them went and recited Umm al-Kitāb (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah) over a sheep"","" and the man was cured. He brought the sheep to his companions"","" but they disapproved of that and said: \""You have taken a fee for the Book of Allah.\"" He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him of what had happened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Indeed"","" the most deserving thing upon which you take a fee is the Book of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saydān ibn Muḍārib"","" from Abū Maʿshar. [Bukhārī 5737]"""""
"11682","(11677) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī, Musaddad, and al-Ḥajabī narrated to us; they said: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Abū Bishr, from Abī al-Mutawakkil al-Nājī, from Abī Saʿīd, that a group of the Anṣār from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out on a journey they had undertaken until they encamped near a tribe of the Arab tribes. They sought hospitality from them, but they refused to host them. Then the chief of the tribe was bitten (by a snake), and they tried everything for him but nothing benefited him. Some of them said: \If only you would go to those people who have encamped near you—perhaps some among them may have something that could help your companion.\"" So they came to them and said: \""O group of people"","" our chief has been bitten"","" and we have tried everything for him but nothing has helped him. Is there among you anything that could benefit our companion?\"" One of them said: \""Yes"","" by Allah"","" I do perform ruqyah"","" but by Allah"","" we sought hospitality from you and you refused to host us"","" so I will not perform ruqyah until you set a fee for us.\"" So they agreed upon a flock of sheep. He then went and began to blow upon him while reciting: 'Al-ḥamdu lillāhi Rabb al-ʿālamīn' (All praise is due to Allah"","" the Lord of the Worlds)"","" until he was cured"","" as though he had been released from a rope"","" and he began to walk with no complaint whatsoever. They then paid him the fee upon which which they had agreed. He said: \""Divide it.\"" The one who had performed the ruqyah said: \""Do not do so until we come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mention to him what happened"","" and see what he commands us.\"" So they went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the morning and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said: \""How did you know that it is a ruqyah?\"" He also said: \""You have done rightly. Divide it"","" and set aside a share for me along with you.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh said: He narrated this hadith to us from each of them individually"","" and some of them added to others in the hadith"","" while the meaning is the same.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl and others"","" from Abū ʿAwanah. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim also narrated it from the hadith of Shuʿbah"","" from Abū Bishr. The hadith of the woman married in exchange for teaching the Qurʾān is evidence on this matter"","" and its place is in the Book of the Mahr."""""
"11683","(11678) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Jammāl narrated to us; Idrīs ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Ṣadaqah ibn Mūsā al-Dimashqī narrated from al-Waḍīn ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: There were three teachers in Madīnah who taught the boys, and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to grant each of them fifteen dirhams every month.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah similarly narrated it from Wakīʿ."
"11684","(11679) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī informed us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us; Shuʿbah said: I asked Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah about the teacher's fee. He said: \I see it as permissible for him to have a fee.\"" Shuʿbah said: I also asked al-Ḥakam"","" and he said: \""I have not heard anyone disapprove of it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said in the heading: Al-Ḥakam said: \""I have not heard anyone disapprove of the teacher's fee.\"" He said: Ibn Sīrīn also saw no harm in the teacher's fee.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: It has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ and Abū Qilābah that they both saw no harm in teaching boys for a fee. And from al-Ḥasan (may Allah have mercy on him)"","" who said: \""If the teacher makes a fixed agreement and does not act justly"","" he is recorded among the oppressors.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd 1103]"""""
"11685","(11680) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Rajāʾ al-Adīb informed us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ḥulwānī Abū Jaʿfar narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Khāqān and Faḍl ibn ʿImrān al-Aʿraj said: ʿAlī ibn ʢāṣim narrated to us; he said: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed me from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: There was no ransom set for some of the captives of Badr. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made their ransom that they teach the children of the Anṣār writing. He said: A boy from the Anṣār came weeping to his father one day. His father said to him: \What is the matter with you?\"" He said: \""My teacher hit me.\"" He said: \""The wicked one seeks vengeance for the grudge of Badr! By Allah"","" do not go to him ever again.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11686","(11681) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ruʾāsī, from Mughīrah ibn Ziyād, from ʿUbādah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thaʿlabah, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: I taught some of the people of al-Ṣuffah writing and the Qurʾān. Then a man among them presented me with a bow. I said: \It is not (considered) wealth"","" and I shall shoot with it in the cause of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic. I must go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and ask him.\"" So I came to him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" a man from among those whom I teach writing and the Qurʾān has presented me with a bow. It is not (considered) wealth"","" and I shall shoot with it in the cause of Allah.\"" He said: \""If you would like to be collared with a collar of fire"","" then accept it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11687","(11682) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ narrated to us; he said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said regarding the hadith of ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \If it pleases you to be collared with a collar of fire"",""\"" concerning the one who taught writing.\n\nMughīrah ibn Ziyād al-Mawṣilī narrated it from ʿUbādah ibn Nusayy"","" from al-Aswad ibn Thaʿlabah"","" from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit. Its entire chain is well known"","" except for al-Aswad ibn Thaʿlabah—for we do not preserve from him anything other than this hadith.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from ʿUbādah ibn Nusayy"","" from Junādah ibn Abī Umayyah"","" from ʿUbādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11688","(11683) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān and Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd said: Baqiyyah narrated to us; Bishr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yasār narrated to me. ʿAmr said: ʿUbādah ibn Nusayy narrated to me from Junādah ibn Abī Umayyah, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, with a similar report, though the first version is more complete. I said: \What do you see regarding it"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""It is a burning coal between your two shoulders that you have hung upon yourself or attached to yourself.\""\n\nAbū al-Mughīrah similarly narrated it from Bishr. This is a hadith that differs over regarding ʿUbādah ibn Nusayy"","" as you see. The hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās and Abī Saʿīd has a more authentic chain than it. It has also been narrated through another disconnected chain from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11689","(11684) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Thawr ibn Yazīd; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Muslim narrated to me from ʿAṭiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilābī, who said: Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him) taught a man the Qurʾān. The man went to Yemen and then presented him with a bow. He mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \If you take it"","" then you take a bow of fire.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain from Abī al-Dardāʾ. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11690","(11685) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Sarrāj informed us by dictation; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbaydullāh narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbaydullāh, from Umm al-Dardāʾ, from Abī al-Dardāʾ, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever takes a bow in exchange for teaching the Qurʾān"","" Allah will hang upon him a bow of fire.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11691","(11686) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, and he said: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī granted us permission from Ḥuṣayn, who said: The hadith of Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Whoever takes up a bow for teaching the Qurʾān — it has no basis.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11692","(11687) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Bālawayh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us that Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm and Abū ʿUmar both said: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah from Abū Ḥāzim from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited the earnings of slave women.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\nIt is possible that the prohibition of the earnings of slave women refers to the earnings of the prostitute among them, as Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited the dowry of the prostitute, and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The dowry of the prostitute is impure.\"" We have mentioned both of them in the book of sales.\n\n[Bukhārī 2283]"""""
"11693","(11688) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that Abū Maʿmar narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us that Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the price of a dog and the earnings of the singing slave girl.\n\nThe Sheikh said: It is possible that the prohibition of their earnings refers to the case where it is not known from whence they earned it, by way of caution (tanzīh), out of fear of falling into the ḥarām. And upon this is the indication of what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11694","(11689) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Abū al-Naḍr Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us that Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qurashī narrated to us, who said: Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ came to the gathering of the Anṣār and said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited us today\"" — and he mentioned certain things and said: \""He prohibited us from the earnings of the slave woman except what she produced with her own hands\"" — and he gestured with his finger towards spinning"","" baking"","" and embroidery.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 3426]"""""
"11695","(11690) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ṣaqr narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ḥurayr from his father from his grandfather Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the earnings of the slave woman until it is known from whence it came. The remainder of this topic is mentioned in the book of expenditures, where al-Shāfiʿī mentioned this issue in the chapter on the expenditure for slaves. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11696","(11691) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Abū Yaḥyā al-Ruwayānī informed us that Ibrāhīm — he is ibn Mūsā al-Farrāʾ — informed us that ʿĪsā — he is ibn Yūnus — informed us that Thawr narrated to us from Khālid ibn Maʿdān from Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No child of Adam has ever eaten any food better for him than that which he eats from the work of his own hands. Indeed"","" the Prophet of Allah"","" Dāwūd"","" used to eat from the earnings of his own hands.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā. [Bukhārī 2072]"""""
"11697","(11692) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated to us from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Qurʾān was made easy for Dāwūd"","" so he would command his mounts to be saddled"","" and he would recite the Qurʾān before his mount was saddled"","" and he would not eat except from the work of his own hands.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" at the end of the report.\n\nIt was narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad and Isḥāq ibn Naṣr from ʿAbd al-Razzāq the beginning of the report. We have narrated from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \""The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were people who worked for themselves.\"" And in another narration: \""They would tend to their lands with their own hands.\"" We have narrated from Khabbāb ibn al-Aratt (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \""I was a blacksmith.\"" We have narrated from Anas ibn Mālik in the story of Ibrāhīm"","" the son of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" that he entrusted him to Umm Sayf"","" a blacksmith woman in Madīnah. And from Sahl ibn Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him) in the story of the minbar: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent to a woman: \""Tell your slave carpenter to make me some planks upon which I may sit.\"" And from Sahl regarding the woman who came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a cloak and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I wove this with my own hands to clothe you.\"" And from Abū Masʿūd: \""There was a man from the Anṣār called Abū Shuʿayb"","" and he had a slave who was a butcher\"" — and in another narration"","" a slaughterer — \""so he said: 'Prepare food for me so that I may invite the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'\"" And from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) in the story of the sanctification of Makkah: al-ʿAbbās said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" except for the idhkhir (a type of plant) for our blacksmiths and the roofs of our houses.\"" He said: \""Except for the idhkhir.\"" And from Ibn ʿAbbās: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was cupped and he gave the cupper his fee"","" and had he known it to be impure"","" he would not have given it to him.\""\n\nIn all of this there is evidence for the permissibility of earning through these crafts and their like. The chain of narration of each one of them has passed in the book"","" or will pass"","" if Allah wills. And in the three hadiths there is evidence for that which... [Bukhārī 2073]"""""
"11698","(11693) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us that Ibn ʿĀʾishah narrated to us from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Mājidah, who said: \I fought with a slave and I cut off his ear"","" or he cut off my ear.\"" He said: \""Then Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us"","" and we were brought before him while he was going out. We presented our dispute to him"","" and he referred us to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" who said: 'Retribution has been reached. Call for me a cupper to extract from him twice or three times.' I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'I gifted a slave to my maternal aunt"","" hoping that he would be a blessing for her"","" and I told her: Do not entrust him to a cupper"","" a butcher"","" or a goldsmith.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11699","(11694) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Ḥammād narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated it with its meaning, in a more concise form.\n\nHe said: And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that al-Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq who said: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥuraqī narrated to me from Ibn Mājidah, a man from Banū Sahl, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say\"" — with its meaning.\n\nIt is interpreted as a recommendation (tanzīh)"","" not as a prohibition (taḥrīm). As for the earnings of the cupper"","" the discussion concerning it is mentioned in the abridged work in the fourth quarter. And with Allah lies success. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11700","(11695) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Sarrāj narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr narrated to us from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Seeking lawful earnings is an obligation after the obligation.\""\n\nʿAbbād ibn Kathīr al-Ramlī is the sole narrator of it"","" and he is weak.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us and said: I read in the handwriting of Abū ʿAmr al-Mustamlī: I heard Abū Aḥmad al-Farrāʾ say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā being asked about the hadith of ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr regarding lawful earnings — that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — he said: \""If he said it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11701","(11696) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣfahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī reported to us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited *al-mukhābarah*.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah, from Sufyān.\n\nIt was also narrated by Saʿīd ibn Mīnāʾ and Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Bukhārī 2633, Muslim 1536]"
"11702","(11697) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us: Ibn Rajāʾ al-Makkī narrated to us: Ibn Khuthaym narrated to me from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Whoever does not abandon *al-mukhābarah*"","" let him beware of a war from Allah and His Messenger.\"" [Abū Dāwūd 3406]"""""
"11703","(11698) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar say: \We used to practice *al-mukhābarah* and saw no harm in it"","" until Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had prohibited it"","" so we abandoned it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"","" from Sufyān. [Muslim 3935"","" Abū Dāwūd 3389]"""""
"11704","(11699) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; they said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us, from al-Shaybānī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib, who said: I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn Maʿqil about *al-muzāraʿah*. He said: Thābit ibn al-Ḥaḥḥāk narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited *al-muzāraʿah*.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Muslim 1536]"
"11705","(11700) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿĀrim, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, and Musaddad narrated to them: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Maṭar al-Warrāq, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the leasing out of land.\n\nThis is the wording of ʿĀrim and Musaddad. Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the leasing out of cultivated lands.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Kāmil"","" from Ḥammād. [Muslim 1536]"""""
"11706","(11701) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us: Aḥmad narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿĀrim narrated to us: Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us: Maṭar al-Warrāq narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever has land should cultivate it; if he does not cultivate it"","" let him give it to his brother.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd"","" from Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim. [Muslim 1536]"""""
"11707","(11702) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever has land should cultivate it; if he is unable to do so"","" let him grant it to his Muslim brother"","" and he should not lease it out.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from another chain from ʿAbd al-Malik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11708","(11703) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Umayyah Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us: Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Khālid narrated to us, from al-Shaybānī, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited that a fee or payment be taken for land.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim, from Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr.\n\nIt was also narrated by Rābiḥ ibn Abī Maʿrūf, Hammām ibn Yaḥyā, and others, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11709","(11704) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: Salīm ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Mīnāʾ, who said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever has surplus land should cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it"","" and do not sell it.\"" I said to Saʿīd: \""What does his statement 'do not sell it' mean?\"" He said: \""It means leasing it out.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from another chain from Salīm ibn Ḥayyān.\n\nIt was also narrated by Abū al-Zubayr"","" Abū Sufyān"","" and others"","" from Jābir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""""
"11710","(11705) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm—he is Ibn Milḥān—narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Layth narrated to me, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to lease out his land, until it reached him that Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj al-Anṣārī used to prohibit the leasing out of land. ʿAbdullāh met him and said: \O Ibn Khadīj"","" what do you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the leasing out of land?\"" Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj said to ʿAbdullāh: \""I heard my two uncles—both of whom had witnessed Badr—narrating to the people of the household that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the leasing out of land.\"" ʿAbdullāh said: \""By Allah"","" I knew during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that land was leased out. Then ʿAbdullāh feared that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) might have introduced something new in this matter that he was not aware of"","" so he abandoned the leasing out of land.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it from another chain from Layth. [Bukhārī 2347"","" Muslim 1547]"""""
"11711","(11706) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmā' narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated from Mālik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhrī, that Sālim ibn 'Abdullāh informed him and asked him about the leasing of agricultural land. He said: Rāfi' ibn Khadīj informed 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, on the authority of his two paternal uncles who had witnessed Badr, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the leasing of agricultural land. He said: So 'Abdullāh abandoned leasing it, although he had been leasing it before that. Al-Zuhrī said: I said to Sālim, \Do you lease it?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" 'Abdullāh used to lease it.\"" I said: \""Then what of the hadith of Rāfi'?\"" Sālim said: \""Indeed"","" Rāfi' has imposed upon himself (i.e."","" erred in his narration).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmā'. [Bukhārī 4013]"""""
"11712","(11707) Abū al-Ḥusayn 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Ja'far Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzāz informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhāb, i.e. ibn 'Aṭā', informed us, Ibn 'Awn narrated from Nāfi' that Ibn 'Umar used to take the rent of land until a hadith from Rāfi' ibn Khadīj reached him. Nāfi' said: \I went with him until we came to Rāfi'"","" and he narrated from some of his paternal uncles"","" mentioning the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" that he prohibited the renting of land. So Ibn 'Umar abandoned it after that.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11713","(11708) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abdullāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abdullāh al-Sa'dī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ibn 'Awn narrated this hadith with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim, from Yazīd ibn Hārūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11714","(11709) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abdullāh Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdullāh informed us, Abū 'Amr ibn Abī Ja'far informed me, Abū Ya'lā informed us, Abū al-Rabī' narrated to us. They both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfi', who said: \Ibn 'Umar used to lease his agricultural lands during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" Abū Bakr"","" 'Umar"","" 'Uthmān"","" and the beginning of the governorship of Mu'āwiya (may Allah be pleased with them). Then a man came to him and said: 'Indeed"","" Rāfi' claims that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited the leasing of land.'\"" Nāfi' said: \""So Ibn 'Umar set out towards Rāfi' and I went with him. Ibn 'Umar said to him: 'What is it that has reached me from you"","" that you mention from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the leasing of agricultural lands?' He said: 'Yes"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the leasing of agricultural lands.'\"" Nāfi' said: \""After that"","" when Ibn 'Umar was asked about it"","" he would say: 'Rāfi' claims that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited it.'\"" Nāfi' said: \""Ibn 'Umar said"","" when Rāfi' mentioned what he mentioned: 'I already knew that we used to lease our agricultural lands during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for what was on the irrigation channels and something of fodder that I do not recall precisely.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabī'. [Bukhārī 2344]"""""
"11715","(11710) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, al-Naḍr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, 'Ikrimah, i.e. ibn 'Ammār, narrated to us, Abū al-Najāshī, the freed slave of Rāfi' ibn Khadīj, narrated to us and said: \Rāfi' ibn Khadīj prohibited me from the leasing of land and claimed that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it through another chain from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammār"","" more complete than that. [Muslim 1547]"""""
"11716","(11711) Abū Muḥammad 'Abdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn 'Imrān al-Qāḍī in Harāt informed us, Abū Ḥātim 'Abd al-Jalīl ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, 'Ubaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Awzā'ī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, and Abū 'Abdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Sa'īd ibn 'Uthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Awzā'ī narrated to us, 'Aṭā' narrated from Jābir, who said: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" certain men had surplus lands and they would lease them for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" or one-half (of the produce). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has surplus land should cultivate it or grant it to his brother (to cultivate). If he refuses"","" he should retain his land (i.e."","" leave it as it is).'\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Bishr.\n\nAnd in the narration of 'Ubaydullāh: \""Certain men had surplus lands and they would cultivate them for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" or one-half. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and he said: 'Whoever has land should cultivate it or grant it to his brother. If he does not do so"","" he should retain his land.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Ubaydullāh ibn Mūsā"","" and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Hiql from al-Awzā'ī. [Bukhārī 2341"","" Muslim 1536]"""""
"11717","(11712) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Īsā narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me, Hishām ibn Sa'd informed me that Abū al-Zubayr narrated to him. He said: \I heard Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh say: 'In the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" we used to take land on the basis of one-third and one-quarter of the produce from the irrigation channels.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up and said: 'Whoever has land should cultivate it"","" and if he does not cultivate it"","" he should grant it to his brother"","" and if he does not grant it to his brother"","" he should retain it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn 'Īsā. [Muslim 1536]"""""
"11718","(11713) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir, who said: \We used to practice mukhābarah (sharecropping) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" taking a share of the grain and such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has land should cultivate it"","" or let his brother cultivate it; otherwise"","" he should leave it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim]"""""
"11719","(11714) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ja'far informed us, 'Abd al-Wahhāb ibn 'Aṭā' informed us, Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Arūbah narrated from Ya'lā ibn Ḥakīm, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Rāfi' ibn Khadīj, who said: \We used to practice muḥāqalah (leasing land for a share of the produce) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""Then one of his paternal uncles came to him\"" — Qatādah said: \""His name was Ẓuhayr\"" — and said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited a matter that was beneficial to us"","" and obedience to Allah and His Messenger is more beneficial for us and better.\"" The people said: \""What is that?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has land should cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it"","" and he should not lease it for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" or a specified quantity of food.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it through various chains from Ibn Abī 'Arūbah. [Muslim 1548]"""""
"11720","(11715) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Karābīsī informed us, Abū 'Abdullāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, who said: \Ya'lā ibn Ḥakīm wrote to me"","" from Sulaymān ibn Yasār"","" from Rāfi' ibn Khadīj"","" who said: 'We used to practice muḥāqalah with land and lease it for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" and a specified quantity of food. At that time"","" there was neither gold nor silver; we would lease it for land. I did not feel any day when one of my paternal uncles met me and said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited us from a matter that was beneficial to us"","" and obedience to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is more beneficial for us and better. We used to practice muḥāqalah with land and lease it for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" and a specified quantity of food.\"" So he prohibited us from that and commanded the owner of the land to cultivate it or to let (another) cultivate it"","" and he disliked its leasing and anything other than that.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. By \""a specified quantity of food\"" he meant what came out of that land"","" and this is clarified in some of the narrations from Rāfi'. \""And he disliked its leasing\"" — he meant by that what is implied in its meaning"","" and Allah knows best. [Muslim 1517]"""""
"11721","(11716) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: my father narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Abū al-Najāshī narrated to me, he said: I accompanied Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj for six years. He said: He narrated to me from his uncle Ẓuhayr ibn Rāfiʿ that he met him one day and said to him: \Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from a matter that was profitable for us.\"" Rāfiʿ said: I said to him"","" \""Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said is the truth.\"" He said: \""What do you think of your lands under the muḥāqalah arrangement — what do you do with them?\"" We said: \""We lease them out for one-fourth or for measures of dates and barley.\"" He said: \""Do not do so. Cultivate them or leave them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū ʿAwānah"","" 5144]"""""
"11722","(11717) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays, that he asked Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj about the leasing of land, and he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leasing of land.\"" He said: I said: \""What about with gold and silver?\"" He said: \""As for with gold and silver"","" there is nothing wrong with it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Rāfiʿ heard the prohibition from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and he is most knowledgeable of the meaning of what he heard. Rāfiʿ only reported the Prophet's ﷺ prohibition of leasing land for one-third or one-quarter"","" and that was how land used to be leased. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1425]"""""
"11723","(11718) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, that he asked Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh about the leasing of land, and he said: \There is nothing wrong with it.\"" I said to him: \""What do you think of the ḥadīth that is mentioned from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj?\"" He said: \""Rāfiʿ has exaggerated. If I had land"","" I would lease it out.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Bukayr.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: It may be that Sālim heard the report from Rāfiʿ in general terms"","" and he understood that he narrated it regarding leasing for gold and silver"","" so he saw nothing wrong with leasing for gold and silver"","" because he knew that land is leased for gold and silver. Others besides Mālik ibn Anas have clarified from Rāfiʿ that he forbade the leasing of land for some of what comes out of it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1392]"""""
"11724","(11719) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: al-Layth narrated to me, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays, that he asked Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj about the leasing of land, and he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the leasing of land for some of what comes out of it.\"" He said: \""So I asked him about leasing it for gold and silver"","" and he said: 'There is nothing wrong with leasing it for gold and silver.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 2073]"""""
"11725","(11720) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ narrated to me: al-Layth — he is Ibn Saʿd — narrated to me, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: My paternal uncles narrated to me that they used to lease land during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for what grew on the borders of the watercourses or for something that the owner of the land would exclude. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that. I said to Rāfiʿ: \How is it with dinars and dirhams?\"" Rāfiʿ said: \""There is nothing wrong with it with dinars and dirhams.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Khālid from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11726","(11721) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, Aḥmad ibn Salamah, and Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, all saying: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays al-Anṣārī, who said: I asked Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj about the leasing of land for gold and silver, and he said: \There is nothing wrong with it. The people used to lease land during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the water meadows and the heads of the streams and portions of the crop. This would perish and that would be safe"","" and that would be safe and this would perish. The people had no lease except this. That is why he ﷺ forbade it. But as for something known and guaranteed"","" there is nothing wrong with it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11727","(11722) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays, that he heard Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj say: \We were the Anṣār with the most fields. We used to lease land on the condition that this portion would be ours and that portion would be theirs. Sometimes this would produce and that would not"","" so he ﷺ forbade us from that. As for silver"","" he did not forbid us.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11728","(11723) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Ḥanẓalah ibn Qays al-Anṣārī informed him that he heard Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj say: \We were the people of Madīnah with the most cultivated land. We used to lease land for a portion of it that was designated for the owner of the land. Sometimes that portion would be afflicted and the land would be afflicted"","" and sometimes that portion would be safe and the land would be safe.\"" He said: \""So we were forbidden from that. As for gold and silver"","" that was not in that time.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Yazīd ibn Hārūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11729","(11724) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, from Usayd — he is Ibn Ẓuhayr, the nephew of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj — who said: \One of us"","" when he no longer needed his land"","" would give it for one-third"","" one-quarter"","" or one-half"","" and stipulate three water channels"","" and stipulate the chaff and what the spring water irrigated. At that time"","" life was hard. We used to work in it with iron tools and whatever Allah willed"","" and we would derive benefit from that. Then Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj came to us and said: 'Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbids you from a matter that was beneficial to you"","" and obedience to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more beneficial for you. He forbids you from the muḥāqalah and says: \""Whoever no longer needs his land"","" let him grant it to his brother or leave it.\"" And he forbids you from the muzābanah"","" and the muzābanah is that a man has a great wealth of date palms"","" and a man comes to him and says: \""I have taken it for such-and-such a measure of dates.\""'\"" [Ibn Mājah"","" 2460]"""""
"11730","(11725) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Ṭāriq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the muḥāqalah and the muzābanah"","" and he said: 'Only three types of people cultivate: a man who has land and he cultivates it; a man who has been granted land and he cultivates what he has been granted; and a man who leases land for gold or silver.'\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd"","" 3400]"""""
"11731","(11726) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to me: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym — al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn — informed us: Bukayr ibn ʿĀmir narrated from Bukayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿaym, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj that he cultivated a piece of land. The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was irrigating it and asked: \For whom is the crop"","" and for whom is the land?\"" He replied: \""The crop is mine — from my seed and my labor — and half is mine and half belongs to Banī So-and-so.\"" He said: \""You have engaged in usurious practice. Return the land to its owners and take your expenses.\""\n\n[Weak. Abū Dāwūd 3402]"""""
"11732","(11727) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Hāshim ibn Yaʿlā narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf al-Zuhrī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Labībah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \People used to lease agricultural land in exchange for what grew along the water channel and what the water carried upward from the area around the well. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them from that and commanded them to lease in exchange for gold and silver.\""\n\n[Weak]"""""
"11733","(11728) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Ayyūb narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Burqān, from Thābit ibn al-Ḥajjāj, from Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-mukhābarah.\"" I asked: \""What is al-mukhābarah?\"" He said: \""That you take a piece of land in exchange for one-half"","" one-third"","" or one-quarter [of its produce].\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 21970]"""""
"11734","(11729) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: Abū ʿAwānah narrated from al-Shaybānī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib, who said: \I entered upon ʿAbdullāh ibn Maʿqil and asked him about al-muzāraʿah. He said: 'Thābit claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muzāraʿah and commanded us to practice al-muʾājarah (leasing for a fixed wage)"","" and said: There is no harm in it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 16502]"""""
"11735","(11730) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān informed us: ʿAbd al-Karīm informed me from Saʿīb ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The most exemplary thing you can do is to lease the white (uncultivated) land in which there are no trees.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĪsā"","" from Mūsā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd"","" who said: \""Ibn ʿUmar was asked about the leasing of land"","" and he said: 'My land and my camel are equal (i.e."","" I may lease out either).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11736","(11731) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he was asked about leasing land in exchange for gold and silver, and he said: \There is no harm in it.\""\n\nHe said: And Mālik informed us from Hishām"","" from his father"","" something similar to it.\n\nHe said: And Mālik informed us from Ibn Shihāb"","" from Sālik"","" the same as that.\n\n[Mālik 1319]\n\n[Chapter] Regarding the one who permitted al-muzāraʿah for a known"","" shared portion"","" and interpreted the prohibition as being one of discourishment (tanzīh)"","" or as applying to a case in which the contract contains a corrupt condition."""""
"11737","(11732) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr that Mujāhid said to Ṭāwūs: \Come with us to Ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj so that we may hear from him the hadith from his father from the Prophet ﷺ.\"" He rebuked him and said: \""By Allah"","" if I knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prohibited it"","" I would not have done it. However"","" one who is more knowledgeable than them informed me\"" — meaning Ibn ʿAbbās — \""that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That a man grants his brother the use of his land is better for him than that he take from him a fixed yield.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Muslim 1550]"""""
"11738","(11733) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us: Abū al-Qāsim — Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī — narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār. He said: \I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: 'We used not to disapprove of al-muzāraʿah until I heard Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muzāraʿah.\""'\""\n\nAnd from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from Ṭāwūs"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" that the Prophet ﷺ did not prohibit al-muzāraʿah"","" but said: \""That one of you grant his brother the use of his land is better for him than that he take a fixed payment.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qabīṣah"","" without the narration of Ibn ʿUmar from Rāfiʿ. And Muslim narrated the hadith of Ibn ʿUmar from the narration of Wakīʿ from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū ʿAwānah 5181]"""""
"11739","(11734) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār. He said: \I said to Ṭāwūs: 'If only you would abandon al-mukhābarah"","" for they claim that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited it.' He said: 'O ʿAmr"","" I give to them and assist them"","" and the most knowledgeable among them informed me'\"" — meaning Ibn ʿAbbās — \""that the Prophet ﷺ did not prohibit it"","" but said: 'That one of you grant his brother the use of his land is better for him than that he take from it a fixed yield.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Bukhārī 2330]"""""
"11740","(11735) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Khālid narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that when he heard the people's frequent practice of leasing land, he said: \Glory be to Allah! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: 'Why does he not grant it to his brother?' And He did not prohibit its leasing.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth. [Bukhārī and Muslim]"""""
"11741","(11736) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ibn Nājiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abī Rizmah narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated from Sharīk, from Shuʿbah, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not prohibit sharecropping (al-muzāraʿah), but rather he commanded that people show gentleness toward one another.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr from al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā. [Muslim 1550]"
"11742","(11737) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyysh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us, Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq, from Abī ʿUbaydah ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār, from al-Walīd ibn Abī al-Walīd, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that he said: \May Allah forgive Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj! By Allah"","" I was more knowledgeable of the ḥadīth than him. Two men from the Anṣār came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who had fought with one another"","" and he said: 'If this is your affair"","" then do not lease out the cultivated lands.' So he (Rāfiʿ) heard his words: 'Do not lease out the cultivated lands.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Zayd ibn Thābit and Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) appear to have rejected it—and Allah knows best—the absolute prohibition of leasing out cultivated lands. What Ibn ʿAbbās intended by that which was not prohibited is the leasing of land for gold and silver"","" and for that which involves no uncertainty (gharar). Some of the narrators from Rāfiʿ qualified the types regarding which the prohibition occurred and explained the reason for the prohibition"","" which is the fear of destruction of the crop"","" and that constitutes uncertainty in the countervalue which invalidates the contract.\n\nIf Ibn ʿAbbās intended by that which was not prohibited the leasing of land for a portion of what it produces"","" then we have narrated from those who heard his prohibition regarding it"","" and the ruling belongs to them over him. We have narrated from Zayd ibn Thābit what agrees with the narration of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj and others"","" which indicates that what he rejected was other than what they affirmed. And Allah knows best.\n\nAmong the scholars are those who interpreted the narrations of prohibition as referring to sharecropping conducted with corrupt conditions"","" such as the condition of specified irrigation channels (al-jadāwil) and the waterways (al-mādhīyānāt)"","" which are the streams—that is"","" what the landowner would stipulate upon the cultivator to plant specifically along these waterways for the owner exclusively. Similarly"","" the condition of al-quṣārah"","" which is what remains of the grain in the ears after threshing"","" also called al-qirṣī. And similarly"","" the condition of what is watered by the spring stream (mā saqā al-rabīʿ)"","" which is the small river such as a channel or a rivulet"","" the plural of which is arbiʿāʾ. They said: These and similar conditions were stipulated by the owner for himself exclusively"","" apart from the stipulation of a half"","" a quarter"","" or a third. We hold that the Prophet's (ﷺ) prohibition of sharecropping was due to these conditions"","" because they are unknown (uncertain). If the shares are known—such as a half"","" a third"","" or a quarter—and the corrupt conditions are absent"","" then the sharecropping is permissible. This was the position of Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal (may Allah have mercy on him)"","" Abū ʿUbayd"","" Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah"","" and others from the people of ḥadīth. Abū Yūsuf and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan"","" from the people of opinion (aṣḥāb al-raʾy)"","" also held this view. The narrations that have come regarding the Prophet's (ﷺ) transaction with the people of Khaybar for half of what the land produced of fruit or crop serve as evidence for them in this matter. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal declared the ḥadīth of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj weak and said: \""It has many variants\""—meaning the discrepancies in its chain and text to which we have alluded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Rāziq 14454]"""""
"11743","(11738) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Abū al-Azhar both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that he used to lease out his land. He was informed of the ḥadīth of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, so he went to him and asked him about it, and he informed him. Ibn ʿUmar said: \You know that the people of the land used to give their lands during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and the owner of the land would stipulate for himself the waterways (al-mādhīyānāt) and what is watered by the spring stream"","" and he would stipulate from the threshing floor a known quantity of straw.\"" Ibn ʿUmar used to think that the prohibition was due to what they used to stipulate. [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Rāziq 14454]"""""
"11744","(11739) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Abū ʿUbayd, Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, from Usayd ibn Ẓuhayr, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding sharecropping: \One of them used to stipulate three irrigation channels"","" the quṣārah"","" and what is watered by the spring stream"","" so the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited that.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nThe Shaykh said: Whoever holds this view claimed that the narrations in which the prohibition occurred regarding leasing for a half"","" a third"","" or a quarter was only because they would attach corrupt conditions to it. Some of the narrators abbreviated by mentioning them"","" while others mentioned them. The prohibition pertains to them and not to anything else. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11745","(11740) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Ḥakīm, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said during the illness in which he died: \May Allah fight the Jews and the Christians; they have taken the graves of their prophets as places of worship. Let there not remain two religions in the land of the Arabs.\"" When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) became caliph"","" he expelled the people of Najrān to al-Najrāniyyah"","" purchased their contracts and their wealth"","" and expelled the people of Fadak"","" Taymāʾ"","" and the people of Khaybar. He appointed Yaʿlā ibn Munyah as his agent and gave them the open land on the condition that the seed"","" the oxen"","" and the iron tools would be from ʿUmar"","" so two-thirds would be for ʿUmar and one-third for them. If it was from them"","" then half would be for ʿUmar and half for them. He gave them the date palms and the grapes on the condition that two-thirds would be for ʿUmar and one-third for them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī alluded to it in the heading of the chapter"","" and it is a mursal ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī said in the heading of the chapter: And Qays ibn Muslim narrated from Abū Jaʿfar: \""There is no household of emigrants in Madīnah except that they cultivate on the basis of a third or a quarter.\"" Al-Bukhārī said: ʿAlī"","" Saʿd ibn Mālik"","" Ibn Masʿūd"","" ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"","" al-Qāsim"","" ʿUrwah"","" the family of Abī Bakr"","" the family of ʿUmar"","" the family of ʿAlī"","" and Ibn Sīrīn all practiced sharecropping. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad said: \""I used to partner with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd in cultivation.\"""""""
"11746","(11741) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab used to say: \There is no harm in leasing land for gold and silver.\"" It had reached us that Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj used to narrate that his two uncles"","" who had witnessed Badr"","" used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the leasing of land. Because of the ḥadīth of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj"","" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to abandon the leasing of his land and would not lease it out for gold"","" silver"","" or anything else. Some people followed the fatwā of Rāfiʿ"","" while others abandoned it.\n\nAs for the transaction on the basis of a half"","" two-thirds"","" or whatever they agreed upon"","" it has reached us that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) transacted with the Jews of Khaybar when Allah granted the Muslims victory over them"","" on the basis of a half"","" and that is the most wholesome and lawful state of affairs regarding land.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Whoever holds the first view responded to this and claimed that nothing is established from the Prophet (ﷺ) in this regard"","" and there is no proof in the statement of anyone other than him. The ḥadīth of Rāfiʿ is a firmly established ḥadīth"","" and in it is evidence of his prohibition of transacting on the basis of a portion of what the land produces. However"","" he narrated it on one occasion from some of his uncles and sent it as a mursal on another. He narrated it fully on one occasion and abbreviated it on another. Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh and others followed him in his narration"","" as we have previously mentioned. The ḥadīth of the transaction for half of what Khaybar produced of fruit or crop is accepted as authoritative when the crop is among the date palms"","" and in this there is a reconciliation between the narrations that have come regarding it. And with Allah is success"","" and Allah knows best."""""
"11747","(11742) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Sharīk narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Mazzī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Sharīk narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever cultivates the land of a people without their permission"","" he has nothing of the crop"","" and his expenses shall be returned to him.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū al-Walīd. In the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Ādam"","" he said: \""He attributed it to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'He shall have his expenses"","" and he shall have nothing of the crop.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11748","(11743) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq al-ʿAṭṭār said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Ḥasan narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabīʿ, narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said the same. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"11749","(11744) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿImrān al-Qāḍī in Harāt narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim ʿAbd al-Jalīl ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Harawī narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us, Bukayr narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿm, that Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj informed him: that he had cultivated a land that he had taken from Banī So-and-so. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by him while he was watering his crop and asked: \To whom does this belong?\"" He said: \""The crop is mine"","" and it is the land of Banī So-and-so; I took it for half and for them is half.\"" He said: \""Shake the dust of it from your hands"","" return the land to its people"","" and take your expenses.\"" He said: \""So I went and informed them of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had said.\"" He said: \""So he took his expenses and returned their land to them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11750","(11745) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Khaṭmī narrated, who said: My uncle sent me, along with a young boy of his, to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab. He said: \So we said to him: 'Something has reached us from you regarding sharecropping.'\"" He said: \""Ibn ʿUmar used to see no harm in it until the ḥadīth of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj reached him. So he went to him"","" and Rāfiʿ informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Banī Ḥārithah and saw a crop in the land of Ẓuhayr"","" and he said: 'How excellent is the crop of Ẓuhayr!' They said: 'It does not belong to Ẓuhayr.' He said: 'Is it not the land of Ẓuhayr?' They said: 'Yes"","" but it is the crop of So-and-so.' He said: 'Take your crop and return to him the expenses.'\"" Rāfiʿ said: \""So we took our crop and returned to him the expenses.\"" Saʿīd said: \""Give your brother his land or lease it out for dirhams.\""\n\nThe outward meaning of these narrations indicates that the crop follows the land. The jurists of the amṣār hold that the crop follows the seed. Were these narrations to be established"","" there would be no proof for anyone in opposition to them. However"","" the first ḥadīth is narrated exclusively by Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ. Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ is considered weak by the scholars of ḥadīth"","" and Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh is a matter of disagreement regarding him. Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān used not to narrate from him and would declare his ḥadīth very weak. Moreover"","" it is mursal.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in the book al-Buwayṭī: \""The ḥadīth is discontinuous (munqaṭiʿ)"","" because ʿAṭāʾ did not meet Rāfiʿ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 3401]"""""
"11751","(11746) Abū Sa'd al-Mālīnī informed us — Abū Aḥmad, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdīy al-Ḥāfiẓ, said: I used to think that ʿAṭāʾ's narration from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj was mursal (disconnected), until it became clear to me that Abū Isḥāq's narration from ʿAṭāʾ was also mursal. Abū Aḥmad said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rafīʿ, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever plants crops in the land of a people without their permission shall have no share of the harvest"","" and the value of his expenditure shall be returned to him.\"" Yūsuf said: Other than Ḥajjāj do not say \""ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz\""; rather they say: from Abū Isḥāq"","" from ʿAṭāʾ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Abū Isḥāq used to practise tadlīs (concealing defects in the chain)"","" and the scholars of ḥadīth say: \""ʿAṭāʾ from Rāfiʿ is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\"" Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī said: \""This ḥadīth is not established among the people of knowledge of ḥadīth.\"" Abū Sulaymān said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyá narrated to me from Mūsā ibn Hārūn al-Ḥammāl that he used to reject this ḥadīth"","" declare it weak (ḍaʿīf)"","" and say: \""No one other than Sharīk narrated it"","" and no one other than Abū Isḥāq narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ"","" and ʿAṭāʾ did not hear anything from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj.\"" Abū Sulaymān said: And al-Bukhārī also declared it weak. The Shaykh said: And ʿUqbah ibn al-Aṣamm narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ"","" saying: \""Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated to us\"" — however"","" ʿUqbah is weak and cannot be used as evidence. As for the ḥadīth of Bukayr ibn ʿĀmir al-Bajalī from Ibn Abī Nuʿm from Rāfiʿ — although Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj used him as evidence in other than this ḥadīth"","" he was declared weak by Yaḥyá ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"","" Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth"","" Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"","" and Yaḥyá ibn Maʿīn.\n\nAs for the third ḥadīth"","" it is the narration of Abū Jaʿfar ʿUmayr ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī — and I have not seen al-Bukhārī or Muslim using him as evidence in any ḥadīth"","" and Allah knows best. And it has also been narrated from Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj from the Prophet ﷺ with its meaning"","" and it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)."""""
"11752","(11747) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Qatādah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no Muslim who plants a tree or sows a crop"","" and then a bird"","" a human"","" or an animal eats from it"","" except that it becomes a charity (ṣadaqah) for him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá"","" and al-Bukhārī extracted it from Qutaybah and others from Abī ʿAwānah."""""
"11753","(11748) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us — and Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us — both said: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār narrated to us — Qatādah narrated from Anas: that the Prophet ﷺ entered a date-palm grove belonging to Umm Mubashshir, a woman from the Anṣār, and said: \Who planted this — a Muslim or a disbeliever?\"" They said: \""A Muslim.\"" He said: \""No Muslim should plant a tree from which a human"","" a bird"","" or an animal eats"","" except that it becomes a charity (ṣadaqah) for him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"","" and Muslim said: \""And Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm.\"""""""
"11754","(11749) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz in Baghdad informed us — Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq narrated to us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Munādī narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no Muslim who plants a tree"","" except that it becomes a charity (ṣadaqah) for him — for what is eaten from it"","" what is stolen from it"","" what birds eat from it"","" and what wild beasts eat\"" — or he said: \""predators.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another chain from ʿAbd al-Malik with part of its meaning."""""
"11755","(11750) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us — Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Layth narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Umm Mubashshir al-Anṣāriyyah in her date-palm grove. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \Who planted this date-palm — a Muslim or a disbeliever?\"" She said: \""Nay"","" rather a Muslim.\"" He said: \""No Muslim should plant a tree or sow a crop from which a human"","" an animal"","" or anything eats"","" except that it becomes a charity (ṣadaqah) for him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth."""""
"11756","(11751) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṭṭār in Baghdad, a trustworthy shaykh, narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb al-Mawṣilī narrated to us in the year two hundred and sixty — Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from Layth, from Mujāhid, who said: \Do not say 'I planted crops (zaraʿtu)'; rather say 'I ploughed (ḥaraṯtu).' Indeed"","" Allah is the One Who causes to grow (al-Zāriʿ).\"" This is from the statement of Mujāhid. And a marfūʿ (elevated) ḥadīth has been narrated concerning it"","" though it is not strong."""""
"11757","(11752) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Khalaf ibn ʿAmr and Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham, the neighbour of ʿUbayd al-ʿIjlī, narrated to us — Muslim ibn Abī Muslim narrated to us — and Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Qutaybah Salm ibn al-Faḍl al-Adamī in Makkah narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Muslim al-Jurmī narrated to us — Makhlad ibn Ḥusayn narrated from Hishām, from Muḥammad, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \None of you should say 'I planted crops (zaraʿtu)'; rather let him say 'I ploughed (ḥaraṯtu).'\"" Muḥammad said: Abū Hurayrah said: \""Have you not heard the statement of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic: *'Do you consider what you cultivate? Is it you who cause it to grow"","" or are We the Ones Who cause it to grow?'*\"" (Qurʾān 56:63–64)"""""
"11758","(11753) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khayrūwayh informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī informed me — al-Haytham ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from his father, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that those jamājim (skulls/bones) be placed in the crops because of the evil eye. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah and said: \O company of Quraysh"","" you love livestock"","" so reduce your holdings of them"","" for you are the people with the least rainfall. And cultivate the land"","" for cultivation is blessed"","" and place abundant jamājim in it.\"" And this narration is also mursal (disconnected).\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us — Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us — Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated from ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī"","" and he mentioned it."""""
"11759","(11754) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us — Abū ʿUbayd narrated — Yazīd narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Bābā — thus Yazīd said — who said: Saʿd, meaning Ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, used to carry a miktal of ʿurrah to his land. And Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us — ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Bābā, from Saʿd, similarly, except that he said: And Saʿd said: \A miktal of ʿurrah is a miktal of wheat.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-ʿUrah is human excrement (al-ʿadhirah).\""\n\nAnd the opposite of that has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar specifically regarding al-ʿadhirah."""""
"11760","(11755) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Ibn Abī Yaḥyá narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar: that he used to stipulate to the one to whom he leased his land that he should not place ʿurrah (manure/excrement) upon it — and this was before ʿAbdullāh (ibn ʿUmar) abandoned leasing. And a weak ḥadīth has been narrated concerning it."
"11761","(11756) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, that Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl informed us, that al-Ḥajjāj ibn Ḥassān narrated from his father, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \We used to lease the land of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stipulate upon them that they would not fertilize it with human excrement.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11762","(11757) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, that my father narrated to us, that Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥuṣayn, from Asīd, who said: \I heard Ibn ʿUmar when a man came to him and said: 'I used to sweep until I married"","" freed a slave"","" and performed Ḥajj.' He asked: 'What did you used to sweep?' He said: 'Excrement.' He replied: 'You are impure"","" your freeing of the slave is impure"","" and your Ḥajj is impure. Exit from it just as you entered it.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"11763","(11758) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, that Abū Muḥammad ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Naṣr ibn ʿAlī informed us, that Abū Usāmah narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān, from Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥubshī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever cuts down a lote-tree (sidrah)"","" Allah will plunge his head into the Fire.\"" [Abū Dāwūd 5241]"""""
"11764","(11759) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, that Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated it in a manner similar to the narration of Abū Dāwūd, except that he said: from Ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥubshī, from the Prophet ﷺ. [Denounced (Munkar)]"
"11765","(11760) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣilḥī narrated from Fam al-Ṣilḥ that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Mawhab al-Ramlī narrated to us that Masʿadah ibn al-Yasaʿ narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever cuts down a lote-tree (sidrah)"","" Allah will plunge his head into the Fire.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh said: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""Thus we wrote it from the ḥadīth of Masʿadah"","" and he was not followed upon it"","" and it is an error. Rather"","" Ibn Jurayj narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"","" as his own statement (mawqūf).\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī informed us"","" ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Salm narrated to us"","" Mūsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Masrūqī narrated to us"","" Abū Usāmah narrated from Ibn Jurayj. Thus the narration of Naṣr ibn ʿAlī from Abū Usāmah through this chain becomes defective (maʿlūlah). And it is possible that Abū Usāmah narrated it both ways. [Denounced (Munkar)]"""""
"11766","(11761) And Maʿmar narrated it, as Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, that Maʿmar narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān, from a man of Thaqīf, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who raised the ḥadīth regarding the one who cuts the lote-tree, saying: \Punishment will be poured upon him"",""\"" or he said: \""His head will be plunged into the Fire.\""\n\nThe narrator from Thaqīf said: \""I asked the sons of ʿUrwah about that"","" and they informed me that ʿUrwah had cut down a lote-tree that was in a wall and made it into a gate for the wall.\""\n\nIt is likely that the man of Thaqīf was ʿAmr ibn Aws. [Weak]"""""
"11767","(11762) For Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Abū ʿUthmān, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAmr ibn Aws, from ʿUrwah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Those who cut down the lote-tree (sidrah)"","" Allah will pour them headlong into the Fire.\""\n\nAbū ʿUthmān here is Muḥammad ibn Sharīk al-Makkī"","" and this is the preserved narration from him as a mursal ḥadīth. [Weak]"""""
"11768","(11763) And al-Qāsim ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it from Wakīʿ, from Muḥammad ibn Sharīk al-ʿĀmirī, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from ʿAmr ibn Aws, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Those who cut down the lote-tree (sidrah) will be poured headlong into the Fire.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"","" al-Ḥusayn ibn Idrīs al-Anṣārī narrated to us"","" al-Qāsim ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it.\n\nAbū ʿAlī said: \""I do not think he preserved it from Wakīʿ"","" and they have spoken critically of him (i.e."","" al-Qāsim). The preserved narration is that of Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī and those who followed him in his narration from Muḥammad ibn Sharīk"","" from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from ʿAmr ibn Aws"","" from ʿUrwah: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ (said it) as a mursal ḥadīth.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""""
"11769","(11764) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Aws, who said: \I came upon an elder of Thaqīf whose crops the lote-tree had ruined. I said: 'Why do you not cut it down"","" when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Except from crops\""?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""Whoever cuts down the lote-tree except for the sake of crops"","" punishment will be poured upon him.\""' So I dislike cutting it for the sake of crops or otherwise.\""\n\nThis is another chain of narration for ʿAmr ibn Aws"","" apart from his narration from ʿUrwah"","" if Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd preserved it. [Weak]"""""
"11770","(11765) And it has been narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd, as Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Wakīʿ narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Naṣr al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, that Ṣāliḥ ibn Mismār narrated to us, that Hishām ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, that Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Go out and announce among the people"","" on behalf of Allah"","" not on behalf of His Messenger: May Allah curse the one who cuts down the lote-tree (sidrah).\""\n\nThus our shaykh stated it in *Gharāʾib al-Shuyūkh*. [Weak]"""""
"11771","(11766) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿImrān ibn Khuzaymah al-Dīnawarī, Abū Bakr, informed us; Abū ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makhzūmī, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, informed us; Hishām ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd al-Makkī narrated to me, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from ʿAlī, and he mentioned it. Abū ʿAlī said: \Thus this shaykh told us"","" and Ibn Jurayj is in its chain"","" and this is an error.\""\n\nIbrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated it from Hishām ibn Sulaymān"","" from Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd"","" and he did not mention Ibn Jurayj in its chain"","" and that is the correct version.\n\nʿAlī ibn Thābit narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd"","" from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī"","" as a mursal hadith. And ʿAlī ibn Hāshim ibn al-Burayd narrated it from Ibrāhīm al-Khūzī"","" from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Sulaymān al-Aḥwal"","" from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"","" from his father"","" from his grandfather"","" from ʿAmr ibn Aws al-Thaqafī"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" and he said: \""Except from crops.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""The hadith of Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīm is confused (muḍṭarib)"","" and Ibrāhīm is weak (ḍaʿīf).\"" The Shaykh said: \""And al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated it from ʿAmr"","" from Abū Jaʿfar.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11772","(11767) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, he said: \I heard al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrating from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from Abū Jaʿfar"","" who said: 'The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī during the illness in which he died: \""Go forth"","" O ʿAlī"","" and say on behalf of Allah"","" not on behalf of the Messenger of Allah: May Allah curse the one who cuts the sidr tree (lote tree).\""'\"" Imam Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: \""All of that is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ) and weak (ḍaʿīf)"","" except the hadith of Ibn Jurayj"","" for I do not know whether Saʿīd heard from ʿAbd Allām ibn Ḥubshiyy or not. And it is possible that he did hear it. And Allah knows best.\"" And it was narrated through another chain"","" connected (mawṣūl)"","" if it is preserved. [Weak]"""""
"11773","(11768) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Zubayr ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — I asked him — Muḥammad ibn Nūḥ al-Jundaysābūrī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Kabīr ibn Shuʿayb ibn al-Ḥabbāb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one who cuts the sidr tree — Allah will plunge his head into the Fire.'\"" [Munkar. Al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"","" 1610]"""""
"11774","(11769) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; al-Zubayr ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Mālikī in al-Shajarah narrated to us; Zayd ibn Akhzam informed us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, from his brother Mukhāriq ibn al-Ḥārith, from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \It is from Allah"","" not from His Messenger: May Allah curse the one who fells the sidr tree.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11775","(11770) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Maysarah and Ḥumayd ibn Masʿadah both narrated to us; Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us. He said: \I asked Hishām ibn ʿUrwah about cutting the sidr tree"","" while he was leaning against the wall of ʿUrwah's palace. He said: 'Do you see these doors and panels? They are from ʿUrwah's sidr trees. ʿUrwah used to cut them from his land"","" and he said: \""There is no harm in it.\""'\"" Ḥumayd added"","" and he said: \""O Iraqi"","" you have brought me an innovation (bidʿah)!\"" He said: \""I said: 'The innovation is rather from your side. I heard someone in Makkah say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who cuts the sidr tree.\""'\"" Abū Dāwūd said"","" then he narrated its meaning.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said"","" meaning the one who cuts the sidr tree in an open wasteland under which the wayfarer and animals take shade"","" wantonly and unjustly"","" without any right to do so.\n\nImam Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: \""I read in the book of Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿĀṣimī his narration from Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf"","" from Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Farajī"","" from Abū Thawr"","" that he said: 'I asked Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" about cutting the sidr tree"","" and he said: \""There is no harm in it.\"" It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \""Wash him with water and sidr (lote leaves).\""'\""\n\nI said: \""The hadith regarding the one who cuts the sidr tree is to be understood according to the interpretation given by Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" if its chain is authentic. And in it there is the discrepancy that we have mentioned above.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr that he used to cut it from his own land"","" and he was one of those who narrated the prohibition. It is as though the prohibition was specific"","" as Abū Dāwūd"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd I read in the book of Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" that Ismāʿīl ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzanī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" was asked about this"","" and he said: \""Its meaning is that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about one who aggressively cuts the sidr belonging to a people"","" or to an orphan"","" or concerning that which Allah has forbidden to be cut"","" and he overstepped by cutting it"","" and thus he deserved what was said. The question preceded the one who heard it; he heard the answer but did not hear the question. He compared it to the hadith of Usāmah ibn Zayd"","" that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Interest (ribā) is only in deferred payment (nasīʾah).' He heard the answer but did not hear the question"","" while he had said: 'Do not sell gold for gold except like for like"","" hand to hand.'\"" And al-Muzanī cited as evidence what al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah have mercy on them both"","" cited"","" from the Prophet's ﷺ permissibility of washing the deceased with sidr. Had it been forbidden"","" benefiting from it would not have been permissible. He said: \""And the leaves (waraq) of the sidr are like the branches"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ equated"","" regarding the trees of the Ḥaram whose cutting is forbidden"","" between their leaves and other parts. Since I have not seen anyone prohibit the leaves of the sidr"","" this indicates the permissibility of cutting the sidr tree.\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd"","" 5241]"""""
"11776","(11771) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Khallād informed us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd, Abū al-Ḥārith, narrated to me; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to me, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever cultivates a land that belongs to no one"","" he has the most right to it.\"" ʿUrwah said: \""ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" judged accordingly during his caliphate.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" from al-Layth. [Bukhārī"","" 2335]"""""
"11777","(11772) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Saʿīd ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever revives a dead (uncultivated) land"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for a wrongful claim (ʿirq ẓālim).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd"","" 3073]"""""
"11778","(11773) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Nāfiʿ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿUrwah, who said: \I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged that the land is the land of Allah"","" and the servants are the servants of Allah"","" and whoever revives dead (uncultivated) land has the most right to it.\"" Those who brought us this from the Prophet ﷺ are the same ones who brought us the prayers (Ṣalawāt) from him. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Abū Dāwūd"","" 3073]"""""
"11779","(11774) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever revives dead (uncultivated) land"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for a wrongful claim (ʿirq ẓālim).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""""
"11780","(11775) He said: \And Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us"","" from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"","" from his father"","" who said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever revives a dead (uncultivated) land"","" he has the most right to it"","" and there is no right for a wrongful claim (ʿirq ẓālim).\""'\"" He said: \""And Hishām said: 'The wrongful claim (al-ʿirq al-ẓālim) is that a man comes to another's property and digs in it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""""
"11781","(11776) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad — narrated to us. Al-Ḥasan narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us. Abū Shihāb narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a dead land that belonged to no one before him"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for an oppressive root (i.e."","" one who wrongfully claims ownership).\"" He (the narrator) said: The narrator of this hadith informed me that he saw two men from Banī Bayāḍah disputing before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) over a thicket in which one of them had planted palm trees. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled in favour of the owner of the land regarding his land"","" and ordered the owner of the palm trees to remove his palm trees from it. He said: \""I saw him striking the bases of the palm trees with axes"","" and they were ʿumm palm trees.\""\n\nYaḥyā ibn Ādam said: \""And al-ʿumm\"" — some of them said: \""That which is neither short nor long.\"" Some of them said: \""Al-ʿamm means ancient.\"" And some of them said: \""Long.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār that he said: \""Al-ʿumm means youthful (young trees).\"""""""
"11782","(11777) Abū Naṣr — ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah — informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāb ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣabbāghī — narrated to us. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us. Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us. Kathīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a dead land without infringing upon the right of any Muslim"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for an oppressive root.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11783","(11778) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz — narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us. Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever encloses something (with a boundary)"","" he has the greatest right to it"","" and there is no right for an oppressive root.\"" [Authentic through other chains]"""""
"11784","(11779) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us. Abū Dāwūd narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to me. ʤAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to me. Umm Janūb bint Numaylah narrated to me, from her mother, Suwaydah bint Jābir, from her mother, ʿUqaylah bint Asmar ibn Muḍarris, from her father, Asmar ibn Muḍarris, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and gave him my pledge of allegiance. He said: \Whoever reaches something before any other Muslim reaches it"","" it belongs to him.\"" He said: \""So the people went out racing one another"","" stretching out (their hands to claim land).\"" [Weak]"""""
"11785","(11780) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us. Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us. Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us. Zamaʿah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The servants are the servants of Allah"","" and the lands are the lands of Allah. So whoever revives anything of the dead land"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for an oppressive root.\"" [Denounced (Munkar)]"""""
"11786","(11781) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us. Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us. Al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Mālik informed us, from Hishām, from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a dead land"","" it belongs to him"","" and there is no right for an oppressive root.\"" [Authentic through other chains]"""""
"11787","(11782) He said: And Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from his father, that ʿUmar said: \Whoever revives a dead land"","" it belongs to him.\"""""""
"11788","(11783) Abū al-Qāsim — Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī — and ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Najjār in Kufah informed us. They both said: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us. Qabīṣah narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The dead lands belong to Allah and His Messenger"","" then to you after me. So whoever revives anything of the dead lands"","" its ownership belongs to him.\""\n\nAnd Hishām ibn Ḥujayr narrated it from Ṭāwūs"","" who said: \""Then it is for you from me.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11789","(11784) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The dead lands belong to Allah and His Messenger"","" then to you thereafter. So whoever revives anything of the dead lands"","" its ownership belongs to him.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11790","(11785) And with the same chain, he said: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us. Ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The dead lands belong to Allah and His Messenger"","" and to you thereafter. So whoever revives anything of the dead lands"","" he has the greatest right to it.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11791","(11786) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Nājiʿah informed us, Abū Kurayb informed us, Muʿāwiyah informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The dead (uninhabited) land belongs to Allah and His Messenger. So whoever revives any part of it"","" it is his.\""\n\nMuʿāwiyah ibn Hishām is alone in narrating it as marfūʿ (elevated) and mawṣūl (connected). [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""""
"11792","(11787) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik narrating, he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called the Anṣār to grant them land in al-Baḥrayn. They said: 'No"","" unless you grant our brothers from the Muhājirūn the same as you grant us.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'You will"","" after me"","" see preferential treatment (given to others over you). So be patient until you meet me.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī"","" 3794]"""""
"11793","(11788) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, who said: I heard ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil al-Ḥaḍramī narrating from his father: \The Prophet (ﷺ) granted him a piece of land — I do not know him (the narrator) except that he said: in Ḥaḍramawt.\"" [Al-Ṭayālisī"","" 1110]"""""
"11794","(11789) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Ḥajjāj al-Aʿwar informed us, Shuʿbah informed me, from Simāk, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil, from his father: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted him a piece of land. He said: He sent Muʿāwiyah with me to give it to me"","" or he said: to mark it out for me. Muʿāwiyah said to me: 'Let me ride behind you.' I said: 'You are not one to ride behind kings.' He said: 'Give me your sandals.' I said: 'Walk in the shade of the she-camel.' He said: When Muʿāwiyah became caliph"","" I went to him and he seated me with him on the couch. He said: Then he reminded me of the ḥadīth.\"" Simāk said: Wāʾil said: \""I wished I had carried him before me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad"","" 26697]"""""
"11795","(11790) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿd al-Bazzāz al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdah both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us, Ḥammād ibn Khālid, who is al-Khayyāṭ, narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted al-Zubayr the distance his horse could cover at a gallop. He set the horse running until it stopped"","" then he threw his whip. He (ﷺ) said: 'Give him (the land) as far as the whip reached.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11796","(11791) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muʿāwiyah Abū Khālid al-Qurashī informed us, Muḥriz ibn Wazar narrated from his father Wazar, who narrated from his father ʿImrān, who narrated from his father Shuʿayb, who narrated from his father ʿĀṣim, who narrated from his father Ḥuṣayni ibn Mushammis, who informed him: \He came as a delegation to the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" pledged the pledge of Islam"","" and brought his wealth as charity. The Prophet (ﷺ) granted him several water sources and named them — except that our shaykh did not accurately retain the names of those places.\"" He said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) stipulated for Ibn Mushammis regarding what he granted him that its water should not be made freely available (for others)"","" its pasture should not be cut down"","" and its trees should not be felled.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11797","(11792) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz and Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father: \Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) granted al-Zubayr the land between al-Jurf and Qanāh.\""\n\nYaḥyā said"","" and al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ said: I heard Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad say: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted ʿAlī the land between Qays and al-Shajarah.\"" He said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan say: \""Indeed"","" ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" and he granted him Yanbūʿ.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11798","(11793) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Ḥasan informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Thaqafī, who said: \There was a man in Baṣrah called Nāfiʿ Abū ʿAbd Allāh. He came to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'There is a piece of land in Baṣrah that is not land of kharāj and does not harm any of the Muslims.' Abū Mūsā had written to him (ʿUmar) informing him of that. So ʿUmar wrote to Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with them both): 'If it does not harm any of the Muslims and is not land of kharāj"","" then grant it to him.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11799","(11794) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Ḥasan informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from ʿAwf al-Aʿrābī, who said: \I read the letter of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) to Abū Mūsā: 'Abū ʿAbd Allāh has asked me for a piece of land on the bank of the Tigris where his horses graze. If it is not land of jizyah and the water of jizyah does not flow to it"","" then grant it to him.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11800","(11795) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū ʿAwanah informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir narrated from Mūsā ibn Ṭalḥah: \ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) granted land to five Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): al-Zubayr"","" Saʿd ibn Mālik"","" Ibn Masʿūd"","" Khabbāb"","" and Usāmah ibn Zayd. I saw the two neighbors — Saʿd and Ibn Masʿūd — leasing out their lands for one-third (of the produce).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11801","(11796) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Shahīd informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Yūnus informed us: Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us — he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the Anṣār so that he might grant them a writ concerning al-Baḥrayn. They said: No, by Allah, unless you write something similar for our brothers from Quraysh. He said to them: That is what Allah wills. They all kept saying that. He then said: Indeed, you will see after me a preference [given to others over you], so be patient until you meet me.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Yūnus, and some of them narrated it from Yaḥyā, and he said in the hadith: He granted the Anṣār al-Baḥrayn and wished to write a document for them regarding it. [Bukhārī 2377]"
"11802","(11797) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū Uways informed us: Kathīr ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf narrated to me from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muzanī the mines of al-Qabaliyyah — its upland and its lowland — and whatever land was suitable for cultivation from Qadas, and he did not give him the right of any Muslim. The Prophet ﷺ wrote for him: \In the name of Allah"","" the Most Merciful"","" the Most Compassionate. This is what Muḥammad"","" the Messenger of Allah"","" gave to Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith: he gave him the mines of al-Qabaliyyah — its upland and its lowland — and whatever land was suitable for cultivation from Qadas"","" and he did not give him the right of any Muslim.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11803","(11798) And Muḥammad informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū Uways narrated to me from Thawr ibn Zayd, the freedman of Banī al-Dīl ibn Bakr ibn Kinānah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar narration. [Weak]"
"11804","(11799) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdillāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Sulaymān informed us: ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Muqaddam informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed me from his father, who said: I entered upon Muʿāwiyah, and he said to me: What happened to the sword? I said: It is with me. He said: By Allah, I fashioned it with my own hand. Abū Bakr granted al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with them both — a piece of land, and I was the one writing it down. Then ʿUmar came, and Abū Bakr took the document and placed it inside the bedding. ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — entered and said: It seems you had some matter [to attend to]. Abū Bakr — may Allah be pleased with him — said: Yes. He then went out, and Abū Bakr brought out the document, and I completed it. [Weak]"
"11805","(11800) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓafar ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah informed us: al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn informed us: Fiṭr ibn Khalīfah, the freedman of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, informed me from his father, that he heard ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth say: My father took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was a young boy, and he invoked blessing upon me, wiped my head, and drew for me a bow-shaped house in Madīnah, and then said: Shall I increase it for you?\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Khaythamah in al-Tārīkh 3624]"
"11806","(11801) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿdah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah, he granted the people houses. A clan from Banū Zuhrah, known as Banū ʿAbd ibn Zuhrah, said to him: Remove Ibn Umm ʿAbd from our midst. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Then for what purpose did Allah send me? Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not sanctify a nation in which the right of the weak among them is not taken [and restored to them]. [Weak. Al-Umm 4/48]"
"11807","(11802) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from Hishām from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted al-Zubayr a piece of land, and that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — granted al-ʿAqīq entirely, and he said: Where are those who seek grants?\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy on him — said: Al-ʿAqīq is near Madīnah. [Weak. Al-Umm 4/48]"
"11808","(11803) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Hishām informed us from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted al-Zubayr, and that Abū Bakr granted, and that ʿUmar granted the people al-ʿAqīq. [Weak]"
"11809","(11804) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed me: ʿAbdillāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me: My father informed me: Abū Usāmah informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed me: My father informed me from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr — may Allah be pleased with them both — who said: I used to carry date-stones from the land of al-Zubayr, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had granted him, on my head, and it was at a distance of two farsakhs from me. Both [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Abū Usāmah. [Bukhārī 3151, Muslim 2182]"
"11810","(11805) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibn Milḥān and ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk both said: Yaḥyā informed us: al-Layth informed us from Yūnus from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah from Ibn ʿAbbās from al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There is no reserved pasture (ḥimā) except for Allah and His Messenger. He said: And it reached us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reserved al-Naqīʿ as a pasture, and that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb reserved al-Sharaf and al-Rabadhah.\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd. It was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, thus. [Bukhārī 2370]"
"11811","(11806) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Ibn ʿAbbās that al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \There is no reserved pasture (ḥimā) except for Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nAl-Zuhrī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb had a reserved pasture — it has reached me that he reserved it for the camels of ṣadaqah (charity).\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 19750]"""""
"11812","(11807) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAwan — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Māhān al-Kharrāz — informed us in Makkah: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās from al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jathāmah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reserved al-Naqīʿ and said: \There is no reserved pasture (ḥimā) except for Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: This is an error.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Because his statement \""he reserved al-Naqīʿ\"" is from the statement of al-Zuhrī.\n\nAnd similarly"","" Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith. [Authenticated]"""""
"11813","(11808) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʴmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (ﷺ) reserved al-Naqīʿ for the horses of the Muslims to graze therein. [Weak]"
"11814","(11809) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl — informed us: Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed a freed slave of his named Hunayy over the reserved pasture (ḥimā) and said to him: \O Hunayy"","" restrain your hand from the Muslims"","" and beware of the supplication of the oppressed"","" for the supplication of the oppressed is answered. And admit the owner of al-Ṣuraymah and al-Ghunaymah (i.e."","" the owner of a small flock of sheep and goats)"","" but beware of the livestock of Ibn ʿAffān and Ibn ʿAwf"","" for if their livestock perish"","" they will return to their palm groves and crops. But the owner of al-Ṣuraymah and al-Ghunaymah — if his livestock perish"","" he will come to me with his children and say: 'O Commander of the Faithful! O Commander of the Faithful! Shall I leave them? I have no one but you.' For water and grass are easier upon you than gold and silver. By Allah"","" they think I have wronged them — these are their lands; they fought for them in the Jāhiliyyah and accepted Islam while upon them. By the One in whose Hand is my soul"","" were it not for the wealth I carry upon it in the cause of Allah"","" I would not have reserved even a hand-span of their land for the people.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways from Mālik. [Bukhārī"","" 3059]"""""
"11815","(11810) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abū Naḍrah narrated from Abū Saʿīd, the freed slave of Abī Usayd al-Anṣārī, that he heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \The delegation of the people of Egypt had arrived"","" so he went out to meet them. When they heard of his coming"","" they came toward him"","" and he disliked that they should come to him in Madīnah. So they came to him and said to him: 'Bring the Muṣḥaf and open the seventh (sūrah).' They used to call Sūrah Yūnus 'the seventh.' So he recited it until he reached this verse: {Say: 'Tell me what provision Allah has sent down for you"","" and you have made of it lawful and unlawful.' Say: 'Has Allah permitted you"","" or do you invent a lie against Allah?'} [Yūnus: 59] They said to him: 'Stop. Tell me about what you have reserved as a pasture (ḥimā) — has Allah permitted you"","" or are you inventing a lie against Allah?' He said: 'Continue. It was revealed concerning such-and-such.' As for the pasture"","" ʿUmar had reserved the pasture before me for the camels of ṣadaqah. When I assumed office"","" the camels of ṣadaqah increased"","" so I increased the pasture in proportion to the increase in charity.\"" [Authenticated. Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 37690]"""""
"11816","(11811) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū Muḥammad — Dalaj ibn Aḥmad ibn Dalaj — informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Yaʿfūr narrated from his father that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \I purchased camels and sent them to the reserved pasture (ḥimā). When they became fat"","" I brought them.\"" He said: \""Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the market and saw fat camels and said: 'To whom do these camels belong?' It was said: 'To ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar.' He began saying: 'O ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"","" bakh bakh! Son of the Commander of the Faithful!'\"" He said: \""So I came running to him and said: 'What is the matter"","" O Commander of the Faithful?' He said: 'What are these camels?' I said: 'Lean camels which I purchased and sent to the reserved pasture"","" seeking what the Muslims seek.' He said: 'Graze the camels of the son of the Commander of the Faithful! Water the camels of the son of the Commander of the Faithful! O ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"","" go forth with your principal capital and place the remainder in the Bayt al-Māl of the Muslims.'\"" [Weak]\n\n(Q) This narration indicates that other than the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" no one has the right to reserve a pasture for himself. And in it and in what precedes it is evidence that the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ): \""There is no reserved pasture except for Allah and His Messenger\"" — he thereby meant a pasture similar to that which His Messenger reserved for the welfare of the Muslims. And Allah knows best."""""
"11817","(11812) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Rāzī narrated to us: Abū Zurʿah al-Rāzī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: \Whoever cultivates a land that belongs to no one"","" he has the most right to it.\"" ʿUrwah said: \""ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb judged according to this during his caliphate.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Authenticated]"""""
"11818","(11813) Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī — informed us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us: Kathīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf narrated from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives dead (uncultivated) land has the most right to it"","" and there is no right for a wrongful claim (ʿirq ẓālim).\"" [Weak]"""""
"11819","(11814) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Rāfiʿ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever revives a dead (barren) land shall have reward therein"","" and whatever the wild creatures (ʿāfiyah) eat from it shall be counted as charity on his behalf.\"" [Authenticated]"""""
"11820","(11815) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned it — adding: \…from it shall be charity on his behalf.\"" [Authenticated]"""""
"11821","(11816) And it was narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hisham, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir — Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us — Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us — Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated it, except that he said: \And it is for him.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11822","(11817) And Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghayyath narrated to us — Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us — from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet ﷺ said — he mentioned it with a meaning similar to the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah from Hisham — adding, meaning: \birds and predatory animals.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11823","(11818) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Hisham narrated, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever encloses a wall around a piece of land"","" it is for him.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Al-Tayalisi 948]"""""
"11824","(11819) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi informed us — 'Ali ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahim narrated, from 'Abbad ibn Mansur al-Naji, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, regarding the tracts of land: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whatever you have enclosed and marked"","" it is for you; and whatever has not been enclosed"","" it is for Allah and His Messenger.\"" [Da'if. Ibn 'Adi included it in al-Kamil 1167]"""""
"11825","(11820) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Malik narrated, from Ibn Shihab — (H) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas, he is al-Asamm, narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah, from his father, who said: The people used to mark out land during the era of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: \Whoever revives a dead land"","" it is for him\"" — Malik added: \""a dead (mawat) land.\"" Yahya said: \""It is as though he did not make it permissible for him merely by marking it out until he actually revives it.\"" [Ibn Abi Shaybah 11379]"""""
"11826","(11821) And Abu Sa'id narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us — al-Hasan narrated — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb: that 'Umar set the period of marking (al-tahjir) at three years. If he abandons it until three years pass and another person revives it, then that person has a greater right to it. [Da'if]"
"11827","(11822) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas, he is al-Asamm, informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman said: al-Shafi'i said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasan ibn al-Qasim al-Azraqi informed us — from his father — from 'Alqamah ibn Nadlah: that Abu Sufyan ibn Harb stood in the courtyard of his house, struck the ground with his foot, and said: \The hump of the land — indeed the land has a hump!\"" Ibn Farqad al-Aslami claimed that he did not know his right from his right — \""For me is the whiteness of al-Marwah and for him is its darkness"","" and for me is what is between such-and-such.\"" This reached 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and he said: \""There is no right for anyone except what his walls have enclosed. Indeed"","" the revival of dead land is that which is cultivated"","" or dug"","" or enclosed with walls.\"" The Shaykh said: His words \""Indeed"","" the revival of dead land\"" up to the end — I think they are from the words of al-Shafi'i"","" for al-Humaydi narrated them from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan without this addition. And Allah knows best. [Da'if. Imam al-Shafi'i 4/46]"""""
"11828","(11823) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Hakim ibn Ruzayq, who said: I read the letter of 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz addressed to my father: \Grant them what they have revived with a building or cultivation.\"" [Sahih. Al-Kharaj 292]"""""
"11829","(11824) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us — al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us — Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took charity from the old mountain mines, and that he granted Bilal ibn al-Harith the 'Aqiq in its entirety. When 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, became caliph, he said to Bilal: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant it to you so that you might withhold it from the people; he granted it only so that you would work it.\"" So 'Umar ibn al-Khattab granted the 'Aqiq to the people. [Da'if]"""""
"11830","(11825) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us — Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us — Yunus narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, who said: Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a grant of land, so he granted him a long, broad tract of land. When 'Umar became caliph, he said to him: \O Bilal"","" you asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a long"","" broad tract of land and he granted it to you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not withhold anything that was asked of him"","" and you do not have the capacity to manage what is in your possession.\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then look at what you are able to manage of it and retain it"","" and what you cannot manage"","" hand it over to us so that we may divide it among the Muslims.\"" He said: \""No"","" by Allah"","" I will not do that — anything the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has granted me.\"" 'Umar said: \""By Allah"","" you must do it!\"" So he took from him what he was unable to develop and divided it among the Muslims. [Da'if]"""""
"11831","(11826) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from a man of the people of Madīnah, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) granted the ʿAqīq to a single man. Then"","" during the time of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" it became too much for him"","" so he gave part of it to him and distributed the rest among the people.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11832","(11827) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Mahrī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Sabrah ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Juhanī narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that: \The Prophet (ﷺ) encamped at the site of the mosque beneath a dom tree and remained there for three days. Then he departed for Tabūk. The people of Juḥaynah caught up with him at al-Rakhiyyah"","" and he said to them: 'Who are the people of Dhī al-Marwah?' They said: 'Banū Rifāʿah of Juḥaynah.' He said: 'I have granted it to Banū Rifāʿah.' So they divided it among themselves; some of them sold their share and some retained it and worked it. Then I asked my father"","" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"","" about this hadith"","" and he narrated part of me but did not narrate all of it.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11833","(11828) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Nuʿaym, meaning Ibn Ḥammād, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Qays al-Maʾribī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and Muḥammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-ʿAsqalānī — the meaning is one and the same — both said: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Qays al-Maʾribī narrated to them, saying: My father narrated to me, from Thumāmah ibn Sharāḥīl, from Sumayy ibn Qays, from Shumayr — Ibn al-Mutawakkil said: Ibn ʿAbd al-Madan — from Abyaḍ ibn Ḥammāl, that: \He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) as a delegate and asked him for the salt mine.\"" Ibn al-Mutawakkil said: \""The one at Maʾrib.\"" So he granted it to him. When he turned to leave"","" a man from the council said: 'Do you know what you have granted him? You have granted him a perpetual water source.' So he took it back from him.\"" He said: \""And I asked him about what is to be protected of the arāk trees.\"" He said: \""That which the hooves do not reach.\"" Ibn al-Mutawakkil said: \""The hooves of camels.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11834","(11829) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Ibn Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from Yaḥyā ibn Qays al-Maʾribī, from a man, from Abyaḍ ibn Ḥammāl, that: \He asked the Prophet (ﷺ) for the salt mine at Maʾrib"","" and he intended to grant it to him"","" but a man said: 'It is like a perpetual water source.' So he refused to grant it to him.\""\n\nAl-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-māʾ al-ʿidd is the perpetual water that does not cease"","" such as the water of a spring or the water of a well.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11835","(11830) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Kahmas narrated from Sayyār ibn Manẓūr, a man from Banī Fazārah, from his father, from a woman called Buhaysah, from her father, who said: \My father sought permission from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and he entered and pressed himself between him and his shirt"","" kissing and embracing him. Then he said: 'O Prophet of Allah"","" what is it that it is not permissible to withhold?' He said: 'Water.' He said: 'O Prophet of Allah"","" what is it that it is not permissible to withhold?' He said: 'Salt.' He said: 'O Prophet of Allah"","" what is it that it is not permissible to withhold?' He said: 'That you do good is better for you.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"11836","(11831) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar and Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl — the meaning is one and the same — both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥassān al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us, saying: My two grandmothers, Ṣafiyyah and Duḥaybah, daughters of ʿUlaybah — and they were the foster-mothers of Qaylah bint Makhramah, and the mother of their father — informed me, saying: \We came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" She said: \""My companion — meaning Ḥurayth ibn Ḥassān"","" the delegate of Banī Bakr ibn Wāʾil — came"","" and he gave him the pledge of Islam for him and his people. Then he said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" write between us and Banī Tamīm regarding al-Dahnāʾ"","" that none of them cross over to us except a traveller or a resident.' He said: 'Write it for him"","" boy — al-Dahnāʾ.' When I saw that he had commanded it to be written for him"","" it stirred within me"","" for it was my homeland and my home. So I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" he did not ask you for an equal portion of the land when he asked you; this al-Dahnāʾ"","" in your view"","" is the tethering place of the camel and the pasture of the sheep"","" and the women of Banī Tamīm and their children are behind that.' He said: 'Hold back"","" boy. The poor woman has spoken the truth. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. Water and trees suffice them both"","" and they cooperate against the devils (al-futtān).'\"" [Weak]"""""
"11837","(11832) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us; Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān narrated from Ḥibbān ibn Zayd al-Sharʿabī, from a man of Qurayn.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū Dāwūd said: And Musaddad narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; Abū Khidāsh narrated to us — and this is the wording of Musaddad — that he heard a man of the Muhājirūn, from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), say: \I fought alongside the Prophet (ﷺ) three times"","" and I heard him say: 'The Muslims are partners in three things: water"","" pasture"","" and fire.'\"" Abū Khidāsh is Ḥibbān ibn Zayd al-Sharʿabī.\n\nAnd likewise Thawr ibn Yazīd and Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated it from Ḥarīz. And Yazīd ibn Hārūn said: Ḥabbān ibn Zayd (with a fatḥah on the Ḥāʾ). [Authentic]"""""
"11838","(11833) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated from Thawr ibn Yazīd, who raised it to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The Muslims are partners in pasture"","" water"","" and fire.\"" Al-Thawrī sent it on from Thawr"","" but Thawr only took it from Ḥarīz. [Authentic]"""""
"11839","(11834) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ al-Bazzārī narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Ghāzī narrated to us; Abū Ḥafṣ ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Yaḥyā, meaning al-Qaṭṭān, narrated to us; Thawr narrated from Ḥarīz, from Abī Khidāsh, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \I fought alongside the Prophet (ﷺ) on three expeditions"","" and I heard him say: 'The Muslims are partners in three things: water"","" pasture"","" and fire.'\""\n\nHe said: \""And I heard Abū Ḥafṣ say: 'I asked Muʿādh about it"","" and he narrated to me"","" saying: Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; Ḥibbān ibn Zayd al-Sharʿabī narrated to us"","" from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" who said: \""I fought alongside the Prophet (ﷺ).\""'\"" Abū Ḥafṣ said: \""Then Yazīd ibn Hārūn came to us and narrated it to us — I think from Ḥarīz — who said: Ḥabbān ibn Zayd al-Sharʿabī narrated to us.\"" Yazīd ibn Hārūn alone said Ḥabbān (with a fatḥah). [Authentic]"""""
"11840","(11835) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A man shall not remove another man from his sitting place and then sit in it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Bukhārī 6269"","" Muslim 2177]"""""
"11841","(11836) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Isfahani — informed us; Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan — informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Bundar ibn Ibrahim al-Dabbi — narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah — narrated to us; al-Nu'man ibn 'Abd al-Salam — narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak; Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham — narrated to me; al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah al-Mujashi'i — narrated to me: that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went out to the market and found that shops had been built in the market. He ordered that they be demolished, and so they were levelled. He passed by the houses of Banu al-Bakka' and said: \These are from the market of the Muslims.\"" He ordered them to relocate"","" and they were demolished. 'Ali said: \""Whoever is the first to occupy a place in the market"","" he has the most right to it.\"" The narrator said: \""I have seen us selling to a man in one place today"","" and tomorrow he would be in another place.\"" [Weak. Jidd 1]"""""
"11842","(11837) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari — informed us; my grandfather Yahya ibn Mansur — narrated to us; Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Salamat ibn al-Jarud — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan al-Jarjara'i — informed us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu Ya'fur, who said: \In the time of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah"","" whoever was the first to occupy a place in the market had the most right to it until nightfall.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"11843","(11838) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Warraq — narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman — narrated to us; Sharik, from Sa'd al-Katib, from Bilal al-'Absi, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \There is no reserved pasture (himā) except in three cases: the water of a well"","" the tethering place of a horse"","" and the gathering place of a people.\"" This is a mursal hadith. [Weak]"""""
"11844","(11839) Abu Tahir al-Faqih — informed us; Hajib ibn Ahmad al-Tusi — narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Munib — narrated to us; Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi — informed us; Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \If a man rises from his seat and then returns to it"","" he has the most right to it.\"" A man stood up from his seat"","" so I sat in it. When he returned"","" Abu Salih made me get up from it. [Sahih. Narrated by Ma'mar ibn Rashid in al-Jami' 19792]"""""
"11845","(11840) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr — narrated to us; Abu Dawud — narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Razi — narrated to us; Mubashshir al-Halabi, from Tamam ibn Najih, from Abu 'Abbs al-Iyadi, who said: \I used to visit Abu al-Darda'"","" may Allah be pleased with him.\"" Abu al-Darda' said: \""The Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" when he would sit and we would sit around him"","" and then he would stand and intend to return"","" he would place his shoes or some of his belongings there"","" so his Companions would understand that and remain seated.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 4658]"""""
"11846","(11841) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah — narrated to us; Abu Dawud — narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah, from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from more than one person: that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, granted Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, which are in the direction of al-Fur'. Those mines are such that nothing is taken from them except the zakah, to this day. [Weak. Abu Dawud 4854]"
"11847","(11842) And Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar — narrated to us; Isma'il al-Qadi — narrated to us; Ibn Abi Uways — narrated to me; my father — narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Zayd al-Dili and from his maternal uncle Musa ibn Maysarah, the freedman of Banu al-Dil, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: \The Prophet"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" granted Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of al-Qabaliyyah — their elevated parts and their low-lying parts — and wherever cultivation is suitable.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11848","(11843) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq — informed us; Muhammad ibn Ghalib — narrated to us; 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Maslamah, from Malik ibn Anas.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajanī — informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us; Malik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu Nasr — Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Faqih — narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Nasr and Ja'far ibn Muhammad — both said: narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya — said: I read to Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The surplus water should not be withheld so that thereby the pasture (kalā') may be prevented.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf"","" from Malik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Bukhari 2353"","" Muslim 1566]"""""
"11849","(11844) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar — narrated to us; 'Ubayd ibn Sharik — narrated to us; Yahya ibn Bukayr — narrated to me; al-Layth — narrated to us; Yunus.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Nasr — Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Faqih — both said: narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il — narrated to us; Abu al-Tahir — informed us; Ibn Wahb — informed me; Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \The surplus water should not be withheld so that thereby the pasture (kalā') may be prevented.\"" In the narration of al-Layth"","" he said: narrated to me Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" said: \""Do not withhold surplus water so that you thereby withhold the pasture (kalā').\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Tahir"","" and al-Bukhari narrated it from Yahya ibn Bukayr"","" from al-Layth"","" from 'Uqayl"","" from al-Zuhri. [Bukhari 2353"","" Muslim 1566]"""""
"11850","(11845) Abu al-Hasan — Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi — informed us; Abu Nasr — Muhammad ibn Hamdawayh ibn Sahl al-Marwazi — narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Adam al-Marwazi — narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who I think narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \There are three persons whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection"","" nor will He look at them"","" and for them is a painful punishment: a man who swore a false oath to seize the property of a Muslim; a man who swore an oath after the 'Asr prayer that he was given more for his merchandise than he was actually given"","" while he is lying; and a man who withheld surplus water. For Allah"","" Glorified and Exalted is He"","" will say: 'Today I will withhold My bounty from you"","" just as you withheld the bounty of that which your hands did not produce.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad"","" and Muslim narrated it from 'Amr al-Naqid"","" both from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah. [Bukhari 2369"","" Muslim 108]"""""
"11851","(11846) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik narrated from Abū al-Rijāl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥārithah, from his mother ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The water of a well should not be withheld.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain. Mālik 1428]"""""
"11852","(11847) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Sufyān narrated; Abū al-Rijāl said: \I heard my mother say: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the withholding of the water of a well.'\"" This is the preserved version"","" and it is mursal. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain]"""""
"11853","(11848) And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us; Abū al-Azhar from his original copy informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Abū al-Rijāl, from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the withholding of the water of a well. Thus he narrated it as mawṣūl (connected), whereas it is known as mawṣūl only from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Rijāl from his father. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain. Aḥmad 6/112]"
"11854","(11849) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Rijāl said: \I heard my father narrate from his mother ʿAmrah"","" from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" who said: 'The water of a well should not be withheld"","" and it is al-rahw (a shared resource).'\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""I heard my father say: 'Al-rahw is that a well belongs to partners in water"","" and a man has surplus water in it; he should not prevent his companion from it.'\"" Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār also narrated it from Abū al-Rijāl as mawṣūl"","" and Ḥārithah ibn Muḥammad also narrated it from ʿAmrah as mawṣūl"","" except that Ḥārithah is weak. [Ṣaḥīgh]"""""
"11855","(11850) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Dāwūd al-Munādī informed us; Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd informed us; Ḥārithah ibn Muḥammad narrated from ʿAmrah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Surplus water should not be withheld"","" nor the water of a well.'\"" This Ḥārithah is weak. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain]"""""
"11856","(11851) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd and Hishām ibn Ḥassān, from al-Ḥasan, that a man came to the people of a water source and asked them for water, but they did not give him any until he died of thirst. So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed the blood-money (diyah) upon them. [Weak]"
"11857","(11852) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim informed us; Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \That one of you should take his rope"","" go to the mountain"","" bring a bundle of firewood on his back"","" sell it"","" and thereby become self-sufficient through its price is better for him than asking people—they may give him or refuse him.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā from Wakīʿ. And in the ḥadīth of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \""I arranged with a man that he would travel with me so that we could bring idhkhir (a type of fragrant grass) which I would sell to the goldsmiths and thereby use the proceeds for the feast of my wedding.\"" [Bukhārī 1471]"""""
"11858","(11853) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī; ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn informed me that Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī informed him that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \I had a she-camel from my share of the spoils of war on the day of Badr"","" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me a she-camel from the khums on that day. When I intended to build a home with Fāṭimah"","" the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" I arranged with a goldsmith from Banī Qaynuqāʾ that he would travel with me so that we could bring idhkhir"","" which I intended to sell to the goldsmiths and thereby use the proceeds for the feast of my wedding.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān. [Bukhārī 2375"","" Muslim 1979]"""""
"11859","(11854) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us; Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī informed us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd said: I heard Ibn Shihāb narrate from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that a man from the Anṣār disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding the water channels of al-Ḥarrah by which they irrigated their date palms. The Anṣārī said: \Release the water and let it flow!\"" But al-Zubayr refused. So they both brought their dispute before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Irrigate"","" O Zubayr"","" then release the water to your neighbor.\"" The Anṣārī became angry and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" is it because he is the son of your paternal aunt?\"" The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed"","" and then He said: \""Irrigate"","" O Zubayr"","" then retain the water until it reaches the wall (al-jadr).\"" Al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By Allah"","" I reckon that this verse was revealed concerning that: {But no"","" by your Lord"","" they will not truly believe until they make you judge in all disputes between them} until His words: {and submit with full submission}.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ"","" all from al-Layth. [Bukhārī 2360"","" Muslim 2357]"""""
"11860","(11855) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: \Al-Zubayr disputed with a man from the Anṣār regarding the water channels of al-Ḥarrah. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Irrigate"","" O Zubayr"","" then release the water to your neighbor.' The Anṣārī said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" is it because he is the son of your paternal aunt?' The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) changed"","" and then He said: 'Irrigate"","" O Zubayr"","" then retain the water until it reaches the wall (al-jadr)"","" then release the water to your neighbor.'\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ensured al-Zubayr received his full right in the explicit judgment when the Anṣārī provoked him"","" whereas before that He had indicated to them both a matter in which there was flexibility for them.\"" Al-Zubayr said: \""I do not think this verse was revealed except concerning that: {But no"","" by your Lord"","" they will not truly believe until they make you judge in all disputes between them}.\"" He said: \""I heard someone other than al-Zuhrī say: 'The statement of the Prophet (ﷺ)—\""then retain the water until it reaches the wall\""—was examined"","" and it was determined to mean up to the ankles (al-kaʿbayn).'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān from Ibn al-Mubārak in abridged form. [Bukhārī 2361"","" Muslim 2357]"""""
"11861","(11856) And he narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, in its entirety, and at the end of it: Ibn Shahab said: \The Ansar and the people estimated what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Irrigate"","" then hold back the water until it reaches the wall.' That was up to the two ankles.\"" Abu al-'Abbas al-Adib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Hajjaj narrated from Ibn Jurayj"","" from Ibn Shahab"","" and he mentioned it. And Ibn Shahab said: \""Ikhadh (a furrow) in the rocky ground holds back the water.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11862","(11857) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated from al-Walid ibn Kathir from Abu Malik ibn Tha'labah from his father Tha'labah ibn Abi Malik, that he heard their elders mentioning that a man from Quraysh who had a share in Banu Qurayzah came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a dispute regarding the watercourse of Mahzur, whose water they divided among themselves. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged between them that the water should reach up to the ankles, and the one above should not withhold it from the one below. [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Abu Dawud 3639]"
"11863","(11858) Abu al-Hasan al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us; al-Mughirah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me; my father 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged regarding the watercourse of Mahzur that the water should be held until it reaches the ankles, then the one above should release it to the one below. [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Abu Dawud 3639]"
"11864","(11859) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah ibn Abi 'Ayyash al-Asadi narrated to me; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: \Among the judgments of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was that he ruled regarding the irrigation channel of palm trees from the watercourse that the highest should irrigate before the lowest"","" and the water should be retained in it up to the ankles"","" then the water should be released to the one below adjacent to it"","" and so on until all the orchards are watered.\""\n\nIshaq ibn Yahya's narration from 'Ubadah is mursal. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"11865","(11860) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated: I heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Khurrit narrating from 'Ikrimah, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled that a neighbour may place his rafters or his timber upon the wall of his neighbour"","" whether he consents or refuses.\"" And he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rule that if people dispute over their roads"","" the width should be set at seven cubits.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il. [Bukhari 2473"","" Muslim 1613]"""""
"11866","(11861) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us; 'Imran ibn Musa narrated to us; Abu Kamil narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us; Khalid narrated from Yusuf ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \If you differ over a road"","" let its width be seven cubits.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Kamil. And it was also narrated by Bishr ibn Ka'b from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Sahih]"""""
"11867","(11862) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us; al-Minhal ibn Khalifah Abu Qudamah narrated from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If you are uncertain about a road"","" make it seven cubits"","" wherein two laden camels may pass each other.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Without his words \""wherein two laden camels may pass each other\""]"""""
"11868","(11863) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to me; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: \Among the judgments of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding an open space (rahbah) that lies between roads"","" when its inhabitants wish to build upon it"","" he ruled that a road of seven cubits should be left from it.\"" He said: \""That road was called al-Mayta'.\"" [Da'if. Ahmad 22272]"""""
"11869","(11864) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Bazzaz in Baghdad informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fakihi narrated to us; Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masrrah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated from 'Amr ibn Yahya, from his father — 'Abd al-'Aziz said: \I do not know except that it was from Abu Sa'id\"" — who said: \""Two men disputed over a palm tree. The Prophet (ﷺ) cut a palm frond from its fronds and measured it"","" and found it to be five cubits"","" and he made that its harim (boundary).\""\n\nYahya ibn Muhammad said: \""And Ibn Abi Tuwalah informed me that he said: 'He found it to be seven cubits.'\"" [Hasan. al-Tabrani in al-Awsat 1898]"""""
"11870","(11865) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us; Ibn Kasib narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated from Abu Tuwalah 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar and 'Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and he mentioned it.\n\nIn the hadith of 'Amr, \he found it to be five cubits"",""\"" and Abu Tuwalah said: \""Seven cubits.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"11871","(11866) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah narrated to me from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmiṭ (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was that he ruled regarding one palm tree, two palm trees, and three palm trees belonging to a man among palm trees, and they differed concerning the rights thereof. He ruled that for each of those palm trees, the extent of its trunk's reach from the ground belonged to those [owners]. [Weak]\n\nAnd in what Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl with his chain from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled regarding the ḥarīm (surrounding precinct) of the palm grove as the length of its trunk."
"11872","(11867) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Hushaym narrated from ʿAwf al-Aʿrābī from a man from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The ḥarīm of a well is forty cubits from all its sides"","" for the watering places of camels and sheep"","" and the wayfarer has the first right to drink. And the surplus water shall not be withheld so as to prevent thereby the grazing of livestock.\""\n\nAnd Ibn al-Mubārak narrated it from ʿAwf"","" who said: \""It reached me from Abū Hurayrah"","" and he mentioned it as his own statement.\"" [Weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it in al-ʿIlal"","" 1848.]"""""
"11873","(11868) And we recorded it from the ḥadīth of Musaddad from Hushaym: ʿAwf informed us, Muḥammad narrated to us from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he mentioned it.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, and he mentioned it. [Weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it in al-ʿIlal, 1848.]"
"11874","(11869) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yūnus from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib informed me that the ḥarīm of a newly-dug well (al-badʾ) is twenty-five cubits from all its sides, and the ḥarīm of an ancient well (al-ʿādiyyah) is fifty cubits from all its sides, and the ḥarīm of a well for cultivation is three hundred cubits from all its sides.\n\nHe said: And al-Zuhrī said: \And I heard the people say: The ḥarīm of springs is five hundred cubits.\"" And Maʿmar likewise narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Sound]"""""
"11875","(11870) And Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah narrated it from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The ḥarīm of an ancient well is fifty cubits"","" and the ḥarīm of a newly-dug well is twenty-five cubits.\"" Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib said on his own authority: \""And the ḥarīm of a cultivation well is three hundred cubits.\""\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us"","" Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī informed us"","" Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"","" Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us"","" Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah"","" and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd it was narrated from the ḥadīth of Maʿmar and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī ʿAblah from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd from Abū Hurayrah"","" marfūʿ (elevated) and mawṣūl (connected)"","" and it is weak. [Weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī in al-ʿIlal.]"""""
"11876","(11871) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The ḥarīm of a well is fifty cubits"","" and the ḥarīm of a spring is two hundred cubits.\"" [Weak. Al-Kharāj"","" 335.]"""""
"11877","(11872) He said: And Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Shāmī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, who said: My father narrated to me, who said: \I witnessed Ḥabīb ibn Maslamah rule regarding the ḥarīm of an ancient well as fifty cubits"","" and regarding a newly-dug well as twenty-five cubits.\"" [Weak. Al-Kharāj"","" 336.]"""""
"11878","(11873) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Ibn Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Saʿīd, who said: I heard ʿIkrimah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Verily"","" Allah has made for cultivation a ḥarīm (precinct) of a bow's flight.\""\n\nYaḥyā said: They said: \""And the bow's flight (al-ghalwah) is between three hundred and fifty cubits to four hundred cubits.\"" [Weak. Al-Kharāj"","" 325.]"""""
"11879","(11874) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us in al-Marāsīl, Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Jarīr narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū Dāwūd said: And I read it to Saʿīd ibn Yaʿqūb from Ibn al-Mubārak from Maʿmar from Ayyūb from Abī Qilābah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Do not cause harm in digging.\""\n\nSaʿīd added: \""That is"","" that a man should dig beside another man's well so as to draw away his water.\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd"","" al-Marāsīl"","" 408.]"""""
"11880","(11875) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Sharīk and Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated from Saʿd al-Kātib from Bilāl al-ʿAbsī from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \There is no reserved pasture (ḥimā) except in three things: the vicinity of a well"","" the tethering place of a horse"","" and the gathering place of a people.\"" [Weak. Al-Kharāj"","" 324.]"""""
"11881","(11876) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād from Kulthūm from Zaynab: that she used to delouse the head of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and with him was the wife of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān and women from among the Muhājirāt, and they were complaining about their dwellings, saying that they were too narrow for them and that they wished to be removed from them. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that the houses of the Muhājirūn be inherited by their womenfolk. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd died, and his wife inherited a house in Madīnah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 6/363]"
"11882","(11877) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated to me from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is that he ruled: \There shall be no harming nor reciprocal harming.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"11883","(11878) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed him from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There shall be no harming nor reciprocal harming.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"11884","(11879) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Ibn Shihāb from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \None of you should prevent his neighbour from fixing his wooden beam in his wall.\"" Abū Hurayrah then said: \""Why do I see you turning away from it? By Allah"","" I shall certainly cast it upon your shoulders.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Mālik 1462]"""""
"11885","(11880) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Muʾaddib narrated to us; Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Mālik ibn Anas from Ibn Shihāb from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz, who is al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: \If his neighbour asks him to fix his wooden beam in his wall"","" he should not prevent him.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11886","(11881) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿwar narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me that Hishām ibn Yaḥyā informed him from ʿIkrimah ibn Salamah ibn Rabīʿah, who informed him that two brothers from Banī al-Mughīrah — one of them had sworn an oath that the other would not fix a wooden beam in his walls. They met Jāmiʿ ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī and many other men from the Anṣār, and they said: \We bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that a neighbour should not prevent his neighbour from fixing a wooden beam in his wall.\"" The one who had sworn the oath said: \""O my brother"","" I know that the ruling is in your favour against me"","" but I have already sworn an oath. So erect a pillar alongside my wall.\"" The other did so and fixed his wooden beam in the pillar. ʿAmr said: \""I saw that with my own eyes.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. al-Ṭabarī in Tahdhīb al-Āthār 1162"","" 1163]"""""
"11887","(11882) Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī from his father that al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Khalīfah dug a small canal for himself from al-ʿUrayḍ and wished to run it through the land of Muḥammad ibn Maslamah. Muḥammad refused. Al-Ḍaḥḥāk then spoke to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābillāh be pleased with him about it. He summoned Muḥammad ibn Maslamah and ordered him to give way. Muḥammad ibn Maslamah said: \No.\"" ʿUmar (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) said: \""Why do you prevent your brother from what benefits him and is also beneficial to you? You will drink from it first and last"","" and it will not harm you.\"" Muḥammad said: \""No.\"" ʿUmar (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) said: \""By Allah"","" it shall pass"","" even if it be over your belly.\"" This is a mursal narration. Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī also narrated something similar"","" and it is also mursal. A marfūʿ ḥadīth has also been narrated to the same effect. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 1431]"""""
"11888","(11883) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Wāṣil, the freedman of Abū ʿUyaynah, who said: I heard Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub that he had some palm branches in the garden of a man from the Anṣār. The man had his family with him, and whenever Samurah ibn Jundub entered his palm trees, it caused him hardship and distress. He asked Samurah to sell them to him, but he refused. He asked him to exchange them, but he refused. He then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. The Prophet (ﷺ) asked him to sell, but he refused. He asked him to exchange, but he refused. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Then gift it to me"","" and you shall have such and such\"" — a matter that would encourage him — but he refused. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""You are one who causes harm.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to the Anṣārī: \""Go and uproot his palm trees.\"" It has also been narrated in opposition to this that indicates he cannot be compelled. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3636]"""""
"11889","(11884) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \So-and-so has a palm tree cluster in his garden"","" and it has harmed me and become burdensome to me due to the location of his palm tree cluster.\"" The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) sent to him and said: \""Sell me your palm tree cluster that is in so-and-so's garden.\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then gift it to me.\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then sell it to me in exchange for a palm tree cluster in Paradise.\"" He said: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""I have not seen anyone more miserly than you"","" except the one who is miserly with the greeting of salām.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11890","(11885) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb informed me from al-Zuhrī. He said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab informed me that the first matter in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rebuked Abū Lubābah ibn ʿAbd al-Munẓir was that he had a dispute with an orphan under his care over a palm tree cluster. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled in favour of Abū Lubābah regarding the palm tree cluster. The orphan became distressed and complained to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abū Lubābah: \Give me this palm tree cluster"","" O Abū Lubābah"","" so that we may return it to the orphan.\"" Abū Lubābah refused to gift it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""O Abū Lubābah"","" give it to this orphan"","" and you shall have its like in Paradise.\"" Abū Lubābah refused to give it. A man from the Anṣār said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what do you think if I buy this palm tree cluster and give it to the orphan — will I have its like in Paradise?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Yes.\"" The Anṣārī — who was Ibn al-Ḥadḥāḥah — set out until he met Abū Lubābah and said: \""O Abū Lubābah"","" I wish to buy this palm tree cluster from you in exchange for my garden.\"" He had a date-palm garden. Abū Lubābah said: \""Yes.\"" So he bought it from him in exchange for a garden. It was not long before the disbelievers of Quraysh came on the day of Uḥud. He went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and fought them"","" and he was killed as a martyr. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Many a trailing palm tree cluster shall be for Ibn al-Ḥadḥāḥah in Paradise.\""\n\n(Q) As for the ḥadīth \""There shall be no harming nor reciprocal harming"",""\"" it is mursal and its indication is shared. As for the ḥadīth of the wooden beam"","" some of the scholars took it at face value"","" as the narrator understood it to be obligatory"","" as you see. I did not find any statement from al-Shāfiʿī that contradicts it; rather"","" he explicitly stated in both the old and new recensions something that agrees with it. As for the ḥadīth of ʿUmar (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu)"","" Muḥammad ibn Maslamah opposed it"","" and there are those who abandon acting upon it entirely"","" on the basis that every Muslim has the most right to his own wealth"","" and thus they expand upon the basis of his opposition.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in the old recension — and I think the ruling of ʿUmar (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) regarding the wife of the missing person falls under some of these aspects in which he prevented harm to the woman when the harm to her was more evident.\n\nHe said in the new recension: And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) said regarding the wife of the missing person: \""A woman who has been afflicted — let her be patient. She should not be married until certainty of his death comes to her.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (raḥimahullāh) said: \""And this is what we follow.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11891","(11886) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ibn ʿAwn informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf ibn Khallād al-ʿAṭṭār in Baghdād narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Usāmah al-Tamīmī narrated to us: Ashhal, meaning Ibn Ḥātim, narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us: Ibn ʿAwn informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired a piece of land in Khaybar and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired a piece of land"","" and by Allah"","" I have never acquired any property more precious to me than it. What do you command me"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""If you wish"","" you may give it in charity and retain its principal.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) made it a charity that is not to be sold"","" gifted"","" or inherited. He gave it in charity for the poor"","" the relatives"","" in the cause of Allah"","" and for the emancipation of slaves.\n\nIbn ʿAwn said: \""And I think he said: 'and for the guest.' And there is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner and feeds a friend"","" without accumulating wealth from it.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Bishrān.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī ʿĀṣim from Ibn ʿAwn. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī"","" 2737; Muslim"","" 4223]"""""
"11892","(11887) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraīʿ narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired a piece of land in Khaybar. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \I have acquired a piece of land; I have never acquired any property more precious to me than it. How do you command me?\"" He said: \""If you wish"","" you may retain its principal and give it in charity.\"" So ʿUmar gave it in charity"","" stipulating that its principal shall not be sold"","" inherited"","" or gifted — for the poor"","" the relatives"","" the emancipation of slaves"","" in the cause of Allah"","" the guest"","" and the wayfarer. And there is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner or feeds a friend"","" without accumulating wealth from it.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11893","(11888) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Dalaj ibn Aḥmad informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Sulaym ibn Akhḍar narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired a piece of land in Khaybar. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to seek his counsel regarding it and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired a piece of land in Khaybar; I have never acquired any property more precious to me than it. What do you command regarding it?\"" He said: \""If you wish"","" you may retain its principal and give it in charity.\"" He said: \""So ʿUmar gave it in charity"","" stipulating that its principal shall not be sold"","" inherited"","" or gifted.\"" He said: \""ʿUmar gave it in charity for the poor"","" the relatives"","" the emancipation of slaves"","" in the cause of Allah"","" the wayfarer"","" and the guest. There is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner and feeds a friend"","" without accumulating wealth from it.\""\n\nHe said: \""So I narrated this ḥadīth to Muḥammad"","" and when I reached this point — 'without accumulating wealth' — Muḥammad said: 'Without amassing wealth.'\""\n\nIbn ʿAwn said: \""And someone who read this book informed me that in it is: 'without amassing wealth.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11894","(11889) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I acquired a piece of land in Khaybar; I never acquired any property more precious to me than it. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to seek his counsel and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired a piece of land in Khaybar; I have never acquired any property more precious to me than it.' He said: 'If you wish"","" you may retain its principal and give it in charity.' So ʿUmar gave it in charity on the condition that it shall not be sold"","" gifted"","" or inherited.\"" He said: \""He gave it in charity for the poor"","" the near relatives"","" in the cause of Allah"","" for the emancipation of slaves"","" the wayfarer"","" and the guest. There is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner and gives in a reasonable manner to a friend"","" without accumulating wealth.\""\n\nIbn ʿAwn said: \""So I mentioned it to Ibn Sīrīn and he said: 'Without amassing wealth.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Abī Dāwūd al-Ḥafarī from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11895","(11890) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād ibn Bishr al-Baṣrī in Makkah narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Sahl al-Tustarī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired property in Khaybar; I have never acquired any property more beloved to me than it.\"" He said to him: \""If you wish"","" you may give it in charity"","" and if you wish"","" you may retain its principal.\"" He said: \""So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it in charity for the weak"","" the destitute"","" and the wayfarer. There is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats or feeds a friend"","" without accumulating wealth from it"","" or amassing wealth from it.\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Yūnus ibn Muḥammad from Ḥammād from Ayyūb"","" and from Yazīd ibn Zuraīʿ from Ayyūb"","" and a group narrated it as a mursal report from Ḥammād. And al-Bukhārī narrated the end of it from Qutaybah from Ḥammād as a connected (mawṣūl) narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11896","(11891) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī informed me: Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to me: Hārūn narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd, the freedman of Banī Hāshim, narrated to us: Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave in charity a property of his during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). It was called Thamgh, and it was a date palm grove. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired a property that is most precious to me"","" and I wish to give it in charity.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Give its principal in charity; it shall not be sold"","" gifted"","" or inherited"","" but its produce shall be spent.\"" So ʿUmar gave it in charity"","" and its charity was for the cause of Allah"","" for the emancipation of slaves"","" the destitute"","" the guest"","" the wayfarer"","" and the relatives. And there is no sin upon the one who manages it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner or feeds his friend"","" without accumulating wealth thereby.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it thus. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11897","(11892) And with this meaning it was narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar consulted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about giving his property that was in Thamgh in charity. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \Give its produce in charity and retain its principal; it shall not be sold or inherited.\"" Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us of it: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us by dictation: Muḥammad ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā and Aḥmad ibn Abī Bakr said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed me"","" from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Muṭṭalib"","" from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11898","(11893) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, regarding the charitable endowment (ṣadaqah) of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He said: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb dictated it to me concerning Thamgh: that it goes to Ḥafṣah for as long as she lives; she may spend its produce as Allah directs her. If she passes away, then it goes to the one of sound judgment among her family. Its principal shall never be purchased or gifted. And whoever manages it, there is no blame upon him regarding its produce if he eats from it or feeds a friend, without amassing wealth. Whatever surplus remains from its produce is for the beggar, the deprived, the guest, the relatives, the wayfarer, and in the cause of Allah — she may spend it as Allah directs her from that. If Ḥafṣah passes away, then it goes to the one of sound judgment among my children. And the one hundred wasqs that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fed me with in the valley — I did not destroy them — they shall be with Thamgh according to the practice that I have commanded. And if the guardian of Thamgh wishes, he may purchase slaves from its produce for its maintenance. And Muʿayqīb wrote, and ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Arqam witnessed: \In the name of Allah"","" the Most Gracious"","" the Most Merciful. This is what ʿAbdillāh ʿUmar"","" the Commander of the Faithful"","" has bequeathed. If he passes away"","" then Thamgh"","" Ṣirmah ibn al-Akwāʿ"","" the slave therein"","" the one hundred shares in Khaybar"","" the slave therein"","" and the one hundred wasqs that Muḥammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fed him — Ḥafṣah shall manage it for as long as she lives"","" then the one of sound judgment among her family. It shall not be sold or purchased. He shall spend it as he sees fit for the beggar"","" the deprived"","" and the relatives. And there is no blame upon its guardian if he eats"","" feeds"","" or purchases slaves from it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11899","(11894) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith ibn al-Muṣṭaliq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left nothing except a white mule, weapons, and land that he made a charity. [Ibn al-Jaʿd, 2534; Ibn Saʿd, 2/316]"
"11900","(11895) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal informed us: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: al-Nufaylī narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, the brother-in-law of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — the brother of his wife — who said: \By Allah"","" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left neither a dīnār nor a dirham"","" neither a male slave nor a female slave"","" nor anything at all"","" except his white mule"","" his weapons"","" and land that he left as charity.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah"","" Abī al-Aḥwaṣ"","" and al-Thawrī"","" from Abī Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11901","(11896) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Nadhir ibn Muḥammad ibn Junāḥ al-Muḥāribī informed me in al-Kūfah, that al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Abī al-Aḥwaṣ al-Thaqafī narrated to us, that my father narrated to me, that al-Ḥasan ibn Ziyād al-Hamdānī narrated to us, that Abū Ḥafṣ al-Abbār narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, designated seven gardens of his in Madīnah as ṣadaqah upon Banī al-Muṭṭalib and Banī Hāshim. [Fabricated]"
"11902","(11897) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with them both, granted ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib Yanbuʿ as a grant. Then ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, purchased additional portions from ʿUramayyah of ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he dug a well therein. While they were working in it, a spring of water gushed forth upon them like the neck of a slaughtered camel. ʿAlī was brought and given glad tidings of this. He said: \Give glad tidings to the heir"","" then give it in ṣadaqah upon the poor"","" the destitute"","" in the cause of Allah"","" and the wayfarer — near and far — in times of peace and in times of war"","" for a day when faces shall be whitened and faces shall be blackened"","" so that Allah"","" the Most High"","" may thereby turn my face away from the Fire and turn the Fire away from my face.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from another chain from Abī Jaʿfar that ʿUmar and ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" jointly designated a piece of land as a waqf"","" irrevocably and unconditionally. [Weak]"""""
"11903","(11898) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Shāfiʿ informed me, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥasan ibn Ḥasan informed me, from more than one member of his household — and I think he said Zayd ibn ʿAlī — that Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, gave her wealth in ṣadaqah upon Banī Hāshim and Banī al-Muṭṭalib, and that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, gave ṣadaqah upon them and included others alongside them. [Weak — al-Umm of al-Shāfiʿī, 4/57]"
"11904","(11899) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Aḥmad ibn Sahl informed me, that Ibrāhīm ibn Maʿqil narrated to us, that Ḥarmalah narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb narrated to me, that Mālik informed me that Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, had made waqf his house which was in al-Baqīʿ and his house which was near the Masjid, and he wrote in the deed of his waqf according to what ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, had established as waqf. Mālik said: \The waqf of Zayd ibn Thābit is with me [in writing].\"" He said: \""And Zayd ibn Thābit"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" used to reside in a dwelling within the house he had made waqf near the Masjid until he died therein. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" had done likewise — he made his house waqf and used to reside in a dwelling from it.\"""""""
"11905","(11900) Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Mihrajānī al-Khaṭīb informed us, that Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī informed us, that Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, that Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his house in Makkah in ṣadaqah upon his children, and it remains so to this day. And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his property at al-Marwah and at al-Thaniyyah upon his children, and it remains so to this day. And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his land at Yanbuʿ in ṣadaqah, and it remains so to this day. And al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his house in Makkah in the Ḥarāmiyyah and his house in Egypt and his wealth in Madīnah upon his children, and that remains so to this day. And Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his house in Madīnah and his house in Egypt upon his children, and that remains so to this day. And ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, gave Rūmah [a well] in ṣadaqah, and it remains so to this day. And ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, may Allah be pleased with him, gave al-Waḥṭ of al-Ṭāʾif and his house in Makkah upon his children, and that remains so to this day. And Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, may Allah be pleased with him, gave his house in Makkah and Madīnah upon his children, and that remains so to this day. He said: \And there are many that I do not recall"","" more than what I have mentioned.\"" He said: \""And in what I have mentioned regarding those who gave their houses in Makkah as ṣadaqah"","" there is evidence for the people of Makkah regarding the ownership of their houses and the leasing of their residences"","" because Abū Bakr"","" ʿUmar"","" al-Zubayr"","" ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"","" and Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām"","" may Allah be pleased with them"","" did not intend anything in which the people were equal partners; rather"","" they gave it in ṣadaqah upon their children exclusively"","" without making them co-owners alongside them.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11906","(11901) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūd al-Marwazī narrated to us, that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, that al-Anṣārī narrated to me, that my father narrated to me, from Thumāmah, from Anas, that he made a house in Madīnah as waqf, and whenever he performed Ḥajj and passed through Madīnah, he would stay in his house. [Weak]"
"11907","(11902) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ al-Bazzāz narrated to us, that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \ʿUmar acquired land in Khaybar and came to the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired land in Khaybar"","" and by Allah"","" I have never acquired any property more precious to me than it. What do you command me to do?' He said: 'If you wish"","" give its produce in ṣadaqah and retain its principal (aṣl).' So ʿUmar stipulated that it should not be sold"","" gifted"","" or inherited"","" and he gave it in ṣadaqah upon the poor"","" the destitute"","" the wayfarer"","" in the cause of Allah"","" and for the freeing of slaves. There is no sin upon the one who administers it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner and feeds others without accumulating wealth from it. Then he bequeathed its administration to Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" and then to the senior members of the family of ʿUmar.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in the book al-Baḥīrah: \""More than one person from the families of ʿUmar and ʿAlī informed me that ʿUramayyah administered his ṣadaqah until he died"","" and he appointed Ḥafṣah after him"","" and that ʿAlī administered his ṣadaqah until he died"","" and Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī administered it after him"","" and that Fāṭimah"","" the daughter of the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" administered her ṣadaqah until she died. And I have been informed by more than one of the Anṣār that he administered his ṣadaqah until he died.\""\n\nHe said in the older work: \""And al-Zubayr administered his ṣadaqah until Allah took him"","" and ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ administered his ṣadaqah until Allah took him"","" and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah administered his ṣadaqah until Allah took him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11908","(11903) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us, that ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, that Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from ʿĪsā ibn al-Musayyib, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said: \Four matters have been determined and completed: creation (al-khalq)"","" character (al-khulq)"","" provision (al-rizq)"","" and the appointed term (al-ajal). No one earns more than anyone else [in these matters]. And ṣadaqah is valid whether it is formally received or not.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11909","(11904) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, that al-Shāfiʿī informed us, that Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUramayyah owned one hundred shares in Khaybar which he purchased. He came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired property the like of which I have never acquired"","" and I wish to draw near to Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" through it.\"" He said: \""Retain the principal (al-aṣl) and dedicate the produce (al-thamarah) [in charity].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11910","(11905) And Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Khaṭīb informed us, that Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī informed us, that Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, that Sufyān narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated — for more than seventy years — that Nāfiʿ informed him from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that ʿUramayyah said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have acquired property the like of which I have never acquired — the one hundred shares in Khaybar — and I wish to draw near to Allah"","" the Most High"","" through it.\"" The Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" said to him: \""Retain the principal (al-aṣl) and dedicate the produce (al-thamarah).\""\n\nAbū Yaḥyā al-Sājī said: And it has been narrated that al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn — one of them — made waqf portions of his houses"","" and the scholars permitted that. And Ibn ʿUramayyah gave in ṣadaqah the share at al-Ghābah which Ḥafṣah had gifted to him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11911","(11906) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Lahīʿah reported from one who heard ʿIkrimah narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: When the obligatory shares of inheritance were revealed in Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no withholding (ḥabs) after Sūrat al-Nisāʾ.\""\n\n[Weak]"""""
"11912","(11907) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah informed us: Ibn Lahīʿah informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿIkrimah, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say, after Sūrat al-Nisāʾ was revealed and the obligatory shares of inheritance were prescribed therein: \There is no withholding (ḥabs) after Sūrat al-Nisāʾ.\""\n\n[Weak]"""""
"11913","(11908) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Mahdī bi-llāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Mūsā al-Ṣadafī in Egypt informed us: ʿAmr ibn Khālid informed us: Ibn Lahīʿah reported from his brother ʿĪsā ibn Lahīʿah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no withholding (ḥabs) from the obligatory shares of Allah.\""\n\nʿAlī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: No one other than Ibn Lahīʿah narrated it from his brother"","" and both of them are weak.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This wording is only known as a statement of Sharīḥ al-Qāḍī.\n\n[Weak]"""""
"11914","(11909) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib said: I came to Sharīḥ during the time of Bishr ibn Marwān, and he was at that time a judge. I said: \O Abū Umayyah"","" give me a legal ruling.\"" He said: \""O son of my brother"","" I am merely a judge and not a muftī.\"" I said: \""By Allah"","" I have not come seeking a dispute; rather"","" a man from the tribe has made his house a ḥabs (withheld endowment).\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: He entered through the door that was in the mosque"","" into the maqṣūrah"","" and I heard him when I followed him as he was saying to Ḥabīb"","" who brought the disputants to him: \""Inform the man that there is no withholding (ḥabs) from the obligatory shares of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\n[Authentic]"""""
"11915","(11910) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Miʿsar reported from Abū ʿAwn, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Muḥammad (ﷺ) came with the annulment of the sale of ḥabs (withheld property).\""\n\n[Authentic. Ibn Abī Shaybah 29031]"""""
"11916","(11911) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us. He said: I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam say: I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: Mālik said: \The ḥabs (withholding) that Muḥammad (ﷺ) came with regarding its abolition is that which is in the Book of Allah: 'Allah has not made baḥīrah"","" nor sāʾibah"","" nor waṣīlah"","" nor ḥām' [al-Māʾidah: 103].\"" Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh said: Mālik spoke about this to Abū Yūsuf in the presence of the Commander of the Faithful.\n\n[Authentic]"""""
"11917","(11912) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī informed me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥātim said: I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam say: I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: Mālik and Abū Yūsuf gathered in the presence of the Commander of the Faithful and they spoke about waqf (endowments) and what people withhold as ḥabs. Yaʿqūb (Abū Yūsuf) said: \This is false.\"" Sharīḥ said: \""Muḥammad (ﷺ) came with the abolition of ḥabs.\"" Mālik said: \""Muḥammad (ﷺ) came only with the abolition of what they used to withhold for their idols—namely"","" the baḥīrah and the sāʾibah. As for waqf"","" this is the waqf of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" who asked permission of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and he said: 'Withhold its origin and dedicate its fruit (to charity).' And this is the waqf of al-Zubayr.\"" This amazed the Caliph"","" and Yaʿqūb remained silent.\n\n[Authentic]"""""
"11918","(11913) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us by dictation: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: Al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān reported from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih—the one who was shown the call to prayer (in a dream)—that he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" this garden of mine is charity"","" dedicated to Allah and His Messenger.\"" Then his two parents came and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" it was our means of livelihood.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned it to them. Then they both passed away"","" and their son inherited them thereafter.\n\n[Al-Dāraquṭnī 4/202]\n\nThis is a mursal hadith. Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm did not meet ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd. It has also been narrated through other chains from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd"","" all of which are mursal.\n\nThe hadith pertains to a specific charitable endowment (ṣadaqah munqaṭiʿah)"","" as though he gave it as voluntary charity and designated its disbursement at the discretion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave it in charity to his parents."""""
"11919","(11914) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: He informed me—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb reported from al-Zuhrī, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab say: \The baḥīrah is the she-camel whose milk was withheld for the idols; no person would milk it. The sāʾibah is the animal they used to set free for their idols"","" and nothing was loaded upon it.\""\n\nHe said: And Abū Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""I saw ʿAmr al-Khuzāʿī dragging his intestines in the Fire"","" and he was the first to set free the sawāʾib (pl. of sāʾibah).\""\n\nIbn al-Musayyab said: \""The waṣīlah is the young she-camel that is born as the first offspring of the camels"","" giving birth to a female"","" and then giving birth again to a female. They used to set it free for their idols and call it waṣīlah when one female was followed by another with no male between them.\""\n\nIbn al-Musayyab said: \""The ḥām is the male camel that had served a set number of copulations; when he had fulfilled his service"","" they would dedicate him to the idols and spare him from carrying any load"","" and they called him ḥām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Bukhārī 3531; Muslim 2856]"""""
"11920","(11915) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ informed us: Shabbābah reported from Warqāʾ, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect the ṣadaqah (zakāh). Ibn Jamīl, Khālid ibn al-Walīd, and al-ʿAbbās refused to pay. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Ibn Jamīl resents nothing except that he was poor and Allah enriched him. As for Khālid"","" you are wronging Khālid"","" for he has withheld his armour and his equipment in the cause of Allah. As for al-ʿAbbās"","" the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" it is my responsibility"","" and the same again.\"" Then he said: \""Did you not know that the uncle of a man is like his father"","" or like his father's equal?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Warqāʾ"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the hadith of Shuʿayb and others from Abī al-Zinād. Some of them reported from Abī al-Zinād: \""his armour and his servants.\"" [Bukhārī 1458; Muslim 983]"""""
"11921","(11916) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz narrated to me; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hayyuwayh narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman informed us; Shu'ayb narrated to us; Abu al-Zinad narrated from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded the giving of charity, and it was said: \Ibn Jameel"","" Khalid ibn al-Walid"","" and 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib have withheld.\"" He mentioned the hadith and said: \""His shields and his servants are in the cause of Allah. As for 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib"","" the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" it is a charity upon him and the like of it along with it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Abu al-Yaman. [Sahih]"""""
"11922","(11917) And thus narrated Musa ibn 'Uqbah from Abu al-Zinad, except that he said: \It is for him and the like of it along with it.\"" 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; Isma'il ibn al-Fadl narrated to me; Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated from Musa ibn 'Uqbah"","" and he mentioned it. [Sahih]"""""
"11923","(11918) And thus narrated Abu Uways from Abu al-Zinad, except that he said: \It is upon him and the like of it along with it.\"" Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us; 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to me; my father narrated from Abu al-Zinad"","" and he mentioned it. [Sahih]"""""
"11924","(11919) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il al-Qadi informed us; Musaddad narrated to us; 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated from 'Amir al-Ahwal from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah from Ibn 'Abbas. He said: And Isma'il narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us; 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us; 'Amir ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal narrated to me; Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani narrated to me from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) intended to perform Hajj, so a woman said to her husband: \Perform Hajj with me along with the Prophet (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""I do not have that upon which I can perform Hajj for you.\"" She said: \""Perform Hajj for me on your such-and-such camel.\"" He said: \""That is dedicated in the cause of Allah.\"" She said: \""Then perform Hajj for me on your water-camel.\"" He said: \""That is one we take turns using"","" I and your son.\"" She said: \""Then sell your fruit.\"" He said: \""That is my provision and your provision.\"" When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived"","" her husband sent her to the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and she said: \""Convey to him the salam and the mercy of Allah"","" and ask him what is equivalent to a Hajj performed with you.\"" Her husband came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" my wife conveys to you the salam and the mercy of Allah"","" and she asked me to perform Hajj for her"","" and I said: 'I do not have that upon which I can perform Hajj for you.' She said: 'Perform Hajj for me on your such-and-such camel.' I said: 'That is dedicated in the cause of Allah.'\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Had you performed Hajj for her upon it"","" it would have been in the cause of Allah.\"" She said: \""Then perform Hajj for me on your water-camel"",""\"" and I said: \""That is one we take turns using"","" I and your son.\"" She said: \""Then sell your fruit.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) laughed at her eagerness for Hajj. And Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj said in his hadith: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) laughed in wonder at her eagerness for Hajj.\"" He said: \""She commanded me to ask you what is equivalent to a Hajj performed with you.\"" He said: \""Convey to her the salam and the mercy of Allah"","" and inform her that an 'Umrah performed in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj performed with me.\""\n\nAl-Qadi said: Thus narrated 'Abd al-Warith from 'Amir al-Ahwal from Bakr from Ibn 'Abbas"","" and Hisham added in his isnad an additional man. [Bukhari 1782; Muslim 1256]"""""
"11925","(11920) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtuwayh narrated to me; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Ibn Abi Uways narrated to me; my cousin Malik narrated from Ishaq ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abu Talhah was the wealthiest of the Ansar in Madinah in terms of palm trees, and the dearest of his possessions to him was a well called Bayruha, which faced the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to enter it and drink from the fresh water that was in it. Anas said: When this verse was revealed — \You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love\"" (3:92) — Abu Talhah stood up and went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" indeed Allah says: 'You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love"",""' and indeed the dearest of my wealth to me is Bayruha. It is charity for Allah; I hope for its goodness and its reward with Allah. Place it"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" wherever Allah directs you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""That is a profitable wealth. I have heard what you said"","" and I think you should distribute it among your relatives.\"" Abu Talhah said: \""I will do so"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So Abu Talhah distributed it among his relatives and the sons of his paternal uncle.\n\nIsma'il said: By \""profitable wealth\"" he means that which goes forth with goodness and returns with goodness.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya from Malik. [Muslim 998]"""""
"11926","(11921) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi and Musa ibn Muhammad al-Dhuhli both said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us. He said: I recited to Malik, and he mentioned it in a similar manner, except that he said: \Place it"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" wherever you wish.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Bakh! That is a profitable wealth.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11927","(11922) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us; Khalaf ibn Salim narrated to us; Bahz narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Thabit narrated from Anas, who said: When this verse was revealed — \You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love\"" (3:92) — Abu Talhah said: \""I see that our Lord is asking us from our wealth. I bear witness"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" that I have made my land"","" Bayruha"","" for Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Distribute it among your relatives.\"" So he distributed it among Hassan ibn Thabit and Ubayy ibn Ka'b.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Bahz ibn Asad. [Sahih]"""""
"11928","(11923) Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said in what he cited as evidence against the Ansar on the day of Saqifah: \Allah sent Muhammad (ﷺ) with guidance and the religion of truth. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called to Islam"","" and Allah took hold of our hearts and our forelocks towards that to which he called. We"","" the people of the Muhajirun"","" were the first of the people to accept Islam"","" and we are his kin and his relatives.\""\n\nAbu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Baghdadi informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Lahi'ah narrated from Abu al-Aswad from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr.\n\n(And) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Attab informed us; al-Qasim ibn 'Abdillah informed us; Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated"","" and they both mentioned it from Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). Musa added in his narration: \""And his kinsfolk.\"" [Bukhari 3679; Muslim 2213]"""""
"11929","(11924) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Husayn ibn Waqid narrated from 'Abdillah ibn Buraydah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was delivering a sermon when al-Hasan and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) approached, wearing two red shirts, stumbling and rising. When he saw them, he descended, took them, then ascended with them in his lap, and said: \Allah has spoken the truth: 'Indeed"","" your wealth and your children are a trial' (64:15). I saw these two"","" and I could not restrain myself until I took them.\"" [Hasan. Ahmad 23383; Abu Dawud 1109]"""""
"11930","(11925) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us; Abu Ya'la narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Abu Musa, who said: I heard al-Hasan say: I heard Abu Bakrah say: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) upon the pulpit, and with him was al-Hasan ibn 'Ali. He would look at him once and at the people once, and he would say: \Indeed"","" this son of mine is a master"","" and perhaps Allah will set right through him two factions of the Muslims.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from 'Ali ibn 'Abdillah from Sufyan. [Bukhari 2704]"""""
"11931","(11926) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhāb al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us, from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from Hānʾ ibn Hānʾ, from ʿAliyy, who said:\n\nWhen al-Ḥasan was born, I named him Ḥarb. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and said: \Show me my son. What have you named him?\"" I said: \""Ḥarb.\"" He said: \""Rather"","" he is Ḥasan.\""\n\nThen al-Ḥusayn was born"","" and I named him Ḥarb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came and said: \""Show me my son. What have you named him?\"" I said: \""Ḥarb.\"" He said: \""Rather"","" he is Ḥusayn.\""\n\nWhen the third was born"","" I named him Ḥarb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to see him and said: \""Show me my son. What have you named him?\"" I said: \""Ḥarb.\"" He said: \""Rather"","" he is Muḥassin.\""\n\nThen he said: \""I have named them after the names of the children of Hārūn: Shabbīr"","" Shabīr"","" and Mushabbir.\""\n\nYūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated it from his father and said in the hadith: \""Indeed"","" I have named these sons of mine with the naming of Hārūn's sons.\""\n\nMany narrations have been reported to this effect."""""
"11932","(11927) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zurārah al-Raqqī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥarb al-Laythī informed us; Hāshim ibn Yaḥyā ibn Hāshim al-Muzanī informed us; Abū Daghfal al-Hujaymī informed us, saying: I heard Maʿqil ibn Yāsār al-Muzanī say: I heard Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq say: \ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib is the ʿitrah (progeny) of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nIn this chain of narration there are some who are unknown. It is reported from Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said on the day of al-Saqīfah: \""We are the ʿitrah (progeny) of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"""""""
"11933","(11928) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ziyād al-Naḥwī in Baghdād informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us; Bishr ibn Mihrān informed us; Sharīk informed us, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar came to al-Ḥajjāj.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us; Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Khālid al-Hāshimī in al-Kūfah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Tamīmī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Nuḥās informed us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Mūsā al-Ṭalḥī informed us; ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah informed us, saying: They gathered in the presence of al-Ḥajjāj, and al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī was mentioned. Al-Ḥajjāj said: \He is not from the progeny of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar was present"","" so he said to him: \""You have lied"","" O Commander!\"" Al-Ḥajjāj said: \""Bring me proof from the Book of Allah confirming what you have said"","" or I shall kill you.\"" He recited: \""And from his progeny: Dāwūd"","" Sulaymān"","" Ayyūb"","" Yūsuf"","" Mūsā"","" and Hārūn\"" — until His words: \""And Zakariyyā"","" Yaḥyā"","" and ʿĪsā.\"" He said: \""Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" informed that ʿĪsā is from the progeny of Ādam through his mother"","" and al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī is from the progeny of Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) through his mother.\"" Al-Ḥajjāj said: \""You have spoken the truth. But what compelled you to contradict me in my assembly?\"" He said: \""What Allah took as a covenant upon the prophets: 'You shall make it clear to the people and not conceal it.' And Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" said: 'So they cast it behind their backs and sold it for a paltry price.'\"" Al-Ḥajjāj then exiled him to Khurāsān."""""
"11934","(11929) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us, from Kathīr ibn Zayd, from Walīd ibn Rabāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions.\"""""""
"11935","(11930) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAliyy ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; Abū ʿUbayd informed us; Abū Yūsuf informed us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, that al-Zubayr made his houses as charity (ṣadaqah). He said: \And for the divorced (al-mardūdah) among his daughters"","" she may reside without causing harm or being harmed. If she becomes self-sufficient through a husband"","" then she has no claim.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-mardūdah means al-muṭallaqah (the divorced woman).\"""""""
"11936","(11931) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah informed us; Abū Hammām informed me; Ibn Wahb informed me, from ʿAmr, that Bukayr informed him, that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed him, that he heard ʿUbaydullāh al-Khawlānī mention that he heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, at the time when the people spoke against him as he built the Mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), say: \You have gone too far. Indeed"","" I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever builds a mosque for Allah…'\"" Bukayr said: \""I think he said: '…seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah"","" Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān"","" and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd and others"","" all of them from Ibn Wahb."""""
"11937","(11932) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAliyy ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us; Abū ʿĀṣim informed us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar informed me; my father informed me, from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd, who said:\n\nWhen ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to build the mosque, the people disliked that and wanted him to leave it. ʿUthmān said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever builds a mosque for Allah"","" Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others"","" from Abū ʿĀṣim."""""
"11938","(11933) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Fazārī informed us; ʿAbdān ibn ʿUthmān informed me; my father informed me, from Shuʿbah, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him), when he was besieged, appeared before them and said: \I adjure you by Allah — and I adjure only the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whoever digs the well of Rūmah shall have Paradise'? So I dug it. Do you not know that he said: 'Whoever equips the Army of Hardship (Jaīsh al-ʿUsrah) shall have Paradise'? So I equipped them.\"" And they confirmed what he said.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān."""""
"11939","(11934) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAliyy ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam informed us; ʿAliyy ibn Maʿbad informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said:\n\nWhen ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) was besieged and his house was surrounded, he appeared before the people and said: \I adjure you by Allah — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on Mount Ḥirāʾ and said: 'Be still"","" Ḥirāʾ! Upon you there is nothing but a prophet"","" a ṣiddīq"","" or a martyr'?\"" They said: \""Yes"","" by Allah.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said during the campaign of al-ʿUsrah: 'Whoever spends an accepted expenditure' — and the people at that time were in hardship and distress — so I equipped one-third of that army from my own wealth.\"" They said: \""Yes"","" by Allah.\"" Then he said: \""I adjure you by Allah — do you know that Rūmah was such that no one could drink from it except by purchasing it? So I bought it with my wealth and made it available for the rich"","" the poor"","" and the wayfarer.\"" They said: \""Yes"","" by Allah.\"" He enumerated several such matters."""""
"11940","(11935) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us; ʿAffān informed us; Abū ʿAānah informed us; Ḥuṣayn informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān, from al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays, in a story he mentioned, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said: \Is ʿAlī here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Is Ṭalḥah here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Is al-Zubayr here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Is Saʿd here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"","" besides whom there is no deity — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whoever purchases the mirbad of Banī Fulān"","" Allah will forgive him'? So I purchased it.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I think he said: 'For twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand.' Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'I have purchased it.' He said: 'Make it part of our mosque"","" and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"","" besides whom there is no deity — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Whoever purchases the well of Rūmah"","" Allah will forgive him'? So I purchased it for such-and-such"","" and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'Indeed"","" I have purchased the well of Rūmah.' He said: 'Make it a watering place for the Muslims"","" and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah"","" besides whom there is no deity — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked upon the faces of the people on the day of the Army of Hardship and said: 'Whoever equips these"","" Allah will forgive him'? So I equipped them"","" such that they did not lack even a nose-rope or a hobble.\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""O Allah"","" bear witness! O Allah"","" bear witness! O Allah"","" bear witness!\"" And he mentioned the hadith."""""
"11941","(11936) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marzuq al-Basri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj, from Abu Mas'ud al-Jurayri, from Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri, who said: I was present at the house, and 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) looked out over the people and said: I adjure you by Allah and by Islam — do you know that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madinah, there was no sweet water in it except the well of Rumah, and he said: \Whoever purchases the well of Rumah"","" and his bucket therein will be alongside the buckets of the Muslims"","" he will have something better than it in Paradise\""? So I purchased it from my own wealth"","" and yet today you prevent me from drinking from it"","" to the point that I drink seawater. They said: O Allah"","" yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah and by Islam — do you know that the mosque had become too small for its people"","" and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Whoever purchases the plot of the family of so-and-so"","" he will have something better than it in Paradise\""? So I purchased it from my wealth — or he said"","" from my own wealth — and I added it to the mosque"","" and yet today you prevent me from praying in it. They said: O Allah"","" yes. And he mentioned the hadith regarding the equipping of the Army of Hardship and the story of Thabir. [Hasan due to supporting narrations. Tirmidhi 3703]"""""
"11942","(11937) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us in Baghdad, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Jarrah al-Ghazzi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn Ruzayq and others, from 'Ata' al-Khurasani, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to expand the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), the expansion fell upon the house of al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him). So 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wished to incorporate it into the mosque and to compensate him for it, but he refused and said: It is a gift of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). They disagreed, and so they appointed Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) as an arbitrator between them. They came to him in his house — he was called the \Leader of the Muslims\"" — and he ordered a cushion to be spread for them"","" and they sat before him. 'Umar mentioned what he intended"","" and al-'Abbas mentioned the gift of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Ubayy said: Indeed"","" Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" commanded His servant and Prophet Dawud (peace be upon him) to build a House for Him. He said: \""O my Lord"","" where is this House?\"" He said: \""Where you see the angel unsheathing his sword.\"" He saw it upon the rock"","" and there at that time was a threshing floor belonging to a young man of the Children of Israel. Dawud came to him and said: \""I have been commanded to build this place as a House for Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic.\"" The young man said to him: \""Has Allah commanded you to take it from me without my consent?\"" He said: \""No.\"" Then Allah revealed to Dawud (peace be upon him): \""I have placed the treasures of the earth in your hand"","" so satisfy him.\"" Dawud came to him and said: \""I have been commanded to obtain your consent. You shall have a qintar of gold for it.\"" He said: \""I have accepted"","" O Dawud. Is the House better"","" or the qintar?\"" He said: \""Rather"","" the House is better.\"" He said: \""Then satisfy me.\"" He said: \""You shall have three qintars.\"" He continued to press Dawud until he agreed to nine qintars. Al-'Abbas said: O Allah"","" I shall take no reward for it"","" for I have given it in charity upon the community of the Muslims. So 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted it from him and incorporated it into the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). [Da'if. Ibn 'Asakir 26/369]"""""
"11943","(11938) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us in Baghdad, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustuyah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Kamil al-'Attar narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Al-'Abbas had a house adjacent to the mosque in Madinah. 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Sell it to me"","" or gift it to me"","" so that I may incorporate it into the mosque.\"" He refused. He said: \""Appoint between me and you a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" So they appointed Ubayy ibn Ka'b as arbitrator between them. He ruled in favor of al-'Abbas over 'Umar. 'Umar said: \""There is no one among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) more courageous than you.\"" Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: \""Or more sincere in counsel to you than I?\"" Then he said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"","" has the hadith of Dawud reached you — that Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" commanded him to build the Bayt al-Maqdis"","" and he incorporated into it the house of a woman without her permission? When it reached the private quarters"","" Allah prevented him from building it. Dawud said: 'O my Lord"","" if You have prevented me from building it"","" then make it for those who come after me.'\"" Al-'Abbas said: \""Have you not already ruled in my favor regarding it"","" and it has become mine?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then I bear witness that I have dedicated it for the sake of Allah.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11944","(11939) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Ja'far al-Baqarhi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O Muslim women"","" let no neighbor belittle a gift for her neighbor"","" even if it be a sheep's hoof.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from 'Asim ibn 'Ali"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Sa'id.\n\n[Bukhari 2566. Muslim 1030]"""""
"11945","(11940) Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah al-'Absi narrated to us, Waqi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If I were given a forearm as a gift"","" I would accept it"","" and if I were invited to a shank"","" I would respond.\"" [Bukhari 2568]"""""
"11946","(11941) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-A'mash, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Shu'bah."
"11947","(11942) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, who said: She used to say: \By Allah"","" O son of my sister"","" we would look at the crescent"","" then the crescent"","" then the crescent — three crescents in two months — and no fire was ever lit in the houses of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" I said: \""O aunt"","" what sustained you?\"" She said: \""The two black things: dates and water — except that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had neighbors among the Ansar who had milch animals"","" and they would send some of their milk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" and he would give it to us to drink.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abdillah from Ibn Abi Hazim"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\n[Bukhari 2568. Muslim 2972]"""""
"11948","(11943) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The people would time their gifts for the day of 'A'ishah, seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Ibrahim ibn Musa from 'Abdah, and Muslim narrated it from Abu Kurayb from 'Abdah.\n\n[Bukhari 2581. Muslim 2441]"
"11949","(11944) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl narrated to us in Baghdad, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: that a man from the people of the desert whose name was Zahir ibn Haram used to bring gifts to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) from the desert, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would prepare provisions for him when he wished to depart. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Zahir is our desert-dweller"","" and we are his townsmen.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. [Sahih]"""""
"11950","(11945) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdillah al-Hurfi narrated to us in Baghdad, Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Shafi'i narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If I were given a shank as a gift"","" I would accept it"","" and if I were invited to a forearm"","" I would respond.\"" And he used to command us to give gifts as a means of maintaining ties among the people. He said: \""If only the people would embrace Islam"","" they would give gifts without being hungry.\"" [Sahih"","" up to his words \""I would respond.\"" Ahmad 13209. Tirmidhi 1338]"""""
"11951","(11946) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bukayr al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us: Ḍimām ibn Ismāʿīl al-Miṣrī narrated from Mūsā ibn Wardān, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Give gifts to one another"","" so that you may love one another.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" 594.]"""""
"11952","(11947) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī say: I heard Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī say regarding the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: \Give gifts to one another (tahādaw)"","" so that you may love one another (taḥābbū)\"": \""If it is pronounced with tashdīd (emphasis)"","" it derives from al-maḥabbah (love)"","" and if it is pronounced with takhfīf (lightness)"","" it derives from al-muḥābah (mutual affection).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11953","(11948) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and others from among the people of knowledge informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed them from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \Indeed"","" Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" had given her as a gift (naḥala) twenty wasq of freshly cut dates from his property at al-Ghābah. When death approached him"","" he said: 'By Allah"","" O my daughter"","" there is no one among the people whose prosperity after me is dearer to me than yours"","" and no one whose poverty after me is more grievous to me than yours. I had given you as a gift twenty wasq of my dates. If you had harvested them and taken possession of them"","" they would have been yours. However"","" they are the property of the heirs"","" and they are your two brothers and two sisters. Divide them according to the Book of Allah.' She said: 'O father"","" by Allah"","" even if it were such and such"","" I would have left it. It is only Asmāʾ. Who is the other one?' He said: 'The one in the womb of the daughter of Khārijah. I think she is a girl.'\""\n\nHe said: And Ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim"","" from his father"","" from ʿĀʾishah"","" to that effect.\n\nHe said: And Ibn Wahb informed us: I said: I heard Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān narrate that he heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad narrate likewise"","" except that he said: \""A piece of land called Thamrad"","" which was in her possession"","" but she had not taken hold of it.\""\n\n[Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ"","" 806.]"""""
"11954","(11949) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: A number of people of knowledge among them Mālik ibn Anas and Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed them from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, that he said: \What is the matter with men who give gifts to their children and then withhold them? If the son of one of them dies"","" he says: 'My property is in my possession; I have not given it to anyone.' And if he himself dies"","" he says: 'I had already given it to him.' Whoever gives a gift that the one to whom it was given has not taken possession of"","" so that if he dies it belongs to his heirs — then it is void.\""\n\n[Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ"","" 1475.]"""""
"11955","(11949) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn al-Sabbāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, to that effect.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11956","(11951) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar, from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \A gift (al-anḥāl) remains part of the estate (mīrāth) so long as it has not been taken into possession.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿUthmān"","" Ibn ʿUmar"","" and Ibn ʿAbbās"","" may Allah be pleased with them"","" that they said: \""A charitable gift (ṣadaqah) is not valid until it has been taken into possession.\"" And from Muʿādh ibn Jabal and Sharīḥ that they both used to not permit it until it had been taken into possession.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11957","(11952) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb said: Men from among the people of knowledge, among them Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and others, informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed them from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, that he said: \Whoever gives a gift to his young child who has not yet reached the age of taking possession"","" and he makes it public and calls witnesses over it"","" then it is valid"","" and his father is his guardian over it.\""\n\n[Mālik"","" 1503.]"""""
"11958","(11953) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā ibn Asad narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \What is the matter with people who give gifts to their children"","" and when one of them dies"","" he says: 'My property is in my possession"",""' and when he himself dies"","" he says: 'I had given it to my son.' There is no valid gift except one over which the child takes possession"","" to the exclusion of the father. If the child dies"","" it is inherited from him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11959","(11953) He said: And Abū Yaḥyā narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \That matter was referred to ʿUthmān"","" and he was of the view that the father may take possession on behalf of his child when they are minors.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11960","(11955) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Warrāq informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey"","" and I was riding a refractory young camel belonging to ʿUmar. It would overtake me and go ahead of the people"","" and ʿUmar would pull it back and restrain it. The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿUmar: 'Sell it to me.' He said: 'It is yours"","" O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Sell it to me.' So he sold it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: 'It is yours"","" O ʿAbd Allāh. Do with it as you wish.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Bukhārī"","" 2116; Muslim"","" 715.]"""""
"11961","(11956) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Warraq narrated to us: Thabit ibn Muhammad al-'Abid narrated to us: Mis'ir ibn Kidam narrated from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was in the mosque — I think he said, at forenoon (duha) — and he said to me: \Pray"",""\"" or he said"","" \""Pray two rak'ahs.\"" I owed him a debt"","" and he repaid me and gave me more.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Thabit ibn Muhammad. [Bukhari 443; Muslim 715]"""""
"11962","(11957) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Jabir ibn 'Abdillah say: I sold a camel to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he weighed (the payment) and gave me extra. Some of those dirhams remained with me until they were lost on the day of Harrah.\n\nBoth al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from the hadith of Shu'bah. [Sahih; narrated by al-Tayalisi 1831]"
"11963","(11958) Abu Ahmad 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakk narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanj narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taym informed me from 'Isa ibn Talhah ibn 'Ubaydillah from 'Umayr ibn Salamah al-Damr, who informed him from al-Bahz that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out intending Makkah while he was in a state of ihram. When he arrived at al-Rawha', a wild ass was found wounded. It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: \Leave it"","" for its owner will soon come.\"" Then al-Bahz"","" who was its owner"","" came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" do as you wish with this ass.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" and he divided it among the companions. Then he proceeded until he reached al-Athayyah"","" between al-Ruwaythah and al-'Arj"","" where a gazelle was found crouching in the shade with an arrow in it. He asserted that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded a man to stand by it so that no one would disturb it until the people had passed by.\n\nMuslim narrated al-Batin: that Husayn ibn 'Ali inherited bequests and gave them in charity before they were divided"","" and this was permitted.\n\n[Sahih; Malik in al-Muwatta' 1139]"""""
"11964","(11959) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us: Abu al-Hasan ibn Mahmud al-Marwaz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahd narrated to us: Hammam narrated from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas, who said: Anas gifted me half of his house. Abu Burdah said: \If it pleases you"","" take possession of it"","" for 'Umar ibn al-Khattab ruled regarding gifts (anhāl) that whatever has been taken possession of is valid"","" and whatever has not been taken possession of is inheritance.\"" So I called Yazid al-Rishk"","" and he divided it.\n\n[Sahih]"""""
"11965","(11960) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Malik narrated.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to me: Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Saffar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated — he said: I read to Malik — from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man to whom a lifetime gift (ʿumrā) is given for himself and his descendants"","" it belongs to the one to whom it was given"","" and it does not return to the one who gave it"","" because he gave a gift in which inheritance has taken effect.\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Shafi'i: \""It belongs to the one to whom it is given.\"" And the remainder is the same.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Muslim 4197]"""""
"11966","(11961) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated to us: Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated from Salih from Ibn Shihab, with its chain and meaning.\n\n[Sahih]"
"11967","(11962) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Zahid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Layth narrated.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharık and Ibn Milhan both said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever is given a lifetime gift (ʿumrā) for himself and his descendants"","" his statement has confirmed his right to it"","" and it belongs to the one to whom it was given and to his descendants.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"","" Qutaybah"","" and Muhammad ibn Rumh with this wording"","" except that Yahya ibn Yahya said at the beginning of his hadith: \""Any man to whom a lifetime gift (ʿumrā) is given"","" it is for him and his descendants.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: The narration of the group from al-Layth is as has been stated above.\n\n[Sahih]"""""
"11968","(11963) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqr' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to me: Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us: 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ibn Shihab informed me regarding the ruling on the ʿumrā from the hadith of Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, that Jabir ibn 'Abdillah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man to whom a lifetime gift (ʿumrā) is given for himself and his descendants\"" — he said: \""I have given it to you and to your descendants"","" as long as any of you remains.\"" So it belongs to the one to whom it was given"","" and it does not return to its original owner"","" because he gave a gift in which inheritance has taken effect.\n\nThe wording of both their hadiths is the same"","" except that in the hadith of Fulayh it says: \""in which inheritance takes effect.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam. [Sahih]"""""
"11969","(11964) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: The only ʿumrā that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permitted is when one says: \It is for you and your descendants.\"" But if he says: \""It is for you as long as you live"",""\"" then it returns to its original owner.\n\n[Sahih]"""""
"11970","(11965) And Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated it with the same. He added: Ma'mar said: \And al-Zuhri used to give fatwa according to it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih]"""""
"11971","(11966) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī in Kūfah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn Mūsā, informed us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a ruling regarding the ʿumrā (gift for life): that it belongs to the one to whom it was given and to his progeny, irrevocably. The giver has no right to stipulate any condition or exception therein. Abū Salamah said: Because he gave a gift in which inheritance became operative, and inheritance nullified his condition.\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Fudayk. In the narration of ʿUbayd Allāh it reads: \Whoever is given an ʿumrā"","" it belongs to him and to his progeny"","" irrevocably. The giver has no right to stipulate any condition or anything therein.\"" And he did not mention the statement of Abū Salamah.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11972","(11967) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh al-Miṣrī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to me; Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a ruling regarding the ʿumrā: that a man may give it to another man and to his progeny, and may stipulate an exception: \If your progeny ceases"","" then it shall return to me and to my progeny.\"" Indeed"","" it belongs to the one to whom it was given and to his progeny.\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿUqayl with the same meaning as the narration of these narrators. However"","" al-Awzāʿī contradicted them and narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11973","(11968) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd, that is Ibn Mazīd, informed me; my father narrated to me; al-Awzāʿī narrated to me; Ibn Shihāb narrated to me; ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is given an ʿumrā"","" it belongs to him and to his progeny. It shall be inherited by those who would inherit from his progeny.\""\n\nLikewise"","" Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated it from al-Awzāʿī"","" from al-Zuhrī"","" from Abū Salamah and ʿUrwah"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 3552]"""""
"11974","(11969) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥawārī narrated to us; al-Walīd narrated it. And Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated it from Abū Salamah, from Jābir, without restriction (muṭlaqan). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11975","(11970) Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Bayrūtī informed me; Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Shābūr narrated to me from Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Hishām narrated — both of them — from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The ʿumrā belongs to the one to whom it was given.\"" And in the narration of Shaybān: \""He gave a ruling regarding the ʿumrā that it belongs to the one to whom it was given.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym from Shaybān"","" and Muslim narrated it from two routes from Hishām al-Dastawāʾī. And with the same meaning"","" ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ narrated it from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh."""""
"11976","(11971) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who heard ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Hudbah narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Qatādah narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The ʿumrā is permissible (jāʾizah).\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Hammām.\n\nAnd Abū al-Zubayr narrated it from Jābir"","" as follows: [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11977","(11972) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Tamīmī informed me; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Hold on to your wealth and do not corrupt it. For whoever gives an ʿumrā"","" it belongs to the one to whom it was given"","" whether alive or dead"","" and to his progeny.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Aḥmad 1/1472]"""""
"11978","(11973) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Sufyān; Abū al-Zubayr informed me, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Hold on to your wealth; do not give it to anyone. Whoever is given something as an ʿumrā"","" it belongs to him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr and others from Wakīʿ from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11979","(11974) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū al-Aḥraz Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Jamīl al-Azdī in Ṭūs narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Khaythamah narrated to us; Abū Maʿmar narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh. He said: The Ansār used to give ʿumrā gifts to the Muhājirūn. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Hold on to your wealth; do not give it as ʿumrā. For whoever is given something"","" it belongs to him during his lifetime"","" and upon his death it belongs to his heirs.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith from his father from his grandfather. Likewise"","" Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated it from Abū al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11980","(11975) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: A woman in Madīnah gave her garden as an ʿumrā to her son. Then he died, and she died after him, leaving a son, while the one who had given the ʿumrā had other sons. The son of the woman who gave the ʿumrā said: \The garden has reverted to us.\"" The sons of the one to whom the ʿumrā was given said: \""Rather"","" it belonged to our father during his lifetime and after his death.\"" They disputed before Ṭāriq"","" the freedman of ʿUthmān. He called Jābir"","" and he testified before him that the Prophet (ﷺ) ruled that the ʿumrā belongs to its recipient. Ṭāriq gave judgment accordingly"","" then wrote to ʿAbd al-Malik informing him of that and of Jābir's testimony. ʿAbd al-Malik said: \""Jābir has spoken the truth.\"" Ṭāriq upheld the ruling"","" and that garden remained with the sons of the one to whom the ʿumrā was given"","" until this day.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Muslim 1625]"""""
"11981","(11976) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī both said: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, who heard Sulaymān ibn Yasār say: that Ṭāriq, who was an amīr in al-Madīnah, ruled regarding al-ʿumrā in favour of the heir, based on the statement of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11982","(11977) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī informed us, ʿUbayd ibn Ghannām informed us, Abū Bakr — (ḥ) and he said: al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj — (ḥ) and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, my father narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj from Ṭāriq al-Makkī from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a ruling concerning a woman from the Anṣār whose son had given her a date-palm garden. She died, and her son said: \I only gave it to her for her lifetime"",""\"" and he had other brothers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""It is hers during her lifetime and after her death.\"" He said: \""But I gave it as charity (ṣadaqah) upon her.\"" He said: \""That is even more binding upon you.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"","" similar to the narration of his son from him"","" though it is not strong. Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it differently"","" and that is mentioned in this chapter. [Ḍaʿīf — Abū Dāwūd 3557]"""""
"11983","(11978) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us from the original of his book, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān ibn Hishām said to me: \This one — meaning al-Zuhrī — does not leave us to eat anything without commanding us to perform wuḍūʾ from it.\"" I said: \""I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab about it"","" and he said: 'When you eat it"","" it is pure"","" so there is no wuḍūʾ upon you regarding it; but when it comes out"","" it is impure"","" so wuḍūʾ is required of you regarding it.'\"" He said: \""I see that you two have disagreed. Is there anyone in the city?\"" I said: \""Yes"","" the foremost man in the island of Arabia.\"" He said: \""Who?\"" I said: \""ʿAṭāʾ.\"" So he sent for him and he was brought. He said: \""These two have disagreed with me. What do you say?\"" He said: \""Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to me that they ate bread and meat with Abū Bakr"","" then he stood and prayed without performing wuḍūʾ.\"" He said to me: \""What do you say about al-ʿumrā?\"" I said: \""al-Naḍr ibn Anas narrated to me from Bishr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Al-ʿumrā is permissible (jāizah).'\"" He said: al-Zuhrī said: \""It is not al-ʿumrā until it is made for him and his descendants.\"" He said: \""What do you say"","" ʿAṭāʾ?\"" He said: \""Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Al-ʿumrā is permissible (jāizah).'\"" Al-Zuhrī said: \""The caliphs did not rule according to that.\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: \""ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān ruled according to it in such and such a case.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ in an abbreviated form with the two chains of narration"","" without the story. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11984","(11979) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah from al-Naḍr ibn Anas from Bishr ibn Nahīk from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Al-ʿumrā is permissible (jāizah).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah and Ibn Abī ʿArūbah"","" both from Qatādah.\n\n[Al-Bukhārī 2626"","" Muslim 1626]"""""
"11985","(11980) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr from Ṭāwūs from Ḥujr al-Madarī from Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ made al-ʿumrā for the heir.\n\nIbn Abī Najīḥ corroborated it from Ṭāwūs. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11986","(11981) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Al-ʿumrā is permissible (jāizah).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi]"""""
"11987","(11982) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, who said: I was with Ibn ʿUmar when a man from the people of the desert came to him and said: \I gave a she-camel to my son for his lifetime"","" and she has given birth to camels.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: \""She is his during his lifetime and after his death.\"" He said: \""But I gave it as charity (ṣadaqah) upon him.\"" He said: \""That is even more binding upon you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11988","(11983) He said: and Ibn ʿUyaynah informed me from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, similar to it, except that he said: \She gave birth abundantly and produced offspring\"" — thus it was narrated. Abū Sulaymān said: The correct wording is \""ḍannat"",""\"" meaning she gave birth abundantly.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This indicates that which was narrated from Ibn ʿUmar regarding:"""""
"11989","(11984) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar bequeathed to Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar her house. Ḥafṣah, may Allah be pleased with her, had given residence to the daughter of Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb for as long as she lived. When the daughter of Zayd passed away, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar took possession of the dwelling and considered it to be his. This was narrated regarding al-ʿāriyah (a loan for use) rather than al-ʿumrā, and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Mālik 1481]"
"11990","(11985) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ayyūb from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: I was present when Shurayḥ gave a ruling of al-ʿumrā for a blind man. The blind man said to him: \O Abū Umayyah"","" on what basis have you ruled in my favour?\"" Shurayḥ said: \""It is not I who have ruled for you"","" but Muḥammad ﷺ ruled for you forty years ago.\"" He said: \""Whoever is given something for his lifetime"","" it belongs to his heirs when he dies.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Umm lil-Shāfiʿī 4/65]"""""
"11991","(11986) Abū Ḥāziṃ al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Khamīrūyah informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Hushaym informed us, and Hishām and Manṣūr narrated on the authority of Ibn Sīrīn that a man granted another man a house as an *ʿumrā* (life grant) for his lifetime. The latter subsequently disputed over it and brought the matter before Sharīḥ. The one to whom the house had been granted as an *ʿumrā* was blind. Sharīḥ ruled in his favor and said: \Whoever is given ownership of something for his lifetime"","" it belongs to him in his lifetime and after his death.\"" The blind man said: \""How have you ruled for me"","" O Abū Umayyah?\"" He replied: \""It is not I who have ruled; rather"","" Allah decreed through the tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fifty years ago: 'Whoever is given ownership of something for his lifetime"","" it belongs to him and to his heirs after him.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11992","(11987) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Shaybān informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us orally, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of ʬāʾiẓ, on the authority of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not give *ʿumrā* and do not give *ruqbā*. Whoever is given something as an *ʿumrā* or as a *ruqbā*"","" it shall be subject to inheritance.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Umm"","" by al-Shāfiʿī 4/65]"""""
"11993","(11988) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Wāsiṭī informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed us, on the authority of Abī al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The *ʿumrā* is a valid grant for the one to whom it is given"","" and the *ruqbā* is a valid grant for the one to whom it is given.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11994","(11989) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ibn Jābir informed us, Ḥāmid ibn Yaḥyā informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Makhzūmī said: Shibl ibn ʿAbbād narrated to me, on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī said: I read to Maʿqil, on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, on the authority of Ṭāwūs, on the authority of Ḥujr, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever is given something as an *ʿumrā*"","" it belongs to the one to whom it was given"","" in his lifetime and after his death. And do not give *ruqbā*. Whoever gives something as a *ruqbā*"","" it shall be subject to its ruling.\"" And in the narration of Shibl: \""It shall be subject to inheritance.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 21989]"""""
"11995","(11990) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us. Abū ʿUbayd said: The meaning of *ʿumrā* is that a man says to another man: \This house is yours for your lifetime"",""\"" or he says to him: \""This house is yours for my lifetime.\"" He said: Ḥajjāj narrated to me"","" on the authority of Ibn Jurayj"","" on the authority of ʬāʾiẓ"","" regarding the interpretation of *ʿumrā*"","" something similar to that or close to it. Abū ʿUbayd said: As for *ruqbā*"","" Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to me"","" on the authority of Ḥajjāj ibn Abī ʿUthmān"","" who said: I asked Abū al-Zubayr about *ruqbā*"","" and he said: It is that a man says: \""If you die before me"","" it reverts to me"","" and if I die before you"","" it is yours.\"" He said: Ibn ʿUlayyah also narrated to me"","" on the authority of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"","" on the authority of Qatādah"","" who said: *Ruqbā* is that one says: \""Such and such belongs to so-and-so; if he dies"","" it belongs to so-and-so.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11996","(11991) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Jarrāḥ informed us, on the authority of ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā, on the authority of ʿUthmān ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujāhid, who said: *ʿUmrā* is that a man says to another man: \It is yours for as long as I live.\"" When he says that"","" it belongs to him and to his heirs. And *ruqbā* is that a person says: \""It belongs to the last of us two to remain alive.\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 3560]\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) held the old opinion based on the apparent meaning of what al-Zuhrī narrated"","" which is that he would make it for the recipient and his descendants. If he made it for him without mentioning his descendants"","" he said in one place: \""It is invalid"",""\"" and in another place he said: \""When the recipient of the *ʿumrā* dies"","" it reverts to the one who granted it.\"" Then he adopted the new opinion in light of the other narrations which indicate that when he grants it to him for his lifetime and delivers it to him"","" it belongs to him and to his descendants. This is the established position. And likewise regarding *ruqbā*."""""
"11997","(11992) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us orally, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. I read to Mālik, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, on the authority of Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad ibn al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, both narrating to him, on the authority of al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: His father brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \I have given this son of mine a slave boy who belonged to me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Have you given the same to all your children?\"" He said: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Then take it back.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf"","" on the authority of Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Bukhārī 2587. Muslim 1623]"""""
"11998","(11993) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn Shaybān informed us, Sufyān narrated, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr and Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, that they both heard al-Nuʿmān say: \My father gave me a slave boy"","" and my mother commanded me to go with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and have him witness it.\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Have you given the same to all your children?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then return him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" on the authority of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11999","(11994) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Baghdad, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān informed us, Tamīm informed us, Muḥammad informed us, Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar informed us, Abū ʿAwānah narrated, on the authority of Ḥuṣayn, on the authority of ʿĀmir, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr say while he was on the pulpit: \My father gave me a gift"","" so ʿAmrah bint Rāwāḥah said to him: 'I will not be pleased until you make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a witness.' So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'I have given the son of ʿAmrah bint Rāwāḥah a gift"","" and she has commanded me to make you a witness"","" O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Have you given the same to all your children?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Fear Allah and be just among your children.' He said: So he went back and took back his gift.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar"","" and Muslim narrated it through two other chains from Ḥuṣayn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12000","(11995) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Naṣr al-Dāraburdī informed us in Marw, Abū al-Muwajjih informed us, ʿAbdān informed us, ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī narrated, on the authority of al-Shaʿbī, on the authority of al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: \My father asked my mother for some gift for me from his wealth"","" but she deferred it for a year. Then it occurred to him"","" so he gifted it to me. But she said: 'I will not be pleased until you make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a witness to what you have gifted to my son.' So he took my hand—I was a young boy at that time—and brought me to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" the mother of this boy is the daughter of Rāwāḥah. She has been arguing with me for a year over a gift for this son of mine. Now it has occurred to me"","" so I have gifted it to him"","" and she would like you to be a witness"","" O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'O Bashīr"","" do you have any children other than this child of yours?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then do not make me a witness'—or he said: 'I do not bear witness to injustice.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of ʿAbdān"","" and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Bishr"","" on the authority of Abī Ḥayyān"","" and he said at the end of it: \""Then do not make me a witness"","" for I do not bear witness to injustice.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12001","(11996) Abu Bakr ibn Furak narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that his father gave him a gift and wished to have the Prophet (ﷺ) witness it. He said: \Have you given all your children what you have given him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""It is a right upon you that you be just among your children"","" just as it is a right upon them that they treat you with kindness.\"" Mujalid is alone in narrating this wording. [Sahih by virtue of other narrations. Up to his statement \""gave him"",""\"" it was narrated by al-Tayalisi.]"""""
"12002","(11997) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Harashi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated from Jabir, who said: The wife of Bashir said: \Give my son your servant and have the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) witness it.\"" So he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""The daughter of so-and-so is asking me to give her son my servant"","" and she said: 'Have the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) witness it.'\"" He said: \""Does he have siblings?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Have you given all of them the same as you have given him?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""This is not proper"","" and I do not witness injustice.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus. And 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated it from Zuhayr with the same meaning"","" except that he said: \""I do not witness except upon what is right.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12003","(11998) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated it. [Sahih]"
"12004","(11999) Abu Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari narrated in Baghdad, Isma'il al-Saffar narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, Sulayman, i.e., ibn Harb, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Hajjib ibn al-Mufaddl ibn al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from his father, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir delivering a speech, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Be just among your children. Be just among your children.\"" The wording of both is the same. [Sahih by virtue of other narrations.]"""""
"12005","(12000) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz and Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated from Sa'id ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Be equal among your children in giving. Were I to favor anyone"","" I would favor the women.\"" [Sahih by virtue of other narrations. Up to \""in giving.\""]"""""
"12006","(12001) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us, Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri narrated in Makkah, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Za'farani narrated to us, Rabi'i ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ulayyah narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: My father brought me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" bear witness that I have given al-Nu'man such-and-such from my wealth.\"" He said: \""Have you given all your sons what you have given al-Nu'man?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then have someone other than me witness this. Would it not please you that they be equal toward you in kindness?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""Then no.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih through various routes from Dawud ibn Abi Hind. And al-Mughirah narrated from al-Sha'bi: \""Would it not please you that they be equal to you in kindness and gentleness?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then have someone other than me witness this.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12007","(12002) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrating the entire story. At the end of it, he reported from the Prophet (ﷺ): \I do not witness this. This is injustice. Have someone other than me witness this. Be just among your children in giving"","" just as you would love them to be just toward you in kindness and gentleness.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12008","(12003) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir narrating the entire story. At the end of it, he reported from the Prophet (ﷺ): \I do not witness this. This is injustice. Have someone other than me witness this. Be just among your children in giving"","" just as you would love them to be just toward you in kindness and gentleness.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12009","(12004) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us, Qasim ibn Zakariya al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn 'Isa al-Bistami narrated to us, Azhar narrated from Ibn 'Awn, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: My father gave me a gift, then he brought me to the Prophet (ﷺ) to have him witness it. He said: \Have you given all your sons this?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Do you not wish from them the same kindness that you wish from this one?\"" He said: \""Of course.\"" He said: \""Then I will not witness.\"" Ibn 'Awn said: I narrated this to Muhammad"","" i.e."","" ibn Sirin"","" and he said: \""We were only narrated that he said: 'Be close (in fairness) among your children.'\"" [Sahih]\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn 'Uthman al-Nawfali from Azhar ibn Sa'd.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) favored 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) with a gift.\n\nThe Sheikh said: And this is what Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us"","" Abu Muhammad al-Muzani narrated to us"","" 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us"","" Abu al-Yaman narrated to us"","" Shu'ayb narrated from al-Zuhri"","" who narrated to me: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated that 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) gave me twenty wasq of freshly picked dates from his wealth. When his death approached"","" he sat"","" wrapped himself in his garment"","" pronounced the tashahhud"","" and then said: \""Now then"","" O my dear daughter"","" the dearest of people to me in wealth after me is you. I had given you twenty wasq of freshly picked dates from my wealth. By Allah"","" I wish you had taken them and harvested them. But today it is the wealth of the heirs"","" and they are your two brothers and your two sisters.\"" She said: \""O Father"","" this is Asma'—who is the other?\"" He said: \""The one in the womb of the daughter of Kharijah—I think she is a girl.\"" She said: \""Had you given me such-and-such"","" I would have returned it to you.\"" [Da'if]\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: 'Umar favored 'Asim ibn 'Umar with something he gave him"","" and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf favored the children of Umm Kulthum."""""
"12010","(12005) Abu Zakariya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated from Bukayr ibn al-Ashaj, from Nafi': that Ibn 'Umar allocated three or four equal shares to some of his children over others. [Da'if]"
"12011","(12006) Bukayr said, and al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī narrated to me: that he and Ibn ʿUmar set out until they came to a man of the Anṣār and bargained with him for a piece of land of his, and they purchased it from him. Then a man came to him and said, \I have seen that you purchased a piece of land and gave it in charity.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said"","" \""This land belongs to my son Wāqid"","" for he is a poor man; he (the Prophet ﷺ) gave it to him to the exclusion of his other children.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12012","(12007) Bukayr said, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to me: that his father used to give gifts to some of his children to the exclusion of others.\n\nHe said, and Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb ibn Bashīr ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to me from ʿUmar ibn al-Munkadir that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Every possessor of wealth has the greatest right over his wealth.\"" Ibn Wahb said: \""He may do with it as he wishes.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12013","(12008) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Sarrāj narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd reported to us from Ibn Shihāb from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad ibn al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: My father brought me to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \I have given this son of mine a slave as a gift.\"" He said"","" \""Have you given gifts to all your sons?\"" He said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Then take it back.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. It has already been mentioned in the narrations of Mālik from Ibn Shihāb regarding this hadith"","" where he said: \""Then return it.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12014","(12009) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim narrated to me from Ṭāwūs, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for anyone to give a gift and then take it back"","" except for a father.\"" This is a mursal narration"","" though it has also been narrated in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Authentic through other chains]"""""
"12015","(12010) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar, who both said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not fitting for anyone to give a gift and then take it back"","" except for a father regarding what he gives to his child. The likeness of the one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats until it is full"","" then vomits"","" and then returns to its vomit.\""\n\n[Authentic. Aḥmad 2120. Abū Dāwūd 3539]"""""
"12016","(12011) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us, mentioning it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: from the Prophet ﷺ: \It is not permissible for a man to give a gift or bestow a grant and then take it back"","" except for a father regarding what he gives to his child.\"" Then he mentioned its meaning.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Musaddad."""""
"12017","(12012) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū Maʿmar al-Minqarī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us: ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \None may take back his gift except a father"","" and the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\""\n\nSimilarly"","" Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān and Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it from ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal. And similarly"","" it was narrated from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr from Maṭar and ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal from ʿAmr. [Authentic. Aḥmad 6705. Ibn Mājah 2378]"""""
"12018","(12013) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṭaybī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tinnīsī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr from Maṭar and ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A man shall not take back his gift"","" except a father from among his children"","" and the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\""\n\nAnd it is possible that ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated it from both sources together. Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim is a ḥujjah (authoritative narrator) and ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal is trustworthy (thiqah). And it was narrated from Maṭar and ʿĀmir something similar to the narration of ʿĀmir alone. [Authentic through other chains]"""""
"12019","(12014) And from what has reached us from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from Abī Qilābah, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote: \A man may take back from his child what he gave him"","" so long as the child has not died"","" or the gift has not been destroyed"","" or a debt has not fallen upon it.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12020","(12015) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim narrated to me from Ṭāwūs that the Prophet ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a giver to take back what he has given as a gift"","" except for a father from among his children.\""\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"","" though we have narrated it in a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Authentic through other chains]"""""
"12021","(12016) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ismā'īl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wārith ibn Sa'īd narrated to us, Ḥusayn al-Mu'allim narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbās, who both said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible for a man to give a gift and then take it back"","" except for a father regarding what he gives to his child. The likeness of the one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like the likeness of a dog that eats until it is full"","" then vomits"","" and then returns to its vomit.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12022","(12017) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Īsā narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and Muslim narrated it through another route from Wuhayb.\n\n[Bukhārī 2089"","" Muslim 1622]"""""
"12023","(12018) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Tamtām and Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq both said: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Abān, Hammām, and Shu'bah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed me, 'Alī ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Shu'bah and Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from Sa'īd ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn 'Abbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to its vomit.\"" Ismā'īl added: Hammām said: Qatādah said: \""And I do not know the vomit to be anything but ḥarām.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm from Hishām and Shu'bah"","" and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar from Shu'bah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12024","(12019) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muḥammad al-Qūmisī narrated to us, Abū Nu'aym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Dīnār al-Mu'addil informed us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Abū Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit. We are not to be compared to an evil example.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nu'aym. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12025","(12020) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū 'Amr ibn Najayd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us, 'Īsā ibn Yūnus narrated from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to accept gifts and reciprocate for them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Musaddad from 'Īsā ibn Yūnus. [Bukhārī 2585]"
"12026","(12021) The Shaykh al-Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated by dictation, and the Faqīh Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ma'rūf narrated by recitation upon him, both saying: Abū 'Amr Ismā'īl ibn Najayd al-Sulamī informed us, Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, Abū 'Āṣim al-Nabīl narrated to us, Ibn 'Ajlān narrated from al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah: that a man presented a she-camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he reciprocated for it with six young camels. The man was displeased with them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Who will excuse me regarding so-and-so? He presented me with a she-camel as a gift — and it is as though I can see it in the face of some of my family — and I reciprocated for it with six young camels"","" yet he has shown displeasure. By Allah"","" I have resolved that I shall not accept any gift unless it be from a Qurashī"","" or an Anṣārī"","" or a Thaqafī"","" or a Dawsī.\""\n\nAbū 'Āṣim said: And Abū Hurayrah was a Dawsī. However"","" this is in another ḥadīth; this is the wording of the Faqīh's ḥadīth"","" and the Imām did not mention the statement of Abū 'Āṣim. And Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsār narrated it from Sa'īd al-Maqburī"","" from his father"","" from Abū Hurayrah"","" in an abridged form.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih]"""""
"12027","(12022) Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Hāshimī in Kūfah informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us, 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us, Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān narrated: I heard Sālim ibn 'Abd Allāh narrating from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever gives a gift"","" it is more rightfully his"","" so long as he has not been reciprocated for it.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" 'Alī ibn Sahl ibn al-Mughīrah narrated it from 'Ubayd Allāh"","" and it is an error. [Munkar]"""""
"12028","(12023) What is firmly established from Ḥanẓalah, from Sālim ibn 'Abd Allāh, from his father, from 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, is: \Whoever gives a gift for the sake of Allah"","" then it is his. And whoever gives a gift seeking its reward"","" then he may take it back if he is not satisfied with it.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both narrated it to us"","" saying: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us"","" Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us"","" Ibn Wahb informed us: I heard Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān al-Jumaḥī say: I heard Sālim ibn 'Abd Allāh say"","" from his father"","" from 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" that.\n\nAnd it has also been said: from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Mūsā"","" from Ibrāhīm ibn Ismā'īl ibn Mujammi'. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12029","(12024) As Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed me, Sa'īd ibn Mas'ūd narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Ismā'īl, from 'Amr ibn Dīnār, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \The giver is more entitled to his gift"","" so long as he has not been reciprocated.\"" And this text with this chain is more appropriate. Ibrāhīm ibn Ismā'īl is weak (ḍa'īf) according to the scholars of ḥadīth"","" and 'Amr ibn Dīnār's narration from Abū Hurayrah is disconnected (munqaṭi'). And what is firmly established is: [Ḍa'īf]"""""
"12030","(12025) From 'Amr ibn Dīnār, from Sālim, from his father, from 'Umar, who said: \Whoever gives a gift and is not reciprocated for it"","" he is more entitled to his gift"","" except for a kinsman (dhī raḥim).\""\n\nAbū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated it to us"","" Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us"","" Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us"","" Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us"","" Sufyān narrated from 'Amr ibn Dīnār"","" from Sālim"","" from his father"","" from 'Umar"","" and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhārī said: \""This is more authentic (aṣaḥḥ).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12031","(12026) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us in Baghdad — Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāshimī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak — from Ḥammād ibn Salamah — from Qatādah — from al-Ḥasan — from Samurah — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When a gift is given to a maḥram relative"","" he shall not return it.\"" We have recorded it only with this chain of narration"","" and it is not strong. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12032","(12027) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤabd al-Ḥakam narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us — Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī informed me that ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to him from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \The parable of one who seeks to reclaim what he has given as a gift is like that of a dog that vomits and then eats its own vomit. So when the donor seeks to reclaim his gift"","" let him be stopped. Let him be made known what he has reclaimed"","" and then let what he originally gave be returned to him.\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 3540]"""""
"12033","(12028) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us that he heard Mālik ibn Anas saying — Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrated to me that Abā Ghafūrān ibn Ṭarīf al-Murī informed him from Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever gives a gift for the purpose of strengthening ties of kinship or as an act of charity"","" he shall not take it back. But whoever gives a gift intending thereby a reward [in return]"","" then he is entitled to his gift — he may reclaim it if he is not satisfied with it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 1477]"""""
"12034","(12029) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashr narrated to us — Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ both said — Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of the people of Madinah, who used to say regarding every gift given by a person of means: \There is no compensation in it and no reward.\"" And they said: \""The reward is for the one who gives his gift seeking reward — he is more entitled to his gift so long as he is not compensated from it.\"" And ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" judged accordingly. And ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ said in his narration: \""He is more entitled to his gift so long as he is not compensated from it and so long as it is not broken.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12035","(12030) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Bashr narrated to us — ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me — a man from my people narrated to me — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is given a gift and finds [the means]"","" let him reciprocate with it. And if he does not find [the means]"","" let him praise [the giver]. Whoever praises it has shown gratitude"","" and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: And Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated it from ʿUmārah"","" from Sharḥabīl"","" from Jābir. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12036","(12031) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Zāhid al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Baḥr al-Barrī narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Saylaḥīnī informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah — from Sharḥabīl al-Anṣārī — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever is done a favour and finds [the means]"","" let him requite it. And if he does not find [the means]"","" let him praise it. For whoever praises it has shown gratitude"","" and whoever conceals it has been ungrateful. And whoever adorns himself with that which he was not given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12037","(12032) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Tamtām narrated to us — Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Muslim narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated from Abū Hurayrah — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \He does not thank Allah who does not thank the people.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. And likewise Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and others narrated it from al-Rabīʿ ibn Muslim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 7495. Abū Dāwūd 4811]"""""
"12038","(12033) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sharīk al-ʿĀmirī — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAdī al-Kindī — from al-Ashʿath ibn Qays, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \The most grateful of people to Allah is the most grateful of them to the people.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 22182]"""""
"12039","(12034) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us — Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us — al-Anṣārī narrated to me — Ḥumayd narrated — from Anas, who said: The Muhājirūn said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" we have not seen any people like the people we have come to in Madinah — none more generous in spending from abundance"","" nor more gracious in sharing from little. They have spared us the burden of provisions and included us in their comfort. We fear that they will take all the reward.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Not so — so long as you praise them and invoke Allah's blessings upon them.\"" [Aḥmad 13106. Al-Tirmidhī 2487]"""""
"12040","(12035) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Ḥammād narrated — from Thābit — from Anas, that the Muhājirūn said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" the Anṣār have taken all the reward.\"" He ﷺ said: \""No — so long as you invoke Allah's blessings upon them and praise them.\"" [Al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad 217]"""""
"12041","(12036) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us. ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqiyy narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣalt narrated to us. Mandal ibn ʿAlīyy narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a gift is presented to a person and there are people present with him"","" then they are partners in it.\""\n\nThat has also been narrated from another chain from ʿAmr"","" though there is some discussion regarding it. [Weak]"""""
"12042","(12037) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Manṣūr al-Mudhakkir narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn Dāwūd al-Simnāniyy narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Sarīyy narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a gift is given to a person and there are people present with him"","" then they are partners in it.\""\n\nAl-Azharī also narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" mentioning it as a statement of Ibn ʿAbbās"","" stopped (mawqūf)"","" not raised (marfūʿ)"","" and that is more correct. [Good]"""""
"12043","(12038) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us. Al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAlīyy ibn Shāfiʿ informed me. ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥasan ibn Ḥasan informed me from more than one of his household, and I think he said Zayd ibn ʿAlīyy said: Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), gave charity from her wealth upon Banī Hāshim and Banī al-Muṭṭalib, and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) gave charity upon them and included others alongside them. [Authentic. Al-Umm of al-Shāfiʿī, 4/57]"
"12044","(12039) With his chain, al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father: He used to drink from the water stations that the people had set up between Makkah and Madīnah. I said — or it was said to him — and he said: \Only the obligatory Ṣadaqah has been forbidden for us.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12045","(12040) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghāniyy narrated to us. Abū al-Yamān narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us. Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us. ʿAlīyy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us. Abū al-Yamān informed us. Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī. Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give me gifts, and I would say: \Give it to someone more in need than me.\"" Until one time he gave me wealth"","" and I said: \""Give it to someone more in need than me.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \""Take it and keep it or give it in charity. And whatever comes to you of this wealth while you are neither covetous nor asking for it"","" then take it; and whatever does not"","" then do not let your soul pursue it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Bukhārī 1473"","" Muslim 1045]"""""
"12046","(12041) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us. Ibn Wahb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me. Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us. ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us. Abū al-Ṭāhir informed us. Ibn Wahb informed me. ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh, from his father: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb gifts, and ʿUmar would say to him: \Give it"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" to someone more in need than me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Take it and keep it or give it in charity. And whatever comes to you of this wealth while you are neither covetous nor asking for it"","" then take it; and whatever does not"","" then do not let your soul pursue it.\"" Sālim said: For that reason"","" Ibn ʿUmar would not ask the people for anything"","" nor would reject anything that was given to him.\n\nʿAmr said: And Ibn Shihāb narrated to me the same from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd"","" from Ḥuwayṭib ibn al-ʿUzzā"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Saʿdiyy"","" from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir. [Authentic]"""""
"12047","(12042) The Shaykh al-Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us. Isḥāq ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us. Sharīk narrated from Jāmiʿ ibn Abī Rāshid, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: There was a man from the people of Shām who was held in high regard. ʿUmar said to him: \Why do the people of Shām love you?\"" He said: \""I fight alongside them in battle and I share my wealth with them.\"" ʿUmar offered him ten thousand. He said: \""Take it and use it to support your military expeditions.\"" He said: \""I have no need of it.\"" ʿUmar said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) offered me wealth less than what I have offered you"","" and I said to him the same as you have said to me. He said to me: 'When Allah gives you wealth that you have not asked for and your soul has not coveted"","" then accept it"","" for it is provision that Allah has directed to you.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"12048","(12043) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us. My father and Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth informed us. Al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from ʿAmr, from al-Muṭṭalib: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir sent provisions and clothing to ʿĀʾishah. She said to his messenger: \O my son"","" I do not accept anything from anyone.\"" When he left"","" she said: \""Bring him back.\"" So they brought him back"","" and she said: \""I remembered something the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me.\"" She said: He said: \""O ʿĀʾishah"","" whoever gives you a gift without you asking for it"","" then accept it"","" for it is provision that Allah has presented to you.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12049","(12044) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us. Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Thābit, from Abū Rāfiʾ, that Abū Hurayrah said: \There is no person among the people who presents me with a gift except that I accept it. As for begging"","" I never used to beg.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12050","(12045) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us. Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us. Al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Mālik narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah: The Prophet (ﷺ) entered, and she brought him bread and the condiments of the house. He said: \Did I not see a pot of meat?\"" She said: \""That is something that was given in charity to Barīrah.\"" He said: \""It is charity for her"","" and it is a gift for us.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Bukhārī 1495"","" Muslim 1074]"""""
"12051","(12046) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad al-Faqīh informed us in Ṭabarān: Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr, the grandson of Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr, narrated to us: My grandfather Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from his father from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she purchased Barīrah from a group of the Anṣār, and they stipulated the right of walāʾ (clientage). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The walāʾ belongs to the one who confers the favour of manumission.\"" She said: \""And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave her the choice"","" and her husband was a slave.\"" And Barīrah gifted some meat to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"","" so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""It is charity (ṣadaqah) for her"","" and it is a gift (hadiyyah) for us.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Zāʾidah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12052","(12047) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Quṭn ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qushayrī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād from Abū Hurayrah who said: \When food was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" he would ask: 'Is it a gift (hadiyyah) or charity (ṣadaqah)?' If it was said: 'Charity"",""' he would say to his companions: 'Eat"",""' and he would not eat. And if it was said: 'A gift"",""' he would stretch out his hand and eat with them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān. [Bukhārī 2576"","" Muslim 1077]"""""
"12053","(12048) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾi narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Salām narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Muslim narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ), when food was brought to him, would ask about it. If it was said: \A gift"",""\"" he would eat from it. And if it was said: \""Charity"",""\"" he would not eat from it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Salām. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12054","(12049) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Abū Aḥmad Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: Qays ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Maslamah ibn ʿAlqamah narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Salamah al-ʿIjlī from Salmān al-Fārisī who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a vessel containing bread and meat. He said: 'What is this"","" O Salmān?' I said: 'Charity.' So he did not eat and said to his companions: 'Eat.' Then I came to him with a vessel containing bread and meat. He said: 'What is this"","" O Salmān?' I said: 'A gift.' So he ate and said: 'We eat the gift"","" but we do not eat charity.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12055","(12050) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated. He said: I read to Mālik from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him about lost property (luqaṭah). He said: 'Recognise its container (ʿifāṣ) and its binding (wikāʾ)"","" then announce it for a year. If its owner comes"","" give it to him; otherwise"","" it is your affair.' He said: 'What about a lost sheep?' He said: 'It is for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf.' He said: 'What about a lost camel?' He said: 'What concern is it of yours? It has its water-skin and its hooves; it goes to water and eats trees until its Lord finds it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf and others from Mālik. [Bukhārī 2372"","" Muslim 1722]"""""
"12056","(12051) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about lost property"","" and he said: 'Announce it for a year. If its owner comes"","" give it to him; otherwise"","" spend it.'\""\n\nBoth [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12057","(12052) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾi narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī informed us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, that he heard Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, a companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), say: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about lost gold and silver"","" and he said: 'Recognise its binding and its container"","" then announce it for a year. If it is not recognised"","" spend it"","" and let it be a deposit (wadīʿah) with you. If its claimant ever comes"","" return it to him.'\""\n\nBoth [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12058","(12053) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed me: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Isḥāq from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd from his father Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī that he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a lost sheep"","" and he said: 'It is for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf.' He was asked about a camel"","" and his face became red with anger"","" and he said: 'It has its water-skin and its hooves; it goes to water and grazes on trees.' He was asked about expenses"","" and he said: 'Announce it for a year. If its owner comes"","" return it to him. Otherwise"","" recognise its binding and its container"","" then include it in your wealth. If its owner comes"","" return it to him.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12059","(12054) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān narrated from Abū al-Naḍr from Busr ibn Saʿīd from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about lost property"","" and he said: 'Announce it for a year. If it is not recognised"","" then recognise its container and its binding"","" then eat it. If its owner comes"","" return it to him.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12060","(12055) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Shuʿbah informed me: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated. He said: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafalah say: \I was on an expedition and found a whip"","" so I took it. Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah said to me: 'Throw it away.' I refused. We completed our expedition"","" then I performed Ḥajj and passed through Madīnah"","" where I met Ubayy ibn Kaʿb. I mentioned that to him"","" and he said to me: 'I found a purse during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) containing a hundred dīnārs"","" and I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said to me: \""Announce it for a year.\"" So I announced it for a year but found no one who recognised it. I returned to him"","" and he said: \""Announce it for a year.\"" I announced it"","" then returned to him"","" and he said: \""Announce it for another year.\"" I announced it"","" then returned to him. On the fourth occasion he said: \""Remember its quantity"","" its receptacle"","" and its binding. If its owner comes"","" give it to him; otherwise"","" enjoy it.'\"" Salamah said: \""I do not know whether he said 'Announce it for three years' or 'for a year.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ādam"","" and Salamah's statement is not in the ḥadīth of Sulaymān. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"","" and Muslim narrated it from another chain from Shuʿbah. [Bukhārī 3437"","" Muslim 1723]"""""
"12061","(12056) And it was narrated by Wakīʿ from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said at the end of it: \If its owner comes"","" then give it to him; otherwise"","" it is like your property.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī and Abū Bakr al-Warrāq informed us — they said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān"","" and he mentioned it with its meaning"","" without the statement of Salamah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"","" and ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated it from Sufyān"","" and he said in the hadith: \""Otherwise"","" make use of it.\"" And al-Aʿmash narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"","" and he said: \""Make use of it.\"" And Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"","" and he said: \""Then fulfill your need with it.\"" And Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl"","" and he said: \""And make use of it.\"" All of that refers to a single meaning."""""
"12062","(12057) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — Shuʿbah said: I heard Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrating from Yazīd ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār al-Mujāshiʿī, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever finds a lost item"","" let him have two just witnesses or one just witness testify"","" and let him not conceal it or hide it. If its owner comes"","" then he has the greater right to it; otherwise"","" it is the wealth of Allah"","" which He gives to whom He wills.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Ṭayālisī 11177]"""""
"12063","(12058) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he was asked about the lost item, and he said: \That which is found on a public road or in a well-known settlement — announce it for one year. If its owner comes"","" then return it to him. If he does not come"","" then it is yours. And that which is found in ruined places — in it and in buried treasure"","" one-fifth is due.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Sijistānī 1710]"""""
"12064","(12059) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us — Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr — ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me, from ʿAmr and ʿĀṣim, the two sons of Sufyān ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabīʿah, that Sufyān ibn ʿAbdullāh found a pouch and brought it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \Announce it for one year. If it is recognized"","" then so be it; otherwise"","" it is yours.\"" It was not recognized. Then he met him the following season and mentioned it to him. ʿUmar said: \""It is yours"","" for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with that.\"" He said: \""I have no need for it.\"" So ʿUmar took it and placed it in the public treasury.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that a woman asked her about the lost item"","" and she said: \""Make use of it.\"" [Ḥasan. al-Dārimī 2599. al-Nasāʾī in al-Kubrā 5787]"""""
"12065","(12060) Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed me — al-Dāwaradī narrated from Sharīk ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Namir, from ʬāʾ ibn Yassār, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), that he found a dīnār during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered him to announce it, but no one claimed it. Then he ordered him to consume it. Then its owner came, and he ordered him to compensate him.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) is among those upon whom charity is forbidden, for he is of the Banū Hāshim. [Ḥasan. al-Umm of al-Shāfiʿī 4/72]"
"12066","(12061) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī related as a ḥikāyah from a man, from Shuʿbah, from Abū Qays, who said: I heard Huzayl saying: I saw ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, when a man came to him with a sealed bundle and said: \I have announced it"","" and I found no one to recognize it.\"" He said: \""Make use of it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And such is the established Sunnah from the Prophet ﷺ. And they narrated a hadith from ʿĀmir"","" from his father"","" from ʿAbdullāh"","" that he purchased a slave woman"","" and her owner left"","" so he gave her price in charity and said: \""O Allah"","" on behalf of her owner. If he dislikes her"","" then she is mine and the liability is upon me.\"" Then he said: \""And this is what is done with the lost item.\"" But they contradicted the Sunnah regarding the lost item for which there is no proof"","" and they contradicted the hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd"","" which agrees with the Sunnah and is established among them"","" and they used this hadith as evidence while contradicting it in the very matter it addresses.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) from his own statement that which agrees with the position of the Iraqis."""""
"12067","(12062) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Hārūn informed us orally — Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us — Abū ʿUmar Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, that a man from Banū Ruʾās found a pouch and brought it to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \I found a pouch containing dirhams"","" and I have announced it"","" but we found no one to recognize it. I had hoped that no one would come to recognize it.\"" He said: \""Give it in charity. If its owner comes and is pleased"","" then he shall have the reward. If he is not pleased"","" you shall compensate him"","" and the reward shall be yours.\"" ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah is not strong.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" in a marfūʿ narration"","" the permissibility of consuming it"","" and it has been narrated with sound"","" connected chains from the Prophet ﷺ. And the established Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more deserving of being followed. And success is by Allah. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12068","(12063) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ, that a man found a lost item and came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and said: \I have found a lost item — what do you think?\"" Ibn ʿUmar said to him: \""Announce it.\"" He said: \""I have done so.\"" He said: \""Do more.\"" He said: \""I have done so.\"" He said: \""I do not command you to consume it. If you wished"","" you could have left it.\"" Abū Saʿīd added in his narration.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn ʿUmar"","" perhaps he had not heard the hadith from the Prophet"""""
"12069","(12064) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Qabīṣah narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar being asked about the lost item, and he said: \Hand it over to the amīr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12070","(12065) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥakam ibn Aʿyan al-Miṣrī informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Mālik ibn Anas, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, Sufyān ibn Saʿīd al-Thawrī, and others, that Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to them from Yazīd, the mawlā of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, and he asked him about the lost item. He said: \Recognize its container and its covering"","" then announce it for one year. If its owner comes"","" then it is his; otherwise"","" it is your affair.\"" He said: \""What about stray sheep?\"" He said: \""They are yours"","" or for your brother"","" or for the wolf.\"" He said: \""What about stray camels?\"" He said: \""They have their shoes and their water-skins; they come to water and eat trees until their Lord meets them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ] al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik and al-Thawrī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb from the three of them."""""
"12071","(12066) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Abdillāh al-Ṣūfī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Rabiʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd, the freed client of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhaniyy: that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lost property (al-luqaṭah). He said: \Make it known for one year. Then identify its cord and its covering. Then spend from it. If its owner comes"","" then return it to him.\"" The man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about lost sheep?\"" He said: \""Take it"","" for it is either for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about lost camels?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until his two cheeks turned red — or his face turned red. He said: \""What concern is it of yours? It has its hoof and its water-skin"","" until it meets its owner.\"" And Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb said: \""Leave it until it meets its owner.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and Qutaybah and ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12072","(12067) Abū Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, and Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī narrated to us; they said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr Qashmard informed us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Yazīd, the freed client of al-Munbaʿith, that he heard Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhaniyy, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about lost gold or silver. He said: \Identify its cord and its covering"","" then make it known for one year. If it is not recognized"","" then spend from it"","" and let it be a deposit (wadīʿah) with you. If its claimant ever comes"","" then return it to him.\"" He asked him about lost camels. He said: \""What concern is it of yours? Leave it. It has its hoof and its water-skin; it comes to the water and eats from the trees until its owner finds it.\"" He asked about the sheep. He said: \""Take it"","" for it is either for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways from Sulaymān"","" and Muslim narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12073","(12068) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr; ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me from his father from his grandfather. He said: I heard a man from Muzaynah ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and I was listening — about lost camels. He said: \It has its water-skin and its hoof; the wolf does not eat it. It comes to the water and eats from the trees. Leave it in its place until its seeker comes.\"" He said: \""What about lost sheep?\"" He said: \""It is for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf. Gather it until its seeker comes.\"" He said: \""Lost property (al-luqaṭah) that we find?\"" He said: \""That which is in inhabited areas and well-trodden paths — make it known for one year. If its seeker comes"","" return it to it; otherwise"","" it is yours.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about that which is found in a ruined"","" desolate village?\"" He said: \""In it and in buried treasure (al-rikāz) is the fifth (khums).\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith and Hishām ibn Saʿd from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar. And with the same meaning"","" he said in it: \""What is your view about lost sheep?\"" He said: \""It is food to be eaten — for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf. Detain your brother's lost property for him.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated with its chain in the Book of Zakāh. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 1708. Tirmidhī 1289]"""""
"12074","(12069) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Abī Ḥayyān al-Taymī; al-Ḍaḥḥākh, the maternal uncle of al-Mundhir ibn Jarīr, narrated to me from al-Mundhir ibn Jarīr. He said: I was with my father at al-Bawāzīj in the Sawād. The cattle returned, and he saw a cow that he did not recognize. He said: \What is this cow?\"" They said: \""A cow that joined the cattle.\"" He ordered that it be driven away until it disappeared. Then he said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one gives refuge to lost property except one who is himself lost (ḍāll).'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12075","(12070) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, in Baghdād, informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī al-Khaṭṭabī narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannī narrated to me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated from Abī al-ʿAlāʾ from Abī Muslim from al-Jārūd. He said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I come upon a lost camel — should I leave it?\"" He said: \""The lost property of a Muslim is a burning coal of the Fire.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Ayyūb. And similarly"","" Qatādah narrated it from Abī al-ʿAlāʾ. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12076","(12071) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed it to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatādah from Abī al-ʿAlāʾ from Abī Muslim from al-Jārūd that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The lost property of a believer is a burning coal of the Fire.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated it from Abī al-ʿAlāʾ — Yazīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr — in one of the two narrations from him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12077","(12072) Abū Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from Yazīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr from Abī Muslim from al-Jārūd. He said: We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were on emaciated camels. We said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" we pass through al-Jarf and find camels"","" so we ride them.\"" He said: \""The lost property of a Muslim is a burning coal of the Fire.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated from him from Yazīd from his brother Muṭarrif from al-Jārūd. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12078","(12073) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed it to us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; both saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Sufyān narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from Yazīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr from Muṭarrif ibn al-Shikhkhīr from al-Jārūd al-ʿAbadī, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \The lost property of a Muslim is a burning coal of the Fire — so do not approach it.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from him from Muṭarrif from Abī Muslim from al-Jārūd. And it has been narrated from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr from his father. [Munkar]"""""
"12079","(12074) The master Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Isfarāyinī informed us; Dalaj ibn Aḥmad al-Sijzī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl from al-Ḥasan from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdillāh from his father: that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \We come upon stray camels.\"" He said: \""The lost property of a Muslim — or a believer — is a burning coal of the Fire.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""""
"12080","(12075) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him, said — while he was leaning his back against the Kaʿbah: \Whoever takes lost property is himself lost (ḍāll).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12081","(12076) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us that Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us that Abū Khaythamah narrated to us that Abū al-Juwayriyyah said: \I heard a Bedouin from Banū Sulaym ask Ibn ʿAbbās — meaning about lost property (al-ḍawāll) — and he said: 'What do you think about lost property?' He said: 'Whoever eats from lost property is himself lost (ḍāll).' Then the man fell silent"","" and Ibn ʿAbbās began issuing legal rulings to the people. Abū al-Juwayriyyah said: 'He used to give many legal rulings that I could not retain.' Then the Bedouin said: 'It seems you have dismissed the people other than me. Do you think there is repentance for me?' He said: 'Woe to you! Do not ask about this matter.' He said: 'How severe is your question!' He said: 'I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him for what I have done.' He said: 'Do you know why this verse was revealed: \""O you who believe"","" do not ask about things which"","" if made known to you"","" would harm you\"" (5:101) — until he finished the entire verse?' He said: 'There were people who used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in mockery. A man would say: \""Who is my father?\"" and another would say: \""My she-camel has gone lost — where is my she-camel?\"" So Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" revealed this verse concerning them.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Faḍl ibn Sahl from Abū al-Naḍr"","" in abridged form. [Bukhārī 4622]"""""
"12082","(12077) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Makhlad ibn Khālid narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from ʿAmr ibn Muslim from ʿIkrimah — I think it was from Abū Hurayrah — that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The hidden lost camel: its fine (gharāmah) shall be paid along with the like of it.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12083","(12078) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Bakr ibn Sawādah from Abū Sālim al-Jayshānī from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever shelters lost property (ḍāllah) is himself lost"","" so long as he does not make it publicly known (yuʿarrifuhā).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12084","(12079) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ribḥ narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk that he found a camel and brought it to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, who ordered him to make it publicly known. Then he returned to ʿUmar and said: \It has distracted me from my work.\"" So he said to him: \""Go and release it from where you found it.\""\n\nA similar narration was reported by Mālik ibn Anas"","" though it does not contain evidence indicating that liability falls away from him if he releases it and it perishes. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12085","(12080) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated that he heard Ibn Shihāb say: \Lost camels (ḍawāll al-ibill) in the time of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" were herds of camels left to breed"","" and no one would touch them. Then"","" when the time of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" came"","" he ordered that they be identified and publicly announced"","" then sold. When their owner came"","" he was given their price.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 1488]"""""
"12086","(12081) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: \I went out with Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah"","" and I found a whip at al-Udhayb. They both said: 'Leave it"","" leave it!' I said: 'By Allah"","" I will not leave it for the wild beasts to eat — I will make use of it.' So I came to Ubayy ibn Kaʿb and mentioned that to him. He said: 'You did well"","" you did well! I found"","" during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" a purse containing a hundred dinars. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \""Announce it for a year.\"" So I announced it for a year"","" then I came to him and he said: \""Announce it for a year.\"" So I announced it for a year"","" then I came to him and he said: \""Announce it for a year.\"" After three years had passed"","" I came to him and he said: \""Know its number"","" its binding (wikāʾahā)"","" and its container (wiʿāʾahā). If someone comes who can inform you of its number and its binding"","" then hand it over to him; otherwise"","" make use of it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Bukhārī. Muslim 1723]"""""
"12087","(12082) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Qābūs ibn Abī Ẓabyān from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: \Do not pick it up from the ground — I have nothing to do with it\"" — meaning the dropped item (luqaṭah). And the statement of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar regarding this has already been mentioned in the first section. [Weak. Ibn Abī Shaybah 21663]"""""
"12088","(12083) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī that he said: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about the dropped item (luqaṭah). He said: 'Recognize its container (ʿifāṣahā) and its binding (wikāʾahā)"","" then announce it for a year. If its owner comes"","" then it is up to you regarding it.'\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik.\n\nA similar narration was reported by Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Rabīʿah"","" and by Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12089","(12084) Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Rabīʿah, and he said in the ḥadīth: \Announce it for a year"","" then recognize its binding (wikāʾahā) and its container (ʿifāṣahā)"","" then spend from it. If its owner comes"","" then return it to him.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated it"","" and it has already been mentioned in full. And al-Thawrī narrated from Rabīʿah similarly. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12090","(12085) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us that Isḥāq al-Dabarī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Qabīṣah narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the dropped item (luqaṭah). He said: 'Announce it for a year"","" then recognize its container (ʿifāṣahā)"","" its binding (wikāʾahā)"","" and its wrapping (wiʿāʾahā). If its owner comes"","" hand it over to him; otherwise"","" spend from it or make use of it.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" what about a lost sheep?' He said: 'It is either for you"","" for your brother"","" or for the wolf.' Then he asked about a lost camel"","" and his face changed colour"","" and he said: 'What concern is it of yours? It has its hooves and its water-skin; it drinks water and eats trees. Leave it until it meets its owner.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from two other routes from al-Thawrī"","" without his phrase \""its wrapping (wiʿāʾahā)"",""\"" and he said: \""If someone comes who can inform you of it"","" then spend from it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12091","(12086) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥmmad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us, al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān narrated from Sālim, Abū al-Naḍr, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever picks up a lost item"","" let him publicize it for one year. If its owner comes"","" let him return it; otherwise"","" let him note its quantity and its binding"","" then consume it. If its owner later comes"","" let him return it to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr"","" from Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī"","" except that he said in its text: \""If it is recognized"","" then return it; otherwise"","" note its container"","" its binding"","" and its quantity.\"""""""
"12092","(12087) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj, meaning al-Azraq, narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafalah say: He was on an expedition and found a whip and took it. Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah said: \Throw it away.\"" I refused to do so. We completed our expedition"","" then I performed Ḥajj and passed through al-Madīnah. I went to Ubayy ibn Kaʿb and mentioned that to him. He said: \""I found a purse containing one hundred dinārs during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'Publicize it for one year.' I publicized it for one year but found no one who recognized it. I returned to him and he said the same thing three times. Then he said: 'Keep count of its contents"","" its container"","" and its binding. If its owner comes"","" [return it]; otherwise"","" make use of it.'\"" He said: \""So I made use of it.\"" Salamah said: \""I do not know whether he said 'for one year' or 'for three years.'\"" al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12093","(12088) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: \We were performing Ḥajj and I found a whip\""—and he mentioned the ḥadīth"","" without naming Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah. And he said at its end: \""I said: 'I have publicized it.' He said: 'Make use of it"","" and remember its container"","" its wrapping"","" and count its contents.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12094","(12089) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Khālid al-Ḍhāʾāʾ narrated from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ, from Muṭarrif, from ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār al-Mujāshiʿī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever finds a lost item"","" let him have one or two upright persons bear witness to it"","" and let him not conceal it or hide it. If its owner is found"","" let him return it to him; otherwise"","" it is the wealth of Allah"","" and He gives it to whom He wills.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — Aḥmad 7620"","" Abū Dāwūd 1709]"""""
"12095","(12090) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Badr, that his father informed him: He encamped at a place along the road to al-Shām and found a purse containing eighty dinārs. He mentioned that to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \Publicize it at the doors of the mosque and mention it to anyone who arrives from al-Shām for one year. When the year has passed"","" then it is yours.\"" [Ḍaʿīf — Mālik 1483]"""""
"12096","(12091) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed me—Salamah ibn Kuhayl said: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafalah say: \I went on an expedition"","" along with Zayd ibn Ṣūḥān and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah"","" and I found a whip. I took it and they said to me: 'Discard it.' I said: 'No"","" but I will publicize it. If I find someone who recognizes it"","" [I will return it]; otherwise"","" I will make use of it.' I refused to comply with them. When we returned from our expedition"","" it was decreed that I perform Ḥajj"","" so I came to al-Madīnah and met Ubayy ibn Kaʿb. I informed him about the matter of the whip and about what they had said. Ubayy ibn Kaʿb said: 'I found a purse containing one hundred dinārs during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned it to him. He said: \""Publicize it for one year.\"" I publicized it but found no one who recognized it"","" three times. Then he said: \""Keep count of its contents"","" its binding"","" and its container. If its owner comes"","" [return it]; otherwise"","" make use of it.'\"" Shuʿbah said: \""I later met Salamah and he said: 'I do not know whether it was for three years or one year.'\"" This ḥadīth impressed me"","" so I said to Abū Ṣādiq: 'Come and listen to it from him.'\""\n\nBahr ibn Asad narrated it from Shuʿbah"","" from Salamah. Shuʿbah said: \""I heard him"","" after ten years"","" say: 'Publicize it for one year.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12097","(12092) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us, Bahr narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated—and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Salamah ibn Kuhayl was initially uncertain about it, then he recalled it and became settled upon [the period of] one year. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12098","(12093) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Miqsam narrated to him, from a man, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī: that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, found some dinārs and brought them to Fāṭimah, peace be upon her. She said: \This is provision that Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has provided us. All praise is due to Allah. Go and buy meat and food with it.\"" So he prepared food. He said to Fāṭimah"","" peace be upon her: \""Send to your father and inform him"","" so that if he considers it lawful"","" we may eat from it.\"" When they had prepared the food"","" they invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he came"","" they mentioned it to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""It is the provision of Allah.\"" He ate from it and they ate from it. After that"","" a woman came seeking the dinārs"","" saying: \""I seek Allah's help regarding the dinārs.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""O ʿAlī"","" return the dinārs.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12099","(12094) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir narrated to us, Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Yaʿqūb al-Zamʿī narrated from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who informed him: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib came to Fāṭimah while Ḥasan and Ḥusayn, peace be upon them, were both crying. He said: \What makes them weep?\"" She said: \""Hunger.\"" So ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" went out and found a dinār in the market. He came to Fāṭimah"","" peace be upon her"","" and informed her. She said: \""Go to so-and-so the Jew and get us some flour.\"" He went to the Jew and bought flour with it. The Jew said: \""Are you the son-in-law of the one who claims to be the Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then take your dinār and the flour is yours.\"" ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" went out until he came to Fāṭimah"","" peace be upon her"","" and informed her. She said: \""Go to so-and-so the butcher and get us a dirham's worth of meat.\"" He went and pawned the dinār for a dirham's worth of meat. He brought it"","" and she kneaded [the flour]"","" set [the dough]"","" and baked. She sent for her father and he came to them. ʿAlī said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I mention this to you. If you consider it lawful for us"","" we shall eat from it and you may eat from it.\"" He described the matter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Eat in the name of Allah.\"" So they ate. While they were in their place"","" a boy was calling out for Allah and Islam regarding the dinār. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be called"","" and he asked him. He said: \""It fell from me in the market.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""O ʿAlī"","" go to the butcher and say to him: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says to you: Send me the dinār"","" and your dirham is upon me (i.e."","" I will pay you).'\"" He sent it"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave it to him. [Ḍaʿīf]\n\nThe Shaykh said: The apparent meaning of the ḥadīth from ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" in this chapter indicates that he spent it before publicizing it during the appointed time. We have narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār"","" from ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" in this story"","" that the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to publicize it"","" but no one recognized it"","" so he ordered him to consume it. The apparent meaning of that narration is that he made publicizing it during the time a condition and permitted consuming it before the year had passed. The aḥādīth that have been transmitted regarding the condition of publicizing for one year for the permissibility of consumption are more authentic and more numerous"","" and thus they are more deserving of precedence. It is possible that he permitted him to spend it before the year had passed due to the occurrence of necessity"","" and the story points to that. It is also possible that he did not make the passage of a year a condition for a small amount of lost property. And Allah knows best."""""
"12100","(12095) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Khālid al-Juhanī narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated from Saʿd ibn Aws, from Bilāl ibn Yaḥyā al-ʿAbsī, from ʿAlī, peace be upon him: He picked up some dinārs and bought flour with it. The owner of the flour recognized it and returned the dinārs to him. ʿAlī took them and cut off two qīrāṭs worth and bought meat with it. There is a discrepancy in the text of this ḥadīth and weakness in its chains of narration. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"
"12101","(12096) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, dictating: ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿIjlī narrated to us in Kūfah: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from Zāʾidah, from Manṣūr, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a date on the road and said: \Were it not that it might be from charity"","" I would have eaten it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"","" and al-Bukhārī said: \""And Zāʾidah said"","" from Manṣūr"","" and he mentioned it.\""\n\n[Bukhārī 2055"","" Muslim 1071]"""""
"12102","(12097) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn al-Qazzāz narrated to us: Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a date lying on the road and said: \Were I not afraid that it might be from charity"","" I would have eaten it.\"" He said: And Ibn ʿUmar passed by a date lying on the road and ate it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qabīṣah"","" and Muslim narrated it through another route from al-Thawrī"","" without the mention of Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd we have narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" except that he said: \""I enter my house and find a date thrown on my bed.\"" And in another narration: \""And I do not know whether it is from the dates of charity or from the dates of my household"","" so I leave it.\""\n\nAnd that does not fall under the ruling of luqatah (found property). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12103","(12098) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: al-Walīd ibn Ḥammād al-Ramlī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated from al-Mughīrah ibn Ziyād, from Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī, that he narrated to him from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted us permission regarding the staff, the whip, the rope, and the like — that a man may pick it up and benefit from it.\n\nThe wording is that of Abū Dāwūd. In the narration of al-Ramlī, he said: \from Abū al-Zubayr"",""\"" and the rest is the same. Abū Dāwūd said: al-Nuʿmān ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated it from al-Mughīrah"","" Abū Salamah"","" with its isnād. The Shaykh said: \""It is as though Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb took it from him.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd 1717]"""""
"12104","(12099) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed me: A man informed me: Abū Salamah al-Mughīrah ibn Ziyād narrated to me from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted us permission — and he mentioned it, but he did not mention the rope.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: And Shabābah narrated it from Mughīrah ibn Muslim, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: \They did\"" — and he did not mention the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""There is doubt regarding the raising (rafʿ) of this ḥadīth"","" and there is weakness in its isnād. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12105","(12100) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿlā narrated from his grandmother Ḥukaymah, from Yaʿlā ibn Murrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever picks up a small found item — a rope"","" a dirham"","" or the like — let him make it known for three days. If he wishes to go beyond that"","" let him raise it for six days.\""\n\nʿUmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿlā is alone in narrating it"","" and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn declared him weak"","" and Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd and others accused him of drinking wine. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12106","(12101) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to us: al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Sufyān, from Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyā al-Qurashī, from Farūkh, the freedman of Ṭalḥah, who said: I heard Umm Salamah being asked about picking up a whip. She said: \Let him pick up his brother's whip — he may use it to tie his hands with it; I see no harm in it.\"" He said: \""And the rope?\"" She said: \""And the rope.\"" He said: \""And the sandal?\"" She said: \""And the sandal.\"" He said: \""And the vessel?\"" She said: \""I do not permit what Allah has forbidden. The vessel may contain provisions and goods.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān"","" from al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṣubayḥ"","" from al-Ḥasan: that he granted permission regarding the whip"","" the staff"","" and the strap — that one may find it and benefit from it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12107","(12102) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from his father, from Umm al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: \Do not ask anyone for anything.\"" I said: \""If I am in need?\"" He said: \""Follow the harvesters and see what falls from them; take it"","" then grind it"","" then knead it"","" then eat it"","" and do not ask anyone for anything.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12108","(12103) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb informed us in Hamadhān: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs informed us: Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us. He said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: \What the hand of the reaper misses or the hand of the picker lets fall — the owner of the crop has no claim over it. It is for the passersby and the wayfarers.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12109","(12104) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us: al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ḥaywah narrated. He said: I heard Abū al-Aswad inform me: Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the freedman of Shaddād, informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed me from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh, the freedman of Shaddād ibn al-Hād, that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever hears a person making an announcement in the mosque about a lost item"","" let him say: 'May Allah not return it to you.' For mosques were not built for this purpose.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb"","" and from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from al-Muqriʾ. [Muslim 568]"""""
"12110","(12105) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Shaybah, from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father: that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard a Bedouin — or a man — say: \Who will call for the red camel?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""You will not find it. These mosques were only built for what they were built for.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Muslim 569]"""""
"12111","(12106) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us. Both said: Ḥammād narrated to us: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who mentioned the hadith from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding al-luqatah (lost property). He said, regarding the period of public announcement: \Announce it for two years or three.\"" And he said: \""Know its number"","" its container"","" and its binding"","" and benefit from it. If its owner comes and identifies its number and its binding"","" then hand it over to him.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: Only Ḥammād says"","" \""and identifies its number.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Bahz from Ḥammād ibn Salamah. This wording was also reported in meaning by Sufyān al-Thawrī from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12112","(12107) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding al-luqatah, and he said: \Know its number"","" its binding"","" and its container. If someone comes and informs you of its number and its binding"","" then hand it over to him; otherwise"","" benefit from it.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr from al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12113","(12108) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Tamtām narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Salamah, and he mentioned the hadith. At the end of it he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Count its number"","" its binding"","" and its thread. If its owner comes and recognizes the description"","" then give it to him; otherwise"","" benefit from it.\""\n\nIts meaning was also reported in one of the two narrations from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah from Salamah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12114","(12109) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Rabīʿah from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ) in the hadith of al-luqatah, and he said: \If the one seeking it comes and recognizes its container and its number"","" then hand it over to him.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: Ḥammād also said"","" from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" a similar narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12115","(12110) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-ʿAwḍī, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad, narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about a lost camel, and he mentioned the hadith. Then he was asked about al-luqatah, and he said: \Know its number"","" its container"","" and its leather pouch"","" and announce it for one year. If its owner comes and recognizes its number and its leather pouch"","" then hand it over to him; otherwise"","" it is yours.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: This is the additional wording that Ḥammād ibn Salamah added in the hadith of Salamah ibn Kuhayl"","" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"","" Rabīʿah"","" and ʿUbayd Allāh: \""If its owner comes and recognizes its leather pouch and its binding"","" then hand it over to him.\"" This is not preserved.\n\nThe Shaykh said: We narrated it from al-Thawrī from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12116","(12111) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: My father narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sufyān from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, narrated to me from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with a lost item, and he said: \Announce it for one year"","" then know its leather pouch and its binding. If someone comes and informs you of it"","" then [hand it over to him]; otherwise"","" spend it.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn ʿAbbās from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī with this wording. And he narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf from Sufyān: \""If someone comes and informs you of its leather pouch and its binding"","" then spend it.\"" This wording is not found in the narration of most of them"","" so it is likely to be unpreserved"","" as Abū Dāwūd said."""""
"12117","(12112) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: He said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī said: The one who finds lost property is given a ruling: if the leather pouch, the binding, the number, and the weight are recognized, and it occurs to his mind that the claimant is not making a false claim, then he should be given it, but he should not be compelled in judgment except by proof, just as proof is required for other rights. Then he continued his speech until he said: His statement (ﷺ), \Know its leather pouch and its binding\"" — and Allah knows best — means that he should return its leather pouch and its binding along with whatever else he returns of it"","" and that when he places it among his wealth"","" he should know that it is al-luqatah and not his own wealth. It may also serve as an indicator of the truthfulness of the one making the claim"","" and this is the more apparent meaning. The statement of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" \""Proof lies upon the claimant\"" — this is a claimant. What is your view if ten or more people describe it and all of them are accurate in their description — should we return it to them as partners in it"","" even if they were a thousand or two thousand"","" and we know that all of them are liars except one"","" without specifying which one? And perhaps the one is also a liar. No one deserves anything by mere description. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12118","(12113) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād said: And Mūsā narrated to us: Abān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥimyarī from al-Shaʿbī. Abān said: ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever finds a beast whose owners have become unable to feed it"","" so they set it free"","" and then someone takes it and revives it"","" then it belongs to him.\"" In the hadith of Abān"","" ʿUbayd Allāh said: I asked"","" \""From whom?\"" He said: \""From more than one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Abū Dāwūd said: This is the wording of the hadith of Ḥammād"","" and it is clearer and more complete. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12119","(12114) And Abū ʿAlī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from al-Shaʿbī, who attributed the hadith to the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said: \Whoever leaves a beast in a place of destruction"","" and a man revives it"","" then it belongs to the one who revived it.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12120","(12115) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Manṣūr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ḥumayd al-Ḥimyarī. He said: I heard al-Shaʿbī say: \Whoever's beast stands still [unable to move] and he leaves it"","" then it belongs to the one who revives it.\"" I asked: \""From whom is this"","" O Abū ʿAmr?\"" He said: \""If you wish"","" I can enumerate for you such and such from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nThis is a hadith concerning which there is disagreement regarding its being raised (to the Prophet). It is disconnected from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and every person has more right to his own wealth until he gives it to another. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12121","(12116) And Abū Ḥāzim informed us — Abū al-Faḍl informed us — Aḥmad informed us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Khālid narrated to us — Muṭarrif narrated from al-Shaʿbī, regarding a man who abandoned his beast and another man took it and restored it. Al-Shaʿbī said: \A ruling has been given concerning this: if he abandoned it in a place of safety"","" with water and pasture"","" then its owner has the greater right to it; but if he abandoned it in a desolate and dangerous place"","" then the one who took it has the greater right to it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12122","(12117) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us — Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us — ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us — Shaybān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — Abū Salamah informed me that Abū Hurayrah informed him that the Prophet ﷺ said, in the story of Makkah: \Its thorns shall not be uprooted"","" its trees shall not be cut"","" and its fallen property shall not be picked up except by one who publicly announces it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym from Shaybān"","" and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā. [Bukhārī 2434"","" Muslim 1355]"""""
"12123","(12118) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd informed me — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us — Mufaḍḍal ibn Muhalhil narrated from Manṣūr — from Mujāhid — from Ṭāwūs — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: \Verily"","" this city is sacred — Allah has made it inviolable. Killing in it was not permissible for anyone before me"","" and it shall remain inviolable"","" having been made sacred by Allah"","" until the Day of Resurrection. Its game shall not be driven away"","" its thorns shall not be cut"","" and its fallen property shall not be picked up except by one who publicly announces it"","" and its herbage shall not be uprooted.\"" Al-ʿAbbās said: \""Except al-idhkir"","" for it is used for their homes.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Except al-idhkir.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"","" and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it from the ḥadīth of Jarīr from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12124","(12119) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us — Rūḥ narrated to us — Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from ʿIkrimah — from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Its herbage shall not be cut"","" its trees shall not be felled"","" its game shall not be driven away"","" and its fallen property shall not be taken except by one who publicly announces it.\"" Al-ʿAbbās"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""Except al-idhkir.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Except al-idhkir.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12125","(12120) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUbayd said: \I have no basis for this ḥadīth except what ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī said — that the one who finds it (al-luqṭah) has no right to it except through perpetual public announcement; otherwise"","" it is not permissible for him to touch it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12126","(12121) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ashajj — from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān al-Taymī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the picking up of lost property by the pilgrim (al-ḥājj).\n\nMuslim narrated it from Abī al-Ṭāhir and others from Ibn Wahb. [Muslim 1724]"
"12127","(12122) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us — Musaddad informed us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Abī Bishr — from Abī al-Mutawakkil — from Abū Saʿīd, that a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ set out on a journey and encamped among a tribe of the Arab tribes. They sought hospitality from them, but they refused to host them. The chief of that tribe was stung (by a scorpion or snake), and they tried everything for him but nothing availed. Some of them said: \If only you would go to those people who have encamped with you — perhaps some among them might have something that could help your companion.\"" Some of them said: \""O group"","" our chief has been striven"","" and we have tried everything for him. Is there anyone among you who has something that might benefit our companion?\"" A man from the group said: \""Yes"","" I can perform ruqyah"","" but we sought your hospitality and you refused to host us. I shall not perform ruqyah for you unless you set a fee (juʿl) for us.\"" So they set a flock of sheep as his fee. He came to him"","" recited Umm al-Qurʾān (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah) over him and spat upon him"","" until he recovered as though he had been released from a tether. He paid them what they had agreed upon. Then one of them said: \""Divide it.\"" The one who had performed the ruqyah said: \""Do not do so until we come to the Prophet ﷺ and consult him.\"" So they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning and mentioned it to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""How did you know that it was a ruqyah?\"" And he ﷺ said: \""You have done well. Divide it"","" and set aside a share for me along with you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān from Abī ʿAwānah"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Abī Bishr. This serves as evidence that the stipulated fee (juʿl) is only valid upon a condition. [Bukhārī 2276"","" Muslim 2201]"""""
"12128","(12123) As for what Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Maḥmūd al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad al-Shāhid informed us — Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Thābit al-ʿAṭṭār al-Dimashqī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Bakr al-Bālīsī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Khuṣayf narrated from Maʿmar — from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding a runaway slave found within the Ḥaram: ten dirhams.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]\n\nThis is weak. What is preserved (al-maḥfūẓ) is the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" who both said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the price for a runaway slave found outside the Ḥaram at ten dirhams\"" — and this is a disconnected (munqaṭiʿ) narration."""""
"12129","(12124) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Muʿammar narrated from al-Ḥajjāj — from al-Shaʿbī — from al-Ḥārith — from ʿAlī, regarding the fee for a runaway slave: \One dinar"","" whether he is apprehended near or far.\""\n\nAnd from al-Ḥajjāj"","" from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"","" that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib used to say that; and from al-Ḥajjāj"","" that Ibn Masʿūd used to say: \""When he leaves the miṣr (city)"","" his fee is forty (dirhams).\""\n\nAl-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a proof (lā yuḥtājju bihi). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12130","(12125) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us — Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Abī Rabāḥ — from Abī ʿAmr al-Shaybānī, who said: \I came upon some runaway slaves in al-ʿAyn"","" so I went to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd and mentioned it to him. He said: 'The reward (ajr) and the spoil (ghanīmah).' I said: 'This is the reward — but what is the spoil?' He said: 'Forty dirhams from each head.'\""\n\nThis is the best (amthal) narration reported on this matter. It is possible that ʿAbdullāh knew the stipulation of their owner — that for each one returned"","" there would be forty dirhams — and so he informed him of that. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12131","(12126) Al-Faqih Abu al-Fath al-'Umari informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abqasi informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' informed us; my grandfather informed us; Sufyan narrated to us from 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq and 'Umar ibn Sa'id, from a man from Khath'am who was called Hazn, from a man among them, who said: \I brought a slave who had escaped from the army"","" but he escaped from me. They brought me before Shurayh"","" and he held me liable for him.\"" He said: \""This matter was then raised to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" and he said: 'Shurayh has lied and the judgment is in error. The black slave shall be made to swear an oath for the red slave that he escaped from him of his own accord"","" and then there shall be nothing against him.'\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12132","(12127) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Farisi informed us; Abu Ishaq al-Isfahani informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn Faris informed us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf said to us, from Sufyan, from Hazm ibn Bashir, from Raja' ibn al-Harith, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding a man who finds an escaped slave and the slave then escapes from him: he is not liable for him, whereas Shurayh used to hold him liable.\n\nAnd we say in accordance with the statement of 'Ali: if the slave escaped from him without any transgression on his part, then he is not liable. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"
"12133","(12128) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; 'Ubayd ibn Sharik informed us; Yahya informed us; al-Layth narrated to me from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, that Salim ibn 'Abd Allah informed him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he does not wrong him and he does not abandon him. Whoever attends to the need of his brother"","" Allah will attend to his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a hardship"","" Allah will relieve him of a hardship from the hardships of the Day of Resurrection. And who covers (the faults of) a Muslim"","" Allah will cover (his faults) on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from Yahya ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from al-Layth. [Bukhari 2442"","" Muslim 2580]"""""
"12134","(12129) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us; Abu al-Walid informed us; Shu'bah narrated from 'Adi, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever leaves wealth"","" it is for his heirs. And whoever leaves a debt (or dependents in need)"","" then refer to me.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Abu al-Walid"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Bukhari 2398]"""""
"12135","(12130) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi informed us orally; Abu al-Qasim 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Baluwayh al-Muzaki informed us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us; 'Abd al-Razaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the closest of people to the believers according to the Book of Allah. So whoever among you leaves a debt or dependents in need"","" call upon me"","" for I am his guardian. And whoever among you leaves wealth"","" let him bequeath it to his next of kin"","" whoever they may be.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi' from 'Abd al-Razaq. [Sahih]"""""
"12136","(12131) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us; Isma'il al-Saffar informed us. Both said: Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from 'Umar, in a story he mentioned. He said: Then 'Umar recited this verse: \Indeed"","" Allah has purchased from the believers their lives and their wealth in exchange for Paradise\"" (the verse). He then joined both transactions together and said: \""By Allah"","" had Allah not provided you with treasures from His own"","" I would have taken the surplus wealth of a man beyond what he and his family need"","" and distributed it among the poor of the Muhajirun.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12137","(12132) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; 'Ali ibn Bayan informed us; 'Arim ibn al-Fadl Abu al-Nu'man informed us; al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated from Fil ibn 'Aradah, from Jarad ibn Tariq, who said: \I came"","" or I went"","" with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) after the morning prayer"","" until when we were in the market"","" he heard the voice of a newborn child crying. He stopped by him"","" and there was his mother with him. He said to her: 'What is the matter with you?' She said: 'I came to this market for some need"","" and labor overtook me"","" and I delivered a boy.' She was beside a house of some people in the market. He said: 'Did anyone from the people of this house become aware of you?' And he said: 'May Allah not destroy the people of this house! If I knew that they became aware of you and then did not help you"","" I would do such-and-such to them.' Then he called for a drink of sawiq for her and said: 'Drink this; it cuts the dryness of the stomach"","" protects the intestines"","" and causes the veins to flow.' Then we entered the mosque and he led the people in prayer.\"" [Hasan]\n\nAl-Sa'q said: Azhar narrated to me from Fil"","" who said: \""If I knew that they became aware of you and then did not help you with anything"","" I would burn upon them.\"""""""
"12138","(12133) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il al-Saffar informed us; Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us; 'Abd al-Razaq informed us; Malik narrated.\n\n(And) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas, that is al-Asamm, informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab, from Sunayn Abu Jamilah, a man from Banu Sulaym, that he found an exposed infant during the time of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He brought him to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and 'Umar said: \What compelled you to take this soul?\"" He said: \""I found it lost"","" so I took it.\"" His tribal chief said to him: \""O Commander of the Faithful"","" he is a righteous man.\"" He said: \""Is that so?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" 'Umar said: \""Go"","" then. He is free"","" his clientage (wala') is yours"","" and his maintenance is upon us.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Shafi'i's hadith. The hadith of 'Abd al-Razaq is abridged: that he picked up an exposed infant and brought him to 'Umar"","" and 'Umar said to him: \""He is free"","" his clientage is yours"","" and his maintenance is upon us from the Bayt al-Mal.\"" [Sahih. Al-Muwatta' 1448]"""""
"12139","(12134) Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Khaliq ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Mu'adhdhin informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khanb informed us; Abu Isma'il al-Tirmidhi informed us; Ayyub ibn Sulayman informed me; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways informed me; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated. He said: Yahya said: Ibn Shihab informed me that Sunayn Abu Jamilah informed him. He said: \We were sitting with Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab.\"" He said: Abu Jamilah claimed that he had met the Prophet (ﷺ): that he went out with him in the year of the Conquest. He informed him that he found an exposed infant during the caliphate of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" and he took it. He said: His tribal chief mentioned that. When 'Umar saw me"","" he said: 'Perhaps the cave is a source of calamity. What compelled you to take this soul?' He said: 'I said: I found it lost"","" so I took it.' My tribal chief said: He is a righteous man. He said: 'Is that so?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then go with it. He is free"","" his clientage is yours"","" and his maintenance is upon us.'\"" [Hasan]"""""
"12140","(12135) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Sarraj informed us; Abu Khalifah informed us; Abu al-Walid and Ibn Kathir narrated from Shu'bah, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he ruled regarding the foundling (laqit) that he is free, and he recited this verse: \And they sold him for a paltry price"","" a few counted dirhams"","" and they were regarding him among the indifferent.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12141","(12136) Juhayr ibn Yazid al-Abadi said: I heard al-Hasan being asked about the foundling — can he be sold? He said: Allah has forbidden that. Do you not recite Surah Yusuf? [Hasan]"
"12142","(12137) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Every child is born upon the fitrah (natural disposition). It is his parents who make him a Jew or a Christian"","" just as camels give birth to sound"","" whole camels — do you find any among them that are mutilated (in the ears)?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about one who dies while still an infant?\"" He said: \""Allah knows best what they would have done.\"" [Bukhari 1358"","" Muslim 2658]"""""
"12143","(12138) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no child born among the children of Adam except that he is born upon the fitrah"","" until his parents make him a Jew"","" or a Christian"","" or a Magian"","" just as an animal gives birth to a sound"","" whole offspring — do you perceive any mutilation in it?\"" Then Abu Hurayrah would say: \""And recite"","" if you wish: '(Adhere to) the fitrah of Allah upon which He created mankind. There is no change in the creation of Allah. That is the upright religion"","" but most of the people do not know.'\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12144","(12139) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no child born except upon the fitrah; his parents make him a Jew.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Ibn al-Musayyib. [Sahih]"""""
"12145","(12140) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever is born is born upon this fitrah; his parents make him a Jew or a Christian"","" just as you produce animals — do you find any among them that are mutilated (in the ears)"","" until you yourselves cut them?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about one who dies while still an infant?\"" He said: \""Allah knows best what they would have done.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12146","(12141) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no child born except upon this religion (millah)"","" until his tongue makes it clear (i.e."","" until he expresses himself). His parents make him a Jew"","" or a Christian"","" or a polytheist"","" or a Magian.\"" He (the narrator) said: They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what about one who died before that (i.e."","" before reaching the age of discernment)?\"" He said: \""Allah knows best what they would have done.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12147","(12142) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Every human being is born by his mother upon the fitrah; his parents make him a Jew"","" or a Christian"","" or a Magian. If both parents are Muslims"","" then he is a Muslim. Every human being born by his mother is pricked by Satan in his two sides (i.e."","" in his lap)"","" except Maryam and her son.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12148","(12143) Al-Aswad ibn Sari' reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: \Every child is born upon the fitrah"","" until he expresses himself (i.e."","" until he reaches the age of speech).\"" Another narrator added: \""His parents make him a Jew or a Christian.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him)"","" in his older opinion"","" narrated from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Baghdadi from him the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Every child is born upon the fitrah upon which Allah created the creation.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made them (subject to this ruling) so long as they have not expressed themselves verbally and chosen one of the two positions — faith or disbelief. There is no independent ruling over them for themselves; rather"","" the ruling over them is according to their fathers. Whatever their fathers were on the day they were born"","" that is their state — either a believer"","" then upon his faith"","" or a disbeliever"","" then upon his disbelief. [Sahih. Ahmad 1578"","" al-Darimi 2463]"""""
"12149","(12144) Al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal said: I heard Hammad ibn Salamah explaining the hadith: \Every child is born upon the fitrah.\"" He said: \""This"","" according to us"","" refers to the time when Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" took the covenant from them in the loins of their fathers"","" when He said: 'Am I not your Lord?' They said: 'Yes (indeed).'\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 4716]"""""
"12150","(12145) Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Every child is born upon the fitrah; his parents make him a Jew"","" a Christian"","" or a Magian.\""\n\nAl-Awza'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""They (the parents) do not remove him from the knowledge of Allah"","" and to the knowledge of Allah they shall return.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12151","(12146) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Mukram al-Tustarī informed us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Sharīk al-Bazzār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth ibn ʿUqayl narrated from Ibn Shihāb that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that ʿĀ'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \By Allah"","" I never knew my parents except that they were upon the religion of Islam"","" and there never passed a day except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to us in the morning and in the evening.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Bukhārī 476]\n\nImām Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: ʿĀ'ishah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" was born upon Islam"","" because her father accepted Islam at the outset of the mission. It is also established from al-Aswad"","" from ʿĀ'ishah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when she was six years old"","" and consummated the marriage when she was nine"","" and he passed away when she was eighteen. However"","" Asmā'"","" the daughter of Abū Bakr"","" was born in the Jāhiliyyah"","" and then she became Muslim through the Islam of her father"","" for she emigrated to the Prophet ﷺ while she was pregnant with ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr. She gave birth to him in Qubā' and did not nurse him until she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ"","" who chewed something and placed it in his mouth (taḥnīk) and supplicated for him. He was the first child born in Islam after the Prophet's arrival in Madīnah."""""
"12152","(12147) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed me: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad said: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām, from his father, from Asmā': She said that she became pregnant with ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr in Makkah. She said: \I departed while my pregnancy was complete"","" and I came to Madīnah and alighted in Qubā'"","" where I gave birth to him. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed him in his lap. He then called for a date and chewed it"","" then spat into his mouth"","" so the first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he performed taḥnīk for him"","" supplicated for him"","" and invoked blessings upon him. He was the first child born in Islam.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Abū Usāmah. ʿAlī ibn Muṣhir added therein"","" from Hishām: \""She did not nurse him until she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mandah mentioned"","" on the authority of Ibn Abī al-Zinād"","" that Asmā' bint Abī Bakr was ten years older than ʿĀ'ishah. Imām Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: The Islam of Asmā's mother was delayed. Asmā'"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" said: \""My mother came to me while she was a polytheist\"" — she mentioned a hadith in this regard — and she (the mother) was Qutaylah from Banī Mālik ibn Ḥisl"","" and she was not the mother of ʿĀ'ishah. Thus"","" Asmā's Islam was through the Islam of her father"","" not her mother. As for ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr"","" it is as though he was of age when his parents accepted Islam"","" but he did not follow them in Islam until he accepted Islam after a long period"","" and he was the eldest of Abū Bakr's children. [Bukhārī 3909; Muslim 2146]"""""
"12153","(12148) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā al-Maʿnī narrated. Aḥmad, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Isḥāq, from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, who said: \I used to recite to Umm Saʿd bint al-Rabīʿ"","" who was an orphan in the care of Abū Bakr. I recited: {وَالَّذِينَ عَاقَدَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ} (And those with whom your right hands have made a covenant). She said: 'Do not recite it as {عَاقَدَتْ} — rather it is {وَالَّذِينَ عَقَدَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ}. This verse was revealed concerning Abū Bakr and his son ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" when he refused to accept Islam. Abū Bakr"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" swore that he would not leave him any inheritance. When he accepted Islam"","" the Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded him to give him his share.'\"" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz added: \""And he did not accept Islam until he was compelled to it by the sword.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: al-Wāqidī claimed that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān accepted Islam during the truce of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. ʿAlī ibn Zayd claimed that he emigrated to the Prophet ﷺ among a group of young men from Quraysh before the Conquest (of Makkah). Abū ʿUbaydah claimed that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān's name in the Jāhiliyyah was ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Muṣʿab ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Zubayrī claimed that the mother of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿĀ'ishah — Umm Rūmān bint ʿĀmir — accepted Islam and her Islam was excellent. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd 2923]"""""
"12154","(12149) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" accepted Islam"","" the people gathered around him and said: 'ʿUmar has become a disbeliever! ʿUmar has become a disbeliever!' And I was on the roof of a house. Then al-ʿĀṣ ibn Wā'il came"","" wearing a silk robe trimmed with brocade"","" and said: 'ʿUmar has become a disbeliever!' I said: 'I am his neighbor (i.e."","" I grant him protection).' The people then dispersed. I was astonished at his might that day.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Sufyān. [Bukhārī 3868]\n\nThus"","" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb accepted Islam while ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar was a young boy"","" and he became Muslim through his father's Islam. This is due to the established hadith from Nāfiʿ"","" from Ibn ʿUmar"","" who said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ presented me on the day of Uḥud while I was fourteen years old"","" and he considered me too young.\"" It has also been said that Ḥafṣah and ʿAbd Allāh both accepted Islam before their father. ʿAbd Allāh was young at that time; his Islam was completed through the Islam of his father. And Allah knows best.\n\nAs for al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" he went out to Badr with the polytheists and was captured until he ransomed himself"","" and then he accepted Islam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3865]"""""
"12155","(12150) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAttāb narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah said: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah said: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me that Anas ibn Mālik informed him that some men from the Anṣār sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \Grant us permission"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" to leave the ransom of our maternal nephew al-ʿAbbās.\"" He said: \""No"","" by Allah"","" you shall not leave a single dirham.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways.\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn al-ʿAbbās at that time was a small boy"","" but his mother had accepted Islam"","" so he became Muslim through the Islam of his mother. al-Bukhārī said: Ibn al-ʿAbbās was with his mother among the oppressed (mustaḍʿafīn) and was not with his father upon the religion of his people. [Bukhārī 2527]"""""
"12156","(12151) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd, who said: \I heard Ibn al-ʿAbbās say: 'My mother and I were among the oppressed (mustaḍʿafīn). My mother was among the women"","" and I was among the children.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from Sufyān. [Bukhārī 1357]"""""
"12157","(12152) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn al-ʿAbbās, regarding this verse: {"
"12158","(12153) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Abī Ḥakīm, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah, from Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar, from Abū al-Aswad al-Duʾilī, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam increases and does not decrease.'\""\n\n[Weak. Abū Dāwūd 2912]"""""
"12159","(12154) ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated it from ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah, from Yaḥyā, from Abū al-Aswad, that a man narrated to him that Muʿādh said — and he mentioned it in that manner, raised (marfūʿan). Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated. His intention — and Allah knows best — was that the ruling of Islam prevails, and among the manifestations of its predominance is that the child is judged to be upon Islam through the Islam of either of his parents. [Weak]"
"12160","(12155) Abū Saʿīd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Shabānah al-Shāhid informed us in Hamadhān: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūyah al-Nasawī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Sarrāj narrated to us: Shabāb ibn Khayyāṭ al-ʿUṣfurī narrated to us: Ḥashraj ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥashraj narrated to me: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from ʿĀ'idh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \He came on the day of the Conquest (of Makkah) with Abū Sufyān ibn Ḥarb"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was surrounded by his Companions. They said: 'This is Abū Sufyān and ʿĀ'idh ibn ʿAmr.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is ʿĀ'idh ibn ʿAmr and Abū Sufyān. Islam is more exalted than that. Islam rises and is not risen over.'\""\n\nImām Aḥmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: al-Ḥasan"","" Sharīḥ"","" Ibrāhīm"","" and Qatādah said: \""When one of the two (parents) accepts Islam"","" the child is with the Muslim (parent).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12161","(12156) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and Abū Muḥammad ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī and Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The pen has been lifted from three: from the boy until he reaches puberty"","" from the mentally incapacitated until he regains his senses"","" and from the sleeper until he awakens.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Ṣaḥīh by other than him]"""""
"12162","(12157) By way of evidence, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Khalīfah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū Khalīfah narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Thābit, from Anas, that: \A Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He fell ill"","" so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to visit him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat near his head. The boy looked at his father"","" who said: 'Obey Abū al-Qāsim.' So he embraced Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left"","" saying: 'All praise is due to Allah"","" Who saved him from the Fire through me.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Bukhārī 1356]"""""
"12163","(12158) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq informed us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who informed me, saying: I heard Abū Ḥamzah, a man from the Anṣār, say: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: \The first person to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib.\"" He said: \""I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm"","" but he rejected it and said: 'It was Abū Bakr.'\"" [Ṣaḥīh. Al-Nasāʾī in al-Kubrā 8333]"""""
"12164","(12159) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Zakariyyā al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Muḥammad ibn ʬāʾ al-Maqdisī narrated to me; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāmī narrated from al-Najīb ibn al-Sarī, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said in a hadith he mentioned: \I preceded them to Islam early on"","" as a boy who had not yet reached the time of my puberty.\""\n\nThe phrase \""early on\"" (qidman) is not in the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān. This is a well-known statement among the people from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" except that it has not reached us through a chain of narration that can be used as evidence. The scholars differed regarding his age at the time he embraced Islam. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12165","(12160) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to me; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me; Abū al-Aswad narrated from ʿUrwah, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) embraced Islam when he was eight years old.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12166","(12161) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, that: \ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) embraced Islam when he was ten years old.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12167","(12162) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us in al-Maghāzī; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Aḥmad narrated to us; Yūnus narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated — I think he said — from Mujāhid, who said: \ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) embraced Islam when he was ten years old.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12168","(12163) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Walīd say: I heard Sharīk say: \ʿAlī embraced Islam when he was eleven years old.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12169","(12164) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us. And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me; ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad and Abū Bashr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan and others: \The first to believe in him was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"","" and he was fifteen or sixteen years old.\"" This is the wording of their two hadiths. And in the hadith of Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr"","" he said: from al-Ḥasan and another"","" who said: \""The first to embrace Islam was ʿAlī"","" after Khadījah (may Allah be pleased with her)"","" and he was fifteen or sixteen years old.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12170","(12165) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us; Miʿsar narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the banner to ʿAlī on the day of Badr"","" and he was twenty years old.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The battle of Badr took place after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madīnah by one and a half years. They differed regarding the length of his stay in Makkah after he was sent as a Prophet. It was said: ten years; it was said: thirteen years; and it was said: fifteen years. If it was ten years"","" and it is established that ʿAlī was twenty years old on the day of Badr"","" then his age at the time he embraced Islam would be close to what ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said. If it was thirteen or fifteen years"","" then it would be less than that"","" and Allah knows best.\n\nThey differed regarding the age of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day he was killed. It was said: sixty-five; it was said: sixty-three; and it was said: less than that. The most well-known is sixty-three"","" at the head of forty years from the Hijrah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Thus"","" his age at the time he embraced Islam"","" according to the one who said the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Makkah for ten years"","" would be thirteen years; and according to the one who said thirteen years"","" it would be ten years.\n\nIn most narrations"","" he (may Allah be pleased with him) had reached an age when it is possible that he had attained puberty. What has been narrated of poetry is open to interpretation"","" despite the weakness of its chain of narration. The ruling of the statement of an adult takes precedence over that of a discerning boy. His legal ruling came after the Islam of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" so his Islam was judged as valid — either because he remained until he described Islam after reaching puberty"","" or because the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed him with the call to Islam while other boys were not so addressed"","" or because the statement of a discerning boy was judged valid before the coming of the Sharīʿah with anything else"","" or because he had attained puberty and thus became an adult thereby. And Allah knows best.\""\n\nAl-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī and others"","" in the narration of Qatādah"","" held that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) embraced Islam when he was fifteen or sixteen years old"","" as has been mentioned above. [Ḥasan. Al-Ḥākim 4562]"""""
"12171","(12166) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for fifteen years. He used to hear sounds and see light for seven years without seeing anything, and for eight years revelation was sent down to him. He remained in Madīnah for ten years. In the narration of Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl: seven years during which he would see light and hear sounds, and eight years during which revelation was sent down to him, and he remained in Madīnah for ten years.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Muslim 2353]\n\nImām Aḥmad said: Al-Ḥasan inclined toward a similar view regarding the period during which revelation was sent to the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah. According to this breakdown, ʿAlī's acceptance of Islam would be after those seven years, which is after revelation had begun to the Prophet (ﷺ). Thus, the Prophet's residence in Makkah after the commencement of revelation was eight years. Accordingly, ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), according to the view of those who said he was killed at the age of sixty-three, would have been at the head of forty years from the Hijrah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he accepted Islam at the age of fifteen, as we have narrated from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī. However, the well-known narrations regarding the Prophet's (ﷺ) residence in Makkah after the commencement of revelation indicate more than that. And Allah knows best. [Bukhārī 3547, Muslim 2237]"
"12172","(12167) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym, al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn, narrated to us: Shaybān narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for ten years during which the Qurʾān was revealed to him, and in Madīnah for ten years during which the Qurʾān was revealed to him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym. And similarly, Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik.\n\n[Bukhārī 3547]"
"12173","(12168) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, from Abū Jamrah, that Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for thirteen years and in Madīnah for ten years, and he passed away at the age of sixty-three.\n\nMuslim narrated it through another chain from Ḥammād ibn Salamah.\n\nAnd similarly, ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and ʿIkrimah narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Bukhārī 3536]"
"12174","(12169) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bazzāz al-Ṭabarānī therein informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remained in Makkah for thirteen years and passed away at the age of sixty-three.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Maṭar ibn al-Faḍl, and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm, both from Rūḥ."
"12175","(12170) Abū Naṣr al-Ṭabarānī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Hishām narrated to us: ʿIkrimah narrated, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sent at the age of forty. He remained in Makkah for thirteen years during which revelation was sent down to him. Then he was commanded with Hijrah, so he migrated for ten years, and he passed away at the age of sixty-three.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Maṭar ibn al-Faḍl from Rūḥ.\n\nAs for al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām (may Allah be pleased with him), the narrations differ regarding his age at the time he accepted Islam, as reported from ʿUrwah."
"12176","(12171) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us: Abū al-Aswad narrated, from ʿUrwah, who said: al-Zubayr accepted Islam when he was eight years old.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us: ʿAbdullāh informed us: Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yūsuf al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated, from Hishām, who informed me: My father informed me that al-Zubayr accepted Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he never remained behind from any battle in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) participated. He was killed at the age of sixty-something. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12177","(12172) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād ibn Anʿum narrated, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Knowledge is three things, and whatever besides that is superfluous: a clear verse (āyatun muḥkamah), an established Sunnah (sunnatun qāʾimah), or a just obligation (farīḍah ʿādilah). [Weak. Abū Dāwūd 2885, Ibn Mājah 54]"
"12178","(12173) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated, from ʿAwf, from one who narrated to him, from Sulaymān ibn Jābir, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Learn the Qurʾān and teach it to the people; learn knowledge and teach it to the people; learn the laws of inheritance (farāʾiḍ) and teach them to the people. For indeed knowledge will be taken away, and tribulations will appear, until two men will disagree regarding an inheritance share and will not find anyone to judge between them.\n\nIt has also been narrated from ʿAwf, from Sulaymān, from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbdullāh. [Weak]"
"12179","(12174) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed him: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: al-Muthannā ibn Bakr al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us: ʿAwf narrated to us: Sulaymān narrated, from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbdullāh, who narrated it in a marfūʿ (elevated) form, except that he said: Indeed I am a man who will be taken (in death), and indeed knowledge will be taken away, until two men will disagree regarding an inheritance share and will not find anyone to inform them of it. [Weak]"
"12180","(12175) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Firās al-Mālikī in Makkah informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥakam, Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Miṣrī, narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmār ibn Abī al-Ṭāf, the freedman of Banū Sahm, narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād al-Makkī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmār al-Madanī narrated, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: Learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to the people, for it is half of knowledge, and it will be forgotten, and it is the first thing that will be removed from my Ummah.\n\nḤafṣ ibn ʿUmār is alone in narrating it, and he is not strong. [Very Weak]"
"12181","(12176) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū ʿAwānah informed us from ʿĀṣim, from Muwarriq, who said: ʿUmar said: \Learn the laws of inheritance (al-farāʾiḍ)"","" grammar (al-laḥn)"","" and the Sunnah just as you learn the Qurʾān.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12182","(12177) He said, and Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Learn the laws of inheritance"","" for they are part of your religion.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12183","(12178) He said, and Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Wakīʿ informed us from Abī Hilāl, from Qatādah, who said: ʿUmar wrote: \When you engage in play"","" then play with archery"","" and when you converse"","" then converse about the laws of inheritance.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12184","(12179) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed us from Abī Isḥāq, who said: I heard Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrating from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Whoever learns the Qurʾān should also learn the laws of inheritance"","" and let him not be like a man whom a Bedouin meets and says to him: 'O servant of Allah"","" am I a Bedouin or a Muhājir?' If he says"","" 'A Muhājir"",""' the Bedouin says: 'A person from my family has died—how should his inheritance be divided?' If he knows"","" it is good—Allah will grant him what He has given him. But if he says"","" 'I do not know"",""' the Bedouin says: 'Then what superiority do you have over us"","" when you recite the Qurʾān but do not know the laws of inheritance?'\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12185","(12180) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Khallād narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Abī Isḥāq narrated to me from Abī ʿUbaydah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: \Whoever learns the Qurʾān should also learn the laws of inheritance. If a Bedouin meets him and says: 'O Muhājir"","" do you recite the Qurʾān?' and he says"","" 'Yes"",""' the Bedouin says: 'And I too recite the Qurʾān.' If the man says"","" 'Do you know the laws of inheritance?' and he says"","" 'Yes"",""' then that is well. But if he says"","" 'No"",""' the Bedouin says: 'Then what superiority do you have over me?'\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12186","(12181) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū Khaythamah informed us from Abī Isḥāq—I think—from Abī ʿUbaydah, from his father, who said: \Whoever recites the Qurʾān should learn the laws of inheritance"","" and let him not be like a man whom a Bedouin meets and says: 'O Muhājir"","" do you recite the Qurʾān?' If he says"","" 'Yes"",""' the Bedouin says to him: 'A person from my family has died—so divide his inheritance.' If he does so"","" it is knowledge he has learned and an increase granted to him by Allah. Otherwise"","" the Bedouin says: 'By what do you surpass us"","" O company of Muhājirs?'\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12187","(12182) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ḥusayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif narrated to us from al-Qāsim ibn al-Walīd, who said: Ibn Masʿūd said: \Learn the laws of inheritance"","" the rites of Ḥajj"","" and the rulings of divorce"","" for they are part of your religion.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12188","(12183) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrīt narrated to us from ʿIkrimah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās used to place a shackle on my foot while teaching me the Qurʾān and the laws of inheritance. [Authentic]"
"12189","(12184) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam informed me, saying: I heard Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah say: \The laws of inheritance are called half of knowledge because all people are tested by it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it is narrated from Ṭāwūs and Qatādah: \""The law of inheritance is one-third of knowledge.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12190","(12185) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated to us from Ibrāhīm, who said: \I asked ʿAlqamah about the laws of inheritance. He said: 'When you wish to learn them"","" then cause your neighbours to die and bequeath to one another.'\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12191","(12186) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Ja'far Muḥammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz informed us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq informed us: Qabīṣah ibn 'Uqbah informed us: Sufyān ibn Sa'īd narrated from Khālid and 'Āṣim, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most merciful of my Ummah is Abū Bakr; the most severe in the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most true in modesty is 'Uthmān; the most knowledgeable of the obligatory duties is Zayd; the most reciting is Ubayy; and the most knowledgeable of the ḥalāl and ḥarām is Mu'ādh. And verily"","" every Umina has an Amīn"","" and the Amīn of this Ummah is Abū 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.\"" And Qutaybah ibn al-'Alā' narrated it similarly from Sufyān"","" from Khālid al-Ḥadhā'"","" from Abū Qilābah"","" from Anas"","" with a connected chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 12935. Ibn Mājah 154"","" 155]"""""
"12192","(12187) And Wahayb ibn Khālid and 'Abd al-Wahhāb ibn 'Abd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī narrated it similarly from Khālid al-Ḥadhā', with a connected chain. Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us: Abū Qilābah informed us: 'Affān and Sahl ibn Bakkār both informed us: Wahayb narrated from Khālid, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most gentle of my Ummah is Abū Bakr; the most severe in the religion of Allah is 'Umar; the most true in modesty is 'Uthmān; the most knowledgeable of the obligatory duties is Zayd; the most reciting is Ubayy; and the most knowledgeable of the ḥalāl and ḥarām is Mu'ādh. And every Ummah has an Amīn"","" and the Amīn of this Ummah is Abū 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12193","(12188) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: 'Alī ibn Ḥamshādh al-'Adl informed us: Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb both informed us: Musaddad informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhāb — (ḥ) And Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us: Abū 'Abd Allāh ibn Ya'qūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Khallād al-Bāhilī informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us: Khālid narrated from Abū Qilābah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most merciful of my Ummah is Abū Bakr; the most severe in the religion of Allah is 'Umar.\"" Then he mentioned the rest with the same meaning. And Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal"","" Ismā'īl ibn 'Ulayyah"","" and Muḥammad ibn Abī 'Adī narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhā'"","" from Abū Qilābah"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" as a mursal narration"","" except for the statement regarding Abū 'Ubaydah"","" for they connected it at the end"","" making it from Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet ﷺ. And all of these narrators are trustworthy and precise"","" and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12194","(12189) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh informed us: Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Ṣāliḥ informed me: Mūsā ibn 'Ulayy informed me from his father, that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people at al-Jābiyah and said: \Whoever wishes to ask about the Qur'ān"","" let him come to Ubayy ibn Ka'b; whoever wishes to ask about the obligatory duties"","" let him come to Zayd ibn Thābit; whoever wishes to ask about jurisprudence (fiqh)"","" let him come to Mu'ādh ibn Jabal; and whoever wishes to ask about wealth"","" let him come to me"","" for Allah"","" the Most High"","" has made me a treasurer and a distributor for it.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""""
"12195","(12190) And Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us: Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed us: Kathīr ibn Hishām informed us: Ja'far ibn Burqān informed us: I heard al-Zuhrī saying: \Had Zayd ibn Thābit not written down the knowledge of the obligatory duties"","" I would have seen it disappearing from the people.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12196","(12191) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us: Abū 'Abd Allāh ibn Ya'qūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī al-Ḥalwānī informed us: 'Ārim informed us: Yūsuf ibn al-Mājishūn informed us: I heard Ibn Shihāb saying: \If 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān and Zayd ibn Thābit"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" had perished at a certain time"","" the knowledge of the obligatory duties would have perished until the Day of Resurrection. A time came upon the people in which no one was proficient in it other than the two of them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12197","(12192) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far ibn Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shu'bah narrated from Qatādah, who said: I heard Anas saying: \The Qur'ān was compiled during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by four persons: Ubayy ibn Ka'b"","" Mu'ādh ibn Jabal"","" Zayd ibn Thābit"","" and Abū Zayd.\"" I said to Anas: \""Who is Abū Zayd?\"" He said: \""One of my uncles.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Mūsā from Abū Dāwūd"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Bundār from Yaḥyā from Shu'bah. [Bukhārī 3526. Muslim 2465]"""""
"12198","(12193) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh informed us: Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū al-Yamān informed me: Shu'ayb — (ḥ) And he said: Ḥajjāj ibn Abī Manī' informed me: My grandfather informed me, in its entirety, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Ibn al-Sabbāq informed me that Zayd ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī said: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: \You are a young"","" intelligent man; we do not suspect you"","" and you used to write for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So pursue the Qur'ān and compile it.\"" This story has been mentioned in full in the Book of Ṣalāh"","" and in it is a virtue of great merit for Zayd ibn Thābit"","" may Allah be pleased with him. [Bukhārī 4986]"""""
"12199","(12194) Hilāl ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥaffār informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn 'Ayyāsh informed us: Yaḥyā al-Sarī informed us: Jarīr — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us: Ya'qūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed us: Jarīr narrated from al-A'mash, from Thābit ibn 'Ubayd, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \Writings will come to me that I would not like anyone to read. Do you know Syriac?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then learn it.\"" So I learned it in seventeen days. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Faḍl. [Aḥmad 21920]"""""
"12200","(12195) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz informed us in Baghdad: Abū Muḥammad 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī informed us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Qaza'ah informed us: 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, from his father, who said: When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in al-Madīnah, I was brought to him and I recited to him. He said to me: \Learn the Book of the Jews"","" for I do not trust them regarding our Book.\"" He said: \""Fifteen days had not yet passed before I had learned it. I would then write for the Prophet ﷺ and read their letters to him.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""""
"12201","(12196) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Tājir informed me; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us; al-Anṣārī Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abū Salamah: that Ibn ʿAbbās took hold of the stirrup of Zayd ibn Thābit and said to him, \Step aside"","" O son of the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He replied"","" \""Indeed"","" we do this with our elders and our scholars.\""\n\nal-Shaʿbī narrated it with the same meaning. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12202","(12197) Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār, who said: When Zayd ibn Thābit died, we sat with Ibn ʿAbbās in the shade of a palace, and he said: \This is how knowledge departs! Indeed"","" today a great deal of knowledge has been buried.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12203","(12198) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Abū Isḥāq from Masrūq, who said: I came to Madīnah and asked about the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and I was told that Zayd ibn Thābit was among those firmly grounded in knowledge. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12204","(12199) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-ʿAnazī narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Idrīs al-Anṣārī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from al-Shaʿbī, who said: The knowledge of Zayd ibn Thābit was in two qualities: the Qurʾān and the laws of inheritance (al-Farāʾiḍ). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12205","(12200) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited me while I was ill. He performed ablution and sprinkled some of the water of his ablution upon me. I said, \O Messenger of Allah"","" I am inherited only by kalālah (i.e."","" collateral relatives"","" neither parents nor children). How shall the inheritance be distributed?\"" Then the Verse of al-Farāʾiḍ (the laws of inheritance) was revealed.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Walīd from Shuʿbah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abī Mūsā from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Bukhārī 6823"","" Muslim 1616]"""""
"12206","(12201) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ṣaydalānī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Jurayj narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) visited me among Banī Salamah and found me unconscious. He called for water, performed ablution, and sprinkled some of it upon me. I regained consciousness and said, \O Messenger of Allah"","" what shall I do with my wealth?\"" Then the following was revealed regarding me: \""Allah enjoins you concerning your children: for the male is equal to the portion of two females\"" (Qurʾān 4:11).\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12207","(12202) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us; Shuraḥbīl ibn Muslim al-Khawlānī heard Abā Umāmah say: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the Farewell Pilgrimage and heard him say: \Indeed"","" Allah has given every rightful person his right. Therefore"","" there shall be no bequest in favour of an heir.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Ṭayālisī 1223]"""""
"12208","(12203) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mujabbir, both from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, who said: A man from the people of al-ʿĀliyah came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"","" a man has died and left behind a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt. Go and distribute his inheritance.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) followed him on a donkey and said"","" \""O Lord"","" a man has left behind a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt.\"" He rode a little further and then said"","" \""O Lord"","" a man has left behind a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt.\"" He rode a little further and then said"","" \""O Lord"","" a man has left behind a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt.\"" Then he said"","" \""I do not think anything will be revealed to me regarding them; they shall receive nothing.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12209","(12204) Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rode to Qubāʾ seeking divine guidance (istikhārah) regarding the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and it was revealed to him that they shall have no inheritance.\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us; Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated it.\n\nIt was also narrated by Abū Nuʿaym Ḍirār ibn Ṣurd from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, with a connected chain mentioning Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) in it. It was also narrated from Sharīk ibn Abī Namir that al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd informed him: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and he remained silent. Then Jibrīl (peace be upon him) descended and said, \Jibrīl has informed me that they shall have no inheritance.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12210","(12205) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad al-Fārisī informed us from his original book; Abū Saʿīd Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī from his father Zayd ibn Thābit: that the meanings of these laws of inheritance and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit. As for the explanation (tafsīr), it is the explanation of Abī al-Zinād upon the meanings of Zayd ibn Thābit. He said: The son of a brother (i.e., nephew through a full or paternal brother) does not inherit through that maternal kinship at all. The grandmother who is the mother of the father of the mother does not inherit—he believed he said—nor the grandfather who is the mother's father, nor the daughter of a brother through the mother and father, nor the paternal aunt who is the sister of the father through the mother and father, nor the maternal aunt, nor anyone more distantly related in lineage than the deceased among those mentioned in this book—none of them inherits through that kinship at all. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12211","(12206) Abu Nasr — 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah — informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Nujayd — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjiyy — informed us: Ibn Bukayr — Malik — informed us: from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm — from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hanzalah al-Zurqiyy — that he informed him on the authority of a freed slave of Quraysh, an elderly man known as Ibn Mursi, who said: \I was sitting with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). When he had performed the Zuhr prayer"","" he said: 'O Yarfā'"","" bring me the letter that I wrote concerning the paternal aunt — he would ask about her and seek her counsel.' So Yarfā' brought it to him. Then he called for a vessel or a cup containing water"","" and he erased that letter in it"","" and then he said: 'If Allah were pleased with you"","" He would grant you permanence! If Allah were pleased with you"","" He would grant you permanence!'\"""""""
"12212","(12207) And with his chain of narration, he said: Malik narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm that he heard his father Kathir saying: \'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: 'How remarkable is the matter of the paternal aunt — she inherits"","" yet she does not leave an heir.'\"" It has also been narrated from 'Umar to the contrary"","" and the narration of the people of Madinah is more deserving of being correct. And Allah knows best."""""
"12213","(12208) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — informed us: they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani — informed us: Qabisah ibn 'Uqbah — informed us: Sufyan — narrated to us from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn 'Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah — from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn 'Abbad ibn Hunayf — from Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: \'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him): 'Teach your young boys swimming and your soldiers archery.' And they used to compete between targets. Then an arrow came from the west and struck a young boy"","" killing him in the lap of his maternal uncle"","" whose lineage was unknown. So Abu 'Ubaydah wrote to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with them both)"","" asking him to whom the blood-money (diyah) should be paid. 'Umar wrote back to him: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: Allah and His Messenger are the mawlā (patron) of the one who has no mawlā; and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir.'\"""""""
"12214","(12209) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — informed us: they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq — informed us: Hashim ibn al-Qasim — informed us: Shu'bah — narrated to us from Budayl al-'Uqayli, who said: \I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talah narrating from Rashid ibn Sa'd — from Abi 'Amir al-Hawzani — from al-Miqdam"","" the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" who said: 'Whoever leaves a debt (kalāl)"","" it falls upon us' — and he may have said"","" 'upon Allah and His Messenger' — 'and whoever leaves wealth"","" it goes for his heirs. I am the heir of the one who has no heir; I shall pay his blood-money and inherit his wealth. And the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir; he shall pay his blood-money and inherit his wealth.'\"""""""
"12215","(12210) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr — informed us: Abu Dawud — informed us: Sulayman ibn Harb, along with others, who said: Hammad — narrated to us from Budayl — from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib — from Rashid ibn Sa'd — from Abi 'Amir al-Hawzani — from al-Miqdam al-Kindi, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves a debt (dayn) or dependents (ḍay'ah)"","" they fall upon me; and whoever leaves wealth"","" it goes to his heirs. I am the mawlā of the one who has no mawlā; I shall inherit his wealth and free his captives. And the maternal uncle is the mawlā of the one who has no mawlā; he shall inherit his wealth and free his captives.'\"" Abu Dawud said: al-Zubaydi narrated it from Rashid ibn Sa'd — from Ibn 'A'idh — from al-Miqdam; and Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated from Rashid ibn Sa'd"","" saying: \""I heard al-Miqdam.\"""""""
"12216","(12211) And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr — informed us: Abu Dawud — informed us: 'Abd al-Salam ibn 'Atiq al-Dimashqi — informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak — informed us: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash — narrated to us from Yazid ibn Hujr — from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam — from his father — from his grandfather, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: 'I am the heir of the one who has no heir; I shall free his captives and inherit his wealth. And the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir; he shall free his captives and inherit his wealth.'\"""""""
"12217","(12212) Abu Muhammad — 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari — in Baghdad — informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shafi'i — informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Azhar — informed us: al-Mufaddal ibn Ghassan al-Ghallabi, who said: \Yahya ibn Ma'in used to reject the hadith: 'The maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir' — meaning the hadith of al-Miqdam — and he said: 'There is no strong hadith in it.'\"" The Shaykh said: \""And it has been narrated from another route"","" weaker than that.\"""""""
"12218","(12213) Abu Tahir al-Faqih — informed us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Saydalani — informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr — informed us: Abu Nu'aym — informed us: Sharik — narrated to us from Layth — from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir — from Abu Hurayrah — from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The maternal uncle is an heir.\"""""""
"12219","(12214) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan — informed us: they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq — informed us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr — informed us: Sharik — narrated to us from Layth — from Abu Hubayrah — from Abu Hurayrah — from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The maternal uncle is an heir.\"" This is a matter in which there is disagreement upon Sharik"","" as you see. And Layth ibn Abi Sulaym is not relied upon as an authority. And Allah knows best."""""
"12220","(12215) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — informed us: they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq — informed us: Abu 'Asim — narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj — from 'Amr ibn Muslim — from Tawus — from 'A'ishah, who said: \Allah and His Messenger are the mawlā of the one who has no mawlā"","" and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir.\"" This is the preserved narration from the statement of 'A'ishah"","" as a mawquf (stopping at the companion) report from her. And 'Abd al-Razzaq similarly narrated it from Ibn Jurayj as a mawquf report. Abu 'Asim used to sometimes raise it (in some of his narrations from him)"","" then he was uncertain about it. The raising (raf') is not preserved. And Allah knows best."""""
"12221","Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Ahwazi narrated to us; 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; Abu 'Asim mentioned it as a marfu' narration. Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Ma'in used to say: 'Amr ibn Muslim, the companion of Tawus, is not strong (in narration). It was narrated from Ibn Tawus as a mursal narration. [Hasan due to other narrations]"
"12222","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to me; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to me; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to me; Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to me; Sufyan narrated to me.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ardistani informed us; Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to me; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to me; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to me; 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to me; Sufyan narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Was'i ibn Habban: that Thabit ibn al-Dahdah — and he was a stranger (atiyy) among the Banu Unayf or among the Banu al-'Ajlan — died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: \Does he have an heir?\"" They could not find any heir for him"","" so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave his inheritance to his sister's son"","" who was Abu Lubabah ibn 'Abd al-Mundhir. This is the wording of the hadith of al-Ardistani"","" and the hadith of Abu 'Abdillah is abridged — he did not name the heir or the legator — and it is munqati' (disconnected).\n\nIt was narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his paternal uncle Was'i ibn Habban from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): that he asked 'Asim ibn 'Adiyy al-Ansari about Thabit ibn al-Dahdah"","" who had died: \""Do you know of any lineage he has among you?\"" He said: \""No"","" he is merely a stranger among us.\"" He said: \""So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed his inheritance for his sister's son.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us of it; Abu al-Hasan al-Karazi narrated to me; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Abu 'Ubayd; 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his paternal uncle Was'i ibn Habban"","" and he raised it (as marfu'). This is also munqati' (disconnected).\n\nAl-Shafi'i responded to this in his earlier works"","" saying: \""Thabit ibn al-Dahdah was killed on the day of Uhud before the revelation of the obligatory shares of inheritance (al-Fara'id).\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: His being killed on the day of Uhud is in the narration of al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib. [Da'if (Weak)]"""""
"12223","That is in what Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu Muhammad al-Muzani narrated to me; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to me; Abu al-Yaman informed me; Shu'ayb narrated from al-Zuhri; Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me in a story he mentioned, saying: \Ibn al-Dahdah did not remain long before the disbelievers of Quraysh came on the day of Uhud"","" so he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and fought them and was killed as a martyr.\"" [Da'if (Weak)]\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""The verse of obligatory shares (al-Fara'id) was revealed concerning what our companions affirm about the daughters of Mahmud ibn Maslamah"","" who was killed on the day of Khaybar. And it has also been said that it was revealed after Uhud concerning the daughters of Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'. All of that is after the matter of Thabit ibn al-Dahdah.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: In what we have narrated from the hadith of Jabir ibn 'Abdillah and his statement to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Only a kalalah inherits me"","" so how is the inheritance to be distributed?\"" — then the verse of obligatory shares was revealed"","" which indicates that it was revealed after Uhud"","" because before Uhud his father was alive"","" and he was killed on the day of Uhud as a martyr"","" and he left behind Jabir and daughters. When Jabir fell ill"","" he had sisters but had no father or son"","" so he said: \""Only a kalalah inherits me.\"" Then the verse of al-Fara'id was revealed. And it has also been said that the verse of al-Fara'id that is at the end of Surah al-Nisa' was revealed concerning him"","" and the one at the beginning of it was revealed concerning the two daughters of Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'"","" as al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said."""""
"12224","Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Jabir narrated to us; Yahya, meaning ibn Yusuf al-Zimmi, narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, who said: \The wife of Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' came with her two daughters from Sa'd and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" these are the two daughters of Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'. Their father was killed as a martyr with you on the day of Uhud"","" and their paternal uncle has taken their wealth and spent it"","" leaving them no property. And they cannot be married unless they have wealth.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Allah will decree concerning that.' Then Allah revealed the verse of inheritance (ayat al-Mirath)"","" so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent for their paternal uncle"","" called him"","" and said: 'Give the two daughters of Sa'd two-thirds"","" give their mother one-eighth"","" and what remains is for you.'\"" [Da'if (Weak)]"""""
"12225","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from al-Sha'bi, who said: \Ziyad was brought a man who had died and left behind his paternal aunt and his maternal aunt. He said: 'Do you know how 'Umayr — may Allah be pleased with him — judged in this matter?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'By Allah"","" I know the judgment of 'Umayr in this better than anyone. He placed the paternal aunt in the position of the brother and the maternal aunt in the position of the sister"","" so he gave the paternal aunt two-thirds and the maternal aunt one-third.'\""\n\nAl-Hasan"","" Jabir ibn Zayd"","" Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani"","" and others narrated that 'Umayr — may Allah be pleased with him — gave the paternal aunt two-thirds and the maternal aunt one-third. All of that is mursal (disconnected)"","" and the narration of the people of Madinah from 'Umayr is more likely to be correct. And Allah knows best. [Da'if (Weak)]"""""
"12226","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; they said: Abu al-'Abbas ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Yazid informed us; Muhammad ibn Salim narrated from al-Sha'bi from Masruq from 'Abdullah, who said: \The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother"","" the paternal aunt is in the position of the father"","" the brother's daughter is in the position of the brother"","" and every person of kinship (dhi rahm) is in the position of the kinship that connects him"","" when there is no heir of established share (dhi sahm).\""\n\nWe have narrated from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani from al-Sha'bi from Masruq"","" who said: 'Abdullah said: \""Place them in the positions of their fathers.\"" He used to say: \""Give inheritance to every person in the position of his father.\"" [Very Weak (Da'if Jiddan)]"""""
"12227","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah al-Isbahani informed us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Qattan narrated to me; al-Hasan ibn 'Isa informed me; Jarir narrated from al-Mughirah from his companions: \'Ali and 'Abdullah"","" when they could not find a person of established share (dhi sahm)"","" would give to the kinsfolk. They gave the granddaughter all the wealth"","" and the maternal uncle all the wealth. Likewise the brother's daughter and the sister's daughter — whether on the mother's side or the father's side or both — and the paternal aunt"","" the paternal uncle's daughter"","" the son's daughter's daughter"","" and the maternal grandfather"","" whether near or distant — if they are a kinsman (rahm)"","" they receive the wealth when no other heir is found. If a granddaughter and a sister's daughter are found"","" then half and half. If a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt are found"","" then one-third and two-thirds. The maternal uncle's daughter and the maternal aunt's daughter receive one-third and two-thirds.\"" [Very Weak (Da'if Jiddan)]"""""
"12228","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hasan and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri' and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-Saydalani narrated to us; they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to me; Abu 'Asim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Shahab from 'Ali ibn Husayn from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever"","" nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu 'Asim. [Bukhari 1485"","" Muslim 1614]"""""
"12229","Abu Muhammad 'Abdillah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us; Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabba' al-Za'farani narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn 'Ali from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman from Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \A disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim"","" nor does a Muslim inherit from a disbeliever.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and others from Sufyan. [Sahih]"""""
"12230","Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rafi' and Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated from al-Zuhri from 'Ali ibn Husayn from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" where will you camp tomorrow?\"" — and that was during the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: \""Has 'Aqil ibn Abi Talib left anything for us?\"" Then he said: \""A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever"","" nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.\"" Then he said: \""We shall camp tomorrow in the valley of Banu Kinanah"","" where Quraysh swore upon disbelief.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Mahmud"","" and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mihran and others from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih]"""""
"12231","(12226) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Quraysh informed us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us that Harmalah ibn Yahya informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me that Yunus ibn Yazid informed me from Ibn Shihab, who said: 'Ali ibn Husayn informed me that 'Amr ibn 'Uthman informed him from Usamah ibn Zayd that he said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" will you descend upon your house in Makkah?\"" He said: \""Has 'Aqil left for us any properties or houses?\"" And 'Aqil had inherited Abu Talib"","" he and Talib"","" and Ja'far and 'Ali did not inherit him because they were both Muslims"","" while 'Aqil and Talib were both disbelievers. For that reason"","" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" used to say: 'A believer does not inherit a disbeliever.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhari from Asbagh from Ibn Wahb"","" and it was narrated by Muslim from Harmalah. [Sahih]"""""
"12232","(12227) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Faqih informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi informed us that Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me that Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed me from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Shaybani informed us that Abu al-'Ala' Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Kufi in Egypt informed us that al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us that Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid informed us that al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us. He said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Yafi'i informed me from Ibn Jurayj from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \A Muslim does not inherit a Christian except if he be his slave or his female slave.\"" [Munkar]"""""
"12233","(12228) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Umar informed us that Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr and Abu al-Azhar both said: 'Abd al-Razzak informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Abu al-Zubayr informed from Jabir, who said: \A Jew or a Christian does not inherit a Muslim"","" nor does a Muslim inherit them"","" except if he be a slave of a man or his female slave.\"" This is a mawquf narration. 'Ali said: \""And this is the preserved (version).\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12234","(12229) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us that Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam al-'Abdi informed us that Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah said: I heard a number of them, among them Ya'qub ibn 'Ata', from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The adherents of two religions do not inherit one another.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Habib al-Mu'allim from 'Amr. [Abu Dawud 291]"""""
"12235","(12230) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us that Tamtam informed us that 'Abd al-Muta'al ibn Talib informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that al-Khalil ibn Murrah informed us from Qatadah from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \A Muslim does not inherit a disbeliever"","" nor does a disbeliever inherit a Muslim"","" and the adherents of two religions do not inherit one another.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"12236","(12231) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajan informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki informed us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushinji informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Malik informed us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath informed him that a paternal aunt of his, who was Jewish or Christian, had passed away, and that Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath mentioned that to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said to him: \Who inherits her?\"" So 'Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to him: \""Her coreligionists inherit her.\"" Then he came to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and asked him about that"","" so 'Uthman ibn 'Affan said to him: \""Do you think I have forgotten what 'Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to you?\"" Then he said: \""Her coreligionists inherit her.\"" [Sahih. Malik 1106]"""""
"12237","(12232) And with this chain of narration, he said: Malik informed us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \We do not inherit the adherents of other religions"","" nor do they inherit us.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12238","(12233) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Halim al-Marwazi informed us that Abu al-Muwajjih informed us that 'Abdan informed me that my father informed me from Shu'bah from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shahab, who said: \A paternal aunt of al-Ash'ath"","" who was Jewish"","" passed away"","" so he came to 'Umar"","" and he refused to let him inherit from her and said: 'Her coreligionists inherit her.'\"" [Sahih. Malik 1081]"""""
"12239","(12234) And with this chain of narration, from Shu'bah from Husayn, who said: \I saw an old man walking on a staff"","" and they said: 'This is the heir of Safiyyah bint Huyayy.' We used to say that when she died"","" he embraced Islam on account of her inheritance"","" but he was not made an heir.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12240","(12235) By way of deduction, from what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us that al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us that al-Shafi'i informed us that Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah from his father that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates it (for himself).\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""Since it is established in the Sunnah of the Prophet"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" that a slave does not own wealth"","" and that whatever the slave owns is owned by his master"","" and the master is not the father of the deceased nor an heir for whom a share has been prescribed"","" were we to give the slave a share on the grounds that he is a father"","" we would in fact be giving it to the master for whom no share has been prescribed"","" and we would be giving inheritance to one whom Allah has not made an heir. For this reason"","" we do not make a slave an heir for the reasons I have described"","" nor anyone in whom freedom"","" Islam"","" and innocence from killing are not all combined.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And Zayd ibn Thabit said the same. [Sahih. Al-Lam li'l-Shafi'i 4/77]"""""
"12241","(12236) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A killer shall not inherit from the blood-money of the one he killed.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12242","(12237) Abū Dāwūd recorded it in al-Marāsīl from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus al-Ṭarsūsī, from Ḥajjāj, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, except that he said in its text: \A deliberate killer and an accidental killer shall not inherit anything from the blood-money.\""\n\nIt was also reported by Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad; Abū al-Fasawī informed us; al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it. [Weak]"""""
"12243","(12238) Abū Saʿīd informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me that Ḥafs ibn Maymūnah narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah al-Aslamī narrated to him, saying: More than one narrator narrated to me that ʿAdī al-Judhāmī had two wives who fought with each other. He threw a stone at one of them, and she died from it. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived, he came to him and mentioned that to him. He (ﷺ) said to him: \Pay her blood-money"","" and do not inherit from her.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12244","(12239) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb: A man from Banī Mudlij, called Qatādah, had an umm walad (slave concubine) by whom he had two sons. He married a woman from the Arabs, who said: \I will not be pleased with you unless you command your umm walad to serve me.\"" He ordered her to serve her"","" but her two sons refused. Qatādah then took up his sword against one of his sons"","" and he died. Surāqah ibn Mālik ibn Juʿshum came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned that to him. He said to him: \""Prepare for me at Qudayd\"" — which is the land of Banī Mudlij — \""one hundred and twenty camels.\"" When ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived"","" he took thirty dharrʿah (young camels)"","" thirty ḥiqqah (three-year-old she-camels)"","" and forty khalifah (pregnant she-camels). Then he said: \""Where is the brother of the slain?\"" I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""The killer has nothing.\""\n\nThese are excellent mursal narrations"","" some of which strengthen others"","" and it has also been narrated as mawsūl (connected) from various routes. [Weak]"""""
"12245","(12240) Among them is what Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī — informed us that Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, Abū al-Shaykh — narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us that Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The killer has nothing. If he has no heir"","" then the closest of people to him shall inherit"","" and the killer shall not inherit anything.\""\n\n[Hasan. Abū Dāwūd 6662]"""""
"12246","(12241) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The killer has nothing from the inheritance.\""\n\nA group narrated it from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh. And it was also reported from him via Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"","" Ibn Jurayj"","" and al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ"","" from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"","" from his father"","" from his grandfather"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" a similar narration. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"12247","(12242) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated on the authority of a man — ʿAbd al-Razzāq said he was ʿAmr Barq — from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever kills a person"","" he shall not inherit from him"","" even if he has no other heir"","" and even if he is his child or his father.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed: \""The killer has no inheritance.\"" [Weak. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 17787]"""""
"12248","(12243) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us that al-Layth narrated on the authority of Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Farwah, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The killer shall not inherit.\""\n\nIsḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh is not used as a proof (ḥujjah) except that his supporting evidences strengthen him. And Allah knows best. [Weak. Ibn Mājah 2645]"""""
"12249","(12244) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdawayh al-Marwazī narrated to us that Maḥmūd ibn Ādam narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated on the authority of Muṭarrif, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar said: \The killer shall not inherit"","" whether by mistake or deliberately.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12250","(12245) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated on the authority of al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī, Zayd, and ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The killer shall not inherit anything"","" whether deliberately or by mistake.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12251","(12246) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah from Khilās: that a man threw a stone and struck his mother, and she died as a result. He then sought his share of her inheritance, but his brothers said to him: \You have no right.\"" They then brought the matter before ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" and ʿAlī said to him: \""Your share of her inheritance is the stone.\"" He also imposed the blood-money (diyah) upon him and did not give him anything from her inheritance. [Weak]"""""
"12252","(12247) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd informed us, Ḥabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from ʿAmr ibn Ḥarim from Jābir ibn Zayd, who said: Any man who kills a man or a woman, whether deliberately or by mistake, from among those from whom he would inherit, shall have no inheritance from either of them. And any woman who kills a man or a woman, whether deliberately or by mistake, shall have no inheritance from either of them. If the killing was deliberate, then retribution (qiṣāṣ) is required, unless the heirs of the slain forgive. If they forgive, then he shall have no inheritance from the blood-money (ʿaql) nor from his wealth. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both), Sharīḥ, and other Muslim judges ruled according to this. [Weak]"
"12253","(12248) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from ʿUbaydah al-Salmānī, who said: Among the Children of Israel there was a man who had no offspring, and he had abundant wealth. His brother's son was his heir. He (the nephew) then killed him, carried him by night, and placed him at the door of a man from another tribe. In the morning, he made accusations against them until they armed themselves and some of them mounted against others. The man of judgment and forbearance said: \Why are you killing one another when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is among you?\"" So they came to him"","" and he said: \""Allah commands you to slaughter a cow.\"" They said: \""Do you take us in jest?\"" He said: \""I seek refuge in Allah from being among the ignorant.\"" He (ʿUbaydah) said: If they had not been obstinate about the cow"","" the least of cows would have sufficed them"","" but they were severe"","" so severity was imposed upon them"","" until they reached the cow that they were commanded to slaughter. They found it with a man who had no other cow besides it. He said: \""By Allah"","" I will not reduce its price from the weight of its hide.\"" So they bought it for the weight of its hide in gold. They slaughtered it and struck him (the slain man) with part of it"","" and he stood up. They said: \""Who killed you?\"" He said: \""This one\"" — meaning his brother's son. Then he fell dead. The brother's son was not given anything from his wealth"","" and no killer was ever made an heir after that. [Good]"""""
"12254","(12249) That is, what Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Maṭīrī narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Maymūn narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us from Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb — who said: My father informed me from my grandfather, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood on the day of the Conquest of Makkah and said: \The people of two religions do not inherit from one another. A woman inherits from her husband's blood-money and his wealth"","" and he inherits from her blood-money and her wealth"","" so long as neither of them kills the other deliberately. If one of them kills the other deliberately"","" he shall inherit nothing from her blood-money or her wealth. If he kills his companion by mistake"","" he shall inherit from his wealth but shall not inherit from his blood-money.\""\n\nHe said: And ʿAlī informed us"","" Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us"","" Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"","" ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us"","" al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated with his chain the same. ʿAlī said: Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Ṭāʾifī is trustworthy.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī narrated it — though he is not authoritative — from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān from ʿAmr from Makhramah ibn Bukayr from his father from ʿAmr. And al-Shāfiʿī was hesitant regarding the narrations of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb unless they were corroborated by something that strengthens them. [Very Weak. Al-Silsilah al-Ḍaʿīfah 4674]\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: There is no followable report regarding the distinction between the killer by mistake inheriting and the killer by deliberate intent not inheriting"","" except the report of a man. If it were established"","" the proof would be in it"","" but it is not permissible to establish something for him and reject something else for him when there is no opposing narration.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And when the ḥadīth is not established"","" then he inherits nothing"","" whether the killing was deliberate or by mistake"","" as is indicated by the general principle that a killer does not inherit from the one he killed."""""
"12255","(12250) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr narrated to us, Abū al-Zinād informed me from Khārijah ibn Zayd from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded me, when the people of al-Yamāmah were killed, to make the living inherit from the dead and not to make some of them inherit from others. [Very Weak]"
"12256","(12251) With this chain of narration, he said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded me during the days of the plague of ʿAmwās. He said: A tribe would perish entirely, and another people would inherit them. He said: He commanded me to make the living inherit from the dead and not to make the dead inherit from one another. [Very Weak]\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī from ʿUmar that he made some of them inherit from one another from their inherited wealth. And in another narration, that he said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \Make these people inherit"",""\"" and he made them inherit from their inherited wealth. And from Qatādah: that ʿUmar made the people of the plague of ʿAmwās inherit from one another — if the hand and foot of one of them was upon the other"","" he made the higher inherit from the lower"","" and he did not make the lower inherit from the higher.\n\nThese two narrations are disconnected (munqaṭiʿ). And it has been said: from Qatādah from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah from Qabīṣah ibn Dhūʾayb from ʿUmar"","" and this is also disconnected. And what has been narrated from ʿUmar is more likely"","" and Allah knows best."""""
"12257","(12252) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād said: My father informed me from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit from his father, Zayd ibn Thābit, that he said regarding a group of people who were mutual heirs and perished in a collapse, drowning, or other such calamities, and it was not known which of them died before the other: \They do not inherit from one another.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12258","(12253) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways and ʿĪsā ibn Mīnāʾ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from the jurists of the people of Madīnah, who used to say: Any group of people who were mutual heirs and died in a collapse, drowning, fire, or other such cause, and the order of their deaths was unknown, they do not inherit from one another and do not exclude one another (as blockers of inheritance). This was the view of Zayd ibn Thābit, and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ruled according to it. [Authentic]"
"12259","(12254) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, Hishām ibn Yūnus narrated to us, al-Dārawardī narrated to us from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, that Umm Kulthūm bint ʿAlī and her son Zayd both perished on the same day, and the two cries (of death) coincided, so it was not known which of them perished first. She did not inherit from him, nor did he inherit from her. And the people of Ṣiffīn did not inherit from one another, and the people of al-Ḥarrah did not inherit from one another. [Weak]"
"12260","(12255) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us, Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād said: Abū al-Zinād said: A trustworthy person informed me that when the people of al-Ḥarrah were afflicted, the judgment regarding them rested with Zayd ibn Thābit, and among the people on that day were many Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and their sons. [Weak]"
"12261","(12256) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us — a man from the people of Basrah narrated to us — from 'Umarah ibn Hazn, from his father, that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, designated the survivors as heirs of those slain at the Battle of the Camel, and the living inherited from them. [Very Weak]\n\nHe said, and Yazid informed us — Nasr ibn Tarif al-Bahili informed us — from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that the slain of the Battle of the Camel and of al-Harrah were inherited from, and the living inherited from them."
"12262","(12257) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us — Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us — from Sufyan — from Hazn ibn Bashir al-Khath'ami, from his father, that 'Ali designated a man as heir, and his son and two brothers were both struck down at Siffin, and it was not known which of the two died before the other; so he made some of them heirs of others. Thus he said, and we only adopt the first narration. [Weak]"
"12263","(12258) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Malik narrated to us — from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from more than one of their scholars, that those who were slain on the Day of the Camel, the Day of Siffin, and the Day of al-Harrah did not inherit from one another. Then on the Day of Qudayd, none of those who were slain inherited anything from his companion, except where it was known that he had died before his companion. [Sahih]\n\nMalik said: \That is the matter regarding which there is no difference of opinion among us"","" and no doubt among any of the people of knowledge in our land.\""\n\nImam Ahmad"","" may Allah have mercy upon him"","" said: and it was narrated from Iyas ibn 'Abd al-Muzani that he said"","" \""Some of them are made heirs of others"",""\"" but the position of the majority is more deserving."""""
"12264","(12259) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us — Yazid ibn Harun informed us — Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us — Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \People of two different religions do not inherit from one another"","" and one who does not inherit does not act as a excluding heir (hajib).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12265","(12260) He said, and Yazid informed us — Shu'bah informed us — from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, who said: 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The polytheist neither acts as an excluding heir nor inherits.\""\n\nAnd 'Abd Allah"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""He acts as an excluding heir but does not inherit.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12266","(12261) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — from Ya'la ibn Ata', from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah ibn Qanif, who said: \I read before Sa'd"","" meaning Ibn Abi Waqqas"","" until I reached {And if a man is inherited from by kalalah"","" or a woman"","" and he has a brother}"","" so Sa'd said: 'A brother from the mother's side.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"12267","(12262) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us — Yazid ibn Harun informed us — 'Asim al-Ahwal informed us — from al-Sha'bi, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about kalalah, so he said: 'I shall give my opinion regarding it; if it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is an error, it is from me and from Satan. It is one who is neither survived by a child nor a parent.'\ Then when 'Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" was appointed as khalifah"","" he said: \""I would feel shy before Allah to reject anything that Abu Bakr said.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"12268","(12263) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — Abu Mu'awiyah informed us — from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid — from al-Sha'bi, who said: \Whoever claims that anyone from the Companions of Muhammad"","" peace be upon him"","" made uterine brothers heirs together with a paternal grandfather has lied.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"12269","(12264) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah informed us — Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Qattan narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Isa informed us — Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us — from al-Sha'bi, who said: \None of the Companions of the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" ever made uterine brothers heirs together with a paternal grandfather in the slightest.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12270","(12265) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Isbahani informed us — Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah informed us — Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Qattan narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Isa informed us — Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us — from al-Sha'bi, who said: \None of the Companions of the Prophet"","" peace be upon him"","" ever made uterine brothers heirs together with a paternal grandfather in the slightest.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12271","(12266) He said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Ibrahim, similarly."
"12272","(12267) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they both said: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Khallad informed us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah who said: \I fell ill"","" and the Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit me. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" how shall I dispose of my wealth? What shall I do with my wealth?' He did not tell me anything until the verse of inheritance was revealed: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah}.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Qutaybah"","" and Muslim narrated it from 'Amr al-Naqid"","" both from Sufyan.\n\n[Bukhari 187"","" Muslim 1616]"""""
"12273","(12268) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us, Sufyan informed us. He said: I heard Ibn al-Munkadir say that he heard Jabir say: \I fell ill"","" and the Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit me"","" he and Abu Bakr walking. I had lost consciousness"","" so I did not speak to him. He performed ablution and sprinkled its water upon me. I regained consciousness and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" what shall I do with my wealth? I have sisters.' He said: 'The verse of inheritance has been revealed: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah} — one who has no child but has sisters.'\""\n\nIn the narration of Shu'bah from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir in this hadith"","" he said: \""Only the kalalah shall inherit me"",""\"" so he named the one who inherits him as kalalah"","" and its mention has already passed.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"","" concerning whom the verse of kalalah was revealed"","" had neither child nor parent"","" because his father was killed on the day of Uhud"","" and this verse was revealed after that. [Sahih]"""""
"12274","(12269) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us, Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi informed us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr informed us, Waki' informed us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara' who said: \The last verse to be revealed was: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah}.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from 'Ali ibn Khashram from Waki'"","" and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from Abu Ishaq.\n\n[Bukhari 4363"","" Muslim 1618]"""""
"12275","(12270) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb informed us, Zuhayr ibn Harb Abu Khaythamah informed us, Shababah ibn Sawwar informed us, Shu'bah informed us from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talhah al-Ya'muri who said: \'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon and mentioned the hadith. In it he said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not speak to me more sternly about anything"","" nor did I press the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on any matter more than the verse of kalalah"","" until he struck my chest and said: \""Is not the verse of al-Sayf (the summer verse) sufficient for you?\"" — which was revealed at the end of Surah al-Nisa': {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah} to the end of the verse. And I shall give a ruling concerning it that will be known by those who recite and those who do not recite"","" and it is: other than the father"","" as I understand it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb. [Muslim 567]"""""
"12276","(12271) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Dassah informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim informed us, Abu Bakr informed us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib who said: \A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" they ask you about the kalalah. What is the kalalah?' He said: 'The verse of al-Sayf is sufficient for you.' I said to Abu Ishaq: 'It is one who dies and leaves neither child nor parent.' He said: 'That is what they thought it was.'\"" [Hasan. Al-Sijistani narrated it"","" 2889]"""""
"12277","(12272) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us, Abu al-Husayn 'Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Dawudi informed us, Abu 'Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani informed us, Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn al-Aswad informed us, Yahya ibn Adam informed us, 'Ammar ibn Ruzayq informed us from Abu Ishaq from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman who said: \A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah}.' He said: 'One who leaves neither child nor parent — his heirs are the kalalah.'\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: 'Ammar narrated from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara' regarding the kalalah"","" he said: \""The verse of al-Sayf is sufficient for you.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: This is the well-known one"","" and the hadith of Abu Ishaq from Abu Salamah is munqati' (discontinuous) and not well-known. [Da'if. Al-Sijistani in al-Marasil"","" 37]"""""
"12278","(12273) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Dabbi informed us, Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us, Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us, Sufyan informed us from 'Asim al-Ahwal from al-Sha'bi who said: \'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'The kalalah is one who has no child.' Abu Bakr said: 'The kalalah is one who has neither child nor parent.' When 'Umar was stabbed"","" he said: 'I would be ashamed to disagree with Abu Bakr. The kalalah is one who has neither child nor parent.'\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12279","(12274) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us, 'Abd al-A'la informed us, Hammad informed us from 'Imran ibn Hudayr from al-Sumayt ibn 'Umayr that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \There came upon me a time when I did not know what the kalalah was"","" and the kalalah is one who has neither father nor child.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12280","(12275) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad ibn Nasr informed us, Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Hushaym informed us from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah from Abu Ishaq from Sulaym ibn 'Abd al-Sululi that he heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \The kalalah is one who leaves neither child nor parent.\""\n\nAnd likewise Israel narrated it from Abu Ishaq. [Da'if]"""""
"12281","(12276) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from al-Ḥasan — meaning Ibn Muḥammad — who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about al-kalālah. He said: \It is one who has neither parent nor child.\"" I said: \""But Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" says { *If a man dies and he has no child* }.\"" He became angry and rebuked me. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12282","(12277) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us; Sufyān narrated, saying: ʿAmr said: I heard al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad narrating, saying: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about al-kalālah, and he said: \It is one who has neither child nor parent.\"" I said to him: \""Allah said { *If a man dies and he has no child"","" and he has a sister* }.\"" He became angry and rebuked me"","" and said: \""It is one who has neither child nor parent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12283","(12278) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; both said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to me; Sulaymān al-Aḥwal narrated from Ṭāwūs, who said: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās saying: \I was the last of the people to have kept company with ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and I heard him saying: 'The statement is what I said.' I asked: 'And what did you say?' He said: 'Al-kalālah is one who has no child.'\"" This is how it is in this narration. However"","" what has been narrated to us from ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the interpretation of al-kalālah is more consistent with the evidences of the Book and the Sunnah than this narration"","" and it is more deserving of being considered authentic due to the uniqueness of this narration and the prevalence of narrations from them both that contradict it. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12284","(12279) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who heard Murrah say: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Three things — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ explained them is more beloved to me than the red camels: the Caliphate"","" al-kalālah"","" and usury.\"" So I said to Murrah: \""Who doubts about al-kalālah that it is other than the child and the parent?\"" He said: \""They doubt about the parent.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12285","(12280) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Dhakwān narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, from his father: that the meanings of these injunctions and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād based on the meanings of Zayd. He said: \The inheritance of the maternal brothers is that they do not inherit alongside the child"","" nor alongside the son's child"","" whether male or female"","" in anything"","" nor alongside the father"","" nor alongside the paternal grandfather in anything.\"" He said: \""The inheritance of the full brothers is that they do not inherit alongside the male child"","" nor alongside the male son's child"","" nor alongside the father in anything.\"" He said: \""The inheritance of the paternal brothers"","" when there is none of the children of the mother and father present"","" is the same as the inheritance of the full brothers. When the full brothers and the paternal brothers are gathered together"","" and among the children of the mother and father there is a male"","" then there is no inheritance alongside him for any of the paternal brothers.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12286","(12281) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṣabīḥ narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ narrated, saying: Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: \The grandfather is a father"","" so long as there is no father between him and the deceased"","" just as the son's son is a son"","" so long as there is no son between him and the deceased.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12287","(12282) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab: that Zayd ibn Thābit did not allocate any share of inheritance for the grandmother alongside her son. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12288","(12283) He said: And Yazīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sālim informed us from al-Shaʿbī: that ʿAlī and Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them both, did not allocate any share of inheritance for the grandmother alongside her son. [Very Ḍaʿīf]"
"12289","(12284) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Hushaym narrated from Mughīrah from Fuḍayl ibn ʿAmr, from Ibrāhīm: that ʿAlī and Zayd used not to grant the grandmother inheritance alongside her son. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12290","(12285) He said: And Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī: that ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, did not grant the grandmother inheritance when her son was alive. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12291","(12286) As for the one who informed us — Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr, both of whom said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Muhammad ibn Salim informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'Abdillah, regarding the grandmother along with her son, that he said: \The first grandmother whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a share — one-sixth — along with her son"","" and her son was alive.\""\n\nMuhammad ibn Salim is alone in narrating it thus. It has also been narrated from Yunus"","" from Ibn Sirin"","" who said: \""I was informed\""; and from al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar"","" from Ibn Sirin"","" from 'Abdillah; and from al-Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Malik"","" from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ). The hadith of Yunus and al-Ash'ath is munqati' (disconnected). Muhammad ibn Salim is not used as a basis for argument (la yuhtajju bihi). Rather"","" the sound narration in this matter is from 'Umar"","" 'Abdillah"","" and 'Imran ibn Husayn. [Da'if]"""""
"12292","(12287) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu 'Abdillah ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Maisarah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) granted inheritance to the grandmother of a man from Thaqif along with her son. [Da'if]"
"12293","(12288) And Abu Sa'id informed us; Abu 'Abdillah informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us; Abu Qudamah narrated to us; Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu 'Amr, from 'Abdillah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that he granted inheritance to a grandmother along with her son. [Da'if]"
"12294","(12289) And Abu Sa'id informed us; Abu 'Abdillah informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah informed us, from Salamah ibn 'Alqamah, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu al-Dahma', from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that he used to grant inheritance to the grandmother while her son was alive. [Hasan]"
"12295","(12290) Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, all saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Abu al-Munib 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdillah al-'Ataki informed us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave the grandmother one-sixth when there was no mother."
"12296","(12291) Kharijah ibn Zayd informed us, from his father, that the meanings of these ordinances of inheritance and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thabit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abu al-Zinad upon the meanings of Zayd. He said: \The inheritance of grandmothers is that the mother of the mother does not inherit anything alongside the mother"","" and in cases other than that"","" one-sixth is prescribed for her as an obligatory share. And the mother of the father does not inherit anything alongside the mother or the father"","" and in cases other than that"","" one-sixth is prescribed for her as an obligatory share.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12297","(12292) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed me; Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; Adam ibn Iyas narrated to us; Warqa' informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {Allah enjoins you concerning your children: for the male is equal to the share of two females} — he said: \Inheritance used to be for the child"","" and bequest used to be for the parents. Then Allah abrogated from that what He willed. He made for the male child the equivalent of the share of two females"","" and He made for the parents two-sixths"","" and He made for the husband one-half or one-quarter"","" and He made for the woman one-quarter or one-eighth.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yusuf"","" from Warqa'. [Bukhari 2746]"""""
"12298","(12293) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu 'Abdillah ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us; Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Khallali informed us; Abu Ya'la informed us — all saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdillah ibn Dhakwan informed us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father, that the meanings of these ordinances of inheritance and their principles are all from Zayd ibn Thabit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abu al-Zinad upon the meanings of Zayd. He said: \A man inherits from his wife — if she does not leave a child or a son's child — one-half. If she leaves a child or a son's child"","" male or female"","" her husband inherits one-quarter"","" and nothing is diminished from that. And a woman inherits from her husband — if he does not leave a child or a son's child — one-quarter. If he leaves a child or a son's child"","" his wife inherits one-eighth.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12299","(12294) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu 'Abdillah ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Bakr al-Farisi informed us; Isma'il al-Khallali informed us; Abu Ya'la informed us — all saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the meanings of these ordinances of inheritance and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thabit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abu al-Zinad upon the meanings of Zayd. He said: \The inheritance of the mother from her child — when her son or daughter dies and leaves a child or a son's child"","" male or female"","" or leaves two or more siblings"","" male or female"","" whether from both father and mother"","" or from the father"","" or from the mother — is one-sixth. If the deceased does not leave a child"","" a son's child"","" or two or more siblings"","" then the mother receives one-third in full"","" except in two cases only"","" and they are: that a man dies and leaves his wife and his parents — his wife receives one-quarter"","" and his mother receives one-third of what remains"","" which is one-quarter of the original estate; and that a woman dies and leaves her husband and her parents — her husband receives one-half"","" and her mother receives one-third of what remains"","" which is one-sixth of the original estate.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12300","(12295) And Abu Sa'id informed us; Abu 'Abdillah ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, from his father, that he used to exclude the mother (from her full share) on account of two brothers. They said to him: \O Abu Sa'id! Allah says: {And if he has brothers"","" then his mother shall receive one-sixth}"","" and you exclude her on account of two brothers?\"" He said: \""The Arabs refer to two brothers as 'ikhwah' (siblings"","" plural).\"" They said to him: \""O Abu Sa'id! Did you think it meant eight pairs of sheep — two by two — and of goats two by two"","" and of camels two by two"","" and of cattle two by two?\"" He said: \""No. Allah says: {And He made from it pairs — the male and the female} — so they are two pairs; each one of them is a 'zawj' (pair/mate). He says: the male is a mate and the female is a mate.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12301","(12296) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh reported from Khālid, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, that a man asked Ibn ʿUmar about a man who left behind a mother and two brothers. He said: \Go to Zayd and ask him"","" then come back to me and inform me what Zayd says.\"" So he went to Zayd"","" and Zayd said: \""The mother is excluded from the third; her share is one-sixth.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12302","(12297) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us — Muḥammad narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Shabābah narrated to us — Ibn Abī Dhiʾb reported from Shuʿbah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he entered upon ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \Two brothers do not exclude the mother from the third.\"" Allah"","" the Most High"","" said: {If he has brothers} (al-Nisāʾ"","" 4:11). \""Two brothers (ikhwān) are not 'brothers' (ikhwah) in the language of your people.\"" ʿUthmān said: \""I cannot reverse what was established before me and has already been implemented in the provinces and by which people have inherited.\"" It is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the case of parents and brothers that he said: \""The brothers only exclude the mother from the third so that the one-sixth may be for them.\"" This is contrary to the statement of Zayd ibn Thābit and others. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12303","(12298) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Isḥāq and Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both said — ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us — Maʿmar reported from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said regarding the one-sixth by which the brothers exclude their mother: \It is for the brothers and not for the father. The mother's share is reduced so that it may go to the brothers.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\nIbn Ṭāwūs said: \""It reached me that the Prophet ﷺ gave them the one-sixth.\"" I met one of the children of that man who had been given the one-sixth by his brothers"","" and he said: \""It reached us that it had been a bequest (waṣiyyah) for them.\"""""""
"12304","(12299) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to us — Manṣūr and Sulaymān reported from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" when he walked with us on a path"","" we found him to be gentle. A case involving a woman and two parents was brought to him"","" and he assigned the woman one-quarter and the mother one-third of what remained.\"" Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah also narrated it from Manṣūr and added: \""And what remained was for the father.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12305","(12300) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus and Wakīʿ reported from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" when he walked a path and we followed him"","" we found him to be gentle. A case involving a woman and two parents was brought to him"","" and he gave the woman one-quarter"","" the mother one-third of what remained"","" and the father two shares.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12306","(12301) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to us. He said: I heard Ayyūb — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Sufyān al-Thawrī reported from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Abī Qilābah, from Abī al-Muhallab, from ʿUthmān, regarding a woman and two parents, that he made it out of four shares: the woman received one-quarter as one share, the mother one-third of what remained as one share, and the father received what remained. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12307","(12302) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Ḥajjāj ibn Minḥāl narrated to us — Ḥammād reported from al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿUmayr ibn Saʿīd, from al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him: \For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother one-third of what remains"","" and for the father two shares.\"" It is narrated from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās"","" may Allah be pleased with both of them"","" a view contrary to this. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12308","(12303) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Yazīd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah reported from al-Ḥakam, from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding a husband and two parents. He said: \For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother one-third"","" and for the father one-sixth.\"" Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah is abandoned (matrūk). It is also narrated through another chain that is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12309","(12304) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Abū Kāmil narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah reported from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh, regarding a woman and two parents: \For the mother is one-third of what remains.\"" He said: And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""For her is one-third of the entire estate.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12310","(12305) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us — al-Thawrī narrated to us — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us — Sufyān reported from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aṣbahānī, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās sent me to Zayd ibn Thābit to ask him about a husband and two parents. Zayd said: 'For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother one-third of what remains"","" and for the father the remainder of the estate.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""For the mother is the full one-third (of the entire estate).\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yazīd ibn Hārūn. In the narration of Rūḥ: \""For the mother is one-third of what remains"","" which is one-sixth.\"" So Ibn ʿAbbās sent word to him: \""Do you find this in the Book of Allah?\"" He said: \""No"","" but I dislike giving preference to a mother over a father.\"" And Ibn ʿAbbās used to give the mother one-third of the entire estate. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12311","(12306) Abū ʿAbdullāh and Abū Saʿīd both reported to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sharīk ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aṣbahānī from ʿIkrimah, a similar narration. He (ʿIkrimah) said: \I came to Ibn ʿAbbās and informed him. He said: 'Go back to him and say to him: Did you say this based on the Book of Allah"","" or based on your own opinion?'\"" He said: \""So I went back to him"","" and he said: 'Based on my own opinion.'\"" He said: \""So I returned to Ibn ʿAbbās and informed him.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""And I too say"","" based on my own opinion"","" that the mother receives the full third.\"" [Ṣaḥīh (authentic) from other sources. Excluding his statement: \""And I too say based on my own opinion.\""]"""""
"12312","(12307) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from a man from Fuḍayl from Ibrāhīm, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās opposed the people regarding this matter.\"" [Ṣaḥīh (authentic)]"""""
"12313","(12308) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Abū ʿAbdullāh from Fuḍayl from Ibrāhīm, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās opposed all the people of prayer (i.e."","" the scholars) regarding the case of a husband and two parents.\"" [Ṣaḥīh (authentic)]"""""
"12314","(12309) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Yazīd al-Rishk, who said: \I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib about a man who died and left behind a wife and two parents.\"" He said: \""Zayd divided it into four shares: the wife receives one share"","" the mother receives one-third of what remains"","" and the father receives the remainder of the estate.\"" [Ṣaḥīh (authentic)]"""""
"12315","(12310) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥmad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Abū Qays said: \I heard Huzayl ibn Sharḥbīl say: 'Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī was asked about a daughter"","" a daughter of a son"","" and a sister. He said: \""For the daughter is half"","" and for the sister is half.\"" He said: \""Go to Ibn Masʿūd"","" for he will follow me (in this ruling).\""' So Ibn Masʿūd was asked about it and was informed of Abū Mūsā's statement. He said: 'Then I would indeed be astray"","" and I would not be among the rightly guided. I judge in this matter according to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) judged: for the daughter is half"","" for the daughter of the son is one-sixth — completing the two-thirds — and whatever remains is for the sister.'\"" He said: \""So we went to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī and informed him of Ibn Masʿūd's statement. He said: 'Do not ask me about anything as long as this scholar (al-ḥabr) is among you.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīh from Ādam. [Ḥasan (good)]"""""
"12316","(12311) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) until we came to a woman from the Anṣār in the Aswāf. She was the grandmother of Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit.\"" He mentioned the hadith and said: \""The woman came with her two daughters and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" these are the two daughters of Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās. He was killed alongside you on the day of Uḥud"","" and their paternal uncle has taken their entire estate and inheritance"","" leaving nothing that he did not take. What is your opinion"","" O Messenger of Allah? By Allah"","" they will never be married unless they have some wealth!'\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" will judge in this matter.\"" Then Sūrat al-Nisāʾ was revealed: {Allah enjoins you concerning your children...} (the verse). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Call the woman and her companion (the uncle) for me.\"" He said to their paternal uncle: \""Give them two-thirds"","" give their mother one-eighth"","" and whatever remains is for you.\""\n\n(G) His statement: \""Istafāʾa mālahumā\"" — its meaning is: he reclaimed and recovered their rightful share of the inheritance. Its root is from al-fayʾ"","" which means \""return.\""\n\n(J) His statement: \""Thābit ibn Qays\"" — this is an error; rather"","" it is Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ. [Ḍaʿīf (weak)]"""""
"12317","(12312) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed it to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn al-Sarḥ narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Dāwūd ibn Qays and others from the people of knowledge narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl from Jābir that the wife of Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" Saʿd has passed away and left behind two daughters.\"" He then narrated the hadith.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""This is the correct version.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (weak)]"""""
"12318","(12313) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr al-Fārisī informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Khallālī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us. Both said: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from Khārijah ibn Zayd from his father Zayd ibn Thābit that the meanings of these shares of inheritance and their fundamental principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit, while the explanation (tafsīr) is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād based on the meanings (understood) from Zayd. He said: \The inheritance of the child is that when a man or a woman dies and leaves behind one daughter"","" she receives half. If there are two or more females"","" they receive two-thirds. If there is a male among them"","" then no one among them has a fixed share (farīḍah). Rather"","" one begins with whoever among them shares in a fixed share; he is given his fixed share"","" and whatever remains after that is distributed among them — the male receiving the equivalent of the portion of two females.\""\n\nHe said: \""The status of the children of sons"","" when there are no children (of the deceased) below them"","" is the same as the status of the children (themselves) — their males are like their males and their females are like their females. They inherit as they inherit and they exclude (others) as they exclude (others). If the children and the children of the son are combined"","" and there is a male among the children"","" then no one among the children of the son inherits alongside him. If there is no male among the children"","" and there are two or more daughters"","" then the daughters of the son do not inherit alongside them unless there is a male among the daughters of the son who is of the same degree as they are (in relation to the deceased) or is more distant than they are. In that case"","" he returns the surplus to those who are of his degree and those above him among the daughters of the sons"","" if there is a surplus"","" and they divide it — the male receiving the equivalent of the portion of two females. If there is nothing surplus"","" then they receive nothing.\""\n\n\""If the children consist of only one daughter"","" and he left behind a daughter of a son or more than that among the daughters of the son"","" all of them being of the same degree"","" then they receive one-sixth"","" completing the two-thirds. If there is a male among the daughters of the son who is of their same degree"","" then they receive neither one-sixth nor a fixed share. However"","" if there is a surplus after the fixed shares of the people of inheritance (ahl al-farāʾiḍ)"","" that surplus goes to that male and to those females who are of his degree — the male receiving the equivalent of the portion of two females. Those who are more distant than they are receive nothing. If nothing remains surplus"","" then they receive nothing.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (weak)]"""""
"12319","(12314) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Maʿbad ibn Khālid from Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah regarding two daughters, daughters of a son, sons of a son, two full sisters, and brothers and sisters from the father's side: she made the daughters of the son and the sons of the son share together with the brothers and sisters from the father's side in what remained — meaning according to the principle {the male receives the equivalent of the portion of two females}. He said: \And ʿAbdullāh (ibn Masʿūd) did not make them share together — meaning he allocated what remained exclusively to the males"","" excluding the females.\"" [Ḥasan (good)]"""""
"12320","(12315) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah, who said: \Masrūq arrived from Madīnah and he was making them share together (in the residue).\"" ʿAlqamah said to him: \""Is there anyone more authoritative in your estimation than ʿAbdullāh (ibn Masʿūd)?\"" He said: \""No"","" but I came to Madīnah and I saw Zayd ibn Thābit and the people of Madīnah making them share together in the case of a man who left behind full sisters"","" brothers and sisters from the father's side"","" daughters"","" daughters of a son"","" and sons of a son.\"" [Ṣaḥīh (authentic)]"""""
"12321","(12316) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Jarīr informed us, from al-Mughīrah, from his companions, and from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī: This is the matter in which ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh, and Zayd differed: two daughters, a son's son, and a son's daughter. According to the view of ʿAlī and Zayd: the two daughters receive two-thirds, and what remains goes to the son's son and the son's daughter, the male receiving the share of two females. And according to the view of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd: the two daughters receive two-thirds, and what remains goes to the male, not the female, because he did not increase the daughters' share beyond two-thirds.\n\nA daughter, a son's daughter, and a son's son. According to the view of ʿAlī and Zayd: the daughter receives half, and what remains goes to the son's son and the son's daughters, the male receiving the share of two females. And according to the view of ʿAbdullāh: the daughter receives half, and the son's daughters receive the complement of two-thirds, and what remains goes to the son's son.\n\n[Weak]"
"12322","(12317) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī in al-Kūfah informed us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym informed us: Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā and Qabīṣah informed us, from Sufyān.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī informed us, from Abū Qays, from al-Huzayl ibn Shuraḥbīl, who said: A man came to Abū Mūsā and Salmān ibn Rabīʿah and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister. They said: The daughter receives half, and the full sister receives what remains. And they said to him: Go to ʿAbdullāh and ask him, for he will follow us. He said: So I went to ʿAbdullāh and mentioned that to him. He said: Then I would be astray, and I would not be among the guided. Rather, I shall judge in the matter as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged: the daughter receives half, the son's daughter receives one-sixth — the complement of two-thirds — and the sister receives what remains. The wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh, and in the narration of Janāḥ it is: as the Prophet (ﷺ) judged.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, from Sufyān. [Bukhārī 6239]"
"12323","(12318) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us: My father informed me: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us: Sufyān narrated it with its meaning: I shall judge in the matter with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — or he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — thus. Sufyān said: The daughter receives half, the son's daughter receives one-sixth, and what remains goes to the sister.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12324","(12319) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Isḥāq al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us, from al-Mughīrah and al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm: that ʿAlī and ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd used not to give the brother's son any inheritance alongside the grandfather.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12325","(12320) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sālim informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: None among the people used to give a maternal brother or a brother's son any inheritance alongside the grandfather.\n\n[Weak]"
"12326","(12321) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Yaḥyā informed us: Yazīd informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: I was informed that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to assign the sons of a brother, alongside the grandfather, the positions of their fathers, and none of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) used to do that other than him."
"12327","(12322) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym informed us, from Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rabīʿah ibn Qānif: that Saʿd used to recite: {And if a man or a woman leaves property to be inherited by neither parents nor offspring, and he has a brother or a sister} — from the mother.\n\n[Weak]"
"12328","(12323) And Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Rūḥ informed us: Saʿīd informed us, from Qatādah: that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) said in his sermon: Know that this verse which is at the beginning of Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, concerning the matter of inheritance, Allah revealed it regarding the child and the parent. And the second verse in Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, Allah revealed it regarding the husband and the wife and the maternal siblings. And the verse with which He concluded Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, Allah revealed it regarding the full siblings and the paternal siblings.\n\n[Weak]"
"12329","(12324) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā informed us. Both said: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Dhakwān informed us, from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī, from his father: that the meanings of these inheritances and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād upon the meanings of Zayd ibn Thābit. He said: The inheritance of the maternal siblings is that they do not inherit alongside the child, nor alongside the son's child, whether male or female, nor alongside the father, nor alongside the grandfather, the father's father. And in all other cases besides that, one-sixth is assigned to one of them, whether male or female. And if they are two or more, male or female, one-third is assigned to them, and they share it equally.\n\n[Weak]"
"12330","(12325) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Hishām al-Dastawāʾī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us, from Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbdillāh, the companion of al-Dastawāʾī, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: I fell ill and I had seven sisters. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me and sprinkled water upon my face, and I regained consciousness. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath two-thirds for my sisters? He said: Hold back. I said: Half? He said: Hold back. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) left, then he returned and said: O Jābir, I consider you near death — or he said: I consider you dead from this illness — and Allah has revealed concerning your sisters, and He has clarified it and assigned two-thirds for them. Jābir used to say: These verses were revealed concerning me: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning one who has neither parents nor children} and the rest of the verses. The wording is from the ḥadīth of Wahb ibn Jarīr, and the ḥadīth of al-Ṭayālisī is abridged.\n\nAnd Kathīr ibn Hishām narrated it from Hishām, similar to the narration of Wahb, except that he said: He said: O Jābir, I do not consider you dead from this illness of yours.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad 15062]"
"12331","(12326) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn Thābit, that the principles and foundations of these laws of inheritance are from Zayd ibn Thābit. As for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād upon the meanings of Zayd ibn Thābit. He said: The inheritance of the full siblings (brothers and sisters from the father and mother) is that they do not inherit alongside a male child, nor alongside a male child of a son, nor alongside the father at all. However, alongside the daughters and the daughters of the sons—provided the deceased has not left a grandfather (father's father)—they are residuary heirs (ʿaṣabah). One begins with those who have a fixed share (farīḍah), and they are given their fixed shares. If anything remains after that, it goes to the full siblings (from the father and mother) among them according to the Book of Allah, whether they are male or female, the male receiving the portion of two females. If nothing remains, then they receive nothing.\n\nIf the deceased has not left a father, nor a grandfather (father's father), nor a male child, nor a female child, then for a single full sister (from the father and mother), the fixed share is one-half. If there are two or more full sisters, their fixed share is two-thirds. If there is a male full brother with them, then none of the sisters has a fixed share. One begins with those who share with them among the people of fixed shares, and they are given their fixed shares. Whatever remains after that is distributed among the full brothers and sisters (from the father and mother), the male receiving the portion of two females—except in one specific case in which nothing remained for them, so they shared with the children of their mother. That is the case of a woman who died and left behind her husband, her mother, her maternal brothers (brothers from her mother), and her full sisters. The husband received one-half, the mother received one-sixth, and the two maternal sons received one-third, and nothing remained. So the full children of the father and mother shared in this inheritance with the children of the mother in their one-third, the male receiving the portion of the female, because they are all children of the deceased's mother.\n\nHe said: The inheritance of the half-siblings from the father (ʿallātī brothers), when there are no full siblings (from the father and mother) with them, is the same as the inheritance of the full siblings (from the father and mother)—their males are like their males and their females are like their females—except that they do not share with the children of the mother in this particular inheritance in which the full children of the father and mother shared. When the full siblings (from the father and mother) and the half-siblings from the father gather, and among the children of the father and mother there is a male, then none of the half-siblings from the father inherits alongside him. If the children of the father and mother consist of only one female, and the children of the father consist of one female or more, with no male among them, then the fixed share for the full sister (from the father and mother) is one-half, and the fixed share for the daughters of the father is one-sixth, completing the two-thirds. If there is a male half-brother from the father with the daughters of the father, then they have no fixed share. One begins with the people of fixed shares, and they are given their fixed shares. If anything remains after that, it is distributed among the children of the father, the male receiving the portion of two females. If nothing remains, then they receive nothing.\n\nIf the children of the father and mother are two females or more, then their fixed share is two-thirds, and the daughters of the father do not inherit alongside them—unless there is a male from the father with them. If there is a male with them, one begins with the fixed shares of those entitled to them, and they are given their shares. If anything remains after that, it is distributed among the children of the father, the male receiving the portion of two females. If nothing remains, then they receive nothing. [Weak]"
"12332","(12327) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Jarīr narrated from al-Mughīrah, from his companions, and from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, and from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī: A full sister (from the father and mother) and a half-brother and half-sisters from the father. According to the opinion of ʿAlī and Zayd: the full sister (from the father and mother) receives one-half, and the remainder goes to the half-sisters and half-brother from the father, the male receiving the portion of two females. According to the opinion of ʿAbd Allāh: the full sister (from the father and mother) receives one-half, the half-sisters from the father receive the completion of two-thirds, and the remainder goes to the half-brother from the father.\n\nTwo full sisters (from the father and mother) and a half-brother and half-sister from the father. According to the opinion of ʿAlī and Zayd: the two full sisters (from the father and mother) receive two-thirds, and the remainder is shared between the half-sister and half-brother from the father, the male receiving the portion of two females. According to the opinion of ʿAbd Allāh: the two full sisters (from the father and mother) receive two-thirds, and the remainder goes to the male to the exclusion of the female, because he did not hold the view that the sisters' share could exceed two-thirds. [Weak]"
"12333","(12328) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhab al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ narrated to us: Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated from Sufyān, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed that debt takes precedence over the bequest, and you recite: \After any bequest that was made or debt\"" (al-Nisāʾ"","" 4:11). And indeed"","" the children of the mother (maternal siblings) inherit to the exclusion of the children of the ʿallāt (half-siblings from the father). A man inherits his brother from his father and mother to the exclusion of his brothers from his father. [Weak]"""""
"12334","(12329) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Qays, from Huzayl, who said: A man came to Abū Mūsā asking him about a woman who had left behind her daughter, her son's daughter, and her sister. He said: For her daughter is one-half, and for her sister is one-half, and the son's daughter receives nothing. Go to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, for he will tell you the same as I have told you. So he went to ʿAbd Allāh and asked him, and informed him of what Abū Mūsā had said. He said: \Then I would be astray"","" and I would not be among the guided! Rather"","" I shall judge in this matter according to what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) decreed: for her daughter is one-half"","" for her son's daughter is one-sixth"","" completing the two-thirds"","" and whatever remains goes to her sister.\"" He went back to Abū Mūsā and informed him"","" and he said: \""Do not ask us about anything as long as this learned man (al-ḥabr) is among you.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam from Shuʿbah. [Authentic]"""""
"12335","(12330) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us: Bishr, who is ibn Khālid, narrated to us: Muḥammad, who is ibn Jaʿfar, narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, who said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal judged among us during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding a woman who had left behind her daughter and her sister: one-half for the daughter and one-half for the sister.\n\nSulaymān said afterwards: He judged among us but did not mention \during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Bishr ibn Khālid al-ʿAskarī. [Bukhārī"","" 6741]"""""
"12336","(12331) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, who said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Yazīd say: Muʿādh judged among us in Yemen regarding a man who had left behind his daughter and his sister: he gave the daughter one-half and he gave the sister one-half.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Shuʿbah said, and al-Aʿmash informed me, saying: I heard Ibrāhīm narrate from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd, who said: Muʿādh judged among us in Yemen that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought [a case of] a man who had left behind his daughter and his sister, and he gave the daughter one-half and the sister one-half. This is how Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it, and the narration of Ghundar is more authentic. al-Bukhārī has narrated it from the ḥadīth of Shaybān from al-Ashʿath, as a mawqūf (stopped) narration. [Authentic]"
"12337","(12332) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān narrated from al-Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, from al-Aswad ibn Yazīd, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr judged between a daughter and a sister, giving the daughter one-half and giving the ʿaṣabah (residuary heirs) the rest of the wealth. I said to him: Indeed, Muʿādh judged in Yemen, giving the daughter one-half and giving the sister one-half. ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr said: \Then you are my messenger to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah—narrate this ḥadīth to him"",""\"" and he was the judge over Kūfah. [Authentic]"""""
"12338","(12333) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Imam Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Fayyāḍ ibn Zuhayr both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: A man died and left behind his daughter and his full sister (from his father and mother). He said: For the daughter is one-half, and for the sister is nothing; whatever remains goes to the ʿaṣabah (residuary heirs). A man said to him: Indeed, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) judged otherwise—he gave the daughter one-half and the sister one-half. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Are you more knowledgeable"","" or is Allah?\"" Maʿmar said: I did not understand the reasoning behind this until I met Ibn Ṭāwūs"","" so I mentioned the ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī to him. He said: My father informed me that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: Allah"","" Blessed and Exalted"","" said: \""If a man dies and has no child"","" but has a sister"","" she shall have half of what he left\"" (al-Nisāʾ"","" 4:12). Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""You say she gets one-half even if he has a child.\"" [Weak]\n\nThe Shaykh said: What is meant by \""child\"" (walad) here is the son (ibn)"","" as evidenced by what has been transmitted from the Prophet (ﷺ) and from those after him."""""
"12339","(12334) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Khallālī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us. Both said: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dhakwān narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, from his father: that the principles and foundations of these laws of inheritance are from Zayd ibn Thābit. As for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād upon the meanings of Zayd. He said: The inheritance of the father from his son or his daughter, if he dies—if the deceased left behind a male child or a male child of a son, then the fixed share for the father is one-sixth. If the deceased did not leave behind a male child or a male child of a son, then the father is made a residuary heir (yuʿkhalaf). One begins with those who share with him among the people of fixed shares, and they are given their fixed shares. If one-sixth or more of the wealth remains, it goes to the father. If one-sixth or more does not remain for them, then the father is assigned one-sixth as a fixed share. [Weak]"
"12340","(12335) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us from his book: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj said: I said to Ibn Ṭāwūs: [A man] left behind his father, his mother, and his daughter—how is it? He said: For his daughter is one-half, she is not given more; one-sixth for the mother; one-sixth for the father; and the remaining one-sixth is for the father. Then he informed me from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Attach the wealth to the fixed shares (farāʾiḍ). Whatever the fixed shares leave over"","" then it goes to the nearest male relative.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12341","(12336) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Wahb ibn Khālid narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Wahb narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs narrated from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Assign the fixed shares of inheritance to those entitled to them. Whatever remains is for the nearest male relative.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"","" and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād from Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12342","(12337) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated, having read it to Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, he said: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUthmān ibn Isḥāq ibn Kharashah, from Qabīṣah ibn Dhuʾayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) asking about her inheritance. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said to her: \You have nothing in the Book of Allah"","" and I know of nothing for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Go back until I ask the people.\"" Then al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah said: \""I was present with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he gave her one-sixth.\"" Abū Bakr said: \""Is there anyone else with you?\"" So Muḥammad ibn Maslamah al-Anṣārī stood up and said the same as al-Mughīrah had said. Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) then carried it out for her. Then the other grandmother came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) asking about her inheritance. He said: \""You have nothing in the Book of Allah"","" and the ruling that was given was for someone other than you. I am not one to add anything to the fixed shares. However"","" it is that one-sixth. If you two are both present"","" it is between you"","" and whichever of you survives alone"","" it is for her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12343","(12338) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted a grandmother one-sixth. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"
"12344","(12339) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿAtakī, Abū al-Munīb, narrated from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave one-sixth to the grandmother when there was no mother. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"
"12345","(12340) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave the grandmother one-sixth. And it was narrated from Shuʿbah, from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"
"12346","(12341) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bishr, brother of Khaṭṭāb, narrated to us: Ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mukhtār narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAnd likewise Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayd. Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayd was alone in narrating it, and he is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). The preserved narration is the ḥadīth of Maʿqil regarding the grandfather. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"
"12347","(12342) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: Two grandmothers came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him), and he intended to give the one-sixth to the one on the mother's side. A man from the Anṣār said: \Are you not leaving the one who"","" if she were to die while the deceased were alive"","" would inherit from him?\"" So Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq made the one-sixth between the two of them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12348","(12343) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated, he said: It was read to Ibn Ṣāʿid: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, that two grandmothers came to Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him)—the mother of the mother and the mother of the father. He gave the inheritance to the mother of the mother and not to the mother of the father. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl, brother of Banī Ḥārithah, said to him: \O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah"","" you have given it to the one who"","" if she were to die"","" would not inherit from him.\"" So Abū Bakr made it between the two of them"","" meaning the one-sixth.\n\nAnd this has also been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a mursal chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12349","(12344) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Yaḥyā ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: Among the rulings of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was that he decreed for the two grandmothers, between them, one-sixth equally. Isḥāq's narration from ʿUbādah is mursal. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12350","(12345) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from ʿAbd Rabbih ibn Saʿīd, that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām used to assign a share only to the two grandmothers. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik 1100]"
"12351","(12346) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: \We do not know of anyone who was granted inheritance in Islam except two grandmothers.\"" This was also the view of Rabīʿah.\n\nIt was narrated from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ that he said to Ibn Masʿūd: \""You are the ones who assign inheritance to three grandmothers"",""\"" as though he was rejecting that. In another narration: \""Make the grandmothers among his heirs.\"" Its chain of narration is not strong. [Weak]"""""
"12352","(12347) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr said: \Reports have come from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and from a group of the Successors that they used to grant inheritance to three grandmothers"","" along with the disconnected (munqaṭiʿ) hadith narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he granted inheritance to three grandmothers. We do not know of anyone among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who opposed that"","" except what we narrated from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ"","" whose chain of narration the scholars of hadith do not consider established.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12353","(12348) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah, Sufyān, and Sharīk informed us, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted three grandmothers a sixth (of the estate).\"" I said to Ibrāhīm: \""Who are they?\"" He said: \""Your two grandmothers from your father's side and your mother's grandmother.\"" This is a mursal hadith.\n\nIt was also narrated from Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab"","" from Manṣūr"","" from Ibrāhīm"","" from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" and it is also mursal. [Weak]"""""
"12354","(12349) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed him; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us; Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who mentioned it. [Weak]"
"12355","(12350) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Wakīʿ informed us, from al-Faḍl ibn Dalham, from al-Ḥasan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted inheritance to three grandmothers. This is also mursal, and it corroborates the first narration, which is what is reported from a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. [Weak]"
"12356","(12351) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us; Muʿtamir narrated to us; he said: I heard Ibn ʿAwn narrating from Muḥammad regarding the four grandmothers: that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) assigned them a sixth (shared equally). [Weak]"
"12357","(12352) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Hushaym informed us, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Shaʿbī, that Zayd ibn Thābit and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to grant inheritance to three grandmothers: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side. [Weak]"
"12358","(12353) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr al-Fārisī informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Khallālī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; they both said: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, from his father, that the principles and foundations of these shares of inheritance are from Zayd, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād upon the meanings of Zayd's words. He said: \If the deceased leaves three grandmothers of equal standing"","" with no mother or father between them"","" then the sixth is shared equally among the three of them"","" and they are: the mother of the mother's mother"","" the mother of the father's mother"","" and the mother of the father's father.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12359","(12354) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Shaybān narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; Ḥumayd and Dāwūd informed us that Zayd ibn Thābit said: \Three grandmothers inherit: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side.\"" [Good]"""""
"12360","(12355) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Wakīʿ informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Three grandmothers inherit: two from the father's side and one from the mother's side.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12361","(12356) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The four grandmothers together inherit as co-heirs.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12362","(12357) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ashʿath ibn Sawwār narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \Four grandmothers came racing to Masrūq"","" and he excluded the mother of the father's mother and made three grandmothers heirs.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12363","(12358) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā and Shaybān both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from al-Shaʿbī and Ḥumayd from al-Ḥasan, who both said regarding the mother of the father's mother: \She does not inherit.\"" And Dāwūd narrated from al-Shaʿbī: \""Her son"","" through whom she claims her share"","" does not inherit"","" so how can she inherit?\"" [Sound]"""""
"12364","(12359) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Hushaym narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Shaʿbī that ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give inheritance to the nearest of the grandmothers. [Weak]"
"12365","(12360) He said, and Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Ashʿath from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give inheritance to the nearest of the grandmothers"","" and then the next nearest.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12366","(12361) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give the grandmother"","" or two or three of them"","" one-sixth"","" neither reducing it from that nor increasing it"","" when their closeness to the deceased was equal. But if one of them was nearer"","" then the one-sixth was for her to the exclusion of the others. And ʿAbdullāh used to share the one-sixth between the nearest and the farthest of them if they were in different positions"","" and he did not exclude the grandmothers from the one-sixth except by the mother.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12367","(12362) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, Ḥusayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, Sharīk narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm, who said: \ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give the nearest of the grandmothers one-sixth"","" and if they were equal"","" it was shared among them. And ʿAbdullāh used to say: 'Nothing excludes the grandmothers except the mother"",""' and he would make them inherit even if some were nearer than others"","" unless one of them was the mother of the other"","" in which case he would give the inheritance to the daughter.\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd with the same meaning"","" and it was narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) with the same meaning. [Weak]"""""
"12368","(12363) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us from his book, ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: \When two grandmothers are present"","" the one-sixth is between them. If the one on the mother's side is nearer than the other"","" the one-sixth is for her. And if the one on the father's side is nearer"","" then it is between them both.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12369","(12364) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Khallālī informed us, Abū Yaʿlā informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us, Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, who said: \We have heard that if the one on the mother's side is more entitled (closer in degree)"","" she receives the one-sixth to the exclusion of the one on the father's side. And if both are of the same standing in relation to the deceased"","" or if the one on the father's side is more entitled"","" then the one-sixth is divided between them equally"","" half and half.\"" [Sound]"""""
"12370","(12365) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Abū Umayyah ibn Yaʿlā al-Thaqafī narrated from Abī al-Zinād from ʿAmr ibn Wahb from his father from Zayd ibn Thābit that he used to say: \If the grandmother on the mother's side is closer in degree than the grandmother on the father's side"","" she is more entitled to the one-sixth. And if the grandmother on the father's side is closer in degree"","" I share the one-sixth between her and the grandmother on the mother's side.\"" It was asked: \""How does the grandmother on the mother's side attain this status?\"" He said: \""Because the grandmothers were given the one-sixth on account of the mother's one-sixth.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12371","(12366) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Wakīʿ informed us, from Sufyān, from Abū al-Zinād, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, who said: When the grandmother on the mother's side is closer than the grandmother on the father's side, she is entitled to one-sixth. And when the grandmother on the father's side is closer than the grandmother on the mother's side, the one-sixth is shared between them.\n\nHe said: And Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Wakīʿ informed us, from Fiṭr, from a shaykh from the people of Madīnah, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that he used to say that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12372","(12367) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us; Khālid informed us, from Ḥumayd, from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: When the grandmother on the mother's side is closer, she is more entitled to the one-sixth. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12373","(12368) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fulayḥ informed me, from his father, from Hilāl ibn ʿAlī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \There is no believer except that I am the closest of all people to him in this world and the Hereafter. Recite"","" if you wish: {The Prophet is more worthy of the believers than themselves} [al-Aḥzāb: 6]. And whoever leaves wealth"","" let his ʿaṣabah inherit it"","" whoever they may be. And whoever leaves a debt or dependents"","" let me know"","" for I am his mawlā (guardian).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir. [Bukhārī 4781"","" Muslim 1619]"""""
"12374","(12369) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; Shabbābah narrated to us; Warqāʾ informed me, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"","" there is no believer upon the earth except that I am the closest of all people to him. So whichever of you leaves a debt or dependents"","" I am his mawlā. And whichever of you leaves wealth"","" then it goes to the ʿaṣabah"","" whoever it may be.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12375","(12370) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sābiq narrated to us; Isrāʾīl informed us, from Abū Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am closer to the believers than their own selves. Whoever leaves wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the mawālī of the ʿaṣabah. And whoever leaves dependents or a debt"","" I am his walī (guardian).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Maḥmūd"","" from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā"","" from Isrāʾīl.\n\nThe term mawālī applies to the sons of the paternal uncles. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12376","(12371) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār the ʿAdl and Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb both said: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Wuhayb narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād and Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj both said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Assign the wealth to the fixed shares (farāʾiḍ). Whatever remains after the fixed shares goes to the closest male relative.\"" And in the narration of Mūsā: \""Assign the fixed shares to their rightful recipients. Whatever remains goes to the closest male relative.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"","" and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12377","(12372) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jarīr informed us, from al-Mughīrah, from his companions, regarding the statement of Zayd ibn Thābil, ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, and Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with them): If the deceased leaves a son, the wealth belongs to him. If he leaves two sons, the wealth is between them. If he leaves three sons, the wealth is shared equally among them. If he leaves sons and daughters, the wealth is distributed among them such that the male receives the share of two females. If he leaves no direct offspring but leaves grandsons and granddaughters through a son, their lineage to the deceased is one and the same; the wealth is distributed among them such that the male receives the share of two females, and they take the place of direct offspring when there are no direct offspring. If he leaves a son and a grandson, the grandson receives nothing. Similarly, if he leaves a grandson and below him another grandson and granddaughters of a lower grandson, the lower one receives nothing alongside the higher one, just as the grandson receives nothing alongside the son.\n\nHe said: If he leaves his father and no one else, the wealth belongs to the father. If he leaves his father and a son, the father receives one-sixth and the remainder goes to the son. If he leaves a grandson and no son, the grandson takes the place of the son. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12378","(12373) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed us, from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, from his father, that the meanings of these fixed shares and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit, and the explanation is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād regarding the meanings of Zayd ibn Thābit's statements. He said: The full brother (for the mother and father) is more entitled to inheritance than the paternal brother (for the father only). The paternal brother is more entitled to inheritance than the son of the full brother. The son of the full brother is more entitled to inheritance than the son of the paternal brother. The son of the paternal brother is more entitled to inheritance than the son of the son of the full brother. The son of the paternal brother is more entitled to inheritance than the paternal uncle, the full brother of the father. The paternal uncle, the full brother of the father, is more entitled to inheritance than the paternal uncle, the paternal brother of the father. The paternal uncle, the paternal brother of the father, is more entitled to inheritance than the son of the paternal uncle, the full brother of the father. The son of the paternal uncle is more entitled to inheritance than the paternal uncle of the father, the full brother of the father of the father. And everything you are asked about regarding the inheritance of the ʿaṣabah follows this pattern. So whatever you are asked about in this regard, trace the lineage of the deceased and trace the lineage of those who dispute regarding guardianship among his ʿaṣabah. If you find one of them who reaches the deceased through a father that none of them reach except through a father above that, then assign the inheritance to the one who reaches through the nearer father, to the exclusion of the others. And if you find that all of them reach him through one common father who unites them, then look at the closest of them in lineage. If it is only a son of a son, then assign the inheritance to him to the exclusion of the more distant. If the more distant one is a son of a full mother and father, and you find them equal in the number of fathers reaching a single number until they meet the lineage of the deceased, and they are all sons of a father or sons of a father and mother, then distribute the inheritance equally among them. And if the father of some of them is a brother of the father of that deceased through his father and mother, and the father of the others is only a brother of the father of that deceased through his father, then the inheritance goes to the sons of the father and mother to the exclusion of the sons of the father only. And the grandfather, the father of the father, is more entitled to inheritance than the son of the full brother and more entitled to inheritance than the paternal uncle, the full brother of the father. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12379","(12374) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: I was with ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, and he was a judge. A people came to him disputing over the inheritance of a woman called Fukayhah bint Simʿān. This one would say: \I am so-and-so son of so-and-so son of Simʿān"",""\"" and that one would say: \""I am so-and-so son of so-and-so son of Simʿān.\"" He could not understand"","" so a man stood up and wrote their case in a document"","" then brought it to him. He read it and said: \""Yes"","" I have understood. al-Ḍaḥḥāq ibn Qays narrated to me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) judged regarding the people of the plague of ʿAmwās that when they are equal on the father's side"","" the children of the mother are more entitled to the wealth. And if one of them is closer through a father"","" he is more entitled to the wealth.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12380","(12375) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us; Qabīṣah narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī informed us, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the debt takes precedence over the bequest, and you recite {after a bequest that is made or a debt} [al-Nisāʾ: 11]. And the full siblings (banū al-umm) inherit to the exclusion of the paternal siblings (banū al-ʿallāt)—that is, the brothers and sisters for the father and mother inherit to the exclusion of the brothers and sisters for the father only. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12381","(12376) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhawayh, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā, and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, they said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bisṭām narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Assign the fixed shares of inheritance to their rightful recipients. Whatever remains after the fixed shares"","" give it to the nearest male relative.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Umayyah ibn Bisṭām. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12382","(12377) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Aws ibn Thābit from Ḥakīm ibn ʿIqāl, who said: \Shurayḥ was brought a case concerning a woman who left behind two sons of her paternal uncle — one of them was her husband and the other was her maternal brother. He gave the husband one-half and gave the remainder to the maternal brother. This reached ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" so he sent for him and said: 'Summon for me the servant.' So Shurayḥ was called and ʿAlī said: 'What did you rule?' He said: 'I gave the husband one-half and the maternal brother the remainder.' ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'By the Book of Allah or by a Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' He said: 'Rather"","" by the Book of Allah.' He said: 'Where?' Shurayḥ said: '{And blood relatives are closer to one another in the Book of Allah.}' ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Did He say one-half for the husband and the remainder for this one?' Then ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the husband one-half and the maternal brother one-sixth"","" then divided the remainder between them.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Shuʿbah from Aws al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12383","(12378) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was presented with two sons of a paternal uncle"","" one of whom was a maternal brother. It was said to him: 'ʿAbd Allāh used to give the maternal brother the entire estate.' He said: 'May Allah have mercy upon him; he was indeed a man of deep understanding. Had it been me"","" I would have given the maternal brother one-sixth"","" then divided the remainder between them.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12384","(12379) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī: \A woman who left behind two sons of her paternal uncle — one of them being her husband and the other her maternal brother — according to the view of ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both): the husband receives one-half"","" the maternal brother receives one-sixth"","" and they are partners in what remains. And according to the view of ʿAbd Allāh: the husband receives one-half and the maternal brother receives the remainder.\"" Yazīd said: \""The ruling followed is that of ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12385","(12380) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Aḥmad ibn Shuʿayb al-Nasāʾī in Miṣr narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) wished to purchase a slave-girl in order to free her. Her owners said: \We will sell her to you on the condition that the walāʾ (clientage) remains for us.\"" She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" who said: \""Do not let that prevent you"","" for walāʾ belongs to the one who sets free.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Qutaybah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12386","(12381) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Walāʾ (clientage) is a bond like the bond of lineage; it cannot be sold nor given away.\""\n\nThis was also narrated as a connected (mawṣūl) hadith through another chain from Ibn ʿUmar"","" but it is not authentic. It was also narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both) as their own statement. All of that will be discussed in the Book of Walāʾ"","" if Allah the Most High wills. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12387","(12382) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd narrated from Ashʿath ibn Sawwār from al-Ḥasan that the Prophet (ﷺ) went out to al-Baqīʿ and saw a man being sold. He bargained for him, then left him. A man purchased him and freed him, then brought him to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \I bought this man and freed him. What do you think about him?\"" He said: \""He is your brother and your mawlā (client).\"" He said: \""What do you think about his companionship?\"" He said: \""If he is grateful to you"","" it is good for him and bad for you; and if he is ungrateful to you"","" it is good for you and bad for him.\"" He said: \""What do you think about his wealth?\"" He said: \""If he dies and leaves no heir"","" then his wealth is for you.\"" This is how it came as a mursal hadith. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12388","(12383) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ruʾbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Naṣrī from Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A woman has precedence over three heirs: her foundling (laqīṭ)"","" her freed slave (ʿatīq)"","" and her child against whom she invoked liʿān (mutual cursing).\"" This is not firmly established. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12389","(12384) Al-Bukhārī said: \ʿUmar ibn Ruʾbah al-Taghlibī from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Naṣrī — there is scrutiny regarding him.\"" Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us"","" Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us"","" he said: \""I heard Ibn Ḥammād mention it from al-Bukhārī.\"" Abū Aḥmad said: \""His narrations from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Naṣrī have been rejected (munkar).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12390","(12385) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād that the daughter of Ḥamzah freed a slave-boy of hers. He died and left behind a daughter and the daughter of Ḥamzah. He (the narrator) claimed that the Prophet (ﷺ) divided half for her (the daughter of Ḥamzah) and half for his daughter. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12391","(12386) Abu 'Abd Allah and Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Qabisa narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Mansur ibn Hayyan al-Asadi from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, who said: A freed client of the daughter of Hamza passed away and left behind a daughter and the daughter of Hamza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave his daughter half and the daughter of Hamza half.\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl and al-Sha'bi from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad. And Ibn Shaddad was the brother of the daughter of Hamza through fosterage. The hadith is munqati' (disconnected). It was also narrated from al-Sha'bi from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad from his father, but this is not preserved. Ibn Abi Layla narrated it from al-Hakam from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad from the daughter of Hamza. All these narrators from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad unanimously agreed that the daughter of Hamza was the one who had been manumitted. Ibrahim al-Nakha'i said: A freed client of Hamza ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the daughter of Hamza half as a gift and withheld the other half. This is an error. Sharik said: Ibrahim ventured into this statement boldly, unless he heard something and narrated it. [Da'if]"
"12392","(12387) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us: Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated from Hasan ibn Salih from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Abu Burda: A man died and left behind a daughter and his patrons (mawali) who had manumitted him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave his daughter half and his patrons (mawali) half. This is also mursal (disconnected). [Da'if]"
"12393","(12388) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Isfahani narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Jarir narrated from al-Mughira from his companions, who said: Zaid, when he could not find any of these — meaning the 'asabah (residuary heirs) — would not return (the remainder) to the sharers of fixed portions, but would return it to the patrons (mawali). If there were no patrons (mawali), then it would go to the Bayt al-Mal (public treasury). [Da'if]"
"12394","(12389) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad narrated from al-Sha'bi, who said: 'Abd Allah would not grant the patrons (mawali) any inheritance alongside blood relatives. And 'Ali and Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: When the blood relative is a sharer of a fixed portion, he receives his fixed share, and whatever remains goes to the patrons (mawali); they are the kalalah. [Sahih]"
"12395","(12390) Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I saw the woman whom 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) granted inheritance. He gave the daughter half and the patrons (mawali) half. The narrations on this matter from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) vary, and it has been narrated from him in this manner. [Hasan]"
"12396","(12391) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us in Baghdad: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abu 'Awana narrated from Mansur from Hayyan, the seller of saddlecloths, who said: I was sitting with Suwayd ibn Ghafala. [Da'if]"
"12397","(12392) Ya'qub said: And Yahya ibn 'Isa narrated to me from Ibn al-Mubarak from Sufyan from Hayyan al-Ju'fi, who said: I was with Suwayd ibn Ghafala when a case concerning a daughter, a woman, and a freed client was brought to him. He said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give the daughter half, the woman one-eighth, and return the remainder to the daughter. [Da'if]"
"12398","(12393) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub al-'Adl narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri and Shu'ba narrated from Mansur from Fudayl ibn 'Amr from Ibrahim, who said: 'Umar and 'Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to grant inheritance to blood relatives to the exclusion of the patrons (mawali). I said to him: Did 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) do that? He said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was the strictest of them in that regard. [Sahih]"
"12399","(12394) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from 'Awsaja from Ibn 'Abbas: A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \See if he has any heir.\"" They said: \""No"","" except a slave boy whom he had manumitted.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Give his inheritance to him.\"" And similarly"","" Ibn 'Uyayana narrated it from 'Amr. [Da'if]"""""
"12400","(12395) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from 'Amr from 'Awsaja from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and left no heir except a slave whom he had manumitted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him his inheritance. Hammad ibn Zayd contradicted them both, narrating it from 'Amr ibn Dinar in a mursal (disconnected) form. [Da'if]"
"12401","(12396) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Sulaymān and ʿĀrim narrated, both saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr from ʿAwsajah, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, that a man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and left no heir except a mawlā of his, who was the one he had manumitted. The Prophet ﷺ gave him the inheritance. Al-Qāḍī said: Thus did Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrate it as a mursal hadith, not tracing it back to Ibn ʿAbbās. The Shaykh said: And thus did Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrate it from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār as a mursal hadith. [Weak]"
"12402","(12397) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najīd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bisṭām narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿAwsajah, that a man manumitted another man, and the one who had done the manumitting died and had no heir. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the inheritance to the manumitted one. [Weak]"
"12403","(12398) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, and I heard Ibn Ḥammād saying: Al-Bukhārī said: ʿAwsajah, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, narrated from him, and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from him, but his hadith is not ṣaḥīḥ. The Shaykh said: And some of the narrators narrated it from ʿAmr from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, and this is an error without doubt. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12404","(12399) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Budayl ibn Mayṣarah from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Rāshid ibn Saʿd from Abū ʿĀmir al-Hawzanī from al-Miqdām al-Kindī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I am the walī of every believer over his own soul. Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents"","" it is upon us. And whoever leaves behind wealth"","" it is for his heirs. I am the walī of the one who has no walī — I inherit his wealth and I ransom his captive. The maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir — he inherits his wealth and ransoms his captive.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""""
"12405","(12400) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us in Naysābūr, and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad, both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān from Ibn al-Aṣbahānī from Mujāhid ibn Wardān from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, that a man fell from a palm tree and died. He left some wealth but left no child and no close relative. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Give his inheritance to a man from the people of his village.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12406","(12401) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aṣbahānī from Mujāhid ibn Wardān from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, that a mawlā of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Is there anyone here from the people of his village?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So the Prophet ﷺ gave him the inheritance. This may be interpreted as follows: if he was a mawlā by other than manumission"","" the Prophet ﷺ did not take his inheritance himself but assigned it to the people of his village on the basis of public interest. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12407","(12402) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Sharīk narrated to me, Abū Bakr al-Aḥmarī informed me from Ibn Buraydah from his father, that a man from Khuzāʿah died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The inheritance was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \See if there is any heir.\"" They searched but found no heir for him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed"","" and the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Give it to the eldest of Khuzāʿah.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12408","(12403) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Kindī narrated to us, al-Muḥāribī narrated from Jibrīl ibn Aḥmar from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah from his father, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \I have the inheritance of a man from al-Azd"","" and I cannot find an Azdī to give it to.\"" He said: \""Go and search for an Azdī for a year.\"" He said: \""He came back after the year and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" I could not find an Azdī to give it to.' He said: 'Go and look for the first Khuzāʿī you meet and give it to him.'\"" When the man turned to leave"","" he called him back. When he came"","" he said: \""Look for the eldest of Khuzāʿah and give it to him.\"" Jibrīl ibn Aḥmar is Abū Bakr al-Aḥmarī. [Weak]"""""
"12409","(12404) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Sufyān narrated from Qays ibn Muslim from Muḥammad ibn al-Muntashir from Masrūq, who said: I came to ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, and said: \A man among us who was a resident went out to the mountain and died"","" leaving three hundred dirhams.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""Did he leave an heir"","" or does any of you have a bond of walāʾ over him?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""He has many heirs here"",""\"" and he placed his wealth in the Bayt al-Māl. [Ḥasan]"""""
"12410","(12405) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Sharḥbīl ibn Muslim from Abī Umāmah al-Bāhilī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in his sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \Indeed"","" Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" has given every rightful one his right. There is no bequest for an heir.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12411","(12406) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sālim informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, from Khārijah ibn Zayd, who said: I saw my father placing the surplus wealth into the Bayt al-Māl and not returning anything to any heir. [Weak]"
"12412","(12407) He said: And Muḥammad ibn Sālim informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) used to return the surplus to every heir in proportion to what they inherited, except for the woman and the husband. And ʿAbd Allāh used not to return anything to a woman, nor to a husband, nor to a son's daughter alongside a daughter of the loins, nor to a paternal sister alongside a full sister, nor to maternal siblings alongside the mother, nor to a grandmother unless there was no other heir besides her. And Zayd used not to return anything to any heir, but would place it in the Bayt al-Māl. [Weak]"
"12413","(12408) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) and said: My grandson has died; what is my share of his inheritance? He said: For you is one-sixth. When he turned to leave, he called him and said: For you is another sixth. When he again turned to leave, he called him and said: The second sixth is a provision (ṭuʿmah). [Weak]"
"12414","(12409) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sawwār, Abū Sawwār al-Qāḍī, narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from Maʿqil ibn Yasār, that ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) asked the people: Who knows anything from the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) regarding the grandfather? Maʿqil said: He gave him one-sixth. ʿUmar said: Alongside whom, may you perish? He said: I do not know. He said: You have not known.\n\nIn the narration of Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, who said: I performed Ḥajj with ʿUmar, and he called out among the people: Whoever heard the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) mention anything regarding the grandfather? So Maʿqil ibn Yasār al-Muzanī stood up and said: I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ): a case of inheritance was brought to him in which there was a grandfather, and he gave him one-third or one-sixth. ʿUmar said: What was the case? He said: I do not know. ʿUmar kicked him and said: You have not known — what prevented you from knowing?\n\nIn another narration from Yūnus in this ḥadīth, he said: So he gathered the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) and assigned the grandfather a share.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Khāld al-Wahbī, from Yūnus; and Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from al-Zaʿfarānī, from Shabābah, from Yūnus. [Weak]"
"12415","(12410) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Aḥmad al-Khallālī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī, from his father Zayd ibn Thābit, that the meanings of these injunctions of inheritance and their principles are from Zayd ibn Thābit, and as for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād based on the meanings of Zayd. He said: The inheritance of the grandfather, the father of the father, is that he does not inherit anything alongside a father, however near. And he is, alongside a male child and alongside a son's son, entitled to one-sixth. And in other cases, when the deceased has not left a brother or a sister from his father, the grandfather is made the residuary heir (khalīfah). And one begins with any of the people of fixed shares who shares with him, and he is given his fixed share. If there remains from the estate one-sixth or more, then it goes to the grandfather. And if there does not remain one-sixth or more, then the grandfather receives one-sixth. [Weak]\n\n(Chapter 40) Chapter on the Severity Regarding Speech on the Issue of the Grandfather alongside Full and Paternal Siblings or Paternal Siblings without Independent Reasoning, and the Abundance of Disagreement Therein."
"12416","(12411) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs, and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Ghanīyah narrated to us, from Abū Ḥayyān, who is Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Taymī, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I heard ʿUmar upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) saying: To proceed, O people — the prohibition of khamr was revealed, and it is from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat, and barley. And khamr is that which overwhelms the intellect. And there are three things, O people — I wished that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) had not departed from us until he had given us a definitive injunction regarding them to which we could refer: kalālah, the grandfather, and certain matters pertaining to ribā.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Bukhārī 5588, Muslim 3033]"
"12417","(12412) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah, who said: I have preserved from ʿUmar regarding the grandfather one hundred rulings, each one of which contradicts the others. [Ḥasan]"
"12418","(12413) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us: Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. He said: I heard Ibn ʿAwn narrating from Muḥammad, from ʿUbaydah, who said: I have preserved from ʿUmar one hundred rulings regarding the grandfather. He said: And he said: Indeed, I have issued various rulings regarding the grandfather, in all of which I have not fallen short of the truth. If I live, in shāʾ Allāh, until the summer, I shall issue a ruling therein by which a woman shall make her demand while she is upon her garment (i.e., without needing to go elsewhere). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12419","(12414) And Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Jarīr narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) took a shoulder blade (katf) and gathered the Companions of Muḥammad (ﷺ) to write down the ruling on the grandfather, and they were of the view that he was placing him in the position of a father. Then a snake emerged upon them, and they dispersed. He said: Had Allāh willed to carry it out, He would have carried it out."
"12420","(12415) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāfilāʾī narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq narrated, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn al-Awdī, who said: I was present with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) when he was stabbed. He mentioned the story, and in it ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: O ʿAbd Allāh, bring me the shoulder blade upon which I wrote the matter of the grandfather yesterday. And he said: Had Allāh willed to complete this matter, He would have completed it. ʿAbd Allāh said: We shall suffice you in this matter, O Amīr al-Muʾminīn. He said: No. So he took it and erased it with his own hand. [Weak]"
"12421","(12416) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from a man from Murād, that he heard ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) say: \Whoever would be pleased to plunge into the depths of Jahannam"","" let him judge between the grandfather and the brothers.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12422","(12417) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Abū Salamah narrated to us: Wahayb narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The one about whom the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'Were I to take a khalīl (close friend)"","" I would take him as a khalīl' — meaning Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) — he (Abū Bakr) made the grandfather a father.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Salamah. [Authentic]"""""
"12423","(12418) ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad ibn Shabbān al-ʿAṭṭār in Baghdād informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, that Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to the people of ʿIrāq: \The one about whom the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'Were I to take a khalīl"","" I would take Abū Bakr as a khalīl' — he made the grandfather a father.\""\n\n[Authentic. Bukhārī 3658]"""""
"12424","(12419) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, that the people of Kūfah wrote to ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr asking him about the grandfather. He said: \As for the one about whom the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'Were I to take anyone as a khalīl"","" I would take him' — he (Abū Bakr) regarded him as a father"","" meaning Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him).\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12425","(12420) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, from al-Shaybānī, from Abū Burdah, from Marwān al-Ḥakam, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allāh be pleased with him), that Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) made the grandfather a father. [Authentic]"
"12426","(12421) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAttāb informed us: al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, from his uncle Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to him: When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him) was stabbed, he said: \I have formed an opinion regarding the grandfather; if you see fit to follow it"","" then follow it.\"" ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""If we follow your opinion"","" it is sound guidance"","" and if we follow the opinion of the elder before you"","" then what a fine holder of opinion he was.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12427","(12422) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym informed us, from Khālid, from Abī al-Mutawakkil al-Nājī, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allāh be pleased with him), that Abū Bakr (may Allāh be pleased with him) used to treat the grandfather in the status of a father. [Authentic]"
"12428","(12423) Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, from ʿAmr, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās: \The grandfather is a father.\"" And he said: \""Had the jinn known that there are grandfathers among people"","" they would not have said: 'Exalted is the majesty of our Lord' (Tājālā jaddu rabbinā).\"" And Sufyān recited: \""O Children of Adam\"" (Yā Banī Ādam) and \""And I followed the religion of my fathers\"" (Wa-ittabaʿtu millata ābāʾī). [Authentic]"""""
"12429","(12424) Abū Saʿīd informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq informed us from his book: Jarīr narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khālid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maʿqil, who said: \A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said to him: 'What do you say about the grandfather?' He said: 'There is no grandfather — which father of yours is greater?' The man fell silent and did not answer him"","" as though he was at a loss for a reply. I said: 'I am Ādam.' He said: 'Do you not hear the words of Allāh: \""O Children of Adam\"" (Yā Banī Ādam)?'\"" [Weak]"""""
"12430","(12425) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us, from Layth, from Abī ʿAmr al-ʿAbdī, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: \The blood-money is for the one who secures the inheritance"","" and the grandfather is a father.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12431","(12426) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us from his book, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, ʬāʾ informed me: that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to treat the grandfather as a father. Some of the people of Iraq rejected this statement of ʬāʾ regarding ʿAlī. The authentic narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is that he used to include the grandfather along with the brothers, and perhaps he treated him as a father in another ruling. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"12432","(12427) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, ʿĀṣim narrated from al-Shaʿbī: that the first grandfather to inherit in Islam was ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). The son of so-and-so ibn ʿUmar died, and ʿUmar intended to take the wealth to the exclusion of his brothers. ʿAlī and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to him: \That is not for you.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Had your two opinions not been united"","" I would not have considered that he is my son nor that I am his father.\"" This is a mursal narration — al-Shaʿbī did not reach the days of ʿUmar — however"","" it is a sound mursal narration. [Authentic]"""""
"12433","(12428) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Ibn Lahīʿa and Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me from ʿUqayl ibn Khālid that Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān ibn Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather Zayd ibn Thābit: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission to visit him one day. He granted him permission, and his head was in the hand of a slave-girl who was combing it. He pulled his head away. ʿUmar said to him: \Let her comb your head.\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"","" if you had sent for me"","" I would have come to you.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""The need is mine; I have come to you so that you may look into the matter of the grandfather.\"" Zayd said: \""No"","" by Allah"","" we say nothing about it.\"" ʿUmar said: \""It is not a matter of revelation that we should add to it or subtract from it. It is a matter we form an opinion about. If I see something that agrees with my view"","" I follow it; otherwise"","" there is nothing incumbent upon you regarding it.\"" Zayd refused"","" so ʿUmar left angrily and said: \""I came to you thinking you would fulfill my need"","" then he came to him again at the same time as the first visit"","" and he kept at him until Zayd said: 'Shall I write something for you about it?'\"" So he wrote it on a piece of saddle-leather and gave him a parable: \""The likeness of the grandfather is like a tree that grew on a single trunk"","" then a branch emerged from it"","" then another branch emerged from that branch. The trunk waters the branch. If you cut the first branch"","" the water returns to the second branch"","" meaning the second one; and if you cut the second"","" the water returns to the first.\"" He brought it to ʿUmar"","" who addressed the people"","" then read the piece of saddle-leather to them"","" then said: \""Zayd ibn Thābit has spoken regarding the grandfather"","" and I have enacted it.\"" He said: \""He was the first grandfather to inherit"","" and he had intended to take all the wealth of his grandson to the exclusion of his brothers.\"" After that"","" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) divided it. [Authentic. Al-Dāraquṭnī 4/98"","" 80]"""""
"12434","(12429) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me, Abū Ṭāhir Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād said: Abū al-Zinād took this letter from Khārija ibn Zayd ibn Thābit and from the elders of the family of Zayd ibn Thābit: \In the name of Allah"","" the Most Gracious"","" the Most Merciful. To ʿAbdullāh Muʿāwiya"","" Commander of the Faithful"","" from Zayd ibn Thābit.\"" Then he mentioned the letter in its entirety"","" and in it: \""I had spoken to the Commander of the Faithful ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) about the matter of the grandfather and the brothers from the father's side in a very forceful discussion. At that time"","" I considered that the brothers had a stronger claim to their brother's inheritance than the grandfather"","" while he considered at that time that the grandfather had a stronger claim than the brothers. Our debate on the matter lengthened until I gave him a parable of some sons inheriting from one another to the exclusion of others. He turned to me as one angered and said: 'By Allah"","" besides whom there is no deity"","" if I were to judge it today for some of them to the exclusion of others"","" I would judge it in favor of the grandfather"","" and I would see that he is more entitled to it. But perhaps they are rightful heirs"","" and perhaps I would not deprive any one of them of their share. And I shall judge between them"","" if Allah wills"","" Exalted is He"","" according to what I see at that time.' I considered that"","" and I seek Allah's forgiveness"","" to be the last of the words I exchanged with the Commander of the Faithful ʿUmar regarding the matter of the grandfather and the brothers. Then I considered that he used to divide after them"","" and then the Commander of the Faithful ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) divided between the grandfather and the brothers according to what I have written to you in this document"","" and I believe I have retained that from what I witnessed of their rulings.\""\n\nAnd others added therein from Ibn Abī al-Zinād from his father from Khārija ibn Zayd from his father: that when ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) consulted them about the inheritance of the grandfather and the brothers"","" Zayd said: \""My opinion at that time was that the brothers were more entitled to their brother's inheritance than the grandfather"","" and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb's opinion at that time was that the grandfather was more entitled to his grandson's inheritance than his brothers.\"" Zayd said: \""So I gave ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) a parable about that and said to him: 'If a tree branched from its root a branch"","" and from that branch two twigs branched"","" and that branch gathers those two twigs to the exclusion of the root and nourishes them — do you not see"","" O Commander of the Faithful"","" that one of the two twigs is closer to its fellow than to the root?'\"" Zayd said: \""Strike the root of the tree as a parable for the grandfather"","" and strike the branch that branched from the root as a parable for the father"","" and strike the two twigs that branched from the branch as a parable for the brothers.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12435","(12430) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿĪsā al-Madanī from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \It was my opinion and the opinion of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that they would make the grandfather more entitled than the brother. And ʿUmar used to dislike speaking about it. When ʿUmar became a grandfather"","" he said: 'This is a matter that has occurred; the people must become acquainted with it.' So he sent to Zayd ibn Thābit and asked him. He said: 'It was the opinion of Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) that we make the grandfather more entitled than the brother.' He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"","" do not make a tree that grew and from which a branch branched"","" and from the branch two branches branched — how can the first branch be made more entitled than the second branch when both branches emerged from the first branch?'\"" He said: \""Then he sent to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him. He said to him as Zayd had said"","" except that he made it a stream that flowed"","" from which a channel branched"","" and from it two channels branched. He said: 'What do you think — if this middle channel were to dry up"","" would it not return to both channels together?'\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and addressed the people and said: \""Is there anyone among you who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mention the grandfather in an inheritance?\"" A man stood and said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) — an inheritance was mentioned before him in which the grandfather was mentioned — and he gave him one-third.\"" He said: \""Who was with him among the heirs?\"" He said: \""I do not know.\"" He said: \""You do not know!\"" Then he addressed the people and said: \""Is there anyone among you who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mention the grandfather in an inheritance?\"" A man stood and said: \""I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) — an inheritance was mentioned before him in which the grandfather was mentioned — and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave him one-sixth.\"" He said: \""Who was with him among the heirs?\"" He said: \""I do not know.\"" He said: \""You do not know!\"" Al-Shaʿbī said: \""Zayd ibn Thābit used to treat the grandfather as a brother until they reached three"","" he being the third of them. When they exceeded that"","" he gave him one-third. And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) used to treat the grandfather as a brother until they reached six"","" he being the sixth of them. When they exceeded that"","" he gave him one-sixth.\"" [Very Weak]"""""
"12436","(12431) ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī narrated it from Sufyān with the same meaning, except that he said: Zayd said: \O Commander of the Faithful"","" do not make a tree that grew and from which a branch branched"","" and from the branch two branches branched — how can the first be made more entitled than the second when both branches emerged from the first branch?\"" Then ʿUmar sent to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him. He said to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) as he had said to Zayd. ʿAlī said as Zayd had said"","" except that ʿAlī made it a stream that flowed"","" from which a channel branched"","" and from it two channels branched. He said: \""What do you think — if the water of this middle channel were to dry up"","" would it not return to both channels together?\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us"","" Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us"","" Sufyān ibn Muḥammad informed us"","" ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us"","" ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated it. [Very Weak]\n\nThe Shaykh said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to include the grandfather along with the brothers and sisters"","" whether from the father and mother or from the father's side."""""
"12437","(12432) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us.\n\n(Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us), Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtba, and Qabīṣa ibn Dhūʾayb narrated to me: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that the grandfather shares with the brothers from the father and mother and the brothers from the father's side, as long as sharing is better for him than one-third of the estate. If the brothers are numerous, the grandfather is given one-third, and the brothers receive what remains, with the male receiving the share of two females. And he ruled that the children of the father and mother are more entitled to that than the children of the father, whether male or female, except that the children of the father share with the grandfather alongside the children of the father and mother, and they reduce them, and the children of the father have nothing with the children of the father and mother unless the children of the father are returned upon the daughters of the father and mother. If anything remains after the obligatory shares of the daughters of the father and mother, it goes to the brothers from the father's side, with the male receiving the share of two females. [Authentic]"
"12438","(12433) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me, Abū Ṭāhir informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād said: Abū al-Zinād took this letter from Khārija ibn Zayd ibn Thābit and from the elders of the family of Zayd ibn Thābit: \In the name of Allah"","" the Most Gracious"","" the Most Merciful. To ʿAbdullāh Muʿāwiya"","" Commander of the Faithful"","" from Zayd ibn Thābit.\"" Then he mentioned the letter in its entirety"","" and in it: \""I have seen something of the division of the Commander of the Faithful"","" meaning ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" between the grandfather and the brothers from the father's side: when there is one male brother with the grandfather"","" what they inherit is divided between them in two halves. If there is one sister with the grandfather"","" one-third is divided for her. If there are two sisters with the grandfather"","" half is divided for them and half for the grandfather. If there are two brothers with the grandfather"","" one-third is divided for the grandfather. If they are more than that"","" I do not think — as far as I recall — that they would reduce the grandfather from one-third at all. Then whatever remains for the brothers from their brother's inheritance after the grandfather"","" the children of the father and mother are more entitled to it"","" some over others"","" by what Allah has ordained for them"","" to the exclusion of the children of the father. Thus I have reckoned something of what ʿUmar"","" the Commander of the Faithful"","" used to divide between the grandfather and the brothers from the father's side"","" and he did not bequeath anything to the brothers from the mother who are not from the father's side along with the grandfather.\"" Then he said: \""I have reckoned that the Commander of the Faithful ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) used to divide between the grandfather and the brothers according to what I have written to you in this document.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12439","(12434) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that it reached him: that Muʿāwiya ibn Abī Sufyān (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Zayd ibn Thābit asking him about the grandfather. Zayd ibn Thābit wrote to him: \You have written to me asking me about the grandfather"","" and Allah knows best. This is a matter that only the commanders — meaning the Caliphs — used to judge. I attended the two Caliphs before you"","" and they used to give him half with one brother"","" and one-third with two brothers. If the brothers were numerous"","" they would not reduce him from one-third.\""\n\nHe said: Mālik informed us that it reached him from Sulaymān ibn Yasār that he said: \""ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"","" and Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with them) assigned the grandfather one-third along with the brothers.\"" [Weak. Mālik 1095]"""""
"12440","(12435) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Isḥāq narrated from his book, Jarīr informed us from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿUbayda al-Salmānī, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give the grandfather one-third along with the brothers"","" and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give him one-sixth. And ʿUmar wrote to ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with them both): 'We fear that we have been unjust to the grandfather; so give him one-third.' When ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived here"","" he gave him one-sixth. ʿUbayda said: 'Their opinion in the united assembly is more beloved to me than the opinion of either one of them in separation.'\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12441","(12436) Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbayd ibn Nuḍaylah: that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, used to give the grandfather one-third, then he shifted to giving him one-sixth; and that ʿAbdullāh used to give him one-sixth, then he shifted to one-third. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12442","(12437) Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUbayd ibn Nuḍaylah, who said: ʿUmar and ʿAbdullāh used to make the grandfather share with the brothers, considering the share to be between that and one-sixth being better for him than sharing with them. Then ʿUmar wrote to ʿAbdullāh: \It seems to us that we have been unjust to the grandfather. When this letter of mine reaches you"","" then make him share with the brothers"","" considering the share to be between that and one-third being better for him than sharing with them.\"" So ʿAbdullāh adopted that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12443","(12438) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from Firās, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with both of them, asking him about six brothers and a grandfather. So he wrote to him: \Treat him as one of them"","" and erase my letter.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12444","(12439) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with both of them, from al-Baṣrah, concerning six brothers and a grandfather. So ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to him: \Give him one-seventh of the estate.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12445","(12440) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Salamah narrate from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him: that he used to treat the grandfather as a brother, until they reached six. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12446","(12441) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm: that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, used to include the grandfather with the brothers up to six, and he would be the sixth among them. When they exceeded that number, he would give the grandfather one-sixth, and give each fixed-share heir his share. He would not make a uterine brother or a uterine sister inherit alongside the grandfather, nor would he make a consanguineous brother share with a full brother alongside the grandfather. He would not give the grandfather more than one-sixth alongside descendants, unless there was no one else. If there was a full sister, a consanguineous brother, and a grandfather, he would give the full sister one-half and divide the remainder between the grandfather and the brother. If there was a full sister, a consanguineous brother, a consanguineous sister, and a grandfather, he would make the estate into ten shares: the full sister would receive one-half, i.e., five shares; the grandfather would receive two shares; the consanguineous brother would receive two shares; and the consanguineous sister would receive one share. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12447","(12442) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us; Ibrāhīm informed us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us; al-Ḥasan informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿAbdullāh used to include the grandfather with the brothers up to one-third. If one-third was better for him than sharing, he would give him one-third, and give each fixed-share heir his share. He would not make a uterine brother or a uterine sister inherit alongside the grandfather, nor would he make a consanguineous brother share with a full brother alongside the grandfather. He would not make a son's son inherit alongside the grandfather. If there was a full sister, a consanguineous brother, and a grandfather, he would give the full sister one-half and give the grandfather one-half, and he would not give the brother anything. If there were brothers, sisters, and a grandfather, along with those who had fixed shares among them, he would give each fixed-share heir his share. If one-third of the remainder was better for the grandfather than sharing, he would give him one-third of the remainder. If sharing was better for him, he would share. If one-sixth of the entire estate was better for him than sharing, he would give him one-sixth. If sharing was better for him than one-sixth of the entire estate, he would share. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12448","(12443) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Mughīrah, from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, and from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, concerning a daughter, a sister, and a grandfather: according to the view of ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, the daughter receives one-half, the grandfather receives one-sixth, and the sister receives the remainder. And he said the same concerning a daughter, two sisters, and a grandfather; and concerning a daughter, multiple sisters, and a grandfather. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12449","(12444) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Masrūq, from ʿAbdullāh, concerning a daughter, a sister, and a grandfather. He said: \Make it four shares: the daughter receives one-half"","" i.e."","" two shares; the grandfather receives one share; and the sister receives one share. If there are two sisters"","" make it eight shares: the daughter receives one-half"","" i.e."","" four shares; the grandfather receives two shares; and the two sisters receive one share each. If there are three sisters"","" make it ten shares: the daughter receives one-half"","" i.e."","" five shares; the grandfather receives two shares"","" which is two-fifths of the remainder; and the three sisters receive one share each.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12450","(12445) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm: that Zayd ibn Thābit used to include the grandfather with the brothers and sisters up to one-third. When it reached one-third, he would give him one-third, and the remainder would go to the brothers and sisters. He would not make a uterine brother or a uterine sister inherit anything alongside the grandfather, nor would he share with them. He would make the consanguineous brothers share with the full brothers, and he would not make them inherit anything. If there was a full brother and a grandfather, he would give each of them one-half. If there were two brothers and a grandfather, he would give them one-third. If they increased in number, he would still give the grandfather one-third, and the remainder would go to the brothers. If there was a sister and a grandfather, he would give her one-third and give the grandfather two-thirds. If there were two sisters and a grandfather, he would give them one-half and give the grandfather one-half, up to five sisters. If they reached five, he would give the grandfather one-third and the remainder to the sisters. If the fixed shares of a wife, a husband, or a mother were combined, he would give the fixed-share heirs their shares, and the remainder would be divided among the brothers and sisters. If one-third of the remainder was better for the grandfather than sharing, he would give him one-third of the remainder. If sharing was better for him than one-third of the remainder, he would share. If one-sixth of the entire estate was better for him than sharing, he would give him one-sixth. If sharing was better for him than one-sixth of the entire estate, he would share. In the case of al-Akdarīyah — when there is a husband, a mother, a sister, and a grandfather — he would make it nine shares, then multiply it by three, making it twenty-seven. He would give the husband nine shares, the mother six shares, the grandfather eight shares, and the sister four shares. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12451","(12446) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Khallālī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, from his father, that the principles and fundamentals of these shares of inheritance were transmitted from Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him). As for the explanation, it is the explanation of Abū al-Zinād regarding the meanings of Zayd ibn Thābit's rulings. He said: The inheritance of the grandfather (father's father) alongside the brothers from the father and mother is such that they are left behind, and whoever among the people of fixed shares is present alongside them is given his share first. Whatever remains thereafter belongs to the grandfather and the brothers. In this matter, consideration is given, and it is calculated which is more beneficial for the grandfather's portion: whether one-third of what accrues to him and the brothers, or whether he acts as a brother and divides with the brothers what has accrued to them and to him, with the male receiving the share of two females, or whether one-sixth of the entire estate unencumbered. Whichever of these is more beneficial for the grandfather's portion, he is given that. Whatever remains thereafter is divided among the brothers from the father and mother, with the male receiving the share of two females, except in one particular case where their division is different. That is when a woman dies and leaves behind her husband, her mother, her grandfather, and her full sister. The husband is assigned one-half, the mother one-third, the grandfather one-sixth, and the sister one-half. Then the grandfather's one-sixth and the sister's one-half are combined and divided into three parts: two-thirds for the grandfather and one-third for the sister. The inheritance of the brothers from the father alongside the grandfather, when there are no brothers from the father and mother with them, is the same as the inheritance of the brothers from the father and mother, whether their males are like their males and their females are like their females. When the brothers from the father and mother and the brothers from the father are combined, the children of the father and mother count the grandfather against the children of their father, thereby preventing him through their greater number from receiving a larger inheritance. Whatever accrues to the brothers after the grandfather's share belongs exclusively to the children of the father and mother, to the exclusion of the children of the father, and nothing from it goes to the children of the father — unless the children of the father and mother consist of only one woman. If it is only one woman, she counts the grandfather against the children of her father, however many they may be. Whatever accrues to her and to them belongs exclusively to her, up to the point that she completes one-half of the entire estate. If there is a surplus beyond one-half of the entire estate in what is apportioned to her and to them, that surplus is divided among the children of the father, with the male receiving the share of two females. If nothing remains surplus, then they receive nothing. [Weak]"
"12452","(12447) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Ismāʿīm ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Mughīrah, from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, and from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī: A mother, a sister, a husband, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): the mother receives one-third, the sister one-half, the husband one-half, and the grandfather one-sixth from nine. According to the ruling of ʿAbd Allāh: the sister receives one-half, the husband one-half, the mother one-third, and the grandfather one-sixth from nine shares. The grandfather combines his one-sixth with the sister's one-half and divides with her, so that he receives two-thirds of the combined portion and she receives one-third. The nine is multiplied by three, making twenty-seven. The mother receives six, the husband nine, and twelve remain: eight for the grandfather and four for the sister. This is the Akdariyyah — the \mother of the chicks.\"" [Sound]"""""
"12453","(12448) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Mughīrah, from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, and from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī: A full sister, a consanguine sister, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh: the full sister receives one-half, the consanguine sister receives one-sixth (completing two-thirds), and the remainder goes to the grandfather. According to the ruling of Zayd: the two sisters receive one-half, and the grandfather receives one-half, and the consanguine sister's share is redistributed to the full sister.\n\nA full sister, two consanguine sisters, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh: the full sister receives one-half, the two consanguine sisters receive one-sixth (completing two-thirds), and the remainder goes to the grandfather. If there are more than two consanguine sisters, they receive no more than this. According to the ruling of Zayd: the grandfather receives two-fifths, and the sisters receive one share each from five. Then the two consanguine sisters redistribute to the full sister until she completes one-half, and there is a surplus for the two of them. If there are three or four consanguine sisters alongside a full sister and a grandfather, the grandfather is not reduced below one-third. The full sister receives one-half, and the remainder is divided among the consanguine sisters.\n\nA full sister, a consanguine brother, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): the full sister receives one-half, and the remainder is divided equally between the brother and the grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him): the grandfather receives one-half, the full sister receives one-half, and the consanguine brother receives nothing. According to the ruling of Zayd: from ten shares, four shares for the grandfather, four for the brother, and two for the sister. Then the brother redistributes three shares to the sister, so she completes one-half, and one share remains for him.\n\nA full sister, a consanguine brother, a consanguine sister, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): the full sister receives one-half, and the remainder is divided in fifths among the grandfather, the brother, and the sister. According to the ruling of ʿAbd Allāh: the full sister receives one-half, the remainder goes to the grandfather, and the consanguine brother and sister receive nothing. According to the ruling of Zayd: from eighteen shares, the grandfather receives one-third (six shares), the brother six shares, and the two sisters three shares each. Then the consanguine brother and sister redistribute to the full sister until she completes one-half (nine shares), and three shares remain between the two of them.\n\nTwo full sisters, a consanguine brother, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): the two sisters receive two-thirds, and the remainder is divided equally between the brother and the grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAbd Allāh: the two full sisters receive two-thirds, the remainder goes to the grandfather, and the consanguine brother is excluded. According to the ruling of Zayd: from three shares, one share for the grandfather, one for the two sisters, and one for the brother. Then the brother redistributes his share to the two sisters, so they complete two-thirds, and nothing remains for him.\n\nTwo full sisters, a consanguine sister, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī and ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both): the two full sisters receive two-thirds, the remainder goes to the grandfather, and the consanguine sister is excluded. According to the ruling of Zayd: from ten shares, four shares for the grandfather, and two shares each for the sisters. Then the consanguine sister redistributes her two shares to the two full sisters, and nothing remains for her. She divided with them but inherited nothing.\n\nTwo full sisters, a consanguine brother, a consanguine sister, and a grandfather. According to the ruling of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): the two full sisters receive two-thirds, the grandfather receives one-sixth, and the remainder is divided between the brother and the sister with the male receiving the share of two females. According to the ruling of ʿAbd Allāh: the two sisters receive two-thirds, the remainder goes to the grandfather, and the consanguine brother and sister are excluded. According to the ruling of Zayd: from three, the grandfather receives one-third (one share), and two shares for the two full sisters. They divided with them, and the consanguine brother and sister inherited nothing. [Weak]"
"12454","(12449) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us; Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Raqqī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Shaʿbī narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā from al-Shaʿbī: that al-Ḥajjāj had him brought in shackles. When he reached the gate of the palace, he said: \I met Yazīd ibn Abī Muslim"","" and he said: 'To Allah we belong"","" O Shaʿbī! What lies between your two sides of knowledge — and this is not a day of intercession. Confess before the commander to disbelief and hypocrisy against yourself"","" so that you may be saved.'\"" Then I met Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥajjāj"","" and he said to me the same thing Yazīd had said. When I entered upon al-Ḥajjāj"","" he said: \""And you"","" O Shaʿbī"","" are among those who rebelled against us and caused much trouble.\"" I said: \""May Allah reform the commander. The dwelling has grieved us"","" the land has become barren"","" the path has narrowed"","" sleeplessness has afflicted us"","" and we have been consumed by fear. We have fallen into a disgrace in which the righteous cannot be pious and the wicked cannot be strong.\"" He said: \""By Allah"","" you have spoken the truth. They did not act righteously by rebelling against us"","" nor did they prevail over us when they committed transgression.\"" Then both of them were released. Later"","" he needed me regarding a share of inheritance"","" so I came to him"","" and he said: \""What do you say regarding a mother"","" a sister"","" and a grandfather?\"" I said: \""Five of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) differed concerning this: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"","" Zayd"","" ʿUthmān"","" ʿAlī"","" and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd.\"" He said: \""What did Ibn ʿAbbās say regarding it — if he was truly knowledgeable (or"","" in the narration of al-Raqqī: if he was truly well-versed)?\"" I said: \""He made the grandfather a father"","" gave the sister nothing"","" and gave the mother one-third.\"" He said: \""What did Zayd say regarding it?\"" I said: \""He made it from nine: he gave the mother three"","" the grandfather four"","" and the sister two.\"" He said: \""What did the Commander of the Faithful — meaning ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) — say regarding it?\"" I said: \""He made it into three.\"" He said: \""What did Ibn Masʿūd say regarding it?\"" I said: \""He made it from six: he gave the sister three"","" the grandfather two"","" and the mother one.\"" He said: \""What did Abū Turāb — meaning ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) — say regarding it?\"" I said: \""He made it from six shares: he gave the sister three"","" the mother two"","" and the grandfather one.\"" And he mentioned the hadith at length. [Weak. See also the compilation 7167]"""""
"12455","(12450) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā al-ʿUqlī narrated to me; my father ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā narrated to me; he said: Abū Bakr al-Hudhalī narrated to me; he said: al-Shaʿbī said to me, and he mentioned this hadith. [Weak]"
"12456","(12451) And Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Mughīrah, from the companions of Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, and from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī: A mother, a full sister, and a grandfather. He mentioned their statements in a manner similar to what al-Shaʿbī narrated alone. [Weak]"
"12457","(12452) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding a mother, a sister, and a grandfather: the sister receives one-half, the mother receives one-third of what remains, and the grandfather receives what remains. [Weak]"
"12458","(12453) He said: And Sufyān informed us from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, who said: ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) used not to give the mother precedence over the grandfather."
"12459","(12454) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Aswad al-ʿIjlī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, from his father: that he was the first to apply ʿawl (proportional reduction) in the shares of inheritance, and the majority of his applications of ʿawl were at two-thirds. [Weak]"
"12460","(12455) And Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): regarding a woman, two parents, and two daughters — her one-eighth becomes one-ninth. [Weak]"
"12461","(12456) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us; Muhriz ibn Awn informed us; Sharik narrated it, mentioning something similar. And in the narration of Ibrahim al-Nakha'i from Ali and Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, there are issues in which he applied 'awl (proportionate reduction of shares). [Da'if]"
"12462","(12457) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, who said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Mas'ud, who said: I and Zufar ibn Aws ibn al-Hadthan went to Ibn Abbas after his eyesight had departed, and we discussed the shares of inheritance. He said: \Do you see the One Who has counted the grains of sand in number — He has not counted in an estate a half"","" a half"","" and a third. When a half and a half have gone"","" where is the place of the third?\"" Zufar said to him: \""O Abu al-Abbas"","" who was the first to apply 'awl to the shares?\"" He said: \""Umar ibn al-Khattab"","" may Allah be pleased with him.\"" He said: \""Why?\"" He said: \""When the matters pressed upon him and some of them mounted atop others"","" he said: 'By Allah"","" I do not know how to deal with you. By Allah"","" I do not know which of you Allah has given precedence and which He has delayed.' And he said: 'I find nothing in this estate better than that I divide it among you according to the shares.'\"" Then Ibn Abbas said: \""By Allah"","" if he had given precedence to whom Allah gave precedence and delayed whom Allah delayed"","" no share would have required 'awl.\"" Zufar said to him: \""Which of them did He give precedence to and which did He delay?\"" He said: \""Every share that does not move except to another share — that is the one Allah gave precedence to. That is the share of the husband: he receives a half"","" and if that lapses"","" then a quarter"","" and he is not diminished below that. And the woman receives a quarter"","" and if that lapses from her"","" it becomes an eighth"","" and she is not diminished below that. And the sisters receive two-thirds"","" and a single one receives a half. If daughters enter upon them"","" they receive what remains. These are the ones whom Allah delayed. If he had given the one whom Allah gave precedence his share in full"","" and then divided what remained among those whom Allah delayed according to their shares"","" no share would have required 'awl.\"" Zufar said to him: \""What prevented you from advising Umar with this opinion?\"" He said: \""I feared him"","" by Allah.\"" Ibn Ishaq said: Al-Zuhri said to me: \""By Allah"","" had he not been preceded by an Imam of guidance"","" his matter would have been upon piety. No two scholars disagreed with Ibn Abbas.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12463","(12458) Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ali ibn Husayn from Amr ibn Uthman from Usama ibn Zayd, reaching the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever"","" and a disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya from Sufyan"","" and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhri. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari"","" Muslim]"""""
"12464","(12459) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Maryam informed us; Ali ibn Ma'bad narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Qist al-Raqqi narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa from 'Adiyy ibn Thabit from Yazid al-Bara' from his father, who said: \I met my uncle and he had a banner with him. I said: 'Where are you heading?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" sent me to a man who married his father's wife"","" and he commanded me to strike his neck and take his wealth.'\"" This is the wording of al-Rudhbari's narration. [Sahih]\n\nSome of our companions have interpreted this to mean that he married her believing it to be permissible"","" thus he became an apostate"","" and his killing and the seizure of his wealth became obligatory.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: \""It has been narrated that Mu'awiya wrote to Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit asking them about the inheritance of an apostate"","" and they both said: 'It belongs to the Bayt al-Mal (public treasury).'\"" Al-Shafi'i said: \""They meant that it is fay' (spoils of war).\"""""""
"12465","(12460) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'a narrated to us from al-Hakam that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, ruled regarding the inheritance of an apostate that it belongs to his Muslim family. This is munqati' (discontinuous), and its narrator from al-Hakam is not used as a hujja (authoritative proof).\n\nIt was also narrated by Sharik from Mughira from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and it is also munqati'."
"12466","(12461) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Humaydi narrated to us from Sufyan; Sulayman narrated to us from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought al-Mustawrid al-'Ijli, so he killed him and distributed his inheritance among his Muslim family. The Christians offered thirty thousand for his corpse, but Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, refused to sell it to them and had it burned. [Da'if]"
"12467","(12462) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Isbahani informed us; Abu 'Amr ibn Hamdan narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that al-Mustawrid al-'Ijli was brought to him and he had apostatized. He presented Islam to him, but he refused. So he killed him and distributed his inheritance among his Muslim heirs.\n\nAl-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \Some of the people of hadith among you claim that it is an error.\"" [Sahih]\n\nAl-Shafi'i said in another place: \""I said to him — meaning the one who argues with him — 'Have you heard from the people of hadith among you anyone who claims that the huffaz did not preserve from Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" that he divided his wealth among his Muslim heirs"","" and we fear that what this narrator added may be an error?'\""\n\nImam Ahmad"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: \""I read in the narration of Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hani' from Ahmad ibn Hanbal"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" that he weakened the hadith narrated from Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" that the inheritance of an apostate belongs to his Muslim heirs.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""The story of al-Mustawrid has been narrated through another chain from Ali"","" but it does not contain this wording; rather"","" it only states that he did not address his wealth.\"""""""
"12468","(12463) Al-Sharif Abu al-Fath informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us; Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi informed us; Ali ibn al-Ja'd informed us; Sharik informed us from Simak from Ibn 'Abid ibn al-Abras, who said: \I was sitting with Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" when a man from Banu 'Ijl called al-Mustawrid was brought to him. He had been a Muslim and then became a Christian. Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to him: 'What is this?' He said: 'I found their religion better than your religion.' He said: 'What is your religion?' He said: 'The religion of 'Isa"","" peace be upon him.' Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: 'And I am upon the religion of 'Isa"","" peace be upon him"","" but what do you say about 'Isa"","" peace be upon him?' He said a word that was obscure to me and I did not understand it. The people claimed that he said: 'He is his Lord.' Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: 'Kill him.' So the people trampled him until he died. Then the people of al-Hira came and offered — meaning for his corpse — twelve thousand"","" but Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" refused them and ordered it to be burned with fire. He did not address his wealth.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by al-Sha'bi and Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" without mention of the wealth. Then al-Shafi'i made it a settled argument for his opponent and excused himself for abandoning his position by the apparent wording of the statement of the Prophet"","" peace and blessings be upon him: \""A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever"","" and a disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim"",""\"" just as they abandoned by it the statement of Mu'adh and Mu'awiya and others regarding a Muslim inheriting from a Jew. [Da'if]"""""
"12469","(12464) That is from what Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Shu'ba narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Abi Hakim from Abdullah ibn Burayda from Yahya ibn Ya'mar from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, who said: \Mu'adh ibn Jabal was brought a man who had died upon other than Islam and left his son as a Muslim"","" so Mu'adh made him his heir and said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" say: \""Islam increases and does not decrease.\""'\"" This is how Shu'ba narrated it. [Da'if]"""""
"12470","(12465) Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated it, as Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abd al-Warith narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Abi Hakim al-Wasiti; Abdullah ibn Burayda narrated to us that two brothers — a Jew and a Muslim — disputed before Yahya ibn Ya'mar, and he made the Muslim the heir of both. He said: \Abu al-Aswad narrated to me that a man narrated to him that Mu'adh said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" say: \""Islam increases and does not decrease.\""'\"" So he made the Muslim the heir.\n\nIf the report is sound"","" its interpretation is not what he went to. Rather"","" he meant that Islam is in increase and does not decrease through apostasy. And this is an unknown narrator"","" so it is munqati' (discontinuous). [Da'if]"""""
"12471","(12466) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥamdān informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated from al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jumayʿ, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \When a person becomes an apostate"","" his children inherit from him.\"" This narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous)"","" for al-Qāsim did not meet his grandfather. [Weak]"""""
"12472","(12467) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from Simāk ibn al-Faḍl al-Khawlānī, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd al-Thaqafī, who said: \I witnessed ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) include the full siblings (brothers from the father and mother) alongside the maternal half-siblings (brothers from the mother) in the one-third share. A man said to him: 'You ruled differently in this matter in the first year.' He asked: 'How did I rule?' The man replied: 'You assigned the share to the maternal half-siblings and gave nothing to the full siblings.' ʿUmar said: 'That was our ruling then"","" and this is our ruling now.'\"" [Weak]"""""
"12473","(12468) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Ibn Thawr, from Maʿmar, from Simāk, from Wahb, from al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd al-Thaqafī, from ʿUmar, with a similar narration.\n\nSufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Maʿmar, and they both said in its chain: \Masʿūd ibn al-Ḥakam.\""\n\nYaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: \""This is an error; it is in fact al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd.\"" He said: \""Masʿūd ibn al-Ḥakam is a Zurqī"","" and the one from whom Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated is al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd al-Thaqafī.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12474","(12469) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Maʿmar.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Maʿmar informed us, from Simāk ibn al-Faḍl, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Masʿūd ibn al-Ḥakam, meaning al-Thaqafī, who said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding a woman who left behind her husband"","" her daughter"","" her maternal half-sisters"","" her full sisters"","" and her mother. He included the maternal half-siblings and the full siblings together in the one-third share"","" making it equal among them. A man said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"","" you did not include them together in such-and-such a year.' ʿUmar said: 'That was our ruling on that day"","" and this is our ruling today.'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nYaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: \""This is an error; it is in fact al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd"",""\"" and he conveyed the same meaning. Al-Bukhārī said likewise. [Weak]"""""
"12475","(12470) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us; ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqamah informed us that Masʿūd ibn al-Ḥakam is a Zurqī, and the one from whom Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated is in fact al-Ḥakam ibn Masʿūd al-Thaqafī. [Weak]"
"12476","(12471) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar included the full siblings (brothers from the father and mother) and the maternal half-siblings (brothers from the mother) together in the one-third share. [Weak]"
"12477","(12472) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Abī Mijlaz, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) included the maternal half-siblings and the full siblings together in the one-third share, whereas ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) did not include them together. [Weak]"
"12478","(12473) Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Abū Umayyah ibn Yaʿlā al-Thaqafī narrated from Abī al-Zinād, from ʿAmr ibn Wahb, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thābit, regarding the case of the \mushrikah\"" (shared inheritance)"","" he said: \""Give their father his share; he is like a donkey's wood—the father only brings them closer (in proximity).\"" And he included them together in the one-third share. [Weak]"""""
"12479","(12474) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us; Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Manṣūr and al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿUmar, ʿAbd Allāh, and Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them), that they said: \For the husband is one-half"","" and for the mother is one-sixth"","" and they included the full siblings (brothers from the father and mother) and the maternal half-siblings (brothers from the mother) together in the one-third share.\"" And they said: \""The father only increased them in nearness (of kinship).\"" [Sound (Ḥasan)]"""""
"12480","(12475) Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) said regarding a case involving a mother, a husband, maternal half-siblings, and full siblings: \For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother is one-sixth"","" and they both included the full siblings (brothers from the father and mother) and the maternal half-siblings (brothers from the mother) together in the one-third share"","" their males and females being equal therein.\"" And they said: \""The father only increased them in nearness (of kinship).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12481","(12476) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym reported to us from Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Shaʿbī: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, made them (the full siblings and the maternal siblings) co-sharers (in the one-third share).\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: It has been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd and Zayd ibn Thābil contrary to this. [Weak]"
"12482","(12477) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Shuʿbah reported to us from Abū Qays from Huzayl ibn Sharḥīl, who said: We came to ʿAbd Allāh regarding a case of a wife, a mother, two maternal siblings, and a full (paternal and maternal) brother. He said: \The shares have been exhausted"","" and nothing has been given to the full brother.\"" [Good]"""""
"12483","(12478) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shuʿbah reported to us from Abū Qays from al-Huzayl, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said regarding a woman who left behind her husband, her mother, her full sisters, and her maternal brothers: \For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother one-sixth"","" and for the maternal brothers one-third — completing the shares — and he did not allot anything to her full brothers.\"" [Good]"""""
"12484","(12479) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Isḥāq informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us: Sharīk reported to us from Abū Isḥāq from al-Arqam ibn Sharḥīl from ʿAbd Allāh, that he said regarding the case of co-sharing (al-musharrakah): \O son of a brother"","" the shares have been completed without you.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12485","(12480) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sālim reported to us from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿAlī and Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: \For the husband is one-half"","" for the mother one-sixth"","" and for the maternal brothers one-third"",""\"" and they did not make the full (paternal and maternal) brothers co-sharers with them. And they said: \""They (the full brothers) are the ʿaṣabah (residuaries); if anything remains (after the fixed shares)"","" it is for them"","" and if nothing remains"","" they receive nothing.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12486","(12481) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr informed us: Hushaym reported to us from Muḥammad ibn Sālim from al-Shaʿbī: that Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, used not to make co-sharers; he would assign the one-third to the maternal siblings to the exclusion of the full (paternal and maternal) siblings. Hushaym said: \I objected to him and said: 'Zayd used to make co-sharers.' He said: 'Al-Shaʿbī narrated to us thus from Zayd"","" that he used to say the same as ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him.' So I objected to him again"","" and he said: 'Between you and me is Ibn Abī Laylā.'\""\n\nThe authentic narration from Zayd ibn Thābil in this matter is what has preceded.\n\n(b) This narration is uniquely reported by Muḥammad ibn Sālim"","" and he is not strong (in ḥadīth).\n\n(c) Al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī are more knowledgeable about the school of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"","" even though they did not see him"","" from the narration of Abū Qays al-Awdī"","" even though it is a connected (mawṣūl) chain; however"","" the narration of Abū Qays has a supporting witness"","" so it is possible that he used to say this and then retracted it in favour of what was established from al-Shaʿbī and al-Nakhaʿī regarding his school. And Allah knows best"","" just as we have narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him. [Weak]"""""
"12487","(12482) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī reported to us from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him: that he assigned the one-third to the maternal siblings and did not make the full (paternal and maternal) siblings co-sharers with them. And he said: \They are the ʿaṣabah"","" and nothing remained for them.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12488","(12483) And with his chain he said: Sufyān informed us from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salamah, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about the maternal siblings, so he said: \Tell me"","" if they were a hundred"","" would you increase them beyond the one-third by anything?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then I will not reduce them from it by anything.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12489","(12484) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Zurārah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Zakarīyā informed us: Isrāʾīl reported to us from Jābir from ʿĀmir: that ʿAlī and Abū Mūsā, may Allah be pleased with them both, used not to make co-sharers. And it was also narrated by Abū Mijlaz from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, as a mursal (disconnected) narration, and by Ḥakīm ibn Jābir from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, as a mawṣūl (connected) narration. Thus it is well-known from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him. [Weak]"
"12490","(12485) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn Muʿādh narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq reported to us from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When the newborn cries (upon birth)"","" it is entitled to inheritance.\""\n\nAnd Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from al-Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb al-Jazarī from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā with this same chain"","" similarly"","" and added in the connected ḥadīth: \""That is the stab of Satan — every child of Adam is touched by that stab — except that which was of Maryam and her son"","" for when her mother delivered her"","" she said: 'I seek refuge for her in You and for her offspring from the accursed Satan.' So a veil was placed before her"","" and he (Satan) stabbed into it"","" meaning into the veil.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ: \""Every child of Adam is stabbed by Satan in his side when his mother gives birth to him"","" except ʿĪsā ibn Maryam. He went to stab him but stabbed into the veil.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""I have seen that cry which the infant makes when his mother gives birth to him"","" and it is from that (i.e."","" from Satan).\"" [Good for other reasons. Narrated by al-Sijistānī"","" 2920]"""""
"12491","(12486) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Ansari informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to me — al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us — Musa ibn Dawud narrated from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Salama — from al-Zuhri — from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib — from Abu Hurayrah, who said: \It is from the Sunnah that an unborn child shall not inherit nor be inherited from until it cries out with a shout.\"" Thus I found it. And Yahya ibn Sa'id reported from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The child does not inherit until it cries out — and the crying out is a shout"","" or a sneeze"","" or weeping — and his blood-money is not yet complete.\"" Sa'id said: \""Funeral prayer is not performed over him.\"" And it is reported from the hadith of Jabir"","" both as a mawquf and a marfu' narration"","" and this has already been discussed in the Book of Funerals. [Hasan]"""""
"12492","(12487) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajan informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzanni narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanj narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"","" Abu Bakr al-Siddiq"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said regarding the measures of dates which he had gifted to her: 'If you had harvested them or taken possession of them"","" they would be yours. But today they are the property of the heirs"","" and they are your brothers and your sisters. Divide them according to the Book of Allah.'\"" 'A'ishah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" said: \""By Allah"","" O my father"","" if such and such were the case"","" I would have left them. They are only names. Who is the other one?\"" He said: \""The daughter of Kharijah — I consider her to be a young girl.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12493","(12488) Abu Ja'far Kamil ibn Ahmad al-Mustamli and Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us — Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us — Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Zayd ibn Thabit — from his grandmother, Umm Sa'd bint Sa'd ibn al-Rabi', the wife of Zayd ibn Thabit — that she informed him, saying: \Zayd ibn Thabit came to me one day and said: 'If you wish"","" we may speak regarding your inheritance from your father"","" for the Commander of the Faithful"","" 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" has today granted the right of inheritance to the unborn child.' And Umm Sa'd had been pregnant at the time of her father Sa'd ibn al-Rabi's death.\"" Umm Sa'd said: \""I would not have asked my brothers for anything.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12494","(12489) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us — Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated from al-Zuhri — from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi — that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" what do you say about a man who sees another man with his wife — should he kill him and then you kill him"","" or how should he proceed?\"" Allah revealed concerning them what was mentioned in the Qur'an regarding the two who invoke mutual curses (al-mula'anayn). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \""The matter between you and your wife has been decided.\"" He said: \""So they performed mutual cursing"","" and I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He then said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" if I restrain her"","" I have lied against her.\"" So he separated them. Thereafter the Sunnah was established that the two who invoke mutual curses are to be separated. And she was pregnant"","" but she denied her pregnancy. Her child was attributed to her. Then the Sunnah was established regarding inheritance that he would inherit from her and she would inherit from him that which Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic"","" had decreed for her.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Rabi'. [Bukhari 4746]"""""
"12495","(12490) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Salama narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar informed us — from Ibn Tawus — from his father — from Ibn 'Abbas — from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Divide the wealth among the people of the obligatory shares according to the Book of Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic. Whatever remains goes to the nearest male relative.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim"","" and al-Bukhari also transmitted it as mentioned above. [Sahih]"""""
"12496","(12491) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Qattan narrated to us — Abu al-Azhar narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to me — Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us — Simak ibn Harb narrated from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Some people came to 'Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and disputed regarding the child of the two who had invoked mutual curses. The child's paternal uncles came seeking his inheritance.\"" He said: \""So he assigned his inheritance to his mother and made her his residuary heir ('asabah).\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12497","(12492) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Salim narrated to us — al-Sha'bi narrated from 'Ali and 'Abd Allah, who both said: \The 'asabah of the child of the mulā'anah is his mother — she inherits all of his wealth. If he has no mother"","" then her 'asabah is his 'asabah"","" and the child of unlawful intercourse (walad al-zinā) is in the same position.\"" [Da'if]\n\nAnd Zayd ibn Thabit said: \""The mother receives one-third"","" and the remainder goes to the public treasury (bayt al-mal).\"""""""
"12498","(12493) And by his chain of narration, from al-Sha'bi, that 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said regarding the son of the mulā'anah who left behind a brother and a mother: \The mother receives one-third"","" the brother receives one-sixth"","" and the remainder is returned to them both according to the proportion of their inheritance shares.\""\n\nAnd 'Abd Allah said: \""The brother receives one-sixth"","" and the remainder goes to the mother"","" for she is his 'asabah.\""\n\nAnd Zayd said: \""The mother receives one-third"","" the brother receives one-sixth"","" and the remainder goes to the public treasury.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12499","(12494) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us — Yahya narrated to us — Yazid narrated from Hammad ibn Salama — from Qatadah — that 'Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both, said regarding the son of the mulā'anah who left behind a brother and a mother: \The brother receives one-third and the mother receives one-third.\""\n\nAnd Zayd said: \""The brother receives one-sixth"","" the mother receives one-third"","" and the remainder goes to the public treasury.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"12500","(12495) Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Ansari informed us — Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah informed us — Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn 'Isa narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubarak informed us — Sa'id narrated from Qatadah — that Ibn Mas'ud used to assign the entire inheritance of the son of the mulā'anah to his mother. If he had no mother, it would go to her 'asabah. He said: And al-Hasan used to say that. He said: And 'Ali and Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: \The mother receives one-third"","" and the remainder goes to the public treasury of the Muslims.\""\n\n(T) And Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated from Sa'id — from Qatadah — from Khilas ibn 'Amr — from 'Ali and Zayd ibn Thabit"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" something similar to that. And the narration from 'Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" varies. And his statement in agreement with Zayd is more consistent with what we have mentioned above of the authentic Sunnah from 'Ali. [Da'if]"""""
"12501","(12496) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated — that it reached him from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr and Sulaymān ibn Yasār: that they were both asked regarding the child of *liʿān* (mutual imprecation) and the child of zinā (fornication) — who inherits from him? They both said: His mother inherits her prescribed share, and his maternal siblings inherit their prescribed shares, and whatever remains of his estate goes to the *mawālī* (patrons) of his mother, if she was a freed slave woman. And if she was a free Arab woman, she inherits her share, and his maternal siblings inherit their shares, and whatever remains of his estate goes to the Muslims.\n\nMālik, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: This is the ruling according to us, and this is what I found the people of knowledge in my city upon. [Weak]"
"12502","(12497) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, and he said: Some people agreed with us regarding both of them except in one particular: if his mother was a free Arab woman or had no *walāʾ* (patronage) attributed to her, they would return the remainder of his inheritance to the *ʿaṣabah* (agnatic heirs) of his mother, and they said: \The ʿaṣabah of his mother are his ʿaṣabah.\"" They cited in support of this a narration that is not established"","" and another that does not constitute a valid proof. [Authentic]"""""
"12503","(12498) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿĀṣim narrated from Hishām ibn ʿAmmār, Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ruʾbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Naṣrī, from Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ al-Laythī, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \A woman is entitled to three inheritances: the estate of her freed slave (*ʿatīqah*)"","" the foundling she picks up (*laqīṭ*)"","" and the child against whom she performed *liʿān*.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: ʿUmar ibn Ruʾbah al-Taghlibī"","" in his narration from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Naṣrī"","" is subject to scrutiny. Abū Aḥmad said: I heard Ibn Ḥammād mention this from al-Bukhārī. [Weak]"""""
"12504","(12499) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Maḥmūd ibn Khālid and Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir both said: al-Walīd narrated to us, Ibn Jābir narrated to us, Makḥūl said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the inheritance of the child of *liʿān* to his mother and to her heirs after her.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12505","(12500) He said: And Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, al-Walīd informed me, ʪsā Abū Muḥammad informed me, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḥārith, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar narration.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The ḥadīth of Makḥūl is *munqaṭiʿ* (disconnected). And ʪsā is Ibn Mūsā Abū Muḥammad al-Qurashī, and he is subject to scrutiny. [Weak]"
"12506","(12501) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Sufyān narrated from Dāwūd, meaning Ibn Abī Hind, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī narrated to me, he said: \I wrote to my brother from Banī Zurayq asking: What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decree regarding the child of *liʿān*?\"" He replied: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed it for his mother.\"" He said: \""She holds the status of his father and his mother.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12507","(12502) Abū Dāwūd narrated it in *al-Marāsīl* from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Dāwūd, from ʿAbd Allāh, from a man from the people of Shām, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The child of *liʿān* — his ʿaṣabah are the ʿaṣabah of his mother.\"" Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us"","" Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us"","" al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us"","" Abū Dāwūd narrated it"","" and this one is also *munqaṭiʿ* (disconnected). [Weak]\n\nThe Ustādh Abū al-Walīd"","" may Allah have mercy upon him"","" interpreted these reports to mean: if his mother was a freed slave woman (*mawlāh*) by manumission. And Allah knows best."""""
"12508","(12503) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Muʿtamir narrated from Salm ibn Abī al-Dhayyāl, one of our companions narrated to me, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no earning of a slave woman in Islam. Whoever earned through a slave woman in the Jāhiliyyah"","" the child is attributed to his patron. And whoever claims a child born out of wedlock"","" he neither inherits nor is inherited from.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12509","(12504) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Rāshid narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed that every child whose lineage is claimed (*mustalḥaq*) after the death of the father to whom he is attributed, and the heirs wish to affiliate him — if he was born from a slave woman whom the father owned on the day he had intercourse with her, then his lineage is established to the one who claimed him. He has no share in any inheritance that was distributed before his affiliation. But if the inheritance has not yet been divided, he receives his share. His lineage is not established if the father to whom he is attributed denied it during his lifetime. And if he was born from a slave woman the father did not own, or from a free woman with whom the father committed zinā, then his lineage is not established and he does not inherit, even if the father to whom he is attributed claimed him during his lifetime — for he is a child of zinā, belonging to the people of his mother's household, whether they were free or slave women. [Good]"
"12510","(12505) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Rāshid, with his chain and its meaning, and he added: \This pertains to one whose lineage was claimed in the early period of Islam. Whatever wealth was divided before Islam has already passed.\"" [Good]"""""
"12511","(12506) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us. He said: We said: When a Magian embraces Islam, and his daughter was his wife or his sister was his mother, we look at the two lines of kinship and consider the more significant of the two. We inherit her through that line and set aside the other. The more significant of the two is the one that is established in all circumstances. If she is both a mother and a sister, we inherit her on the basis that she is a mother, because the mother is established in all circumstances, whereas the sister may cease to be a sister. And all of their fixed shares of inheritance follow this same principle. And some of the people said: I would inherit her through both lines combined. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12512","(12507) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, regarding a Magian under whose marriage was his daughter, or his sister was his wife, and he dies. He said: She inherits through the closer of the two degrees of kinship. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12513","(12508) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī that he was asked about the Magians when they embrace Islam and they have two lines of kinship. He said: They are inherited through the closer of the two. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12514","(12509) The Shaykh said: And it is narrated from Zayd ibn Thābit that he said: He inherits through the nearer of the two matters, and he does not inherit through two lines. This is from what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abī al-Walīd al-Faqīh, Mūsā ibn Sahl informed us, ʿAbd al-Ghannī narrated from Ayyūb al-Khuzāʿī with his chain of narration leading to Zayd. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12515","(12510) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah said: I asked Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān about the inheritance of the Magians. He said: They inherit through one of the two lines—the line that is lawful (ḥalāl). This statement is also narrated from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, may Allah have mercy on him, and from Makḥūl. [Ḥasan]"
"12516","(12511) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār, that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, used to inherit the Magians through both lines combined when his mother was his wife, or his sister, or his daughter. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah is abandoned (matrūk). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12517","(12512) Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, Sufyān narrated from a man, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that they both said regarding the Magians: They are inherited through two lines. Sufyān said: It reached me from Ibrāhīm that he used to inherit the Magians through two lines. The Shaykh said: The narrations from the Companions in this chapter are not strong. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12518","(12513) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī informed me, Bishr ibn Muḥammad informed us, ʿAbd Allāh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Kathīr heard his father say: I witnessed ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, in the case of a hermaphrodite. He said: Look at the outlet of the urine, and inherit him accordingly. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12519","(12514) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jassr. He said: I heard Ibn Maʿqil and their elders mention that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about a newborn whose sex is unknown—whether it is male or female. ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: He is inherited according to the direction from which he urinates. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12520","(12515) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAbd al-Jalīl, from a man of Bakr ibn Wāʾil, who said: I witnessed ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, being asked about a hermaphrodite. He asked the people, but they did not know. So ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If he urinates from the passage of the male organ, then he is a boy; and if he urinates from the passage of the female organ, then she is a girl. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12521","(12516) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā b. Abī Ṭālib informed us, Yazīd informed us, Hammām b. Yaḥyā informed us from Qatādah, who said: Jābir b. Zayd was imprisoned during the time of al-Ḥajjāj, and they sent to him asking him about the intersex person (al-khunthā) — how is the inheritance determined? He said: \You imprison me and then you ask me for a legal ruling!\"" Then he said: \""Observe from which opening he urinates"","" and assign his inheritance accordingly.\"" Qatādah said: I mentioned this to Saʿīd b. al-Musayyab. He said: \""What if he urinates from both?\"" I said: \""I do not know.\"" Saʿīd said: \""The inheritance is assigned according to whichever precedes.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"12522","(12517) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Yaḥyā informed us, Yazīd informed us, Khālid b. Yazīd al-Haddādī informed us from Ṣāliḥ al-Dahhān — or Salamah b. Kulayb — who said: Jābir b. Zayd was asked about the intersex person — how is the inheritance determined? He said: \He should stand and be brought close to a wall and then urinate. If the urine reaches the wall"","" he is a male; and if it flows between his thighs"","" she is a female.\""\n\nA narrated hadith (ḥadīth mursal) has been reported on this matter with a weak chain of narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12523","(12518) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad b. ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Qāsim b. al-Layth al-Rasʿanī narrated to us, Hishām b. ʿAmmār narrated to us, Yaʿqūb b. Ibrāhīm al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad b. al-Sāʾib narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a newborn who was born with both a vulva and a penis — from which is the inheritance determined? The Prophet ﷺ said: \The inheritance is determined from which he urinates.\""\n\nMuḥammad b. al-Sāʾib al-Kalbī is not used as a basis for legal argument. [Very weak — Ḍaʿīf jiddan]"""""
"12524","(12519) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad b. al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us, Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us, Yazīd b. Hārūn informed us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl informed us from Anas b. Mālik that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf emigrated to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between him and Saʿd b. al-Rabīʿ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from Ḥumayd. [Bukhārī, Muslim 1427]"
"12525","(12520) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh and ʿAlī b. Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us, they said: Muḥammad b. Ayyūb informed us, Muḥammad b. Kathīr narrated to us, Ḥammād b. Salamah narrated from Thābit from Anas that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ and Abū Ṭalḥah.\n\nMuslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from Ḥammād. [Muslim 2528]"
"12526","(12521) Abū al-Ḥusayn b. Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Sulaymān b. al-Ashʿath b. Isḥāq — Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us, Abū Salamah narrated to us, Ḥammād b. Salamah narrated from Thābit from Anas that the Prophet ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between al-Zubayr and ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd. [Al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ 929]"
"12527","(12522) Abū al-Ḥusayn b. Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, Muḥammad b. ʿUbayd Allāh — that is, Ibn al-Munādī — narrated to us, Isḥāq b. Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakarīyā b. Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Saʿd b. Ibrāhīm from Nāfiʿ b. Jubayr b. Muṭʿim from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no alliance (ḥilf) in Islam.\"" Anas said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did establish an alliance between the Quraysh and the Anṣār in his house\"" — meaning the house of Anas in Madīnah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad b. al-Ṣabbāḥ from Ismāʿīl"","" and he said: \""in my house.\"" Muslim recorded it in abridged form through another chain from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal. [Bukhārī 2294"","" Muslim 2029]"""""
"12528","(12523) Abū al-Ḥusayn b. Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, Muḥammad b. ʿUbayd Allāh — Ibn al-Munādī — narrated to us, Isḥāq b. Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakarīyā b. Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Saʿd b. Ibrāhīm from his father from Jubayr b. Muṭʿim, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no alliance (ḥilf) in Islam"","" and whatever alliance existed in the Jāhiliyyah"","" Islam only added to it in strength.\"" This is how al-Azraq narrated it"","" and a group contradicted him in its chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12529","(12524) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad b. Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān b. Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Muḥammad b. Bishr, Ibn Numayr, and Abū Usāmah narrated from Zakarīyā from Saʿd b. Ibrāhīm from his father from Jubayr b. Muṭʿim, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim recorded it from Abī Bakr b. Abī Shaybah from Ibn Numayr and Abī Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"12530","(12525) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to me, Idrīs b. Yazīd narrated to us, Ṭalḥah b. Muṣarrif narrated from Saʿd b. Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And those with whom your oaths have made a pact — give them their share} (al-Nisāʾ 4:33). He said: When the Muhājirūn arrived in Madīnah, the Anṣār would be made heirs to the exclusion of their own blood relatives, due to the bond of brotherhood that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had established between them. Then when the verse {And for each We have appointed heirs from what the parents and nearest relatives have left} (al-Nisāʾ 4:33) was revealed, it abrogated that. He said: {And those with whom your oaths have made a pact — give them their share} refers to support and counsel. [Bukhārī 2292]"
"12531","(12526) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, and Abū Usāmah narrated it with a similar wording, adding: \and support"","" and counsel"","" and assistance"","" and he may bequeath for him"","" and the [fixed share of] inheritance has [thereby] been abrogated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others"","" from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12532","(12527) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Thābit narrated to me, ʿAliyy ibn Ḥusayn narrated from his father, from Yazīd al-Naḥwī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Regarding the verse {And those with whom your oaths have made a covenant — give them their share} [al-Nisāʾ 4:33]: A man would enter into a pact of alliance with another man between whom there was no blood relation, and one of them would inherit from the other. Then this was abrogated by Sūrat al-Anfāl, where Allah said: {And those of blood ties are more entitled to inherit from one another} [al-Anfāl 8:75]. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12533","(12528) And with his chain of narration from Ibn ʿAbbās: Regarding the verse {And those who believed and emigrated} and {And those who believed but did not emigrate} — the Bedouin would not inherit from the Muhājir, nor would the Muhājir inherit from him. Then this was abrogated by the verse: {And those of blood ties are more entitled to inherit from one another} [al-Anfāl 8:75]. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12534","(12529) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Muʿādh al-Ḍabbī narrated from Simāk, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established bonds of brotherhood between his Companions and made some of them inherit from others, until this verse was revealed: {And those of blood ties are more entitled to inherit from one another} [al-Anfāl 8:75]. So they abandoned that and inherited on the basis of blood relations. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12535","(12530) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us, ʿAliyy ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah informed me from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abū Ḥudhayfah ibn ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbd Shams — who was among those who witnessed Badr alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — had adopted Sālim as his son and married him to his niece Hind bint al-Walīd ibn ʿUtbah, while Sālim was the freed slave of a woman of the Anṣār, just as the Prophet ﷺ had adopted Zayd. In the Jāhiliyyah, whoever adopted a man, the people would call him his son, and he would inherit from his estate, until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed regarding that: {Call them by [the names of] their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers — then they are your brothers in religion and your freed slaves} [al-Aḥzāb 33:5]. So they were returned to their [biological] fathers. Whoever had no known father was considered a freed slave and a brother [in faith].\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5088, Muslim 1453]"
"12536","(12531) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us, ʿAliyy ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab said: This verse was revealed: {And for all, We have made heirs [mawālī] from what the parents and relatives have left} [al-Nisāʴ 4:33] — concerning those who used to adopt men other than their own sons and make them heirs. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed regarding them that He would grant them a share through bequest, and Allah restored inheritance to the [rightful] heirs among the freed slaves, the blood relatives, and the ʿaṣabah. He refused to grant inheritance to those claimed as sons by those who adopted them, but He granted them a share through bequest. Thus, whatever they had contracted regarding inheritance — that which Allah abrogated for them — was annulled. [Ḥasan]"
"12537","(12532) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us, ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated from ʬAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the word of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And what is recited to you in the Book concerning the orphan girls} [al-Nisāʴ 4:2] — in the beginning of this Sūrah regarding inheritance — he said: They would not grant inheritance to a child until he reached puberty. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"12538","(12533) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the word of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {Allah instructs you concerning your children: for the male, the equivalent of the share of two females} [al-Nisāʴ 4:11] — he said: Inheritance used to belong to the child, and bequest used to be for the parents and the near relatives. Then Allah abrogated from that what He willed. He made for the male child the equivalent of the share of two females, and He made for the parents two-sixths, and He made for the husband one-half or one-quarter, and He made for the wife one-quarter or one-eighth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, from Warqāʾ. [Bukhārī 4531]"
"12539","(12534) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAliyy ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Ḥajjāj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A bequest in favour of an heir is not valid unless the [other] heirs consent.\"" This ʿAṭāʾ is ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī"","" who did not meet Ibn ʿAbbās nor see him. Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī and others stated this. It has also been narrated through another chain from him"","" from ʿIkrimah"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Munkar. Arwāʾ al-Ghalīl 1656]"""""
"12540","(12535) Abū Bakr al-Aṣbahānī informed him, ʿAliyy ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Mahdī bi'llāh narrated to us, Abū ʿUlāthah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Khālid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Rāshid narrated from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A bequest in favour of an heir is not valid unless the [other] heirs consent.\"" ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī is not strong [in narration]. [Munkar]"""""
"12541","(12536) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Ibn 'Uyyaynah narrated from Sulayman al-Ahwal from Mujahid that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no bequest for an heir.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: \""Some of the Syrians narrated a hadith which the scholars of hadith do not authenticate"","" as some of its narrators are unknown. It has been reported from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a disconnected (munqati') form. We rely upon what the scholars of the military expeditions (al-maghazi) generally report"","" that the Prophet (ﷺ) said in the year of the Conquest: 'There is no bequest for an heir"",""' and upon the consensus of the general populace upon this ruling.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""""
"12542","(12537) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us: Ibn 'Ayyash narrated from Shurayhil ibn Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Umamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Verily Allah"","" exalted be His praise"","" has given every rightful one his right. Therefore"","" there is no bequest for an heir.\"" [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""""
"12543","(12538) Abu Sa'd al-Malini narrated to us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi 'Ismah narrated to us: Abu Talib Ahmad ibn Humayd said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal say: \Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash — what he narrates from the Syrians is sound"","" but what he narrates from the people of the Hijaz is not sound.\"" The Sheikh said: \""Al-Bukhari and a group of the huffaz said the same. This particular hadith was narrated by Isma'il from a Syrian. And Allah knows best. It has also been reported from another chain from the Syrians.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12544","(12539) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki narrated to us: Abu al-Husayn 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' al-Qadi narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from 'Amr ibn Kharijah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us at Mina while he was upon his mount and said: 'Verily Allah has apportioned for every person his share of inheritance. Therefore"","" no bequest is valid for an heir.'\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nIt was also narrated by Hammad ibn Salamah from Qatadah"","" and it was reported from another weak chain from 'Amr. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""""
"12545","(12540) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan narrated to us in Baghdad: Abu 'Amr ibn al-Sammak narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Qattan narrated to us: Isma'il ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Ziyad ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to me: Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated from al-Hasan from 'Amr ibn Kharijah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no bequest for an heir"","" unless the heirs permit it.\"" And it was reported from another chain. [Munkar]"""""
"12546","(12541) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, who narrated to me: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated from Anas ibn Malik, who said: \I was beneath the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" its saliva dripping upon me"","" and I heard him say: 'Verily Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has given every rightful one his right"","" and there is no bequest for an heir.'\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nIt was also narrated by al-Walid ibn Mazid al-Bayruti from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id"","" a shaykh of the coastal region"","" who said: \""A man from the people of Madinah narrated to me"","" saying: 'I was beneath the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"",""' and he mentioned it.\""\n\nThis hadith has been reported from other chains"","" all of which are not strong. Reliance is placed upon the first hadith"","" which is the narration of Ibn Abi Najih from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas"","" and upon what al-Shafi'i mentioned regarding the transmission of the scholars of the military expeditions"","" together with the consensus of the general populace upon this ruling. And Allah knows best. [Sahih]"""""
"12547","(12542) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah narrated to us: Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Tawus from his father, who used to say: \The bequest was (prescribed) before the inheritance. When the inheritance was revealed"","" the bequest for the one who inherits was abrogated"","" and the bequest remained for the one who does not inherit. Thus"","" it is established. Whoever bequeaths for other than a relative"","" his bequest is not valid.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12548","(12543) He said: And Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus narrated from al-Hasan regarding the verse of bequest, who said: \The bequest was for the parents and the nearest of kin. That which pertained to the parents was abrogated"","" and their share was established for them in Surah al-Nisa'. And from the nearest of kin"","" every heir was abrogated"","" and the bequest remained for the nearest of kin who do not inherit.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12549","(12544) He said: And Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yunus and Humayd narrated from al-Hasan that he used to say: \Whoever bequeaths for other than his relatives"","" then those for whom he bequeathed shall have one-third of the third"","" and his relatives shall have two-thirds of the third.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"12550","(12545) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim — that is, Ibn 'Ulayyah — narrated from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn 'Abbas, who stood and addressed the people here — meaning in al-Basrah — and recited Surah al-Baqarah, explaining what was in it. When he reached this verse: {If he leaves wealth, the bequest is for parents and nearest relatives} (al-Baqarah: 180), he said: \This has been abrogated.\"" Then he mentioned what came after it. [Da'if]"""""
"12551","(12546) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī narrated to me, ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated from his father, from Yazīd al-Naḥwī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the verse: *\If he leaves any wealth"","" bequest is made for the parents and near relatives\""* — the bequest was thus [obligatory] until it was abrogated by the verse of inheritance. And similarly it was narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar from his own statement. [Weak]"""""
"12552","(12547) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, Sunayd ibn Dāwūd narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from Jahḍam, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Badr, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The verse of inheritance abrogated it\"" — meaning *\""Bequest is made for the parents and near relatives.\""*\n\nAnd it was narrated to us from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he said: \""The verse of inheritance abrogated it.\"" [Sound]"""""
"12553","(12548) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, and al-Shāfiʿī said: And thus said the majority of the common scholars, except that Ṭāwūs and a few with him said: \It remains established for relatives who are not heirs. So whoever bequeaths to other than a relative"","" it is not valid.\"" We found that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding six slaves who belonged to a man who had no wealth other than them"","" and he freed them at the time of death. The Prophet ﷺ divided them into three portions and freed two and kept four as slaves. [Sound. al-Ṭayālisī 884]"""""
"12554","(12549) ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us of it from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, from the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Shāfiʿī said: The indication of the Sunnah in the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn is clear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ treated their emancipation during illness as a bequest, and the one who freed them was a man from the Arabs, and the Arab only owned those between whom and himself there was no kinship from among the non-Arabs. So the Prophet ﷺ permitted the bequest for them. The Shaykh said: This ḥadīth is established through the chain of Abū al-Muhallab and Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from ʿImrān. [Sound]"
"12555","(12550) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkār narrated to us, Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Simāk, from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that a man freed six slaves at the time of his death, and his heirs from the Bedouins came and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what he had done — or what he had acted upon. He said: \Had we known that"","" we would not have prayed over him.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast lots among them and freed two and kept four as slaves. [Sound through other chains]"""""
"12556","(12551) Manṣūr ibn Zādān narrated it from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān, that a man from the Anṣār freed six slaves he owned at the time of his death and left no wealth other than them. Then he mentioned it. Abū Jaʿfar al-Mustamlī narrated it to us, Bishr al-Isfarāyīnī informed us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Hushaym narrated from Manṣūr ibn Zādān, and he mentioned its meaning. [Sound through other chains]"
"12557","(12552) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us by dictation, they said: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us, Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Mālik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif narrated. He said: I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā: \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ make a bequest?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Yet bequest has been made obligatory upon people\"" — or he said: \""They have been commanded with bequest.\"" He said: \""He bequeathed the Book of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic.\"" And in the narration of al-Sulamī: \""How then was it made obligatory?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Khallād ibn Yaḥyā"","" and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Mālik ibn Mighwal. [Bukhārī"","" Muslim]"""""
"12558","(12553) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left behind no dinar"","" no dirham"","" no camel"","" and he did not bequeath anything.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr and from Abū Muʿāwiyah"","" who added: \""and no sheep.\"" [Sound. Muslim]"""""
"12559","(12554) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān narrated to me from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not bequeath anything at the time of his death except three things: he bequeathed to the Rāhāwīyīn one hundred wasqs of produce from Khaybar; he bequeathed to the Dārīyīn one hundred wasqs of produce from Khaybar; he bequeathed to the Shanʾiyyīn one hundred wasqs of produce from Khaybar; he bequeathed to the Ashʿariyyīn one hundred wasqs of produce from Khaybar; he bequeathed the dispatch of the expedition of Usāmah ibn Zayd; and he bequeathed that two religions not remain in the Arabian Peninsula.\"" This is a mursal ḥadīth. [Weak]\n\n(3) Chapter\n\nRegarding the statement of Allah"","" the Most High: *\""And when the division of the estate is attended by relatives"","" orphans"","" and the poor"","" then provide for them from it and speak to them words of kindness.\""*"""""
"12560","(12555) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jarīr al-Ṭabarī informed us, Abū Kurayb informed us, al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Sufyān, from al-Shaybānī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding: *\And when the division of the estate is attended by relatives"","" orphans"","" and the poor\""* — he said: \""It is a muḥkamah (decisive) verse and is not abrogated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Ḥumayd from al-Ashjaʿī. [Bukhārī 4576]"""""
"12561","(12556) Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth added therein, from al-Ashjaʿī, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās"","" when he was the executor (of an estate)"","" would give [from it]"","" and when there was scarcity in the estate"","" he would offer them an apologetic explanation. That is the 'kind word' [referred to in the verse].\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr narrated it to us. al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us. al-Qāsim narrated to us. Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to me. Ibrāhīm narrated it to us"","" and he mentioned it. [Mawḍūʿ]"""""
"12562","(12557) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah narrated to us. Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Dabbī narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us. Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us. Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Abū Bishr, from Saʿīb ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \Some people say that this verse has been abrogated: 'And when the division [of the estate] is attended by relatives"","" orphans"","" and the poor"","" then provide for them from it' (Qurʾān 4:8). No"","" by Allah"","" it has not been abrogated. Rather"","" it is among those matters regarding which the people are negligent. There are two categories of executors: an executor who is an heir — that one provides [from the estate]"","" and an executor who is not an heir — that one speaks a kind word"","" saying: 'This is the property of orphans"","" and I have no share in it.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim"","" from Abū ʿAwanah"","" without doubt. The doubt is from me in my chain. It is also narrated from ʿĀʾishah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" that she said regarding this verse: \""It was not abrogated.\"" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Abū ʿAwanah"","" not going beyond Saʿīb ibn Jubayr. Likewise"","" Shuʿbah and Hushaym narrated it from Abū Bishr. We have also narrated from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī that he used to give [from the estate] on the basis of this verse. [Bukhārī 2759]"""""
"12563","(12558) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Maymūnī narrated to us. Rūḥ narrated to us. Ibn Jurayj narrated to us. Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated to me that Asmāʾ bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr — meaning also al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad — both narrated to him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr divided the inheritance of his father ʿAbd al-Raḥmān while ʿĀʾishah was still alive. He said: \He did not leave in the house any poor person or relative without giving them from his father's inheritance.\"" And he recited: \""And when the division [of the estate] is attended by relatives"","" orphans"","" and the poor\"" (Qurʾān 4:8) — the entire verse.\n\nal-Qāsim said: \""I mentioned that to Ibn ʿAbbās"","" and he said: 'He did not do what was correct. That [provision] pertains to the bequest (waṣiyyah). This verse pertains to the bequest — meaning that the deceased should make a bequest.'\""\n\nIn the narration of a group from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind"","" from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"","" [regarding the verse] \""And when the division [of the estate] is attended\"" — in one narration he said: \""The division of the third [of the estate].\"" In another narration he said: \""That is from the third"","" at the time of the bequest.\"" In another narration he said: \""When the deceased dies"","" the inheritance becomes obligatory for his heirs.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12564","(12559) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us. Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated from Hishām al-Dastawāʾī, from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that he said regarding this verse: \And when the division [of the estate] is attended by relatives"","" orphans"","" and the poor"","" then provide for them from it\"" (Qurʾān 4:8) — he said: \""It was abrogated by the fixed shares of inheritance (farāʾiḍ).\""\n\nLikewise"","" ʿAṭāʾ"","" ʿIkrimah"","" and al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim said it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12565","(12560) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn al-Faḍl al-ʿAsqalānī narrated to us. Ādam narrated to us. Abū Shaybah narrated from ʿAṭāʾ regarding His statement: \And when the division [of the estate] is attended\"" (Qurʾān 4:8) — to the end of the verse — he said: \""It is abrogated. The verse of inheritance abrogated it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12566","(12561) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said: \There has been narrated regarding the precedence of debt over bequest a hadith from the Prophet ﷺ that the scholars of hadith do not establish as authentic.\""\n\nal-Shāfiʿī said: \""Sufyān narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq"","" from al-Ḥārith"","" from ʿAlī"","" that the Prophet ﷺ judged that debt takes precedence over bequest.\""\n\nal-Shaykh said: \""The scholars of hadith refrain from establishing this [as authentic] due to the fact that al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar narrated it solely from ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and al-Ḥārith is not used as evidence for his narration due to the criticism of the ḥuffāẓ regarding him.\""\n\nLikewise"","" Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12567","(12562) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us. Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us. al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us. Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us. Zakariyyā narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \You recite: 'After a bequest that is made or a debt' (Qurʾān 4:11). Indeed"","" Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" has decreed that debt takes precedence over bequest. And indeed"","" the children of the mother (banī al-umm) inherit to the exclusion of the children of the half-siblings through the father (banī al-ʿallāt).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12568","(12563) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us. Ibn Wahb narrated to us. Shabīb ibn Saʿīd narrated to me that he heard Yaḥyā ibn Abī Unaysah al-Jazarī narrating from Abū Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Debt takes precedence over bequest"","" and there is no bequest for an heir.'\""\n\nThis is how Yaḥyā ibn Abī Unaysah brought it"","" from Abū Isḥāq"","" from ʿĀṣim. And Yaḥyā is weak. [Very weak — Ḍaʿīf jiddan]"""""
"12569","(12564) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us. Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Sufyān narrated to us from Hishām ibn Ḥujayr"","" from Ṭāwūs"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" that it was said to him: 'How do you command ʿUmrah before Ḥajj"","" when Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" says: \""And complete the Ḥajj and the ʿUmrah for Allah\"" (Qurʾān 2:196)?' He said: 'How do you recite — debt before bequest"","" or bequest before debt?' He said: 'Bequest before debt.' He said: 'Then which of the two do you begin with?' They said: 'With debt.' He said: 'It is the same as that.'\""\n\nal-Shāfiʿī said: \""He means that the order of precedence is permissible [i.e."","" either may come first].\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12570","(12565) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan all narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me. Men from among the people of knowledge — among them Mālik ibn Anas and Yūnus ibn Yazīd — narrated to me that Ibn Shihāb narrated to them.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us. Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us. al-Qaʿnabī and Ibn Bukayr narrated from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waggāṣ, from his father, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. I had a severe pain that had afflicted me"","" so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" the pain has reached me as you see"","" and I possess wealth"","" and I have no heir except a daughter. Shall I give in charity two-thirds of my wealth?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then half?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then one-third?' He said: 'One-third — and one-third is much"","" or a great deal. Indeed"","" if you leave your heirs wealthy"","" it is better for you than leaving them destitute"","" begging from people. And indeed"","" you will not spend any expenditure seeking the Countenance of Allah without being rewarded for it — even what you place in the mouth of your wife.'\""\n\nHe said: \""So I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" will I be left behind after my companions?' He said: 'Indeed"","" you will not be left behind and perform any righteous deed without being raised thereby in degree and elevation. And perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah"","" complete the emigration of my Companions and do not turn them back on their heels.' But the wretched one is Saʿd ibn Khawlā — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ expressed grief for him because he died in Makkah.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of al-Qaṭṭān. In the narration of Ibn Wahb"","" [Saʿd] said: \""Then half"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""No. One-third — and one-third is much.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"","" from Mālik. And Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"","" from Ibn Wahb"","" from Yūnus. [Bukhārī 1296"","" 2742]"""""
"12571","(12566) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — he read to him in al-Muḥarram of the year three hundred and thirty-seven (337 AH): Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī informed us: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us — Ibn Shihāb said: ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī, and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad informed us, they said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited me during the Farewell Pilgrimage from an ailment from which I feared death, so I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" what you see of this ailment has distressed me greatly"","" and I possess wealth"","" but I have no heir save a single daughter. Shall I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Shall I give half of it?\"" He said: \""No. One-third"","" and one-third is much. Indeed"","" if you leave your heirs wealthy"","" it is better than leaving them dependent"","" begging people. And you shall not spend any expenditure seeking the Countenance of Allah except that you shall be rewarded for it — even the morsel you place in your wife's mouth.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" shall I be left behind after my companions?\"" He said: \""You shall not be left behind such that you perform a righteous deed seeking the Countenance of Allah except that you shall be increased in rank and elevation thereby. And perhaps you shall be left behind so that some people may benefit through you and others may be harmed. O Allah"","" complete the Hijrah of my companions and do not turn them back upon their heels.\"" But the wretched one is Saʿd ibn Khawlāh — the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lamented that he died in Makkah. The wording of the two narrations is one and the same.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" and al-Bukhārī extracted it from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus and others from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd. Likewise"","" Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah"","" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah"","" and Maʿmar narrated it from al-Zuhrī"","" but Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah contradicted them"","" saying: \""ʿĀm al-Fatḥ\"" (the year of the Conquest). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12572","(12567) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz — he read to him: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr ibn Manṣūr, Abū ʿUthmān, informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from al-Zuhrī, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father, that he said: I fell ill in the year of the Conquest with a severe illness, and the Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit me. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have abundant wealth"","" and none shall inherit me save a daughter of mine. Shall I bequeath all of my wealth?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Then half?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Then one-third?\"" He said: \""One-third"","" and one-third is much. Indeed"","" if you leave your heirs wealthy"","" it is better than leaving them dependent"","" begging people. Indeed"","" you shall be rewarded for all of your expenditure — even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I fear dying in a land from which I have emigrated.\"" He said: \""It may be that you shall live on until some people benefit through you and others are harmed. O Allah"","" complete the Hijrah of my companions and do not turn them back upon their heels.\"" But the wretched one is Saʿd ibn Khawlāh — he lamented that he died in Makkah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12573","(12568) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā ibn Asad informed us: Sufyān informed us, mentioning something similar in meaning, except that he said: \You shall not spend any expenditure except that you shall be rewarded for it — even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" shall I be left behind after my emigration?\"" He said: \""You shall be left behind after me"","" and you shall perform a deed seeking Paradise — except that you shall be increased in elevation and rank. And perhaps you shall be left behind until some people benefit through you and others are harmed.\"" Then he mentioned the remainder in similar fashion.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and others — all of them from Sufyān. And Sufyān contradicted the majority in his saying \""ʿĀm al-Fatḥ\"" (the year of the Conquest)"","" whereas the preserved narration is \""ʿām Ḥajjat al-Wadāʿ\"" (the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12574","(12569) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Mūsā ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Mundhir ibn Shādhān informed us: Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī informed us: Marwān from Hāshim ibn Hāshim, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father, who said: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited me. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" supplicate to Allah that He does not turn me back upon my heels.\"" He said: \""Perhaps Allah shall raise you so that people may benefit through you.\"" I said: \""I wish to make a bequest"","" and I have only a daughter. Shall I bequeath half?\"" He said: \""Half is much.\"" He said: I said: \""Then one-third?\"" He said: \""One-third"","" and one-third is much — or great.\"" He said: So he bequeathed one-third"","" and that was permitted for them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm from Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī"","" and he said: \""So the people bequeathed one-third"","" and that was permitted for them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12575","(12570) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī informed us: Wahb ibn Jarīr informed us: Shuʿbah informed us from Simāk, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from Saʿd, who said: Four verses were revealed concerning me — and he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me while I was ill, and I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" shall I bequeath all of my wealth?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Then two-thirds?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""Then one-third?\"" — and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) fell silent"","" so it was [settled at] one-third.\n\nMuslim extracted it. [Muslim 174]"""""
"12576","(12571) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤ al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me — I heard Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAmr al-Makkī saying: I heard ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"","" Allah has given you one-third of your wealth at the time of your death"","" as an increase in your deeds.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12577","(12572) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Men from among the people of knowledge — among them ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, and Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and others — informed me that Nāfiʿ informed them from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about bequest (waṣiyyah). ʿUmar said: \One-third is a middle course regarding the wealth — neither deficient nor excessive.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\n(6) Chapter: Whoever considered it recommended to reduce below one-third when one's heirs are not left wealthy"","" drawing evidence from what we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ."""""
"12578","(12573) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Ḥumaydī informed us: Sufyān informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Wakīʿ informed us — all of them from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If people were to reduce from one-third to one-quarter in bequest"","" it would be more virtuous"","" because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'One-third"","" and one-third is much — or great.'\"" The wording is that of Wakīʿ's narration"","" and in the narration of Ibn ʿUyaynah and ʿĪsā"","" the words \""in bequest"","" it would be more virtuous\"" are not present.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from Sufyān"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā and from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Bukhārī 2743"","" Muslim 1629]"""""
"12579","(12574) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī informed us: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad informed us: Shaybān from Qatādah, who said: It was mentioned to us that Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, bequeathed one-fifth of his wealth, and he said: \I am not pleased with anything from my wealth compared to that with which Allah is pleased from the war gains of the Muslims.\"" And Qatādah said: \""And it was said that one-fifth is commendable"","" one-quarter is burdensome"","" and one-third is permitted by the judges.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12580","(12575) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī informed us: Ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah from Idrīs al-Awdī, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The one who bequeaths one-fifth is better than the one who bequeaths one-quarter"","" and the one who bequeaths one-quarter is better than the one who bequeaths one-third.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12581","(12576) Abū al-Fatḥ informed us, al-Shurayḥī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Zuhayr reported from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \That I bequeath a quarter is more beloved to me than that I bequeath a third. So whoever bequeathed a third"","" let him not leave it (i.e."","" let him not exceed it).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12582","(12577) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar reported from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) visited a man from Banī Hāshim who was ill and whom he was visiting. The man intended to make a bequest, so ʿAlī forbade him and said: \Indeed"","" Allah"","" the Blessed and Most High"","" says: 'If he leaves wealth' (al-Baqarah 2:180) — meaning wealth — so leave your wealth for your heirs.\"" [Weak. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 15351]"""""
"12583","(12578) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us, and Hishām mentioned it with the same meaning, but he did not say \from Banī Hāshim.\"" He said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \""Indeed"","" Allah"","" the Most High"","" says: 'If he leaves wealth' (al-Baqarah 2:180)"","" and indeed you are leaving only a small thing"","" so leave it for your dependents"","" for that is better.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12584","(12579) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah reported from Muḥammad ibn Sharīk al-Makkī, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: A man said to her: \I wish to make a bequest.\"" She said: \""How much is your wealth?\"" He said: \""Three thousand.\"" She said: \""How many dependents do you have?\"" He said: \""Four.\"" She said: \""Allah"","" Glorified is He"","" says: 'If he leaves wealth' (al-Baqarah 2:180)"","" and indeed this is a small thing"","" so leave it for your dependents"","" for that is better.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"","" 2/567]"""""
"12585","(12580) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us, Ibn Jurayj reported from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \If the deceased leaves seven hundred dirhams"","" he should not make a bequest.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"","" 2/659]"""""
"12586","(12581) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ reported from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding His statement: \And let those fear who"","" if they left behind weak offspring"","" would fear for them\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:9) — meaning when death approaches a man and it is said to him: \""Give charity from your wealth"","" free slaves"","" and give from it in the cause of Allah\"" — they were forbidden to command him with that. That is"","" whoever among you attends a sick person at the time of death"","" let him not command him to spend his wealth in freeing slaves"","" giving charity"","" and in the cause of Allah. Rather"","" let him instruct him to clarify what he owes in debts and to bequeath from his wealth for his relatives who do not inherit"","" bequeathing for them a fifth or a quarter. He said: \""Would any one of you be pleased"","" when he dies and leaves behind weak children — meaning young ones — to leave them without wealth"","" so that they become dependent upon people? It is not befitting that you command him with that which you would not be pleased with for yourselves and your own children. Rather"","" speak the truth in this matter.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12587","(12582) Through this chain of narration from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding His statement: \And let those fear who"","" if they left behind weak offspring\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:9) — this man attends another man at the time of his death and advises him with a bequest that harms his heirs. Allah"","" Glorified is He"","" commanded the one who hears this to fear Allah"","" to guide him"","" and to direct him to what is correct. And let him look after his heirs as he would love for his own heirs to be treated"","" when he fears for them ruin and loss.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12588","(12583) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us, Warqāʾ reported from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His statement: \And let those fear who"","" if they left behind weak offspring\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:9). He said: \""This is at the time of making a bequest. The one who attends him says: 'Make it less"","" and bequeath for so-and-so and for the family of so-and-so.' Allah says: 'And let those fear' — those are the ones who should speak as they would love to be spoken to regarding their children after them"","" and let them say a just word"","" meaning justice.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12589","(12584) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū Shihāb reported from al-Aʿmash, from Muslim, from Masrūq, that he attended a man who was making a bequest and was favouring some heirs over others. So Masrūq said to him: \Indeed"","" Allah"","" Glorified is He"","" has divided among you and has made the division excellent. And whoever"","" through his own opinion"","" turns away from the opinion of Allah"","" goes astray. So bequeath for your relatives who do not inherit"","" and then leave the wealth as Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has divided it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"","" 2/177]"""""
"12590","(12585) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbtah ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us, Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥuddānī informed us, al-Ashʿath ibn Jābir informed us, Shahr ibn Ḥawshab informed me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"","" a man — or a woman — may perform acts of obedience to Allah for sixty years"","" then death comes to them and they cause harm through the bequest"","" and thus the Fire becomes obligatory for them.\"" He said: Then Abū Hurayrah recited to me from here: \""After any bequest that was made or debt"","" without causing harm\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:12) until he reached: \""the great success\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:13). [Weak. Abū Dāwūd"","" 2867. Tirmidhī"","" 2117]"""""
"12591","(12586) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād, he said: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī dictated to us in al-Muḥarram in the year three hundred and thirty-seven, he said: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, he said: ʿUmar ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us, he said: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Causing harm in the bequest is among the major sins.\"" [Munkar]"""""
"12592","(12587) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, he said: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us, he said: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, he said: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Injustice in the bequest and causing harm therein are among the major sins.\"" This is the correct version"","" it is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion). And Ibn ʿUyaynah and others narrated it from Dāwūd as a mawqūf report. It was also narrated through another chain as marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet)"","" but its elevation (rafʿ) is weak. [Saḥīh. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"","" 342"","" 344]"""""
"12593","(12588) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Men from among the people of knowledge informed me, among them ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī, that Nāfiʿ narrated to them from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not right for a Muslim person who has something to bequeath to spend two nights except that his bequest is written and kept with him.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb from Yūnus"","" and from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd from Ibn Wahb from Usāmah ibn Zayd. [Bukhārī 2738"","" Muslim 1627]"""""
"12594","(12589) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us, he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, he said: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, he said: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, he said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \It is not right for a Muslim person who has wealth he wishes to bequeath to spend a night or two without his bequest being written and kept with him.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12595","(12590) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yūnus ibn Yazīd and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not right for a Muslim person who has something to bequeath to spend three nights except that his bequest is written and kept with him.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""Not a single night has passed since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this except that my bequest was with me.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf from Ibn Wahb from ʿAmr"","" and from Abū al-Ṭāhir and others from Ibn Wahb from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12596","(12591) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: Abū al-Walīd informed us, he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, he said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated from ʿUmarah al-Ṣaydalānī, from Thābit, from Anas, that he (Anas) bequeathed for him a share equal to the share of one of his children. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah 30796]"
"12597","(12592) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, he said: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us, they said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us, he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, he said: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, he said: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, he said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Abī Qilābah, from Abī al-Muhallab, from ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, and he had no other wealth besides them. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, who spoke to him harshly. Then he called them and divided them into three portions, and drew lots among them. He freed two and kept four enslaved. In the narration of Sulaymān: \He divided them into three portions.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. [Muslim 1668]"""""
"12598","(12593) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Baghdādī informed us, he said: ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, he said: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists whose opinion was relied upon among the people of Madīnah, who used to say: \Whoever bequeaths that one-third of his wealth be given to a man"","" and one-quarter of his wealth to another"","" and one-half of his wealth to another"","" and his heirs say: 'We do not permit it; he is only entitled to one-third of his property'—then that is permissible upon them. The testator places his third wherever he wishes from his wealth at a fair valuation. The wall (property) is like the saddlebag"","" the sword"","" or the garment that he bequeaths. The heirs have no right to say: 'He is only entitled to one-third of his saddlebag"","" his sword"","" and his garment.'\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""""
"12599","(12594) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us in al-Kūfah, he said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us, he said: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn al-ʿUmarī and ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā al-ʿAbsī narrated to us, they said: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed us from his father, from Abī Murāwiḥ, from Abū Dharr, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" which deed is best?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.\"" He said: \""Which slaves (are best to free)?\"" He ﷺ said: \""The most expensive of them and the most precious to their owners.\"" He said: \""What if I am unable?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Then help a weak person or do something for one who is unskilled.\"" He said: \""What if I do not do that?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Then leave the people from your harm"","" for it is a charity that you give on yourself.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīh. Bukhārī 527]"""""
"12600","(12595) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us in al-Kūfah, he said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah informed us, he said: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn al-ʿUmarī and ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā al-ʿAbsī narrated to us, they said: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed us from his father, from Abī Murāwiḥ, from Abū Dharr, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" which deed is best?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.\"" He said: \""Which slaves (are best to free)?\"" He ﷺ said: \""The most expensive of them and the most precious to their owners.\"" He said: \""What if I am unable?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Then help a weak person or do something for one who is unskilled.\"" He said: \""What if I do not do that?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Then leave the people from your harm"","" for it is a charity that you give on yourself.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīh. Bukhārī 527]"""""
"12601","(12596) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq informed us in the year two hundred and sixty-five: Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind informed us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Ḥakīm, the mawlā of the family of al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd ibn Marjānah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever frees a believing slave"","" Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" shall free for every limb of that slave a limb of his from the Fire. Indeed"","" He shall free the hand for the hand"","" the foot for the foot"","" and the private part for the private part.\"" Then ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn said to the narrator: \""Did you hear this from Abū Hurayrah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then summon Muṭarrif for me"",""\"" and he was one of his most devoted servants. When he stood before him"","" he said: \""You are free for the sake of Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 2517]"""""
"12602","(12597) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz informed us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd Abū al-Faḍl informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd informed us: Musaddad ibn Qaṭan informed us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us, from Abū Ghassān Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, from Saʿīd ibn Marjānah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever frees a believing slave"","" Allah shall free for every limb of that slave a limb of his own from the Fire"","" even his private part for his private part.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm"","" from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd"","" and Muslim narrated it from Dāwūd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12603","(12598) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Muʿādh informed us, from al-Ashʿath, from al-Ḥasan, that he said regarding a man who was negligent in paying zakāh and negligent in performing Ḥajj until death overtook him: al-Ḥasan used to say: \Begin with the Ḥajj and the zakāh.\"" Then he later said: \""No"","" by no means — do not leave it until the wealth has passed to others and he says: 'Perform Ḥajj on my behalf and pay zakāh on my behalf.' It is from the third.\"" Thus it is in this narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12604","(12599) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī informed us: Abū al-Azhar informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Hishām informed us, from al-Ḥasan, regarding a man who bequeaths that Ḥajj be performed on his behalf: He said: \If he had already performed Ḥajj"","" then it is from the third; and if he had not performed Ḥajj"","" then it is from the entire wealth"","" whether he made a bequest or not"","" and it is a debt upon him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12605","(12600) He said: And Abū Bakr informed us: Abū al-Azhar informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī and Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: \When a man bequeaths something that is an obligatory duty upon him — such as Ḥajj"","" or expiation for an oath"","" or expiation for ẓihār — then it is from the entire wealth.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12606","(12601) He said: And Abū Bakr informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, from Qays ibn Saʿd, from ʿAṭāʾ, and from Ziyād al-Aʿla, from al-Ḥasan, regarding a man who bequeaths Ḥajj or zakāh: They both said: \It is from the entire wealth.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he said: \""If he bequeaths Ḥajj or zakāh"","" then it is from the third"","" whether he performed Ḥajj or not.\"" And from Ibn Sīrīn is the same. And we hold the view of al-Ḥasan"","" Ṭāwūs"","" ʿAṭāʾ"","" and al-Zuhrī"","" where they said: \""It is in the position of a debt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12607","(12602) By way of evidence, from what Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Firās al-Mālikī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣāʾigh informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Abū ʿAwanah informed us, from Abī Bishr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \My mother vowed to perform Ḥajj but died before performing it. Shall I perform Ḥajj on her behalf?\"" He said:\n\n\""Yes"","" perform Ḥajj on her behalf. Tell me"","" if your mother had a debt"","" would you have paid it?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then discharge the debt of Allah"","" for He is more deserving of fulfillment.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā and Musaddad"","" from Abī ʿAwanah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Bukhārī 1315]"""""
"12608","(12603) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, from ʿĪsā ibn Maʿqil ibn Abī Maʿqil al-Asadī — Asad of Khuzaymah — Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām informed me, from his grandmother Umm Maʿqil, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Farewell Pilgrimage, he commanded the people to prepare themselves to accompany him, so we made preparations. Then I was afflicted with this eruption — smallpox or measles, she said. So there befell us from that what Allah willed. I fell ill, and Abū Maʿqil fell ill. As for Abū Maʿqil, he perished from it, she said. We had a camel upon which we irrigated our palm trees, and it was the one upon which we intended to perform Ḥajj. Abū Maʿqil dedicated it in the cause of Allah. We were preoccupied with what had befallen us, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) departed. When he completed his Ḥajj, I came to him when I had recovered from my illness. I entered upon him and he said: \O Umm Maʿqil"","" what prevented you from going out with us on this journey?\""\n\nShe said: I said: \""By Allah"","" we had prepared ourselves for it"","" but this eruption befell us. Abū Maʿqil perished from it"","" and I was afflicted with illness from it. This is when I recovered from it. We had a camel upon which we intended to go out"","" but Abū Maʿqil bequeathed it in the cause of Allah.\""\n\nHe said: \""Then why did you not go out upon it? For Ḥajj is in the cause of Allah. Now that this Ḥajj has passed you by with us"","" perform an ʿUmrah in Ramadan"","" for it is equal to a Ḥajj.\""\n\nShe said: She used to say: \""Ḥajj is Ḥajj"","" and ʿUmrah is ʿUmrah.\"" And indeed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said regarding this: \""I do not know whether it is specific to me because the Ḥajj passed me by"","" or whether it is for the people in general.\""\n\nYūsuf said: I narrated this ḥadīth to Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam"","" who was the governor of Madīnah in the time of Muʿāwiyah. He said: \""Who heard this ḥadīth with you from her?\"" I said: \""Maʿqil ibn Abī Maʿqil"","" and he is a Bedouin man.\"" Marwān sent for him"","" and he narrated to him the same as I had narrated to him. I said: \""Marwān"","" she is still alive in her house.\"" By Allah"","" he was not reassured by our ḥadīth until he rode to her with the people and entered upon her"","" and she narrated this ḥadīth to him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"12609","(12604) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Isḥāq al-Azraq informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik — meaning Ibn Abī Sulaymān — informed us, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: I said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar: \Dirhams have been sent to me to place in the cause of Allah"","" and among the pilgrims are those who are cut off and those whose provisions have been exhausted. Shall I distribute them among them?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" place them among them"","" for it is in the cause of Allah.\"" I said: \""I fear that my companion intended only the mujāhidīn.\"" He said: \""Place them among them"","" for they too are in the cause of Allah.\"" I said: \""I fear Allah that I may contradict what I have been commanded.\"" He became angry and said: \""Woe to you! Is it not in the cause of Allah?\"" This is the position of Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū al-Dardāʾ that it may be spent on military expeditions. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12610","(12605) Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī al-Sharīf al-Imām informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Shuʿbah informed us, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: A man bequeathed to me his wealth to place in the cause of Allah. I asked Ibn ʿUmar, and he said: \Indeed"","" Ḥajj is part of the cause of Allah"","" so place it therein.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""""
"12611","(12606) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik, from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, that he heard Anas ibn Mālik say: Abū Ṭalḥah was the wealthiest of the Anṣār in Madīnah, and his most beloved property to him was Bayruḥāʾ, which faced the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to enter it and drink from its pleasant water. Anas said: When this verse was revealed — \You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love\"" — Abū Ṭalḥah stood up before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" indeed Allah says in His Book"","" 'You will never attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love"",""' and indeed the most beloved of my properties to me is Bayruḥāʾ. It is a charity for Allah; I hope for its goodness and its reward with Allah. Place it"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" wherever Allah directs you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Bakh! That is a profitable (or 'yielding') property\"" — Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (i.e."","" the narrator) had doubt between the two wordings — \""and I have heard what you have said"","" and I think you should allocate it among your relatives.\"" Abū Ṭalḥah said: \""I shall do so"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So Abū Ṭalḥah distributed it among his relatives and the sons of his paternal uncles. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2769]"""""
"12612","(12607) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Darābjardī narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá said: I read back to Mālik, and he mentioned it, using the word \Bayrīḥā.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"12613","(12608) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Mālik narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \That which is prohibited through suckling (raḍāʿah) is that which is prohibited through birth (wilādah).\"" [Bukhārī]"""""
"12614","(12609) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAtakī narrated to us: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyá ibn Saʿīd, and Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm informed me from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Jibrīl continued to enjoin me regarding the neighbour to the point that I thought he would make the neighbour an heir.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6014]"""""
"12615","(12610) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abī ʿImrān, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have two neighbours; to which of them should I give a gift?\"" He said: \""To the one whose door is closer to you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl and others from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2259]"""""
"12616","(12611) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Dīnawarī informed us: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl ibn Dākhirah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī said: Dallāl bint Abī al-Mudill narrated to us: al-Ṣaḥbāʾ narrated to us from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" what is the right — or he said"","" what is the limit — of neighbourhood?\"" He said: \""Forty houses.\"" [Very Weak]"""""
"12617","(12612) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sarrāj informed us: Abū Muḥammad al-Qāsim ibn Ghānim ibn Ḥammūyah al-Ṭawīl narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Sayf narrated to us: Sukaynah narrated to me: Umm Hānīʾ bint Abī Ṣufrah informed me from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) enjoined me regarding the neighbour up to forty houses: ten from here"","" ten from here"","" ten from here"","" and ten from here.\"" Ismāʿīl said: \""From his right"","" from his left"","" in front of him"","" and behind him.\""\n\nIn both of these chains there is weakness. It is only known from the ḥadīth of Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) as a mursal narration: \""Forty houses constitute a neighbourhood.\"" It was said to Ibn Shihāb: \""How can it be forty houses?\"" He said: \""Forty from his right"","" from his left"","" behind him"","" and in front of him.\"" Abū Dāwūd cited it with his chain from al-Zuhrī in al-Marāsīl. [Very Weak]"""""
"12618","(12613) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī informed me: My grandfather informed us: Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrated from Yaḥyá ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, from his grandfather, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madīnah, he asked about al-Barāʾ ibn Maʿrūr. They said: \He has passed away and bequeathed one-third of his estate to you.\"" He said: \""I have returned his one-third to his children.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. [Weak]"""""
"12619","(12614) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Mūsá ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāfiʿ, the freedman of Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The daughter of Ḥafṣ ibn al-Mughīrah was married to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Rabīʿah. He divorced her with one divorce. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) married her. He was told that she was barren and could not bear children, so he divorced her before consummating the marriage. She remained so during the lifetime of ʿUmar and part of the caliphate of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both). Then ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Rabīʿah married her while he was ill, so that she might share with his other wives in the inheritance, and there was a kinship between them. [Weak]"
"12620","(12615) And with his chain, al-Shāfiʿī said: Saʿīd narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, that he heard ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid say: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Umm al-Ḥakam, during his illness, intended to exclude his wife from her inheritance, but she refused. So he married three other women alongside her, giving each of them a dower of one thousand dinars. ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān approved of this and made her share with them in the one-eighth. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \I consider this to be the equivalent dower (ṣadq al-mithl).\"" Al-Shāfiʿī also said: \""It has reached me that Muʿādh ibn Jabal said during the illness in which he died: 'Marry me (to a woman)"","" for I do not wish to meet Allah while I am unmarried.'\"" [Weak. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 4/104]"""""
"12621","(12616) Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlūsā al-Asadābādhī narrated to us in it: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ḥaywah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \The established Sunnah is that emancipation (of a slave) is to be given precedence in the will (waṣiyyah).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12622","(12617) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \When a man makes bequests and (includes) emancipation (of a slave)"","" precedence is given to emancipation.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12623","(12618) And from Sufyān, from al-Ashʿath, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, similarly: \Precedence is given to emancipation.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12624","(12619) And from Sufyān, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Ḥakam, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Precedence is given to emancipation before the bequests.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12625","(12620) And from Sufyān, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʬAṭāʾ, who said: \Precedence is given to emancipation.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12626","(12621) And from Sufyān, from Hishām, from al-Ḥasan, who said: \Precedence is given to emancipation.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12627","(12622) And from Sufyān, from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: \When a person makes bequests and (includes) emancipation"","" then (the estate is divided) according to shares (proportions).\"" [Weak]"""""
"12628","(12623) And from Sufyān, from Jābir and Muṭarrif, from al-Shaʿbī, a statement similar to that of Ibn Sīrīn. [Weak]"
"12629","(12624) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Layth, from Mujāhid, from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When there is a will and emancipation"","" they shall share proportionally.\"" [Weak]"""""
"12630","(12625) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad, that he said regarding a will in which there is emancipation and it exceeds one-third: \The one-third is to be divided among them proportionally.\"" [Authentic]"""""
"12631","(12626) He said: And Abū Bakr narrated to us, Abū Khālid narrated to us, from Ḥajjāj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \By shares (al-ḥiṣaṣ).\"" [Weak]"""""
